        "review": "Good product something of a learning curve for a non technical user but in the end a solid product Do you know what an upstream port is? Do you now what a downstream port is. It's not hard to learn about it But I needed to consult ChatGPT To be able to use this hub effectively"
    },
    {
        "review": "In a market saturated with crap electronics accessories, I happily pay 2-3x extra for Belkin products because they don't flake — seamless integration with my devices, fast and reliable data transfer, no bugs, etc. This hub meets my expectations on that front perfectly.It's also much cheaper than a true dock if you have enough ports on your machine otherwise and can deal with the extra cord mess.If all you care about is that it works, consider my review a 5. I was so annoyed by some non-functional issues with it, though, that I just can't.1) the protective stickers sealing the box and protecting the surfaces of the hub are maddeningly difficult to remove — like it took longer to remove them than it's taking me to write this review, and I am not a speedy writer. I appreciate that it's better for the environment than plastic film, but other tech companies have solved this problem without making it such a burden on the consumer — someone with less refined fine motor skills would not be able to remove them at all.2) it's a good thing they have it covered in these stickers, though, because this thing picks up fingerprints like mad. It's so bad you can see it from across the room.3) the cord is so short that if you store your laptop vertically, it hangs like a dongle. (Context - if you have a Mac, you need to dock your laptop in such a way that the vents aren't blocked, which puts the ports oriented upwards. Trust me — I fried a work laptop this way).  My plan was to mount it on the underside of my desk, which just wasn't happening with this tiny cord. I had a random male-to-female USB-C cord lying around and was able to extend it, but now I have more cord tidying to deal with, which was the very thing I was trying to avoid in the first place. This is probably not a problem specific to Belkin, to be fair, but if cord length is in the description, I didn't see it.If you don't care about those kinds of things, I highly recommend this hub, but I found them so frustrating that I probably would have returned it had I not made the mistake of adhering the fastener to it before checking cord length."
