    {
        "review": "TLDR: This is a fast, powerful, versatile 7-port USB 3.2 Gbps hub that gives you lots of ports which is especially useful for modern laptops which often only have one port.This connects to a laptop/PC via a USB-C cable. It also needs a power cable to function so make sure you are close to a wall outlet or even better, a surge protector.You get 7 ports - 4 USB-C ports and 3 classic USB-A ports. They are all version 3.2 ports with a speeds up to 10Gbps. You can toggle each one on/off with the buttons on the side. The ports have a light that comes on with enabled.It's got sturdy aluminum body so it's safe to transport and won't get damaged in your backpack.Performance‑wise, it’s handled everything I’ve thrown at it. I’ve had multiple drives, a mouse, a keyboard, and a couple of random accessories plugged in at the same time, and it didn’t choke or overheat — just got slightly warm, which is normal. The 10Gbps ports definitely move files quickly, and the external power supply keeps everything stable. It’s not meant to fast‑charge big devices, but for data and powering smaller gear, it’s been rock‑steady.If you need a dependable, powered hub with a mix of USB‑A and USB‑C ports and don’t want to spend a fortune, this one’s easy to recommend.The company: I'm a big fan of this brand. I own other products from them, and they are all great quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Rosonway 7 Ports Powered USB 3.2/USB C Hub  RSH-H7C4This a really compact and robust feeling device. It is attractive with polished chrome accents against a matte black finish, so it doesn’t fingerprint. The size a small enough to easily fit in my modest laptop bag. It’s small for having so many ports, about the size of a small remote control. The USB cable is thick and feels like it’s designed to carry the throughput it’s intended too. I found no difference between transfer speeds of a hard drive compared to it plugged directly into my computer.1. External Mechanical Hard Drive Throughput: See attachment.2. Good packaging3. The cords aligned with the length coming out the back make it easy to put anywhere. The ports on top make it easy to put in tight spaces. Similar products with the ports on the sides/edges make it difficult to put in tight spaces on small work surfaces4. SD Card reader used in the device:  92mb – 165mb/s  (In computer: 91-167mb/s)5. There are switches on the edge of the unit to turn devices on or off. Very handy.What’s nice is that all of these are contained in a single device. My laptop case gets full of all kinds of extra stuff, and just carrying this one device, I can pretty much take care of all of my input and output tasks.In closing, I would recommend this device. It works as well as described, and the price seems fair considering all of its functions."
