    {
        "review": "My work laptop only has 2 USB-As and 1 USB-C ports and BT is disabled and I need to connect more devices than available ports. So I'm using this to connect my wireless keyboard and mouse, speaker, ring light, and a 2.5Gbps ethernet adapter. It's got 4 USB-C and 3 USB-A plugs so you have your choice of connections. It's compact and the cables are long enough to reach the outlet on the floor. I like the buttons have an audible and tactile click to turn on and does require a long-press to turn off so it doesn't accidentally disconnect a device - something that does happen to one of my other USB hubs.The body is aluminum so it's got a solid feel and the cables are thick and solid so I think it will last a while for travel."
