[
    {
        "review": "Great quality, great battery and connectivity. Good value for the money. Easy to connect and set up. Compact but spacious when using.The sound of the keys, responsiveness, feel, and appearance are all great. The keys sound really pleasing to the ear when typing. I ended up not loving the feeling of the keys for but that is entirely my own fault for not testing what the different key switches feel like since I'm new to mechanical keyboards. Its easily for me to accidentally click a key multiple times due to the lack of strong response from the keyboard - which is a benefit i think for certain kinds of gaming - just not one I'm fully used to yet.Definitely a great purchase and a company / model I would recommend to others. If you're new to the mechanical keyboards, maybe swing through a bigger in person store like Best Buy prior to purchasing and get a feel for what kind of switches you like."
    },
    {
        "review": "I LOVE this keyboard!! After spending two weeks researching I decided on the Aula F99 and I am so happy with my decision. I’m not a gamer but wanted a full keyboard for work and this checked all the boxes. The sound is so creamy and reminds me of marbles or smooth stones. It’s so fun to type on and the RGB is kinda fun too. Bluetooth connected with ease, so did wired. Haven’t tried the dongle yet but so far it’s been plug and play play with no issues. Feels sturdy not cheap. Sounds great out of the box. Ordered the Gatreon Milky Yellow switches but I may not even need them cuz I’m kinda digging this sound already. It’s soooo satisfying. Great value!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "First I want to say that I initially bought this for my husband as he had bought a walmart clicky brand keyboard and was finally growing tired of the clicky sound lol. Well as the keyboard enthusiast I suggested this one as it was simple and a few of the review videos had sounded promising.When it arrived the first thing I noticed was the heft, this was made with durable material and not light weight at all, which put some ease to my mind that it wasn't just made of cheap plastic. The size was just perfect, I couldn't be happier, and when I typed for the first time the creamy and thocky sound just itched the right place in my brain. I could not get enough of it.I love that there are 3 types of way that you can connect, BT; Dongle or wired. I always prefer wired.The keycaps are nice, although I prefer rounded keycaps to the sharp square ones, I did replace the factory keycaps and I just fell in love with this more. The switches sound nice and deep and honestly, this is almost perfect for me, I'll be playing around with this keyboard especially since it's hot swappable and I might try other switches.For those just starting out with interest in the keyboard area, this is a great first start with a not too expensive price point! I did end up having to buy another keyboard for my husband since I stole this one, it was definitely worth it though! Can't wait to mod this one a little more!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve had this keyboard for almost 2 months now and wanted to wait to write a review until I had used it for a while. I’ve got to say this keyboard is awesome. recently got a WFH after only ever working in an office so I knew I wanted to invest in a nice keyboard. I spent at least a week researching and reading reviews on keyboards and didn’t realize how hard it would be to find nice keyboard with a num pad but I kept coming back to this one because of the amazing reviews and of course I love the way it sounds! For the average person yes this is a little bit on the pricier side but to me it was totally worth it, I like that it has 3 forms of connection (Wired, Bluetooth, and USB), there are a million different RGB options and it sounds amazing and it comes with super easy instructions and you can change the key caps if you want nicer keys. I will say, as you can see in the video I have two keys where the lighting under them doesn’t work/ change color, but I still have it 5 stars because it doesn’t affect the function of the key board. Another slight inconvenience is that you do have to charge it with the wire after a few days if you’re using Bluetooth or USB and it doesn’t give a low power warning but besides that it’s perfect. I also want to note that I have seen that this key board had gone a little viral on TikTok and I did purchase before it was trending so I would say if you are coming here from TikTok no, it’s not a scam it’s actually a great keyboard!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my initial return to mechanical keyboards and was purchased impulsively based on Amazon's recommendation.I don't have comparisons to make, but I truly enjoy the sound and feel of this keyboard. I have actively been searching for ways and reasons to type more (this review for example).Of note, and significant for me as the use is often in dark room, the RGB backlighting does not shine through the keycaps - it actually makes it harder to determine the key you are looking for. Once my hands are back on the home row, I am able to find what I need, but I was really hoping a keyboard with backlighting would make the occasional unexpected keypress more convenient. Personally I ordered a set of shine through keycaps, and plan to replace specific keys for convenience.I am currently predominantly using this as my home device for a television connected Mac mini, and as such am unable to utilize the customization software (not compatible with Mac). This hasn't been an issue with functionality, but I am enjoying this experience so much, I have already been using it connected to my work laptop and am considering  switching this to my full time work keyboard as the typing experience is so much better than that of my already great Thinkpad keyboard (I would actually use a keyboard more for work: than I would in my living room).The case is obviously a plastic (ABS, PTB?) but doesn't feel cheap. There is significant weight to the unit; not so much to be uncomfortable in my lap, but noticeable when picking up with one hand (especially compared to the flimsy units was used to -i.e. Logitech, apple. arteck). I love the sound and feel of the switches and keycaps; it only makes me want to explore what other types may offer, and with the hot swappable capabilities I could do so.No notes on battery life yet. Still on first charge with minimal backlighting usage, but the unit does come with appropriate cable if you needed to connect physically.There may be, and probably are better keyboards, or a different keyboard better suited to your needs, but I am pleased with this unit and would recommend. I would normally have shopped around more to compare features and prices, but I didn't and am not disappointed.(The 10-key number pad is huge plus for me, especially when connected for work activities)"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Aula F99 is a \"96%\" mechanical keyboard that comes in around the $90 price point normally, but can get as low as $60 on sale. That form factor means that it does have a numpad and arrow keys as well as home, delete and page up/down keys, but those keys are moved up in-line with the function keys and the numpad/arrow keys are squished up closer to the main keys with the arrow keys set a little further down to make space. Having a numpad was a must for me because I like to play games that often use the numpad for important functions, and I also prefer typing numbers on a numpad when the occasion arises. At this price point, this is probably one of the best options for people who want a numpad and/or arrow keys but still want a keyboard that looks and sounds more like a custom keyboard you see in YouTube shorts of people doing sound tests.It has linear switches meaning there's no \"bump\" or clickiness to them, I'm not 100% sure what exact switches they are because there is some conflicting information online. I think mine has \"Star Vector\" switches? Regardless, the switches are quite light on force and very quiet, which brings us to the sound. This keyboard sounds great for the price. It's a little on the clacky side, but the switches have no scratchiness to them and are obviously pre-lubed, and there appears to be some kind of sound-deadening material inside the case as there is none of that hollow pinginess you get from something like a cheap Logitech mechanical. Overall it is a massive improvement from the Logitech keyboard I had previously to this one.The case is plastic but seems to be fairly high quality. The keyboard is surprisingly heavy which is very confidence inspiring and gives you a very stable feeling typing experience. It also has RGB lighting on all of the keys but the keycaps are not shine-through meaning the lettering doesn't light up. If that's a big deal to you, I'm sure you could swap them out for something else later as it does come with a keycap and switch puller, which also means you can change the switches if you want. It also has 3 different connection modes: \"Wired\" which uses a USB-C port on the board for connection (and it does come with a USB-C to A cable in the box), \"2.4 GHz\" which uses a little wireless dongle that sits in a little slot on the top edge of the board when not in use, and it's also able to connect via bluetooth. I haven't tested the battery life as I use this keyboard at my desktop computer with the wired connection, but having the different modes and a physical switch to change between them means you could have this board connected to multiple different devices and switch between them whenver you want which is cool and useful if you need that.I'm fairly new to the world of mechanical keyboards, this is only the second one I've ever owned, the first being a Logitech board that didn't sound or feel nearly as good as this one. As I type this review out on this very keyboard, I find myself liking the sound and feeling more and more. I'm sure there are things about it that someone with more knowledge and experience could pick apart and criticize, but overall I am very happy with this keyboard and would definitely recommend it to anyone who's not an expert and is looking for something better than the offerings from companies like Logitech and Razer."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had a few mechanical keyboards before, but this one so far is my favorite. The creamy switches have an amazingly satisfying feel and sound. Enough tactile feedback to know you hit the key, a bit \"thocky\", but not so clacky as to be annoying or overly loud. The condensed layout takes a bit of getting used to, but that's true of any \"less than 100%\" sized keyboard. The only key that bothers me a bit in the layout is the \"0\" on the numpad, but I'm getting used to it. I haven't played with the lighting much, but it definitely helps visibility in low light. Bluetooth connection has been rock solid, and the battery life even with the lighting on has been phenomenal; after a few weeks of moderate use, I have yet to have to charge it. Overall I'm extremely happy with the purchase, highly recommend it... it's definitely a leader in \"bang for buck\" vs some of the higher priced brands!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Completely honest I thought this keyboard would be like the hundreds of others offered on Amazon, all claiming to have certain traits and deliver none.. but this one, the AULA F99 isn't one of those! It exceeded expectations right out of the box! Immediately notice the nice packaging, followed by the extremely sturdy build. Feels strong, looks great. But the SOUND ❤️ . The sound you get right out of the box is amazing, that \"marble switch\" type sound. Just perfect. Immediately connected to my windows 11 too, I didn't even have to do anything myself. The best way I can describe this keyboard is a more budget friendly version of the logitech alto key k98!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent keyboard for its price. It has very good build quality, the keys feel comfortable and pleasant when typing and playing, and the battery has given me good performance. Plus, the lighting and design give it a very premium look. So far it has exceeded my expectations and has been one of my best purchases. I would recommend it without problem."
    },
    {
        "review": "Even though the order was placed on Sunday, I received it the same day. My first impressions of the keyboard are that it is really nice. He has a very soft voice. And the application works successfully. I recommend this product, which you will definitely be satisfied with. After three months of use, I can say that it is the best product I have ever bought. First of all, his voice is amazing, I really loved it. It makes me want to write. It is also great that it comes wired and wireless. I tried it wirelessly and with the lights on and it went away for about 10 days, I tried it with the lights off and it went on for more than 3 weeks and it's still going. It charges very fast with the cable, the lighting is great. It is great to write Turkish letters on the keyboard on the shore. Lighting is managed very well from the app. In addition, it would be crazy if the letters also illuminated in the dark. The light does not pass through the letters, but I do not feel the lack of grams. These keys can be changed in the future. They don't shift the weight, they work great. The slope is also very nice and the slope can be given in two levels. I was looking for a keyboard with a keypad, so this product met exactly what I wanted. Once it reaches the end of its life, I will buy the same product of the same brand again. I hope my comment will be useful to someone."
    },
    {
        "review": "Incredible keyboard, with soft keys and pleasant sound, excellent construction, with good materials, very robust and heavy. I had keyboards like the razor blackwidow and it is superior. And the best part, it comes standard abnt2!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The best in class Keyboard I have ever used! The Typing Experience just feels awesome! Earlier, I was using Dell Wireless!Saw some Video on Social Media, and Man'O'Man! FELL IN LOVE WITH THIS KEYBOARD!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have had this keyboard for a month now, and wow! It is by far the best keyboard in my collection. I love a nice creamy typing experience, and this more than delivers. I had been searching for a full keyboard that was versatile and easy to use. I bring it back and forth from work, and with my wedding planning, I've put it through it recently. There are 2 different heights that you can set the keyboard to for wrist support, and thanks to the larger keys, I can have a full set of nails and have 0 issues typing.My only complaint is that the light that indicates the battery is always red, even when fully charged. I'm not too sure why this happens, but it doesn't bother me.Great brand. Great quality. Beautiful design."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Just received my RisoPhy RGB Mechanical Gaming Keyboard and I'm already impressed! Unboxing was smooth — everything was well packaged and arrived in perfect condition.Right out of the gate, the mechanical switches feel fantastic — satisfying and responsive with great tactile feedback. Typing this review on it now and it already feels way better than my old membrane keyboard.The RGB lighting looks amazing — all 104 keys are individually backlit with tons of color and lighting mode options. Instantly upgraded the look of my desk setup.Build quality feels solid and premium — no flex, no creaking, and the keycaps have a nice, smooth texture. It's a standard full-size layout with number pad, so it was easy to jump right in with no learning curve.Can't speak to long-term durability yet, but based on first impressions, this keyboard seems like an excellent value. Will update if anything changes, but so far I'm very happy"
    },
    {
        "review": "My 11 year old autistic child started homeschool keyboarding last year. She was struggling with the small laptop keyboard. She has a lot of the clicking keyboard fidgets so I got the idea to try a clicking keyboard. This keyboard has a lot of wonderful features that make it approachable for a new typer. It lights up in pretty rainbow colors, it has a really pleasing clicking sound, and it is on the larger side. We have not used this for gaming so I can’t speak to those features. However, as a keyboard for typical use it is fantastic. We’ve used it for over a year and it still looks new. Oh and I have connected this to both my Mac laptop and my child’s 7th generation iPad with their respective adapter and it works perfectly. Great keyboard and great value."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this keyboard for my office, as a replacement for a wireless, membrane based keyboard that was starting to show its age.The value of this keyboard is excellent.  Based on the feel, it seems to be a true mechanical keyboard with switches, and not a simulated one using a membrane contact with a clicky mechanism.  The feel is great and the pressure is just right to prevent most accidental touches to adjacent keys from inserting extra letters.  Nice and clicky, maybe not the best for noise if you're in an office with other people, but the feel is great and if you work in a private office like I do the noise won't matter much.  I had thought the RGB colors would be distracting, especially for an office, but actually they are fairly subdued and actually seem to help with positioning (I am a fast hunt-and-peck 3 finger typist, so this actually matters a lot to me).I have a much more expensive Razer mechanical gaming keyboard at home, and the main difference I see between them, other than cosmetic differences, is that the Razer keys seem like they have a hair trigger and require very little motion to produce keystrokes, while this keyboard is a bit stiffer and requires the keys to be depressed a little harder in order to produce a keystroke.  So if you are relying on a hair trigger response for gaming, this maybe is not the best choice, although for a casual gamer like me it's more than adequate.  But for actually getting work done, the hair-trigger of the Razer keyboard makes it really hard not to make typos, and this keyboard is a lot better in that regard.One minor nitpick is that the font used to label the keys is a little odd, and the \"6\" really, really looks like a \"G\", which can be a little off-putting at first.  But that's just a minor quibble.Final verdict:  Definitely worth buying, unless you're an absolutely elite hardcore gamer."
    },
    {
        "review": "OK, I love everything about this keyboard, but one thing. The RGB lights don’t change to solid back light colors. You are stuck with the rainbow and can’t do anything like solid yellow, which is my go to. That said, this is an absolutely awesome keyboard.The click is very crisp and loud, which I absolutely love. It feels so cathartic to type away, especially with the resounding click that the suns throughout my room. The material is very high-quality and easy to clean. I imagine the keys will accumulate oil like most keyboards do and become a little shinier, but overall, it’s pretty easy to remove lint from and would be easy to clean spills off of."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really clicky and bright, and works really good for typing or especially gaming."
    },
    {
        "review": "If you missed the old,clicky Model M from IBM, this keyboard emulates it pretty well.  One must consider though, that it may emulate it too well.  If you have fat fingers, you will find yourself making the same typos that you mad in high school when you learned to type on one.  However, this is no deal breaker in my opinion.  The speed at which I can type has vastly improved with the solid tactile feedback that tells you without a doubt that you press was registered.Setup couldn't be easier, just plug it into any USB port and away you go.  Recognizes immediately as a 104 key with perks.  Having the media controls and other immediate functions right there is nice too.As far as the design goes, it is very rugged and ready for the millions of keystrokes you will put on it as a writer.  You will find a kind of typing joy you haven't experienced in quite a long time.  No soft-touch or sickle keyboard will match the feel from what you get here.The only thing I find really off is the shallow height of the back stands. I think that they should be redesigned to be a bit taller.  I cut a little piece of flat trim to set them on and that made the angle perfect.All-in-all, this keyboard is a joy to type on.  I don't use it for gaming, because I see this as a waste of a premium feeling keyboard, wearing out the ASWD area and ruining it.  I haven't had such a good keyboard in years and I'm not destroying that way.The one caveat I would warn you about is that if you use it on a KVM switch that is USB powered, this keyboard draws quite a bit of power to run the back light.  be aware that you may get video background issues.  Mine works just fine if I turn the backlight down low."
    },
    {
        "review": "This keyboard was just what I was looking for. It is plug-and-play, has loud clacky keys, and works great with my Ubuntu system. However, the keys are VERY loud which isn’t a complaint for me but if you aren’t a fan of obnoxiously loud mechanical keyboards do not buy this. I have no other complaints this product both net and exceeded my expectations in terms of connectivity, ease of use, and quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "After using this mechanical gaming keyboard for well over a year now, I can confidently say it's one of the best purchases I've ever made — not a single issue has come up the entire time. It's seen heavy daily use for both gaming and typing, and it's held up beautifully, including one memorable incident where I accidentally spilled soda right onto it; I was able to quickly disassemble it, clean it thoroughly with water and some rubbing alcohol, and it came back working like nothing ever happened, which speaks volumes about its build quality and durability. The RGB lighting is absolutely vibrant and stunning, with multiple settings and effects that let me customize the look to match my setup, whether I'm going for a subtle glow or a full-blown rainbow light show. The mechanical blue switches are honestly the sweet spot — they offer that satisfying, tactile clicky feel that's so satisfying for typing, while still being incredibly responsive and snappy for gaming, and thanks to the full anti-ghosting on the 104 keys, every single keypress registers perfectly even during the most intense, fast-paced gaming moments. With its rugged build, gorgeous RGB, fantastic switches, and full-sized layout, this keyboard has completely exceeded my expectations — I couldn't recommend it more to anyone looking for a reliable, high-performing mechanical keyboard!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Beautiful keyboard! The tactile keys are so satisfying to press!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolute game changer.  I type everyday as an admin worker and now rarely make a typo.  Blew my mind how this has improved my typing.  Would recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "This mechanical keyboard is amazing for gamers looking to pick up a high-quality blue-switch mechanical keyboard. When I consider and review this product, I keep the following factors in mind:Functionality and Use - 5/5The overall functionality of this keyboard is perfect, leaving me with minimal complains as a high-frequency and intensity user. As a proficient typist, I frequently type over 120 WPM and use combinations of hotkeys to complete tasks efficiently. This keyboard has supported this level of use during work/office settings, and feels highly responsive and crisp during high-intensity gaming moments, due to the blue key-switches creating a noticeable \"click\" with each keypress. If you have roommates or family, you may want to consider the clicking sounds of this keyboard while typing. The fact that they will likely hear your typing due to the pure \"clicky-ness\" of the key switches may present itself as an issue to some. Personally, this is not a factor that applies to my circumstances.Build Quality and Durability - 5/5After 1 Month of intensive use, I have not noticed any issues so far in terms of key-press responsiveness, structural integrity, or wiring/USB issues. The keys hold in place well and the LED's have stayed consistently bright.Product Design - 5/5The design of this keyboard is minimal, but effective. Exactly what I was looking for when shopping for a keyboard within this general price range. The all-black style allows the LED backlights to really *pop*, even in bright light/daylight. The inclusion of a \"Fn\" key allows for the same hotkeys and macros most would be used to with other keyboards, such as volume control and media playback, amongst other things.QoL Features - 4.5/5This keyboard comes with 9 different LED-backlighting effects, such as lighting per keypress, \"breathing\" effects, WASD + Arrow Key backlighting, and more to complement a variety of use-cases. It would be nice to have the option to customize the LED backlighting colours themselves, as the backlighting options are pre-set; however, the crisp glow and colour choice are visually appealing and I am happy with the options provided.Value for Money - 5/5Overall, I am highly satisfied with the purchase of this Keyboard and would recommend it to any gamer, office-worker, or avid tech geek like myself. For such a low price-point, you are getting a physical product that is equal in quality to that of a name brand like Razer or Corsair, without paying for the related bloatware and branding. Anybody looking to pick up their first mechanical keyboard, you cannot go wrong with this!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very satisfied with this purchase. Head and shoulders above my membrane Logitech K120 Wired Business Keyboard, and without breaking the bank too! To be honest, I feel lucky to have gotten this keyboard at such a low price. At this price point, I could not find a single mechanical keyboard that met all of my requirements but this one. In fact, even some of the more expensive mechanical keyboards didn't meet all of my requirements. For starters, the keyboard uses the UK layout with the pound sign and hash symbol key in the right place—very important for me. Second, this is a full-size keyboard with a numeric keypad at the right. This was important for me as I wanted a keyboard that did all of the same things as my previous keyboard, the only difference being that it is mechanical—a requirement that this RisoPhy mechanical keyboard fulfils precisely. (I should note, too, that most of the mechanical keyboards at this price range and even some more expensive ones, being shorter in width, lacked a numeric keypad.) Then there is the feel of the keyboard. The product description says that it uses \"BLUE switches\", seemingly modelling its switches on the classic tactile and clicky Cherry MX Blue switches. (It is unlikely that the keyboard uses actual Cherry MX Blue switches, given the price range, but rather its own knock-off versions of the switches.) While this may not be what some gamers are looking for (looking for something smoother and offering the same resistance all the way down without a slight bump as you press each key), this is perfect for me, as I was looking for a keyboard that produced nice responsive, tactile feedback, mirroring a classic typewriter effect. Some people may be put off by this, thinking that it makes the keyboard too noisy, and while, yes, there is a clicking noise with each key press, it honestly isn't that loud (though because there is still an audible clicking noise, I can understand criticisms saying that this keyboard is inappropriate for an office environment, for example, where such a constant clicking noise can cause distractions.) The keyboard is nice to type on, which is my primary use for it rather than gaming.A feature I don't care as much for is the rainbow backlighting. From my tests, the \"9 different backlights\" settings mentioned in the product description work exactly as expected. Also working as intended (at least from my tests on Windows 11) are the \"12 multimedia combinations\", effectively function keys that perform operations, such as, open a calculator and open Windows search.The major downside to this keyboard that I can think of is that the keyboard switches are not hot-swappable (though at this price point, this isn't a disappointment but just something to be expected.)In all, if you are looking for a keyboard that meets some of the same requirements as I was, at this price, I am unaware of a better keyboard on this website than this one."
    },
    {
        "review": "It was time for a new keyboard again. Since I previously had a rubber dome keyboard and it was sometimes a bit sluggish when making entries in the game, I now had to get a mechanical keyboard. I have enough space on the desk, so it can be a 100% keyboard. Since I had never heard of RisoPhy before, I definitely wanted to give the keyboard a chance. And it was worth it! The inputs are very fast, the keys have a pleasant pressure point and the clicking of the clicky switches is clearly audible, but not too loud. I still wouldn't want to write a term paper in one go😂. If you put on a headset, the clicking is actually no longer audible. Even if the keyboard doesn't have extra media keys or a volume wheel, you can, as usual with other keyboards, simply use the FN keys to switch volume up, down, next song, etc. Clear purchase recommendation from me, especially for the price👍 assuming you like Clickys😉"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This is the first mechanical keyboard that i got and i absolutely love it. It definitely makes the typing experience more relaxing - the keys have the perfect creamy think to it. If you type really fast it sounds like pebbles in the creek ^.^I did some research before getting a keyboard since i wanted something of a good quality but was prepared to drop $100+ on it. Very pleased with the quality of t his one - it feels very sturdy, the keys have just enough resistance to effortless typing.With the knob you can switch different color modes and adjust the brightness or control volume.It also allows pairing with 3 devices (and switch with a brass of a button, well, 2 buttons but u get it) via Bluetooth and it’s very convenient since i can use it with my computer, iPad and steam deck.I use Mac book and the translation from cmd , option and, control buttons are a bit confusing since the keyboard is for windows, but once you get used to it it’s ok.All my friends without mechanical keyboards now want one and all my friends with one approved the buy =DDOh, and I obviously replaced the keycaps - now the light mode really looks magical."
    },
    {
        "review": "This keyboard has a great feel right out of the box. The pre-lubed switches provide a smooth, satisfying keypress, and the sound is pleasant without being excessively loud.The 75% layout is a great balance between compact size and functionality. It keeps the important navigation and arrow keys while taking up considerably less desk space than a full-size keyboard. The wireless connectivity is also convenient and makes for a cleaner setup.The hot-swappable design is a major plus for anyone who enjoys customizing their keyboard. Being able to change switches without soldering gives you plenty of options to personalize the typing experience later.The keys feel responsive and consistent, whether I'm typing or gaming. The overall construction also feels solid, especially for the price.Overall, this is an excellent mechanical keyboard with a smooth typing experience, useful wireless functionality, and plenty of customization potential."
    },
