        "review": "For a stock budget keyboard, I am *in love*. The sound is gorgeous; deep and thocky and super creamy. Sounds like rain on a tarp in the best way. It is super comfortable to use and the keys take very little pressure to press, so typing on this is a breeze. It feels sturdy and heavy and substantial, not cheap, light and rattly. This definitely feels like a quality keyboard and I highly, highly recommend it to those who are particular on their keyboard sounds!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Creamy, adorable, lights are amazing, perfect size, lovely blue! It’s just an amazing product. It comes with a key switcher thing and extra keys in case. It also has a usb so you don’t have to plug it in and it is amazing with computer and has no glitchy features."
    },
    {
        "review": "I mean you can't complain with the price. It is a good quality keyboard for the pricepoint and it doesn't look bad either. I bought this as an alternative to my work membrane keyboard and switched out the switches to a more silent one as these were too loud.  The battery life is decent I find I can get around three work days of battery life with the RGB on before needing to charge. The quality and durability are OK for the price point. It has slight give to it when you put force on it, and sometimes the keys become slightly misaligned and wobbly. Overall, a good keyboard with decent features."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the AULA F75 keyboard as my main keyboard, and it has been a great upgrade from my previous one, especially considering the price. I mainly use it wired, but I also tested the Bluetooth connection and it worked perfectly fine with no issues. The overall connectivity has been excellent, and I haven’t had any problems using it with my games.The RGB lighting looks really nice and adds a lot to the keyboard’s overall appearance. I do wish there were more RGB customization options and selections available, but the included effects are still enjoyable and look great.The Reaper switches feel and sound amazing. In person, the keys have a really creamy sound profile, while in videos they seem to come across as a bit more thocky. The typing experience feels smooth, satisfying, and enjoyable.The multifunction knob is one of my favorite features. I mainly use it for controlling volume, and having quick access without needing keyboard shortcuts is extremely convenient. It’s a small addition, but it makes everyday use much easier.For gaming, this keyboard has been great for me. Everyone has different preferences when it comes to switches and keyboard feel, but personally, I really enjoy using it while gaming. The responsiveness, comfort, and connectivity have all been solid.Overall, the AULA F75 is an excellent upgrade at its price point. I’m very happy with it so far, and I’m definitely interested in trying out other versions of this keyboard in the future. For now, this has been a fantastic choice, and I would recommend it to anyone looking for a quality mechanical keyboard without spending a lot."
    },
    {
        "review": "Obsessed! The pink and cream color combination is gorgeous in person. It’s so clean and cute and the RGB makes it even prettier. It comes with the strawberry mint switches and the keys feel so good to type on (buttery?) and the sound is so satisfying and thocky. I also love how easy it is to switch between devices. It feels really sturdy and it’s honestly one of my favorite desk purchases! 5/5 ⭐️"
    },
    {
        "review": "I highly suggest this keyboard for those who want their keyboard to sound creamy, thocky and silent. the greywood v3 switches the aula f75 sea salt blue uses is very good and silent, while also sounding incredible. I had to watch videos on how the keyboard sounds with these switches, and it sounds way better when you have it in real life. Its really high quality for a budget friendly keyboard, really responsive, beautiful color, and the feeling on the keyboard is insane. Highly recommended :D"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve used the AULA F75 for over six months, and it delivers outstanding typing and gaming performance. The sound is **crisp and satisfying**, with a thocky depth thanks to its gasket mount and five-layer dampening. The factory-lubed switches offer smooth, consistent feedback—no scratchiness or ping—perfect for long sessions.The 75% layout saves space without sacrificing functionality, and the volume knob is a practical addition. Tri-mode connectivity (wired, 2.4GHz, Bluetooth) is reliable, with no lag in gaming. Battery life lasts over a week with RGB off.Build quality is solid, with durable PBT keycaps and minimal wobble. My only note: the **backlight isn’t shine-through**, so RGB is subtle unless keycaps are upgraded.For its price, the AULA F75 offers premium feel, sound, and versatility. Highly recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "Unfforunetly this keyboard doesn't have an app for mac, Have to use other software to for tweking stuff on the keyboard( whihc is a pain). But I love this keyboard, feels great,its heavy and it sounds like im making popcorn, Its not very loud which is a good thing nor is the sound sharp. Quality is 5/5."
    },
    {
        "review": "Genuinely beautiful keyboard I’m in love with it, there are multiple options with lighting and it’s a great value for money."
    },
    {
        "review": "The AULA F75 White is an absolute stunner. The build feels premium — solid frame, no flex, and that clean white finish just makes the whole setup look next-level. The typing feel is insanely good — smooth switches, zero wobble, and that thocky sound that’s just addictive.Connectivity’s flawless too — whether wired or wireless, it wakes instantly and stays super responsive. The RGB is bright and crisp without being overdone, and the keycaps have this nice matte texture that feels great under the fingers.But honestly, the best part? That white aesthetic. It’s sleek, minimal, and makes your desk look so clean and futuristic. It’s the kind of keyboard you keep glancing at just because it looks that good.If you’re into performance and aesthetics, the AULA F75 White nails both. Absolute gem for the price."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Ok, so after spending a couple weeks with this board I can tell you-A couple of things I wasn't really aware of-1) Just how much pressure I'm used to applying at rest on keys2) How much I relied on outside esc and ctrl keys for orientationThese keys are very sensitive compared to the old BW I've used for years. I've been accidentally entering a lot of keystrokes at rest. They are very quiet and soft stroking compared to the green switches in the older Black Widow I've retired. So if you want clicks, feedback or resistance look elsewhere. Believe it or not my main hesitation for getting this board was the outside left row of programmable keys. I was afraid that it would be in the way and get confused with my escape and control keys, which yes has been very challenging to get used to, but it's no fault of the board itself knowing what I was getting. I pulled up all those caps on that row and replaced with wider pudding caps for brighter distinction. Programed those keys to mirror their neighbors, esc ,Ctrl etc so that when an erroneous keystroke is made it should at least still be the function I was looking for, albeit orientation may be off from wasd. So anyway I'm having to look down a lot more at the keyboard and retraining my mind to orient off the *F key"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have the green switch version.Durable and Chroma lighting is excellent. Put O rings in the keys to dampen slightly. Key feeling and clicks are a matter of personal preference.Spilled coffee on this one twice. I thought the keyboard was toast after the last disaster spill. Keys weren't functioning and the leds were out. I took it apart and rinsed it out the affected areas heavily with alcohol. Blew the liquid out with compressed air/compressor. Works fine now.After taking it apart I could see how good the quality was. Keyboard backplate is actually solid metal.2 screws under the top two rubber foot pads. Careful, the pads tear easily.18+- screws under the keys. Remove the keys to find them all."
    },
    {
        "review": "Zero complaints, satisfying sound, a lot of cool features. Very satisying feeling when typing, not loud or clunky at all. You can tell the quality of the build by the weigh it feels and it's weight. I love also the volume wheel, so cool!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Had it for a bit over a week now and it's been great. I originally had the Razer blackwidow V1 with the green clicks switches and it was great the thing finally crapped out on me a few weeks ago. The thing lasted me forever, was super durable and felt very responsive. My biggest complaint was it was hard to clean. So I decided to go with the newest version and try the Yellow switches. I didn't like the softer yellow switches at first but have come to like them and this keyboard solved the cleaning issue. My biggest problem was actually the Macro keys on the left hand side. With my old keyboard I used the edge of they keyboard to orient my hand without looking when gaming, this makes it hard to do that because my fingers end up on the macro keys. I've started to retrain myself to position properly but it wasn't easy. Other than that this keyboard is fantastic."
    },
    {
        "review": "Fun RGB lighting, fully customizable colors within the Razer lighting program. Lighting program is easy to use with plenty of tutorials on installation. Can customize individual keys for different lighting when pressed. Extra macro buttons on the left will take some getting used to, but just imagine what all you can assign them as. Solid keyboard in terms of weight, back wings to lift up to have it at a slight angle. Keycaps nice and solid quality. These are soft and bubbly sounding in my opinion, not sharp and clicky.  In prior experience with Razer, the price is a bit up there, but I would wager its worth it.  Received on September 28th, 2025; will check back after a while to update review if needed."
    },
    {
        "review": "Awesome keyboard!"
    },
    {
        "review": "love it its not too loud feels amazing"
    },
    {
        "review": "Before I got this keyboard, I was using the 2016 edition razer blackwidow ultimate. That keyboard still works perfectly, and the only problem I had with it was that the keyboard was LOUD as heck.Enter the blackwidow v4 x with yellow switches. At first i was extremely happy with the look, feel, and materials of the keyboard, it felt very premium, and the keys were MUCH quieter.I bought it in December of 2023. By March 2024 I noticed an issue with the \"P\" key being unresponsive. Meaning when you press the key, there was a chance of it not registering the keypress. So if you press the key 10 times, it may only display about 5 or 6 times. Not that bad for gaming since the \"P\" key is hardly used. However when typing it could get very annoying. I attached a video showing me trying to press the button 3 times, followed by a space, then the button 3 times, then a space etc. You can clearly see it does not register the keypress quite often.Eventually I decided that since I paid $100+ I was going to get a working product. My RMA process started on April 20, 2024, and after many days of back and forth emails with razer trying to convince them it was a hardware, not software, issue they gave me a shipping label to send out on April 26, 2024. I received the replacement about 3 weeks later on May 17, 2024.Today on May 18, 2024 I noticed the same unresponsive key issue with the \"2\" key above the \"W\" key. This IS a big deal for gaming since it is used very often.I dont want to go through the RMA process again, and im pretty sure I cant get a refund from amazon after 4 months so this keyboard will likely just be tossed in the garbage where it belongs. A lot of time and money wasted on a sub-par product.Been using Razer keyboards and mice since about 2012 but its probably time to try a different brand to try since their quality seems to have gone down. Shame."
    },
    {
        "review": "Fantastic keyboard as per my choice and also this works well. The package was all good at the time I recieved it. All items were there and the experience is amazing."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had my fair share of gaming keyboards but this one in particular feels great and was way better quality than expected.It is relatively quiet for a gaming keyboard and has excellent tactile feedback.The backlight is clean and vibrant as well.My only complaint would be the macro buttons on the left of the keyboard, but only because I am personally not used to it from previous keyboards."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is the first keyboard I have bought. It is a contemporary style. I am happy with my friend, it does not feel cheap until the very recent USB cord. The lights are very nice."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's super clicky which I hate and it's not swappable which is absurd. The RGB is very inaccurate when setting up but when you do, it looks nice enough. I still prefer my KDA Logitech G Pro keyboard but I got this because it's miyabi <3 the keys are very nice to the touch, although I hate that the macro buttons are on the left, they're messing up with my muscle memory but I can get used to them. The keyboard is metal, cool to the touch, and heavy."
    },
    {
        "review": "The switches are a little noisy but I still really liked the design and quality of the keyboard."
    }
