        "review": "Overall a decent product, especially for the price. Bright display with a decent assortment of faces to choose from, not the hundreds mentioned though. The big problem with the majority of them is there is no battery display to know if it’s getting low. Easy to navigate set up and menu. My biggest complaint is that the app has to be open at all times for the watch to sync to the phone and it seems to be draining quite a bit of energy. Also I’m not sure it’s very accurate on steps, but that could be because I didn’t set my “step length” correctly.  Another thing to know is that it does NOT take readings automatically, you have to tell it to take your blood pressure, pulse, etc. But for a cheap smart watch it’s doing okay."
