[
    {
        "review": "The Miracase Magnetic Case for the iPhone 14 Pro is an excellent combination of protection, convenience, and sleek design. The case fits the 6.1-inch iPhone 14 Pro perfectly, with precise cutouts and easy access to all buttons and ports.The built-in magnetic design works great with MagSafe accessories, making it easy to attach compatible chargers and mounts without constantly removing the case. It also feels sturdy without adding unnecessary bulk, and the grip makes the phone comfortable to hold.Overall, this case offers great protection while keeping the iPhone’s slim profile and MagSafe functionality. For the price, it’s a very solid case and one I’d happily recommend to other iPhone 14 Pro owners."
    },
    {
        "review": "Title: Beautiful case with great protectionI really like this case for my iPhone 17 Pro Max. The pink design is beautiful and stylish without being too bulky. It fits the phone well and gives good protection around the edges and cameras. I also love the built-in stand because it makes watching videos or making video calls much more convenient. It feels sturdy, looks great, and still allows easy access to the buttons. Very happy with this case!"
    },
    {
        "review": "If you are looking for a good case that completely surrounds your device, look no further!I bought this as an Otterbox style (thought not fully waterproof) protective case for my iPhone 14. It’s lasted me quite well, but wasn’t a MagSafe version. (That is literally my only complaint.) It meets my needs and is far more capable than the price would indicate. So much so that I am upgrading to a MagSafe version in a slightly different color without hesitation or regret!The glass screen protector has maintained superb clarity despite’s bumps, drops, spills, and even flinging my phone down a hill (on accident). I think the hilly road surface would have caused more harm, but just 2 1/4” scratches resulted. The clarity and usefulness were not affected, and I have to shine a light across the screen to even spot where the damage happened.Because of the double layered edges, this gives really good shock and impact protection. Drops only concrete, asphalt, and tile have cause zero damage to the case or phone. The thicker edges help my grip and make this easier to hold onto, but I have large hands. Despite that this still fits neatly into a belt holster without issue.The case seals well enough, but at the same time it’s not hard to open to clear a speck of dust or drop of moisture off the screen before resealing it. I have dropped my phone into a running shower for almost zero moisture getting into the case.I highly recommend this case as someone who isn’t gentle and often a klutz while handling my electronics."
    },
    {
        "review": "This phone case fits my phone well and feels sturdy without being too bulky. The buttons are easy to press, and the cutouts line up nicely with the ports and camera. It provides good protection for everyday bumps and drops while still looking sleek. Overall, it’s a solid case for the price and I’m happy with the quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Overall, I am happy with this case.Positives: Plastic is slightly soft to the touch so it’s lightly grippy. It doesn’t show fingerprints. Screen cover does show skin oil, but it polishes off easily with microfiber. It looks very nice and lets the color of the phone show through. Light refracts through the clear plastic giving it a muted crystal appearance. The case is rugged and protects the phone very well. It works perfectly with my Anker magnetic charger or plug in usb-c cord.Negatives: I purchased my iPhone 17 with a screen protector. This case has a built in screen protector. It is part of the design. It can’t be removed. When you install the case, you first install the top piece that encloses the sides of the phone and includes the screen protector. Then the bottom of the case snaps on over the sides of the top. This makes the case very sturdy. But if you already have a screen protector under the case screen protector, it desensitizes the screen. It bothers me most when typing. Missed letters and such. There is an adjustment on the phone to increase screen sensitivity. It helps significantly, but not completely. I’m learning to tap harder.Update - I’ve been using this case for over a month. Two things I mentioned in my earlier review have become daily aggravations and I have decided to go with another case. The main problem is the screen desensitivity because of 2 layers of screen protection. It’s a constant issue. The logical fix would be to remove the $40 screen protector I paid Apple to install. I’m familiar with this product from previous phones. It is excellent. It’s fingerprint resistant. It causes no screen desensitization. It stays perfectly clear. You forget it’s there. That leads to the secondary issue. The phone case’s screen protector shows fingerprints and facial oil. It wipes off easily, but it’s not as clear as it was a month ago. My choice of removing a screen protector is to remove the case’s screen protector and since it is integrated… goodbye case. Having 2 screen protectors is not Miracase’s fault. But having the 2nd best screen protector integrated is the reason I’m reducing my rating from 5 to 4 stars."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ordered this case 5 years ago. Dropped it almost everyday on concrete, wooden floors, in sinks both bathrooms and kitchens. My phone is absolutely perfect. No scratches on the phone, no cracks on the screen, nothing. This is worth the money. I’m about to buy another since this one is coming apart."
