    },
    {
        "review": "Long-time fan of Anker gear, and this only adds to my long-time appreciation of their products. I already own several of their magnetic power banks, but the much slimmer profile and Qi2 charging were huge selling points for me to buy this one.  It's well made and looks super durable. It can easily be charging my phone in my pocket without adding notable bulk compared to other models I own.  My only concern is around the heat - it does get pretty warm, especially when it's charging a phone. It's not enough to burn skin or clothing, but it needs to be mentioned as it may be an issue for some users.I literally own several dozen Anker chargers, battery packs, port replicators, and countless cables. This is easily one of their best products I've ever purchased."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love how slim this is and it has a strong magnet. I can easily use my phone with it attached.  I'm glad I got the orange color so I would remember to take it off!  Also it starts charging right away...no need to press a power button too.It does get pretty warm, not uncomfortably, but cools off quickly once unplugged.For this price I'm not sure it's a great value because there are a few cons.It is somewhat slow to charge my phone so it would be better to not wait for your phone to be low.  One thing I noticed is how much the charger loses it's charge during charging.  It only charges my phone once before it needed to be plugged in.  There is also no display to tell how much charge is left.  There are 4 very tiny lights/indicators on the bottom.  I charged my phone this afternoon when it was at about 50%.  The charger was fully charged (4 lights).  After about 2 hours my phone was at 85% and the charger had only 1 light.  Not awesome if I want to go sightseeing.  Better for errands where you're not taking lots of pics or using GPS.I haven't tested how long it stays charged in standby.  But without a display it's hard to check the rate of loss.This will be great for in a purse in a pinch but I will still bring my bulkier non mag charger if I'm out for a longer trip.  Which is what I was trying to avoid on an upcoming trip."
    },
    {
        "review": "Works with Moto G Stylus 2025 when paired with a case that has MagSafe strips built-in. Sticks to the phone well. Does get hot, and loses some of its charge to the heat. Can be slow to charge, and sometimes only slows the discharge of the phone rather than charging it. Comes with a USB-C to USB-C cable and displays battery life with 4 dots on the bottom, near the charging port. Could be cheaper, too; I understand the anodized aluminum is part of the Apple brand and that's who they're catering to with this release, but maybe they could skip that and make a cheaper, plastic-only version with Android phones in mind. Only giving 3 stars for heat, price, and charging speed; technology shows promise, but needs improvement for it to be considered great."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this for my wife who uses an iPhone 17 Pro and it's been a perfect match. The slim profile is the first thing you notice — this doesn't add the awkward bulk that most power banks do when attached to the back of a phone. It snaps on magnetically, sits nearly flush, and the whole setup still fits comfortably in a pocket or bag.5,000mAh is exactly right for the use case. Not trying to be a heavy-duty road warrior battery — just enough to top up through a day of web browsing, social media, and light use without having to hunt for an outlet. For that purpose it delivers reliably and then some.The color options are where it gets personal — picked one that pairs well with her orange iPhone 17 Pro and the combination looks genuinely intentional rather than mismatched. The kind of accessory that people actually notice and ask about.Qi2 certification means fast wireless charging without the guesswork of older Qi standards, and the magnet alignment is strong and consistent every time. No repositioning, no dropped connections mid-charge.For anyone looking for a slim, stylish MagSafe power bank for everyday use — or as a gift for an iPhone user — this is the one to get."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a decent battery pack. All the reviews about it getting hot and not charging very fast, clearly don’t know how to use the product. You need to use the device when you have a full charge!!!If you’re traveling for the day, you need to make sure that your phone is at 100% when you start your day and the battery pack is at 100% when you start today. Then you put the battery pack on your phone!!As you travel, the battery pack will slowly drain and produce little to no heat at all. By the time the battery pack dies, you should be more than halfway through the day and your phone will still have 100% charge!That’s how you’re supposed to use these charging devices. They are not meant for devices at 0. You’re asking for something that is transferring electricity through induction to do a lot."
    },
    {
        "review": "***Update***Anker contacted and gave good recommendations and expectations for slim high speed battery charging battery pack.This is a good travel in a pinch battery pack to keep level battery when traveling when slim design is a priority.It's a solid slim battery pack for the price.It's a great way to top up my iPhone Air.This charges quickly and I use it wireless if I need a quick top up, and if I need all the juice, I use my short USB-C to USB-C cable.The battery pack does get warm, if not hot when topping up my phone from very low phone battery. I've gotten the message that the phone charging is paused due to heat, but I've gotten this with every wireless battery pack so far except for an Apple battery pack.For the price and size, and with my proper expectations, works great.The magnetic strength is as solid as my Belkin and Baesus battery packs.Works well on my iPhone Air, my spouses 14 Pro, and my 13 mini"
    },
    {
        "review": "excellent"
    },
    {
        "review": "Really disappointed over heats 2 mins after being put on my phone and stops charging"
    },
    {
        "review": "It’s great!"
    }
]

