[
    {
        "review": "I've been very impressed with the Apple MagSafe 25W Wireless Charger. The magnetic connection is strong, making it easy to snap my iPhone into the perfect charging position every time. It charges noticeably faster than my older MagSafe charger, especially when paired with a compatible 30W or higher USB-C power adapter and a supported iPhone.The build quality is exactly what you'd expect from Apple. The braided cable feels much more durable than previous versions, and the charger stays securely attached while I'm using my phone. I also appreciate that it works with my AirPods, making it a versatile charger to keep on my desk or nightstand.While it's a little more expensive than some third-party options, the reliability, strong magnetic alignment, and faster charging make it worth the investment. If you're already in the Apple ecosystem, I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is the first time I've had a phone that used a magnetic charger, boat suffice it to say, I'm very pleased with this one. It sticks on firmly, yet not so firmly that I can't pull it off. Seems to charge pretty fast and I don't have to worry all the time now about my phone running out of battery. Cord is the perfect length for my needs and the charging unit seems very strong and sturdy. I appreciate the simplicity of the unit has it's very easy to use and I can take it with me without thinking about it. I was worried it would get warm, but it doesn't seem to do that. Would definitely buy this again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really impressed with this 25W MagSafe charger. The magnetic snap is strong and aligns perfectly every time, and it charges my iPhone noticeably faster than standard wireless pads. It stays cool during use, feels durable, and is lightweight enough to take anywhere. Excellent quality for the price. Definitely recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice item. Is as described. Easy to use. Plug and go. Very sleek flat low profile charger. Charges iPhone perfectly even with case on. Is fairly quick and very low heat. I’ve had other models I’ve returned because they were so slow and phone got very hot. Keeping this one. A good investment and a good price."
    },
    {
        "review": "First, this charger is fantastic at charging fast. I have had no problems with charging any phone fully in half the time my old wireless charger took.The caveats: The charger has two states. It is either fast charging, or it is off. It will not work at all in a car because it doesn't supply enough amps. It won't work with wall plugs under 25 watts (5v, 5A). It doesn't just refuse to fast charge, it won't even power up. So this only works if you have a high-amperage adapter, or a high power computer port.The other issue is weight. The device is small and surprisingly light, but that means if you pick up your charging phone, the charger comes with it. Great in a car, but it won't work there. Terrible on a nightstand or desk. I'm constantly prying off the charger just so I can use the phone.So great in any situation where the above two issues don't matter."
    },
    {
        "review": "These work as intended! Good speed and great magnetic pull. Nice to have by the bed so you don't have to stress about the charger falling out or being half plugged in. We use it for both an iPhone and a Samsung 23 and both work well and have no issues fast charging. Great price as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this charger for a bit more than two weeks, and it’s been great. The strong magnet grabs the phone and holds it well. I’ve accidentally knocked the charger and phone off a table, and it has held on tightly. I bought it in a color (lavender) so it’s easier to find if it gets tangled up in bedclothes. It was compatible not only with our iPhone 17s, but our iPhone 11 and 13 while we were moving files. It can get hot depending on what files you have open, so I close everything out at night and charge it while I sleep. If I need it during the day, it’s fast at recharging, so the heat doesn’t bother me, I just set it aside. They have worked really well for us."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought the white 2-pack for an iPhone 16 Pro and AirPods Pro. One lives on the nightstand, the other sits on the desk. Magnets snap on cleanly and hold well even if you bump the table. Alignment is consistent; you don’t have to fuss with centering like a cheap Qi pad.Charging speed is what you’d expect for this class of product. On a newer iPhone it feels meaningfully faster than old 7.5W/15W pads. Older 12–15 series phones still charge fine, just not at the full 25W the listing advertises. AirPods with a wireless case charge without drama. Pads stay reasonably cool if you use a 30W (or higher) USB-C brick — don’t cheap out on a weak adapter if you want the advertised speed.They’re slim and light, so they travel well. White looks clean on a nightstand. Cables are long enough for a bedside setup. Two pads for the price is the real win: one for home, one for the office or a bag.Caveats: Thick cases can weaken the magnet or slow charging — slim MagSafe-friendly cases work best. These are pads, not stands, so the phone lies flat. Not Apple official, so don’t expect identical behavior to a first-party puck in every edge case.For the money, this 2-pack is an easy buy if you want simple magnetic charging in two spots without paying Apple prices twice."
    },
    {
        "review": "I use this with my iPhone 8 because sometimes the charge port is finicky so I have to use wireless charging, and I gave the second one in the 2 pack to my cousin who has an iPhone 14 Pro Max. The magnet connection is strong, it snaps on tight and doesn't shift. The slim design is great for when it's stuck to the back of your phone and you're using it so it's not bulky in your hand. For my iPhone 8, there's no magnets in the phone, so it doesn't attach, but it works fine as a normal Qi pad if I centre it and it doesn't make my phone hot.It charges my phone at 7.5W. That's an iPhone 8 limit, not the charger's fault. My cousin's 14 Pro Max gets 15W, since 25W Qi2.2 only works on iPhone 15 and newer. No wall adapters are included so you need a 25W+ USB-C PD brick to get fast charging on phones that support it. With my iPhone 8, a basic 10W brick is enough. If you use a weak adapter with a newer phone, charging will be slow.For the price of a 2 pack, it's good if you need a backup for port issues or want Qi2.2 speeds on a newer phone. The strong magnet is great for MagSafe phones, and it still functions as a standard wireless charger for older models."
    },
    {
        "review": "Set of two magnetic chargers in lemon yellow color. At home, we all have iPhones: 12, 14, 17, and these cats are perfect for all our phones. They replace the old basic chargers with less efficient cables and prematurely wear out the phone's charging socket. This helps extend the life of our old iPhones which are no longer able to charge with the cable. Charging is fast and efficient. The magnet is super effective. And the charger remains discreet, plus I love the color!!!!I recommend ++++"
    },
    {
        "review": "This 2-pack Qi2.2 wireless charger is technically well designed and particularly useful if you have multiple compatible devices or want one charger at home and another for travel. The main advantage is support for up to 25W Qi2 charging, which offers a significant step up from basic low-wattage wireless pads when paired with a device that supports the higher charging profile. Magnetic alignment keeps the charging coils correctly positioned, helping maintain a more reliable connection and reducing the efficiency loss that can occur when a phone is slightly misaligned on a conventional Qi pad. The slim puck-style construction takes up very little desk or bedside space, and compatibility across supported iPhones, newer Samsung Galaxy and Google Pixel models, plus accessories such as AirPods, makes the set quite versatile. As with any wireless charger, actual wattage depends on the phone, battery level, temperature, case, and the power adapter supplying the charger, so 25W shouldn’t be expected continuously throughout an entire charging cycle. Wireless charging can also generate more heat and has greater conversion losses than a direct USB-C connection. Those are normal technical limitations rather than major faults, though. The strong magnetic positioning, modern Qi2.2 standard, compact construction, broad compatibility, and convenience of getting two chargers make this an excellent setup for everyday cable-free charging."
    }
]

