[
    {
        "review": "I've only had it for a day, but based on some testing it seems really great.For me this is an upgrade from an older Logitech 920 - and this new EMEET beats it hands down. The sharpness of the image and the colors are really awesome. The lens angle is about the same, it's perfect for work meetings.I really appreciate the mechanical shutter and the little light that comes on when there is video capture.It's really adjustable - once you have the base fixed on your monitor, you can further adjust the camera itself to look a little down, helps if you use large monitors (mine are 27\").It's easy to use as no drivers were needed - and I checked Windows 11, Debian 13 and Ubuntu 24.04 (work computer), web browser based capture as well as the Linux Zoom app.It's connected through a USB switcher I'm using with all my peripherals, and I am not seeing any connection flakiness.The webcam has a feeling of quality, it's well made and quite heavy to be honest. I think the design is attractive."
