        "review": "Excellent camera! Cool way to dial the lens closed for privacy and you can swivel it on the mount. Microphone works very well."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm in the process of interviewing for a new job and want that first impression to make an impact.  I remember when I interviewed for my current job years ago they later commented on how good my streaming quality was.  I used my school's AV room which had excellent webcams, mics, and a studio booth.  I'm on the job market again and need an AV setup that won't break the bank.  This camera fits the bill perfectly because it's cheap enough for just a few uses but still delivers an excellent picture.As with any camera, always learn how to connect and adjust software settings before going live; that aside, I didn't have any issues connecting and making adjustments (mirror, brightness).  You'll need to download their app to make adjustments.  Very intuitive from there.Seems to be forgiving of lighting technique so long as you simply have adequate lighting.  White balance is dead on (5000k Walmart light bulbs), just be ready to adjust light source angles and brightness settings.Microphone works, but any monitor-mounted camera mic won't be great.  I bought a $30 lavalier mic and it made a huge difference.  You can have excellent video quality, but if the audio sucks it's all for nothing.If I could nitpick I wish it shot in 24 FPS.  60 is nauseating, and luckily most streaming services will knock it down to 30 anyway.  More fps is not better.  It just looks unnatural and consumes more resources in doing so in the process."
    },
    {
        "review": "The webcam is great for the price! It seems to be far better than my Logitech and I mainly bought it since I does 4K, my old Logitech was a 1080p camera and while decent, I felt this was a better upgrade. Quality seems nice, the camera is very flexible depending on your lighting conditions. I recommend OBS over the EMEET software which I know people will likely use OBS anyway for streaming/recording. The camera can easily be adjusted in OBS and tweaked to your liking."
    },
    {
        "review": "Camera quality is good, microphone quality is not great so I would recommend using a separate microphone. It connected immediately out of the box, colors were good to my eyes and focus works great too.  The only issue I have is with how large it is.  It's a 2in wide by 4 in long tube, the size makes it so I can't easily place it on my monitor shelf without blocking part of the screen and on top of the screen it looks a bit ridiculous.  I will try a mounting solution instead or go with something else like the obsbot instead due to the smaller form factor."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is an excellent camera for its intended purpose- web conferencing in much better resolution than most built in laptop cameras or conferencing monitors. It's not really meant for streaming (you'll want a DSLR setup for that). It suits its purpose very well!The biggest plus is that it can do 1080p FHD in 60 fps. There are cameras 2x-3x the price that still only shoot 1080p in 30 fps.The camera is very solidly built, and the twist-to-open privacy shutter isn't flimsy like many are. The camera also has 45° of swivel on its mount, very handy for compensating for angled dual monitors, or for keeping unwanted objects out of the background. The retro tubular \"This is a camera\" shape also looks cool!There are 2 inbuilt microphones, which would be useful if you're using a desktop that lacks an inbuilt speakerphone or a monitor that has one. I have an external microphone so I only used the feature to test it. It's better than most conference monitor mics, but not an external dynamic or condenser microphone.The Emeet Link software is very basic, and resolution is altered in your camera settings instead of the app. The only complaint I have is the lack of a manual focus option, but considering the features for the price,  and  the use case, it is forgivable.Overall, it does everything I want it to, the price was right, and it works. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I loved the image quality, good value for money option"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this webcam for almost 12 months now and I honestly can’t fault it. It’s well designed, reliable and performs exactly as expected for video calls and streaming.The camera mounts securely on top of my monitor, with a clever design that allows it to sit flush and hug the screen without slipping or wobbling. It feels stable and unobtrusive, which is ideal for day-to-day use.A standout feature is the built-in privacy cover—a physical lens flap you can close when not in use. This is a must-have in today’s digital environment and offers peace of mind in the unlikely event your system is ever compromised. When closed, you’re completely protected from any unauthorised access to your webcam feed.It connects via USB-A to USB-C, while it does come with a cable (I believe around 1m long), I opted to purchase a 2m extension with a right-angle USB-C plug. The angled plug was important to me, as it allows the cable to sit neatly without jutting out from the back of the camera—especially helpful for keeping things tidy and adjusting placement when your PC isn’t close to your monitor.As for performance, the image quality is excellent for a webcam, especially considering the price. It delivers a sharp, vibrant picture with fast autofocus and smooth frame rates, particularly noticeable at 1080p @ 60fps. It’s absolutely up to the task for Zoom meetings, live streaming, or content creation.The built-in microphones were a pleasant surprise too. I had a separate desk mic on standby assuming the webcam mic would be subpar, but so far I haven’t needed it—the onboard mic does a great job and captures audio clearly with minimal background noise.All in all, I highly recommend this camera. Between the thoughtful design, impressive performance, and practical privacy features, it’s a well-rounded piece of kit that’s been a great addition to my setup. 5 stars without hesitation."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good camera!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great, worth it"
