[
    {
        "review": "I have purchased 3 of these total and they are excellent lights for what I use them for. I have them mounted on the back side of my work benches. I have a Guitar workshop and these lights provide excellent lighting. They were easy to install/setup and perfect size. They are light weight and maneuverable and easily light up my entire work area.  I have had no problems with these lights at all and have had one of them for over a year already. I was an easy decision to add 2 more when I added more workbenches in my shop. Great product!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is hands-down the best lamp I’ve ever owned. The Micomlan LED Desk Lamp with Clamp is incredibly bright, versatile, and perfect for any workspace. The adjustable arm and multiple lighting modes make it easy to dial in the exact lighting you need—whether it’s for studying, working, or detailed tasks.The clamp is strong and secure, and the lamp feels solid and well-built without being bulky. I love how wide the lighting coverage is; it easily lights up my entire desk without glare or shadows. The settings for brightness and color temperature are a huge bonus and make it super customizable.Setup took just a minute, and once it’s in place, it stays exactly where you put it. For the price, the quality is unmatched. This lamp instantly upgraded my desk setup, and I honestly wish I had bought it sooner.Highly recommend—best lamp I’ve had!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I'll be honest. I was looking for something in my local brick and mortar stores. Target, Walmart, Home Depot, Lowes... every place let me down because they all had the same unimaginative junk. And certainly not in store so I can just go get it. I have a pretty deep computer desk with dual 27\" monitors on moving arms. I also have a separate soldering table. I wanted good, shadow free illumination on both and nobody had anything that would work. Lo and behold, I stumble across this on Amazon. I love when someone has a good idea and turns it into a great product.Unboxing is just ridiculously easy. There is no building. All you have to do is screw clamp it to your surface and plug it in. It seems it'll fit a pretty thick surface too. 1 1/8\" (almost 3cm) thick shelf stock for a desk and it has enough space for another inch or so. No flickering that I can see. It's clean smooth light. The color temperature options are plentiful and you can cycle through presets of both temp and brightness or do a smooth transition to what you want. The side panels are separately turned on and off (together) and can fold down 90° (if you really wanted to) or all the way up to upside down on top of the main lamp. It's all folded together in the box, so just unfold and use.Only real issue is there's no telescoping function. So if you have a small desk and want it mounted at the back AND close to your surface, you might have to get creative.The auto brightness is interesting... it gets brighter when the ambient light goes down. I expected the opposite. But maybe this makes sense. I prefer manual control anyway.Overall, very great product for anyone working at a desk, writing, making, what have you. I love this thing already. There's a really good video review that will show you all you need to know. I bought two right then and there (for both tables) and I do not regret my decision at all."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased one of these in April 2025 and was very happy with its versatility and performance. But it wasn't until I purchased another one for my wife 8 months later — which should tell you right away how great I still feel about the lamp — that I felt I had to write a review.The lamp is perfect: it can be mounted on any portion of a desk and be super-usable thanks to its many adjustable 'elbows' and pivots; the light range (color temperature,  brightness and stepless dimming) is very convenient...and all of it can be easily controlled by the remote. But I have to say, the prime motivator for my writing this review has been the vendor support. Here's why (and IF YOU EVER BUY TWO OR MORE OF THESE you should take note):Our two lamps are one wall away from each other. When I set up the new lamp for my wife, I noticed MY lamp was turning on/off and changing brightness when I used her remote. I tried putting duct tape and aluminum foil at the tip of the remotes to lessen their power/effect on controlling the other lamp. No luck. So I wrote to the vendor (Micomlan). Within a day they got back and solved it for me. The default setting of the remotes out of the box is 'unpaired', so that one remote can control any number of these lamps. Which is what happened to me...and not what I desired. Micomlan told me you can pair one remote to one lamp and to follow the instructions in manual that comes in the box for how to do that.Excellent product, excellent service, customer for life. THAT'S how capitalism should work. 😊Needless to say...BUY THIS LAMP!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very versatile and well made piece of equipment.  I needed to replace a standing lamp that just doesn't work for me anymore for desk lighting.  Don't have the space I once did.  So I got something that could attach to my desk.  and move around as needed.  This did not disappoint.  As someone else noted it can get too hot if you turn it to the highest brightness setting.  I like more natural light (not blue or yellow) and so this works great.  The extreme maneuverability is one of its best features.  And it doesn't take up much space do it's design.  I have it attached to my glass desk and I have a desk riser that sits on top of it and it works with the riser up or down.  The arms also make it really good as you can put them up so the light goes to the ceiling or down on what you are doing.  I only give it one less star than five for overheating at the highest setting.  I won't be using the highest setting but briefly sometimes but they need to work on that.  I bought the soft white and I like how the color works with my walls and my desk. Great buy."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a fun-to-use desk lamp with a clamp.  It doesn't have the stability of a lamp with two side-by-side arms, however, when I type, it only wobbles a little.  I've gotten used to it, so it isn't really a distraction.My favorite part of the lamp is the side arms that swing up or down, depending on where you want to put the light.  For more focus on your desk; swing down.  To illuminate the ceiling, or the entire room, swing up.  You can control the brightness or illumination of each type of element, so that the arms that are pointed up can have light, while the ones pointed down can be dimmed or turned off altogether to prevent glare.  The brightness starts as very dim and goes all of the way up to very bright (with some glare), and many steps in between.  Nice!All in all, I've had this lamp for over a month now, and haven't noticed any defects or bad design, except for the slight wobble.  It's great if you like to have a room for computer use while having the ability to light the whole room without glare.  That's why I give it a '5'."
    },
    {
        "review": "Hello:I received my Micomlan Led Desk Lamp today and I LOVE it.  I was about to purchase another desk lamp, when this one came into view and I and I am VERY happy  I waited.  It fits PERFECTLY on my desk and set up.  It was easy to clamp on my desk and it has lit up my desk perfectly.  It is flexible, it highlights my entire desk, and both of my monitors.  Added to that it was a great price (it had just been discounted).  The size was perfect for my desk and the color was just right.  The controls are easy to use.  It has three lights and can be VERY bright or soft if you want it to be.  I'm HIGHLY recommending this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking for a light to use with a computer setup in another room. I use a BenQ screen bar with one setup, but they are pricey. I decided to give the Micomlan Led Desk Lamp a try and I was glad that I did. Lots of features and a variety of settings at a really good price. One of my favorite features is that you can turn the ends up to bounce the light off of the ceiling (especially nice with drop down ceilings) and expand the lighting coverage to illuminate the entire desk. And if you don't need any task lighting you can turn the main light off. It was easy to set up, quite sturdy and stable. It also fit nicely with the multiple monitor setup. Would definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "This LED desk lamp is one of the best purchases I’ve made for my home office. What sets it apart is the innovative design that allows light to be directed toward the ceiling, creating a soft ambient glow that significantly reduces eye strain—especially helpful during long hours of computer work.The lamp offers multiple lighting modes and brightness levels, which is perfect for adjusting the atmosphere depending on the task or time of day. Whether I’m working, reading, or just relaxing, I can easily switch between warm and cool tones to suit my needs.Its sleek and understated design blends seamlessly into any workspace, and the adjustable arm provides excellent mobility. I can position it exactly where I want, and the sturdy clamp ensures it stays securely in place without damaging my desk.Overall, this lamp combines style, functionality, and comfort in a way that’s ideal for modern work-from-home setups. Highly recommended for anyone looking to upgrade their lighting and reduce eye fatigue."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this desk lamp for a month now, and I absolutely love it! I had been searching for a functional, lightweight lamp with multiple settings, and this one checks all the boxes. The light options are versatile and the LED is very bright, the quality overall feels excellent. I even use it for time-lapse recordings by placing my phone on it. truly multifunctional. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Versatile and nice finish with modes and sectional control"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Desk lamp arrived on time and well packaged.  Easy to assemble and no parts missing. Very sturdy, the light is soft an an bright at the same time.  The light spreads well over the screen and not overbearing.  It has adjustable lighting and evening light, very convenient when tired.  I would highly recommend if you ae in front of a screen for many hours,"
    }
