[
    {
        "review": "I use this monitor light all the time, whether it's daytime or late at night. I simply enjoy having it on. It helps me see my keyboard better, and it also provides a nice amount of light for the plants I keep on my desk.The light has several brightness levels and color temperatures, which makes it easy to customize depending on what I'm doing. The quality is excellent, it's very attractive, and installation was incredibly simple.The only thing I would change is the remote control. The power button on the controller stays illuminated all the time, even when the light is off. I prefer sleeping in complete darkness and don't like seeing any small lights on in the room.Even with that minor detail, I still give this product 5 out of 5 stars. It's a fantastic monitor light and I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m not even being dramatic when I say this was the best upgrade for my desk EVER.It is such a reasonable price for how much of a difference it made.Installation was so easy it took maybe 30 seconds to clip it to the stand, set it on the monitor, and plug it in. The stand is flexible but strong enough to hold onto the monitor without falling. It is also super lightweight and doesn't push my monitor down.The lighting is SO good. It’s bright but not harsh, and it doesn’t reflect on the screen at all. I didn’t realize how much eye strain I was dealing with until I started using this. And I love that I can switch between warm and cool lighting depending on the time of day.The remote is also a nice touch. I like that it uses batteries so I don't have to worry about charging it.It honestly just makes my whole setup look cleaner and has made gaming and working much more enjoyable. If you spend a lot of time at your desk, this light bar is definitely worth it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'd been considering a monitor desk light for some time now, but I could not justify the price tag giong as high as $200 on the BenQ \"original\" that sorta started it off with these types of lights. This was a couple years ago now and clearly today there are many different versions of similar monitor lights on the market, the Quntis being among them, and which appears to be a fairly close copy of the BenQ light.I found this one on Amazon, priced around $40 for the non-remote (remote being rather superfluous in my opinion) version and did a little comparison research to see if this might be a good fit. There are many similar monitor lights out there, some cheaper and going as low as ~$25 and some obviously more expensive. I figured the Quntis was a good middle ground price-wise and took a shot to see if this would fit the bill. Indeed it does!Whether or not, or how close a copy to the BenQ the Quntis is I don't know for sure, as I've never seen the alternatives, but I can say this one is very well designed and well constructed, some plastic and also some metal in the construction and on close inspection the quality is definitely there. The mounting system is simple and functional and adapted perfectly to my HP Omen gaming monitor, which I would say has a somewhat non-standard profile shape and thickness, at least at the top where the light mounts. No problem, the mount is easily adjustable and rests perfectly and securely on my top monitor edge with full confidence that it's not going anywhere, or is any way unstable or wonky.The light controls on top of the light are easily accessible, operated by touch and the tactile \"buttons\" are shaped so they can be easily felt when operating the light. There are stepless controls for brightness and color temperature, as well as a sort of \"auto\" button that adjusts the brightness based on the ambient light in the room, which is nice. The lightbar throws a very nice pool of light on your keyboard and desk space in front of, and not directly ON, your monitor  - right where you need it - without any glare, or being too harsh. Again, the quality, brightness and temperature of the light is easily adjustable to your liking.The monitor mounting system is sensible, simple, highly adjustable and highly functional. Lamp is powered by USB and in my case plugs right into a USB port on my monitor and totally invisible, hidden behind. Anyway, I guess I might have got a little carried away with this review, but tldr; the Quntis is an excellent monitor light and if this is something you've been looking at, I don't think you can go wrong with this one."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this monitor light, for several weeks, on an Acer display for daily work, and overall it’s been a really solid addition to my desk setup. Installation was straightforward — it mounted easily and felt secure once positioned. No complicated setup or tools required, which I always appreciate.The lighting itself is where this really shines (no pun intended). The adjustable color temperature range from warm to cool is useful depending on what you’re doing. It can give you more of a relaxed desk lamp vibe in warmer tones or a bright, focused work light when you need better visibility for detailed tasks. There’s also an auto-dimming feature, but I personally prefer setting a static brightness level once and leaving it there. The included remote control is a nice touch and honestly makes the product feel more premium than the price point would suggest.Build quality feels better than expected — not cheap or flimsy. I use this every day for work, and it’s especially helpful during gloomy weather or late afternoons when natural light drops off. It reduces the need for overhead lighting and keeps the workspace evenly illuminated without glare on the screen.My only real complaint is the articulation adjustment. The mounting design doesn’t provide quite enough tension, so adjusting the angle sometimes requires two hands to keep everything aligned. It’s not a dealbreaker, but it’s an area that could be improved in a future version.Overall, this has been a great upgrade for my workspace and something I didn’t realize I needed until I started using it consistently."
    },
    {
