    {
        "review": "Very nice.Using it on LG Ultrafine 4K.Looks sleek.Happy with the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I don't usually write reviews, but this product is so useful that I felt compelled to do so. Using the Quntis Screen linear Pro for a day, and could not be happier. Setup is simple enough, though may be better to refer to a YouTube video rather than the documentation which is confusing. The build quality is outstanding, clean rounded curves, smooth metal, matte finish (I got the black). The touch sensors work like a charm.Most important for me is that it bathes the workspace in front of my monitor with ample even down light, and without reflective glare on the screen or in my eye. My previous desk lamp reflected off the screen irritatingly, and had uneven light over the keyboard. I had always wanted a clutter free solution and tried LED strips (USB-A driven) stuck to the bottom of my monitor which did not work well. The Quntis is the answer to what I was looking for.The touch sensors give you instant on/off, colors (warm, white) and brightness controls. There is also an auto brightness sensor which apparently adjusts based on ambient light, but I have not used that yet.This is well worth the 39.99, and way cheaper than the more expensive BenQ that I also researched before buying this. Does the job for me."
