        "review": "I wanted a good light source for my desk, with large-area illumination and good optics. During the presentation, the photo that caught my eye was that this lamp has several light fields and can cover several monitors. At a price of 40 euros, that was enough reason to buy it. The lamp can be easily attached to a desk with a clamp and is stable here. The alignment of the arms works via four joints, the lighting elements can be rotated so that a somewhat individual positioning is possible, including the option of choosing direct or indirect lighting for each lighting element. I had to make compromises because the lowest element (no light field, but the control buttons) cannot be rotated. Another disadvantage: the keys are mounted almost flat on this lowest element. It's not easy to feel them. If there is no other light in the room, you can't see them and you can hardly feel them. That's unfortunate. Otherwise the lamp does what it's supposed to: bright. The light can be dimmed slightly and the color heat can be regulated. I'm happy with the purchase."
