    {
        "review": "I recently purchased this table desk lamp to use where my 3d printers are located, and I couldn’t be happier with it. The 40-inch height is ideal—it lights up my entire workspace without any glare or harshness. It is tall enough to extend above my P2S printer. The edge-lit design is stylish and modern.The build quality feels sturdy and well-designed, making the lamp is easy to adjust to the desired height and just the right angle. It’s a great investment if you spend a lot of time at your desk or work area and want both style and the functionality provided by the taller height.I highly recommend this lamp for anyone looking to upgrade their workspace lighting!"
    },
    {
        "review": "1. The controls are at the base of the vertical riser. They do not get obstructed by other items on the desk. Controls are very intuitive except for the 45-minute shut-off timer. No silly remote control to lose.2. The base is about 6\" by 6\" and is made out of steel plate. It is large enough and heavy enough that the lamp is very stable. There is a soft, non-skid pad on the bottom that protects the table surface while keeping the lamp from being inadvertantly pushed around. I specifically wanted a lamp with a base such as this rather than a clamp-on type.3. There is enough vertical adjustment to clear the top of large monitors.4. The arms and lamp came pre-assembled.  The only assembly requirment is to slip the upright post onto the base and plug in the power supply.5. The power supply transformer plugs into a standard 120 VAC outlet. The cord is over 6 feet long so placement is not an issue.6. Color temperature and brightness adjustments are easy. The lamp is sufficiently bright for reading printed material.7. The light diffusion is quite uniform and has a wide dispersion angle.  I originally was looking for a unit with a light bar (\"wings\") but this has proven completely adequate.I hope that it lasts for quite a while. The manufacturer states that there is an 18-month waranty but that is hard to count on with Chinese manufacturers.  Really happy with this lamp, especially for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "After purchasing an Omorepa lamp to place behind my Dell UltraSharp U5226KW monitor, I discovered it was not quite tall enough to position properly without shining directly into my eyes. I ended up returning it and trying the LitONES desk lamp instead because it was slightly taller and, importantly, allowed the lamp head to rotate independently.That flexibility turned out to be exactly what I needed. I initially bought one lamp just to test the setup and quickly realized I had finally found the right solution. The lamp is tall enough to work well behind the 26.5-inch-tall Dell monitor, and the adjustable head makes it easy to angle the light over the monitor and down onto the keyboard and work area without glare. The light itself provides a soft white glow and the brightness can be adjusted easily.Because the monitor is extremely wide, I eventually purchased a second lamp and positioned one on each side behind the display. The only minor inconvenience is that each lamp must be turned on separately since there is no remote control. But honestly, that is a very small complaint — I can lean over and switch them both on in about five seconds. A pretty good sign that I may be a little spoiled at this point.If you have a tall monitor and prefer placing lights behind it so the illumination projects over the display onto your workspace, these lights are definitely worth considering."
    },
    {
        "review": "I tried several other lamps before getting this one, and they all had one problem or another--not bright enough, not high enough to put the light up over my monitor, too large a base that took up too much desk space, etc. This one is just about perfect. It has a small flat base that other things can sit on, but is still heavy enough to balance the lamp at the top. The brightness is adjustable, it's tall enough that the light is over my head instead of right in my eyes, and it even has a timer to turn off automatically if you forget. Excellent design and execution."
