[
    {
        "review": "I've been using this SKYLEO LED Desk Lamp for my home office, and it has exceeded my expectations. The light is bright, even, and very comfortable on the eyes, even after working for several hours.I really like the adjustable arm because it's easy to position the light exactly where I need it. The different brightness levels and color temperature settings make it perfect for both daytime work and evening reading.The lamp feels sturdy, doesn't take up much desk space, and the modern design looks great on my desk.Overall, this is a high-quality desk lamp that offers excellent value for the price. I would definitely recommend it to anyone who works from home, studies, or spends long hours at a desk."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've struggled with different desk lights over the years, they were either not bright enough, or wouldn't stayed fixed to certain positions, but this desk light is far superior to those. It stays in the fixed position, it's the right size for my work area, made of good material, and easy to assemble on my desktop. It doesn't shake or bobble around. It's just a solid all around light for my use. Yes, I would recommend it for desktops, mechanic bench tops, and hobby desks. The brightness and cool to warm effects are great."
    },
    {
        "review": "Unfortunately this light is not quite as bright as I was expecting, but that's no fault of the light and more so on me for not reading the description more carefully. The light itself has lots of settings for both white and soft light. The arm is very adjustable and easy to use. Even when the kmob is tightened on the mount, you can still adjust it slightly side to side. The light is also very adjustable for position with not only up and down movement, but rotational movement.All in all, this would be a great light to light up a small work space such as a computer desk or writing table. Basically a work space where you need more light, but not necessarily super bright light. It would also make for a great reading light if you have an end table or somewhere to clamp it nearby."
    },
    {
        "review": "TLDR: Solid build, good light quality, useful brightness and color controls, and a swing arm that does most of what you want. The big catch is that it does not behave the way modern smart home users will expect, and the mounting geometry has some real-world limits the listing photos do not show. Four stars, with caveats worth knowing before you click buy.Let me lead with the good, because there is plenty of it.The light itself is genuinely nice. Plenty of brightness for working, reading, or close-up tasks, and the color temperature options give you warm yellow, neutral white, and a cooler white-blue depending on what you are doing. Eleven brightness levels is more granularity than I expected. The arm extends and folds well, and the head pivots to put light right where you want it. It runs on USB, the wall adapter is included, and the wattage is low enough that you can power it from a laptop port if that is convenient. The clamp mount is solid and holds tight once you have it in place.A note on installation. The clamp wants a specific amount of mounting surface, and my location had less than the lamp wanted in one direction. I pulled out a Dremel and shaved a small relief into the underside so the clamp could sit properly. Not a complaint, just a heads up if your desk has a thick lip, a beveled edge, or a rounded corner where you want this to live.Now, the big thing.This lamp does not default to on when power is restored. If you turn it off and walk away, fine. If your power blips, or if you have it on a smart switch that cuts power, the lamp comes back off. To turn it back on you have to walk over to the lamp and press the little button on the inline cord controller, which sits close to the base of the arm and is not always easy to reach.This matters because the listing advertises a memory function, and modern buyers, especially anyone with a smart home setup, are going to read that and assume something it does not actually mean. Here is what is happening. The memory function does work, in a narrow sense. When you press the on button, the lamp comes back at whatever brightness and color mode you used last. It does not have to be reset every time. That is real and it is useful.What the memory function does not do is preserve the on/off state across a power cut. The reason is that this is a soft-touch push button rather than a mechanical switch. The lamp's electronics have to be powered to know they are on, and when power is removed and restored the default state is off. A traditional mechanical switch physically holds the circuit closed and is why your bedroom lamp comes back on when the power flickers. This one does not, by design.If you live in a fully manual lighting world, this is a non-issue. You will press the button and life goes on. If you have your office lights on a smart switch, or you have ever said the words \"Google (or Alexa), turn on the lights,\" this is going to be an ongoing minor annoyance. I had assumed, like most lights, that I could plug this into the same smart switch as the rest of the room and have it come on with everything else. Instead it sits there dark while everything else lights up, waiting for me to walk over and poke it.The other thing worth flagging is the arm geometry. The first segment, the one closest to the clamp, is not designed to swing forward. It folds up and back, which is fine on an open desk where you have empty wall behind you. If you are mounting this on the back edge of a desk that sits against a wall, on the lip of a hutch, on top of a shelving unit, or inside a cubicle, you are going to discover that the elbow needs room to bow outward behind the lamp. The listing photos all show the lamp on an open desk with nothing behind it, so this is not obvious until you have it in hand. Plan your mounting location with that in mind.There is also a 45 minute auto-off timer button on the controller. Apparently aimed at bedtime reading. I have not used it but it is there if you want it.Four stars. The light is good and the build is good. The memory function exists but means something different than a smart home buyer will assume, and the mounting flexibility has limits that the listing does not show. If you can live with those, this is a nice lamp at a fair price. If you were hoping to drop it into an automated lighting routine, you are going to want to know about the default-off behavior before you order."
    },
    {
        "review": "This headlight was a great light is very adjustable. It bends down the size. Great. It has lighting options. It was very reliable for me. I love the flexibility of the light. It was a great price. Well, I purchase again if need be yes"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a review for the immediate, not long term. I just received my order in about 12 hours. I set this up in less than 5 minutes and it's great. I bought this for my kids room and his art table. I wanted something bright and completely out of the way and this lamp is perfect for that. It's very flexible and lightweight and very easy to install. I believe there are about 4 or 5 different lighting options, a timer and a dimmer or brighten option. The added bonus is they add a wall port so you can use it immediately instead of trying to find an old one you have laying around. I feel like it's pretty good quality as long as your kid is old enough not to mess with it and it's very stable since you install it yourself to the desired tightening. I have zero complaints and would order more for other desks."
