        "review": "I use a 6ft by 3ft dining table as a desk because I need to be able to have textbooks and notebooks open while I also use the computer and take notes, and I was having trouble seeing print well without shuffling everything around as I went along with just the regular desk lamp.  This lamp is clamped to a long side, and it doesn't take away from the valuable work space.  It illuminates the entire tabletop nicely, and at full brightness, I can read everything around me easily.  I keep it at about half brightness for a comfortable illumination when I'm not reading/writing, and that is slightly brighter than my other lamp was.  The arms adjust easily, and allow for more light in specific areas if needed. The included remote control is very handy, and has several preset brightness/color settings, but also easily adjusts each manually, and includes a timer feature.  Batteries are not included, though; it takes 2 AAA.My only reason for taking off one star is because the assembly, while it was essentially simple, was slightly harder because the connector at the top of the flexible arm was on the wrong side of the arm to easily connect to the light bar, and I had to finagle it a while to get it to be able to connect.Overall, I am very pleased with it and would buy again."
