[
    {
        "review": "Nice, lightweight lamp. Versatile in lighting options as well as dimmable."
    },
    {
        "review": "This desk lamp certainly isn’t your typical desk lamp.  The first thing I thought is that it looks like something straight from a science fiction movie.  It’s not the prettiest lamp, but it has more of a clean, modern design with a black matte finish and slender profile.  In my opinion, it’s just a more modern version of the swing lamp from back in my day.  It obviously has more functionality when it comes to temperature and brightness levels, but to be honest, I find the height and angle adjustments to be a bit clunky.  I suppose it’s because the arms are so long, not that they’re hard to turn.  I like the slender profile of the lamp, though, because I can place the long, top light over my work space, and it brightens the area without getting in the way.  I would say that the LED lighting is on par with most lamps of this type.  I can adjust the brightness and temperature that’s suitable for my tasks:  warm light for computer work, natural for crafting or writing.  As you can see in the video when I turn off the lights, it casts a nice bright light over the desk area, but the rest of the room is fairly dark.  Of course, you can adjust the angle of the light if needed, but it’s not going to brighten the entire room like a regular lamp could.  But I suppose that’s why it’s called a DESK LAMP, not a table lamp.Concerning the build, unlike a regular lamp (and the old-timey swing lamp), the base is nice and flat, which means it doesn’t take up space. It can be used to hold a cup of coffee, your phone, or whatever else can fit on there.  The base is not heavy, either, but it works well to counterbalance the lamp arms.  The bottom post that’s connected to it is a little wobbly, though.  Even so, it doesn’t seem to affect the stability.  This lamp looks like it would be very tippy, but it’s surprisingly stable, even at the craziest angles.  The design was obviously planned out well.  Other than the post being a bit wobbly, the craftsmanship is good, too.So far, I’ve used this lamp almost every day since I received it.  I might actually personalize it a little by putting a small plant on the base or put some pretty stickers on it.  For now, it’s doing what I need it to do, and it doesn’t tip over easily, so I’m happy with it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this lamp! I changed the desk in my home office, so I can no longer use lamps that clamp to the desk. I’ve tried other lamps, but they are not tall enough. This lamp is so adjustable. You can twist the three different sections individually. It has multiple light brightness and a timer."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love It  Many Choice settings"
    },
    {
        "review": "The light itself does a good job and has a lot going for it, but the overall build quality left me wanting more, especially considering the price. It is made of metal, but it uses a very thin gauge that feels hollow and doesn’t give the impression of a premium desk lamp.The biggest drawback is the articulating arm. The pivot and rotating joints are extremely stiff and don’t move smoothly, so adjusting the lamp usually takes two hands and more force than it should. Making small positioning changes can be frustrating because the movement isn’t fluid.On the positive side, the lighting is excellent. It gets plenty bright, offers multiple brightness levels, and lets you switch between warmer and cooler color temperatures depending on what you’re doing. The slim, low profile design also looks nice on a desk, and the base is sturdy enough to keep the lamp stable even when the arms are extended into different positions.Overall, it performs well as a desk lamp and the lighting quality is hard to complain about. I just think the mechanical design and build quality should have been better at this price."
