[
    {
        "review": "If you already own Govee products and love their ecosystem, you’ll love this lamp. I started with the Govee Permanent Outdoor Pro Lights, then added TV backlighting, more smart lights around the house, and now this cordless table lamp. It fits right into the collection and works great with the app.If this is your first Govee product, be warned—it might not be your last! Once you see how easy it is to use and how well it integrates with other Govee devices, you’ll probably find yourself adding more to your setup.The lamp looks great, is easy to control, and is another solid addition to the Govee family."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Govee table lamp is simply fantastic! The design is elegant and modern, the light is pleasant, and it can also get impressively bright when needed. The wide range of colors makes it very versatile. What impressed me most is the outstanding battery life. Here in the Dominican Republic, power outages happen from time to time, and thanks to this lamp I still have up to 10 hours of light—often without even noticing the power has gone out. I bought two of them for my bedside tables, and they are among the best purchases I've made. If I could, I would give this product six stars. An outstanding lamp that I would buy again without hesitation."
    },
    {
        "review": "Typical lighting from a multicolor product like this. Definitely gets bright enough but not super dark. Colors get dark but the white options are still pretty bright at 1%. The battery level/charging indicator in the app is the tiniest, glitchiest icon ever. As a portable, rechargeable lamp, knowing where the charging level is at is super important. And it only sometimes flashes to show you how far along you are with charging. They need to fix that in the app asap. Lastly, they say the battery lasts 5-30 hours haha. What an insane range. I know the brighter it is, the shorter the lifespan but at least say something like, “5 hours on max brightness, 30 on lowest” or something. At the end of the day, it does what it’s supposed to. Pretty decent portable lamp"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have an entire govee home system set up and I was missing something on the coffee table for a bit extra lighting. The lamp itself is actually larger than I expect but with less light payoff for its size. It also barely holds a charge for 2 days. Not worth the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have a multitude of Govee products.I update the TV Dreamview backlight whenever Govee comes out with an upgrade for those lights.I also upgrade the Govee floor lamp  (the wand style, I just updated to the Pro 3).I also just purchased the Govee floor lamp with the Aurora projector & I purchased the Nebula projector for my bedroom.I have been very happy with all my Govee products & with Govee customer service.This light is another great product from Govee!It is made well & works better with Google, than most Govee products do.As long as Govee keeps up with making products that are great quality, & are a great value, & keeps up their excellent customer service...I will be a Govee customer for LIFE! Also, I recommend Govee products to everyone I meet & whenever discussing lights & tech products online.Great job again, Govee...THANK YOU!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great product. Very easy to use. I need to learn how to use it better so I don’t have to give it Bluetooth permissions every time I use it, but it’s still great to work with."
    },
    {
        "review": "Let me preface by saying that I love Govee products. I have ecosystems throughout the house and have given light sets, thermostats, and fans to family, who also love them. Everything has worked perfectly for me, and the app is a great feature that keeps all my devices running on timers throughout the house. The Dreamview is my favorite feature that elevates the movie-watching experience, and there is no way I can go back after having my dream set up. I will always continue to buy from Govee. But this lamp... is not it.I like the design, in theory. It looks nice, but falls over at the lightest brush of my cats. It has essentially no functionality besides off and on outside of the app, which falls short of many of their other lights, which have switches for brightness, color, etc. I would have expected touch technology at the $80 price point, but there is a single clicky button and no battery light. To my greatest disappointment, I am struggling to get it to work with Dreamview, which it is supposed to work with. It registers, says it is connected, but never lights up with the rest of the devices on the system. I will keep playing with it in hopes it will work with future updates, but I am still disheartened.As a loyal customer of Govee products, I think this product needed more work before being released. If you are looking for a lamp that lights up and has cool color patterns via an app, this is an okay option. If you are specifically looking for a Govee product to work with your setup, I would recommend waiting for a different generation."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like these Govee lamps.  They can be super bright or just ambient lighting.  Battery life is good and easily rechargeable when necessary.  This was perfect for use in my camper.  I also like the black color as it matches well with my interior."
    },
    {
        "review": "They're really great, it brings life to my living room"
    },
    {
        "review": "It's very good, I recommend it."
