[
    {
        "review": "As I get older, I have discovered something profound: I need more light. Not merely a light, but light in the right place.I previously used a clamp-on lamp attached to the side of my desk. Since I am right-handed, its position often left a shadow exactly where I was trying to write. Moving it to the other side simply relocated the inconvenience, and the lamp itself was always occupying valuable desk space.This over-the-monitor lamp solved the problem beautifully.The long flexible neck lets me position the light exactly where I need it, and it stays where I put it. The two light bars can be spread wide to illuminate most of my work area or brought closer together when I want more concentrated light. I can adjust both brightness and color temperature depending on whether I am typing, reading, handwriting correspondence, working on a manuscript, or merely doodling when I should probably be doing something productive.The lamp is USB-powered. I plugged mine directly into a USB port on the back of my monitor, which is especially convenient because if I am sitting at the desk, the computer is almost certainly running anyway. A USB power adapter is also included, which I appreciate in an age when manufacturers increasingly seem to assume we all maintain a drawer containing seventeen spare charging blocks.My only concern is the mounting hardware. The clamp is holding securely, but while tightening it I felt that the metal bracket was lighter than I expected and that excessive force might distort it. I simply tightened it enough to hold the lamp firmly and stopped there. It has remained steady in normal use. Unless you intend to hang from it like a monkey, I do not see this being a practical problem.Most importantly, the light falls across my work surface instead of creating the shadows I was fighting before. I can type, read, write, analyze, and work comfortably at night without sacrificing desk space to another lamp.This is one of those products that solved an irritating little problem better than I expected.Five stars."
    },
    {
        "review": "Given the price on this lamp had dropped 33% at the time of ordering, this lamp would be a good value even if it were a mediocre light. It's actually a very impressive light; making this a great value.My wife had a special goose-neck clamp light on her studio easel that was designed specifically for artists. She got it used and it's a little broken. I expected this light to be disappointing after one that was designed for the purpose of lighting a canvas while painting.Instead, we were wildly impressed. It's actually a little brighter than the highly expensive specialized lamp.In addition, this one provides the versatility of:• Variable brightness• Variable temperature• Variable focus/concentration by arranging the 2 independent wings of lightAll told, this has been an excellent purchase for an artist. One can only imagine it will work equally well on a desk or workbench."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this lamp! As soon as it was delivered, I assembled it and attached it to the top of my coffee table. That is my work space, whether I am working puzzles (which is the reason I bought this huge coffee table), working on a variety of crafts like painting, crochet, beadwork, and sometimes just eating dinner. Oh, and grooming my dogs! So often I need better light, especially for the puzzles and crafts, and this light provides it perfectly. I love the height, that the clamp is large enough to fit the thick top of my coffee table, the bottom part of the neck is a straight piece of metal pipe but the upper part is flexible in any way you need. And it is sturdy so you can hang it straight out and it will hold its position. The 2 light panels can either be positioned together for a brighter single light source, or they can be pivoted to either side each up to 90 degrees. With them straight across, they will be perfect for puzzles! The light controls are on the lamp head and you just push the buttons to cycle through the various levels in sequence. Being LED, they also do not get hot, and that is definitely a benefit. It is the perfect desk lamp and all this for just $20!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great light;  Very littel assembly required.  Provides  five color temps for your uses.  Multiple brightness settings as well. The desk clamp was well constructed and held with very little  twisting pressure. The shaft was flexible and non intrusive. I really liked the TWO light bars. The ability to adjust them at the corner of my work surface insured maximum illumination where I really needed it without shadows. .  This light sips power from your USB-A port. It also comes with power supply that you can plug into the wall if you prefer. My laptop has USB-C ports so I could not plug into the computer directly. The price was also very reasonable.  I would buy it again"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the amount of coverage this lamp gives without taking up much desk space. The two adjustable light bars can be positioned exactly where you need them, and the flexible neck makes it easy to light a larger workspace or concentrate the light on one area.Having five different light temperatures plus adjustable brightness is especially useful. I can go brighter and cooler when I need to focus, then switch to something warmer and softer later in the evening. The memory function is a nice touch because I don’t have to redo my settings every time I turn it on.The clamp holds securely and keeps the entire base of the desk free, which is probably one of my favorite things about it.Overall, this is a surprisingly versatile little desk lamp. Lots of light, plenty of adjustment, and none of the bulky footprint of a traditional desk lamp."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have received the Voncerus LED desk lamp to try out. The perfect place to try out the LED lamp on my repair or project bench in my office. The setup was seconds attaching the snake to the base then adding the USB A to ac adapter included. My desk has plenty of natural and white lighting now to work on projects etc, Both lights can be adjusted from the panel between the LED lights. The rubber coated snake can be moved around flexible to desired angle. Really nice as I am able to turn, adjust and also move around the light with ease. The table clamp is good but does require a small lip to attach the LED light base to. Very good product to see very well !"
    },
    {
        "review": "We mounted this near my wife's sewing machine to provide extra light for detailed quilting work, and it has worked out great. The mounting system is excellent, taking up very little space while providing a sturdy base that allows the lamp to be adjusted easily without shifting or wobbling.The multiple color temperature settings work very well, as does the adjustable brightness, making it easy to customize the light for different tasks and conditions. The lamp uses a wall-wart power supply with a standard USB connection, which offers the flexibility to power it from alternative USB power sources if needed.Overall, this is a solid, well-designed product that performs as expected and is offered at a reasonable price."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is fantastic. I'm using it for my painting. Its dual heads gives it a bright coverage and last for a good while. The member function is different and will take a little getting used to. The five adjustable mores and dim setting could be used for reading, work, computer, or just plain relaxing.Its space saving goose neck is easy to adjust and gives precise control over the lighting direction.  Very important for painting."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This is an awesome, versatile, sleek/modern lamp for your desk. It was very easy to install, it’s sturdy, all you could ask for at its price point.Has an array of temperature and brightness modes to choose from (which I’ve attempted to show in my pictures). All of the cycles haven’t showcase any flickering. The long rubber tube you attach it to allows you to adjust the light at an angle you prefer.You can choose to cycle through on the differ modes on the lamp itself or use the remote it came with.I recommend this to all my fellow people who wfh or has their own setup for home use!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was a little nervous about buying a lamp made in China, but so far, the Macasa is the best I've ever used. 1) It has both a heavy base and an optional clamp, so I could place it exactly where I wanted, even though the lamp base would have been in the way of my monitor bases. 2) It is over 26\" tall, able to mount behind my 27\" monitors, while the heads go above and over the two monitors. 3) The flexible upper half allows the lamps to be positioned where no shadows are cast if I write, then bent slightly back so no glare reaches my eyes. 4) The 31\" long light bar illuminates nearly my entire work desk. 5) The remote is nice, but the touch controls let me adjust the light intensity and color temperauture to perfection, then turn the lamp on and off with easy touches. My only complaint is that I can now see my desk very clearly, and I'm going to have to clean it more often."
