    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this light for my computer desk in June of 2024. It still works like the first day of purchase!!I got on my Amazon app to search for a light for my sewing table not only for a brighter view of my work space but also for video recording. I was getting so frustrated with the reviews on the lights that I thought would be perfect for my space. I didn't want a light that would be in my way of recording or working. I also need one that wouldn't be too bright and definitely not a glare. After searching the site for several hours and reading tons of reviews I finally decided to search my order history to see exactly what lights I had already ordered for video recording.  This light came up and \"ding\", a light came on in my head. \"Why not get the desk light for the sewing table???\"I did place an order for another desk light since I am so pleased with my first one. Not only is the quality of the light amazing, so is the longevity.  It's been almost 2 years and I have not had one issue with my desk lamp. I'm sure I will be pleased with the new one. Not to mention that the seller is still on Amazon!!  Don't over think it, just get one. You won't be disappointed!"
    },
    {
        "review": "bright enough, adjustable fine for my situation which isn't all that ordinary. i have this fit between the top 2 and bottom 2 of a 4 monitor mount and it sneaks in there fine and looks great. i hope it holds up at least a few more years, but so far so good!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This double headed lamp works well, the gooseneck is quite flexible and lets me put light on the subject easily. It wasn’t too hard to setup, just a bit awkward trying to get it to clamp onto my desk from behind.The remote is handy and lets me turn it on or off from my bed if I want more light in my room, or forgot to turn it off when I left.Only issue is that when you swap to the different colour modes, it forgets the brightness level immediately, so I have to keep adjusting it.It's a good lamp, just needed a way to keep the brightness the way I set it up."
    },
    {
        "review": "This double-headed LED desk lamp with remote control is an ultra-bright 24 W lamp, ideal for the desk, workbench, drawing table or workshop. Its light is adjustable in intensity and temperature. The two sides of the lamp move and thus offer great versatility. The remote control is also a plus. I love the effect. It's super relaxing and practical for detailed work that requires lighting. Great addition to the office. On the other hand, we would have liked to have the choice of foot to install it: it must be screwed to the edge of the desk, which may not always be practical or ideal."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this desk lamp off of Vine for my office because I needed one and was remodeling. I was using just a regular light that is on my ceiling and it was creating a glare on my Monitor that was hard on my eyes. This one is much better.It is adjustable. Bendable,  Dimmable and has eye saving features with different colors of light. A White neon type. A medium light and a Warm light that is very easy on the eyes.Setting it up was pretty easy. Clip it all together. put in a few screws. It even came with a mini screw driver. The light has a spot to hide the cord.. Along its side. It clips right in and hides . I thought this was a very nice feature. More should have it. You cannot even see the cord at all.The lamp comes with a remote for hands free operation. It also has 4 buttons on the top to control the brightness. Mode and a timer function. You can turn it off and on to from there.The neck is flexible and bendable so you can set this up in many different ways. The arms of the lamp both pivot 180 degrees. So you can keep it horizontal looking or pivot them to the front for when working on things. reading documents or need to see fine details. The clip was nice and sturdy on my desk. No bends or breaks. I hooked it on pretty tight to. Solid build quality all the way through.All in all I really like it. I think this lamp makes a great office light and can also be a very good workshop light. Or lab light. Or even just a reading lamp for your room. The retail price was more then fair and it just works. No complaints. I love it and can recommend it. Thanks a  ton."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great desk lamp overall.  The top section can be bent backwards and forwards for a perfect placement.The lamp is held in place with a desk clamp, easy to install.The two led lamp arms can be rotated individually.Brightness and color can be adjusted from the remote or touch buttons on the top.I removed one star because the lamp is a little shaky and not that stable.  When typing or putting a hand a little hard on the desk it does shake."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a double-head LED lamp that is very bright and raised high on desk edge. The head lights are two LED panels that can rotate 90 degrees horizontal between front and side.It doesn’t have a lamp stand on desk. It has a desk edge mounting bracket that can be mount to a variety of thickness of desk. A fixed metal pole attached to the mounting bracket. Then a flexible goose neck attached to the metal pole which then hold the LED heads. The goose neck can be adjusted to any angle of your choice. Both the metal pole and the flexible goose neck bring the LED heads very high over desk that you can place monitors underneath the LED heads.Both LED panels can independently rotate at axis of the center of the LED heads. On top of the center of LED heads there are 4 touch buttons: power on/off, light color temperature, dim and brightness. These buttons are very sensitive and responsive.In addition to the control buttons on the LED heads, the desk lamp comes with tiny remote control for convenience. It has exactly the same 4 buttons as those on the LED heads.The desk lamp comes with a special power adapter which provides 24V/1A power for the lamp. The wire attached to the LED heads can be inserted into the slots of the goose neck and metal pole, so that it is not visible. A very detailed design. Excellent.The bottom screw plate of the mounting bracket is kind of small compare to the weight of the lamp that it needs to hold. Not sure if it will be strong enough and durable. So far so good.Very good desk lamp. Highly recommend."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "The 2000LM output is bright enough to light up my whole desk, and the stepless dimming means I never have to settle for \"too bright\" or \"too dim\" — it's always just right. The LED light is flicker-free, which makes a huge difference during marathon study sessions"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good brightness, smooth stepless dimming. Multiple lighting modes. Solid lamp for desk work."
    },
    {
        "review": "The lamp is very nice, has multiple white color settings and multiple brightness settings. The Wave on/off is a nice touch, and works well. It does not return to previous setting after power outage - so if you unplug it, it defaults to the first setting.The entire thing is very large - takes a decent amount of room on the desk, and if you already use a screen mount it will be off center due to that. It's also very tall - This is needed so it can lean over large screens but honestly it feels overwhelming on a desk, it's almost too big for an average desk even with 2 screens.If that's not an issue then this is a great lamp for you."
    },
    {
        "review": "Finding a desk lamp that has great \"task lighting\" and general workspace illumination is notoriously difficult, especially for modern multi-monitor or ultra-wide setups. The Syrinx Dual-Head LED Desk Lamp delivers great light coverage, has customization, and smart hands-free.Coverage Area:  Up to 70\" workspaceLight Bar Length:  23.7\" extended dual-headColor Temperature:  3000K – 6000K (5 presets)Brightness Levels:  10 distinct levels (50 total lighting combinations)LED Count & Quality:  96 LEDs, CRI90+, flicker-free, low-blue-lightAdjustability:  360° flexible gooseneck + 180° foldable armsControls: Hands-free gesture control + inline wired controller!!Timers & Memory:  15 / 30 / 60-minute auto-off timer + settings memoryMy Notes>Unmatched Coverage for Complex Workstations>The 23.7-inch extended dual-head light bar is unlike standard single-point desk lamps that cast harsh shadows or leave dark edges, the Syrinx easily spans large desks up to 70 inches. By spreading the dual arms flat, you can completely eliminate glare on dual-monitor setups; by angling them inward, you get concentrated, shadow free light directly over your workbench or reading area.>Precise Control & Eye Comfort: With 50 total lighting combinations (10 brightness steps paired with 5 color temperatures ranging from a warm 3000K to a daylight 6000K), dialing in the exact light needed for the time of day or task is effortless. The CRI90+ rating ensures accurate color rendering—a must for artists, crafters, and photo editors—while the flicker-free, low-blue-light array minimizes eye strain during late-night work sessions.>Smart, Practical Usability:  The built-in hands-free gesture sensor is a huge quality-of-life upgrade for hands-on projects. If your hands are covered in paint, ink, or dirt, a simple wave over the sensor toggles the light on or off. For permanent settings, the inline controller, built-in memory function, and selectable auto-off timers (15/30/60 mins) make using this lamp very smooth.*Massive 70\" illumination footprint easily covers dual monitors and large craft tables.*360° gooseneck plus 180° arm flexibility allows virtually unlimited positioning options.*High color accuracy (CRI90+) and flicker-free design drastically reduce eye fatigue.*Gesture control keeps the fixture clean when working on messy DIY tasks.*Supported by US-based customer support and a 12-month technical warranty.Cons:Wired inline controller means extra cord management is required behind the desk.The wide physical footprint may feel overpowering on very small, minimalist writing desks.If you need a heavy-duty lighting solution that adapts to complex desktop setups and hands-on creative projects, this lamp is an outstanding addition to your workspace."
    },
    {
        "review": "So I didn't know what to expect as I've never had a big lamp like this with a flexible, rotating head. I was pleasantly surprised at all of the features and the overall function of this lamp.Build: No issues out of the box with defects. It was packaged well and I had no issue putting it together except it wanting to rotate around a bit as I screwed the main shaft of the light into the base.Function: Pretty neat honestly, it gives off a unique appearance with the tall almost street light look. I like how you can use the small wired controller to adjust between brightness levels as well as color temperature. I like how more lights are giving you total control for brightness and color temperature rather than just a couple options. I found these easy to adjust, no issues. I think it has a timer thing but I won't be using that. The light easily rotates out straight like I have, or forward together. It also bends which can be very nice for certain tasks, but at the moment I am keeping it in one position. The brightest light setting is good, no complaints in any way.Overall I am happy and surprised at how useful this light is. It is functional, neat looking and the base is heavy/sturdy. Will continue to use and update if anything fails."
    },
    {
        "review": "This desk lamp is a strong option for anyone who spends a lot of time working, reading, crafting, or studying at a desk. The dual-light design is particularly useful because it provides both focused illumination and broader coverage across the workspace instead of creating one small bright spot. The 360-degree gooseneck makes it easy to reposition the light exactly where it is needed, and having five color-temperature settings allows the lighting to be adjusted depending on whether you want warmer light or a brighter, more daylight-style setting.The ten brightness levels provide a lot of flexibility, especially when working at different times of day. I also appreciate that the lamp is designed to provide flicker-free lighting, which is important when spending long periods in front of a computer or working on detailed projects. With up to 2000 lumens and 18 watts of output, it provides plenty of illumination without requiring a large traditional desk lamp. The sleek black design also looks professional and fits easily into a home office setup without taking over the workspace."
    },
    {
        "review": "So, of course, as i get older, my eyesight is getting older too! I have been thinking about getting a desk lamp like this for awhile.I needed this for doing jigsaw puzzles in the winter (when it gets dark so soon), and to use to light up the sheetmusic when playing the keyboard. This lamp is perfect for both of those uses!First, you can set it up very high, so it shine downs on your project without being in the way. It allows for a great deal of adjustment (which also helps reduce glare), and it does stay in place! You get a great variety (5) of light colors, and brightness levels. i didn't think i would use the hand swipe to turn it on, but i use it all the time!I think it looks great, is solidly built, and is a good value for the price!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This over monitor light has a remote that is hardwired inline with the power cord and comes with a full plug.  The remote has dimming but also allows for change of the color of light as well.  The coolest feature is the sensor above light band that allows one to wave their hand over it to turn it on and off.  Great convenence.  Also love that the two light bars are adjustable at angles to the pivot point as this allows more light to be projected at distance from above the monitor lighting up the entire desk in front of the monitor.  Just this light above the computer monitor provides great light down to my keyboard tray and mouse as well as surface in front of the monitor.  Hard to capture in last picture, but it is very nice light.  The weighted base on this keeps it upright and stable.  Really could not ask any more of how this was designed.  Very solid materials.  Can HIGHLY recommend.  I love it!"
    }
]

