        "review": "I'm obsessed with these lights—I own two now, one in my bedroom and another in my living room.The only reason I'm not giving it five stars is the night light feature, which ironically is the setting I use the most. It can't be configured through the app, and activating it directly on the lamp is frustrating. You have to turn the unit off and lightly touch both the top and bottom at the same time, which isn't intuitive and doesn't always work on the first try.I also found the preset mood scenes to be somewhat underwhelming. Aside from setting schedules, there isn't much room for customization, so they don't add a lot of value in my opinion.That said, if you're looking for a stylish lamp with excellent ambient lighting and tons of options, I still highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I looked all over for an actual LAMP that worked with Alexa. Everything else seems to be a lamp with an included smart bulb. The issue begins if you can't really use the app nor can verbalize Alexa commands. Since my mom is able to do neither, she didn't really have a reliable way for the lamp to be turned off at night other than a lamp's physical switch. The issue there is that means there's no power to the smart bulb to have Alexa turn it back on.With this lamp, not only are we able to have her turn it off at night, but I can also have it timed to turn on in the morning with 'sunlight' level light to help her wake up, as well as have it timed to turn on a bit before sunset so her room is lit for when she wants to do things there in the evening.Overall, this is a great lamp, and I am fully happy with the purchase and after setting it up. I will note that there are other features I didn't mention, like different types of light (soft light for reading, 'daylight' for helping wake up, etc.) as well as multiple colors of light available."
