[
    {
        "review": "This small, quiet and efficient air purifier is ideal for our needs. It fits neatly into any room, is unobtrusive, and is simple to operate and maintain. The build quality and overall aesthetics is top notch. The cost of replacement filters is reasonable and can be done in less than a minute... about every six to eight months. We noticed that the unit quickly removed any smoke and cooking odors from the area while running. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this during fires in northern CA, & it makes a huge difference. I researched so many air purifiers before purchasing, and this is hands down the best affordable option available. It’s really easy to set up (takes 2 mins) and change the filters. It has 3 fan speeds, the highest being really high with a decent white noise sound (I like this) but lowest fan speed is almost silent. I can notice a difference in air quality in the room I have it in- I feel more awake and the air feels noticeably cleaner (if you walk in from another room, you can tell the difference immediately). This had the highest CADR of all other well-known brand options in the $100-$200 range (143 CFM CADR), which is the rate it cleans/replaces the air in a room per hour (this is 222’^2). I love this product so much and trust the brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "Edit to original review: it’s been several months at this point and I have two in our small farmhouse. They work amazing, best purchase we’ve made.So far: it’s perfect, surpassed all expectations, ALL.Backstory: we’re living in a house from the late 1800s, that has been dormant for about ten years until we moved in a couple years ago. We have five pets, four cats which are strictly indoor and use an automatic litter box (Popur S7 which does great for the smell, it can only do so much though) and one fat, lazy, stinky pitbull. The house is musky, it’s old, it had way too much mold in the detached basement when we moved in. And the pets? They stink bad too, this is coming from someone who is very particular about the house smelling good. The litter box is horrible, the dog is gross, the house is old.I went searching for an air purifier, I’ve been wanting the SHARK never change, but couldn’t break down and buy it for $300. Didn’t try it out, can’t say if it’s good or not.While I was looking at reviews, I found the shark had only 5,000 reviews on Amazon, and it was at 4.3 stars. Okay, that’s not too bad. But this Levoit one had over 100,000 reviews and 4.8 stars. That’s nuts in comparison. I done a lot of looking on Reddit and found that the shark wasn’t even mentioned in the majority of good quality reviews, so I disregarded it.This specific one happened to be in budget and also has amazing reviews.We received it last night and set it up this morning, yep this morning, in our cat’s litter box room which is also unfortunately our closet. That room is the worst room of the house in my opinion. It’s been running for about 6 hours and I already notice a huge impact. It’s easier to breath, the air doesn’t feel so heavy, and the litter box is nonexistent, even right after they use it. Hubby sprayed cologne on himself and not 20 seconds later I walked in and it was gone, already sucked away. I put a box fan on it to help circulation and have it on 3.I’m buying another. Maybe two more. If I remember I’ll come back and review again when it gets a little later in the month. We’re leaving for vacation next Monday, so I’m curious how it will hold up against the cats stagnant litter box, which usually stinks pretty bad when we get home after a week.TLDR; Amazing for pet odor, amazing for muskiness. Perfect and worth every penny."
    },
    {
        "review": "An air purifier is not a complicated device.  It is a fan, and an air filter.  The fan pulls air through the air filter, and catches various particles and impurities in the air.  As long as you have a decent HEPA filter, and a fan that has enough velocity to circulate the room air through the filter effectively, it will work to clean the air.  You can build one yourself with a box fan and some high quality furnace filters and duct tape if you have to.So what distinguishes this one from the hundreds of others out there, why is it so popular?(1) Low up front costs - this has enough power to handle a small room effectively and a true HEPA filter at a pretty low initial cost.(2) Easy to live with - the fan is very quiet except on high, and even on high it isn't obnoxiously loud.  Changing the filter takes about 10 seconds and is easy to do.  There is a pre-filter to catch large dust/animal hair and the like which you can vacuum to extend the life of the HEPA filter for small particles.  The unit itself is not huge or ugly, so it can sit in the corner of most rooms without being objectionable.(3) Available filters - this unit's extreme popularity means that there will likely be filters available for many years.(4) It does work - I bought an air quality meter after the recent wildfire smoke episode, and it shows me that this thing does a pretty good job in small rooms.  In bigger rooms it will still provide some benefit, but it is really not able to move enough air quickly enough to clean a large room.Downsides:The filters are relatively small, so they will have to be changed fairly frequently if you run the unit constantly.  How frequently?  I don't know, your mileage will vary depending on how many pets you have, how much wildfire smoke is in your area, etc.  But I would expect to buy at least two a year if comparing this to other units that may have larger filters you need to change less often.  So think about the total running costs and not just the up front cost when comparison shopping here.  If you are thinking about saving money by trying to run this in a bigger room than it is designed for, don't go down that road.  You do need to size your unit to the area you are trying to keep clean.  A large room needs a larger unit with a bigger fan and a bigger filter.  Also, all of these things are quieter if not running on high.  So it is better to get a bigger unit even one that handles more than you are asking it to, and then run it slower and change the filters less often versus trying to save money up front and then driving the thing as hard as it will go to barely get any benefit."
    },
    {
        "review": "Thank the Lord I got this in time.  I live in a dusty, pollen-filled farming area in eastern Washington state so I like to have an air purifier, especially in my bedroom.  My old filtration unit was ancient and probably not really working anymore other than to make noise. I decided to replace it with this Levoit. Shortly after receiving it, we become overwhelmed with thick smoke from the Spokane fire. That smoke is worse than our normal wildfires even though it is not as dense. I am having worse reactions to this smoke; maybe because of all the chemicals from the homes and other structures that have burned? I mask up and try to work outside everyday, but it’s still really bad. It is just plain nasty!So the big question, does this air purifier work well? I would have to say definitely, YES! I am older and get to feeling choked up, my nose runs all day, and my eyes burn a lot of the time. On the bad days , I even get a bit of a sore throat. So since this fire started I go to bed feeling pretty rough and have to elevate my head to breathe better. Now that I am using the Levoit, I wake up without burning eyes can again breathe deeply, and actually feel more rested.My past concern about a purifier had been about noise, so many bright lights on things for a bedroom, etc. Hey you can turn down the noise  and lighting by using the nighttime setting when you’re trying to sleep. It has easy instructions. THIS IS REALLY CLEANING THE AIR! Now that I am actually using it to breathe, I really am so thankful that I decided to order this Levoit. I can’t imagine many purifiers, especially for this price, that would work better. I don’t know what I would do without it right now. When my filtration unit for the kitchen and living area wears out,  I would definitely replace it with a Levoit of a larger size. I pray for so many others that these fires end soon, but I am more than happy about my purchase and how quickly I received it. Thank you!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I only just got this yesterday and used it last night for the first time but I feel compelled to write a quick review already. This thing is a game. changer. Ever since moving to Texas, I suffer from terrible seasonal allergies. I never have in my life until now (turns out I'm allergic to a handful of trees that are native around here. Fun.) Some years are worse than others but this year is baaad. For the past few weeks my mornings have had me waking up congested and unable to breathe, blowing wads of snot out of my nose (sorry!), and with a itchy/scratchy sore throat. First thing I do is take an allergy pill and wait in misery until it finally seems to kick in around mid morning. (I've had a terrible time finding meds that work too. It just sucks.) I don't know why I never thought to get an air purifier. I guess when I thought of air purifiers I'd always think of the fancy Dyson ones that cost hundreds of dollars. I mean, puh-lease. Not happening. Then I found this little guy. Had great reviews, was the perfect little size for our master bedroom (216sqft), and reasonably priced with reasonably priced replacement filters. In a plee of desperation I talked my husband into us trying it. It got in yesterday (quicker than expected, yay!). I immediately unboxed it upon getting home from work and plugged it in. It says you only need to run it for about 15-20 minutes on high to cycle the room but I set that little baby on high with a two hour timer and let it run. When it was time for bed, I set the 6 hour timer on sleep mode. The sleep mode is great. It's a lot more quiet than I expected. I still expected to be able to hear a little white noise from it (which doesn't bother me at all) but unless I lift my head off the pillow and really listen, I can only just baaarely hear it. And I have it on my side of the bed about 3 feet away. Our home air system is louder than it on sleep mode. If you enjoy white noise, you could probably just run it on low and be fine. It has a button to turn off the indicator lights at night too so you don't have bright lights keeping you awake if that's a problem for you. Anyway, I woke up this morning with NO allergy symptoms. None. No congestion, absolutely clear nasal passages, and NO sore throat at all! I'm blown away. I'll try to come back and revise this review if my opinion changes but after the first night and the relief I was FINALLY able to feel from my allergies this morning I absolutely rate this thing 5 stars. Worth every penny!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m very happy with my Levoit Air Purifier. I can actually feel the difference in the air, especially when I leave it running all night. One thing I’ve noticed is that when I clean my nose, it’s not nearly as dirty as it used to be, which makes me feel like the purifier is really helping with the dust and particles in the air.I also love how quiet it is, so I can comfortably keep it running while I sleep. As soon as I get home, I turn it on and usually keep it running throughout the night. Having pets, I especially like knowing that it helps filter pet hair, dander, dust, and other airborne particles.So far, I’m very satisfied with it and would definitely recommend it, especially for pet owners or anyone wanting cleaner, fresher-feeling air at home."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've hade this for about 2 months now and there's a noticeable difference in the air quality of my room. I have pet rats and it keeps the smell down almost completely. I like that you can choose to have the display light off, which is helpful especially at night when you don't want a little light on in your room. Overall, recommend this air purifier, especially for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been really happy with the Levoit air purifier. It's quiet, easy to use, and has noticeably improved the air quality in my room. It does a great job reducing dust and odors, and the sleep mode is almost silent, making it perfect for overnight use. Overall, it's a reliable and effective air purifier that's well worth the investment."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is such a great buy use it every day"
    },
    {
        "review": "Damaged"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is the second time I have purchased this purifier and that speaks volumes about how satisfied I am with it. I now have 2 and it has been an excellent investment to keep the air cleaner, especially in rooms where I spend many hours. It is easy to use, works quietly and you can notice the difference in the air quality. In addition, the filters are easy to replace and the equipment has proven to be reliable over time. It is also at a very good price when buying from others."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am very happy with this air purifier, it works really well, quite quiet and very powerful at speed 3. The design is very nice and is not too heavy. I recommend"
    }
