    {
        "review": "Although the room is very clean, there are no windows and no air circulation so when I was there for a long time my head started to hurt a little due to smells like humidity or storage, but after having it for a few months it has been more comfortable to be in my room even with fewer allergies now, the difference was noticeable from the first day, the first few days I had it on speed 3 but now I almost always have it on speed 1, this one is clearly of good quality, because there are also some that claim to be air filters but do not have them. no type of certificate and they do not have the appropriate filtration system"
    },
    {
        "review": "It is small, so miracles cannot be expected, but if the manufacturer's instructions are respected by using it in rooms of adequate size, it works very well, and purifies the air correctly. Everything seems to be built with excellent quality: plastics, joints, fan motor etc... Even the filter seems to be well built and of higher quality than others in the same price range. It has a 3-speed adjustment of which only the maximum is noisy but not very annoying, in fact the intermediate speed is barely audible (equal to a breath) and never annoying even if you are nearby. At first speed it is practically impossible to hear anything and this is a HUGE advantage compared to other purifiers on the market in the same category. This speed is perfect for night sleep. No hum or noise. This, perhaps, I believe is also possible thanks to the direct current motor/fan, in fact the purifier is supplied with a small power supply which is found in the package. It also includes 3 \"felts\" for the diffusion of natural essences to be inserted in a special almost invisible side drawer. Overall therefore an excellent, compact purifier, with a good quality/price ratio and above all not very noisy and worth buying."
