[
    {
        "review": "I had been planning on purchasing an air purifier for some time due to our seasonal allergies along with the dog hair from our beagle. I finally decided to buy one during Amazon Prime Days in June. I researched air purifiers and decided on Levoit since I've read many good things about this brand. This particular model helps filter dog hair and dander. We have been running it constantly since we received it a couple of weeks ago and what a difference it has made! We still have some allergies but not nearly as bad and the amount of dog hair it collected in it's pre-filter was amazing! We have it set right between our kitchen and living room and it is just the right size to help clear the air in both rooms. It's unbelievably quiet! On the lowest setting we have checked to see if it's even running and it was! If need be it is light enough to move into our dining room to purify that air. The filters last a very long time since they can be vacuumed and reused. I love this purifier and have bought a second smaller one for my bedroom."
    },
    {
        "review": "The LEVOIT Vital 200S-P Air Purifier is AHAM certified, meaning it has been independently tested by the Association of Home Appliance Manufacturers for air-cleaning performance, safety, and energy efficiency. Products with the AHAM VERIFIDE seal meet strict appliance-performance standards, giving added confidence in their ability to improve indoor air quality. This air purifier is designed with allergy sufferers in mind, helping capture common airborne irritants such as pollen, pet hair, dander, and dust. Its efficient filtration system traps tiny particles to support fresher, cleaner air for you and your family. Built for spaces up to 1,875 square feet, the Vital 200S-P is a strong choice for living rooms, bedrooms, basements, open-concept homes, high-traffic areas, and households with pets. A traditional air inlet works together with an additional U-shaped air inlet to help capture airborne pet hair and odors more efficiently while reducing the chance of clogs, so the purifier can keep air moving smoothly.Verified CADR RatingsThe Vital 200S-P has been tested with the following Clean Air Delivery Rate ratings:• Smoke: 250 CFM• Dust: 254 CFM• Pollen: 289 CFMAfter looking at several air purifiers, this LEVOIT looked to be exactly what I was looking for. It received complimentary reviews and was reasonably priced. It is very quiet and comes with the option to turn the control panel lights off, perfect for bedroom use during the night. This has been a great purchase for my family."
    },
    {
        "review": "These Air Purifiers are great!  The work well!  We have had 2 for some time but we are a multi dog household and summertime shedding is a fact!  I especially love the “screen” pre-filter that catches a ton of stuff in the air!  It is easy to remove the prefilter and and wash, dry and reinstall.  Takes seconds!  Probably will buy more for other areas of the house!  Recommend!  Quiet and does a great job."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this air purifier because with all the animal hair, dust, and seasonal allergens floating around, I was coughing constantly- night and day. I happened to get it a little on sale, and while the cost is a little high, it has proven its worth to the penny. It comes with multiple speeds, modes, and most importantly the sleep function. When its in night/sleep mode, its still releasing air but there is no light pollution or any sounds. It is so quiet I forget its on. I also see a vast improvement on my air quality and I no longer wake up the whole household at night with my coughing. It does its best work in one room, but I have noticed that the room its in has less dust. Ive also noticed it is a little if a deoderizor, which is great for someone who has a sensitive nose. Overall, yes its a little expensive upfront but the design of it, the quality of its work, and being able to finally sleep through the night is priceless. I dont know about its longevity but I did buy a very small and older version from this manufacturer 3 years ago and its still going."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've recently replaced some purifiers with the Levoit models.  My VERY expensive Aeris no longer had a functioning app after Roomba bought the company out, so I tossed it and got a Core 400.  I liked it so much that over the last 2 weeks I got another Core 400, this 200S-P, also today they delivered a 100S-P for the smaller bedroom, and I have another small core one for the master bathroom to keep down the dust.So out of seven purifiers, where I used to have five manufacturer's products, I only have three now.I don't use them for air quality, I don't have breathing issues.  I just like the reduced dust.  Since my son graduated and moved out nearly 3 years ago, I live in the house alone, and am not a fan of dusting.  So all these purifiers really help cut that down.They run silently in auto mode.  And unlike the others, when they do kick into high, they're not NEARLY as annoyingly loud.  Even the bigger Core-400 at the highest setting is only about as loud as the nearby Air+Health that's in the connected great room when it's about 30 to 40%.  The sensors are really capable of noting things.  Tonight was the first time that the purifiers in the first two bedrooms on the OTHER SIDE of the house from the kitchen noticed and responded to the changes in the air when I was cooking chicken on the stovetop.  Tonight is also the first time I had Levoit in them instead of the Winix ones that these replaced today, when the Winix smart apps stopped working right and I couldn't do schedules anymore.The prices are so much better than the expensive ones (this one was LESS than 1/5th the cost of that Aeris I tossed out last week) but they are just as effective in my house.  And the control via the app is superb.  I already had some smart devices using the VeSync app, so adding these was a breeze.  No need to activate a wireless access point on the devices to connect your phone or something - simply hold the power button down until the wifi light blinks, and VeSync finds them right away.  A quick firmware update and they were up and running.  And I love the fact that they UPDATE their firmware in these things...You can't go wrong with any of these models.  I'm loving all of them so far."
    },
    {
        "review": "So far so good.  Very different!  Sometimes not even sure it’s on.  It states air quality excellent all the time which is why I gave 4 stars since I have 2 dogs, I see dust when I clean weekly so not sure how well it’s doing."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've not had the purifier for a full 30 days yet, but so far it is excellent! I did thorough research when replacing my MedifyAir purifier and found that Levoit is one of the few that is actually 3rd party tested and thus markets the correct numbers of how much space it can cover, unlike MedifyAir and some others brands. I am very impressed with the packaging, the ease of set up, and that you don't have to use the app unless you want to. Though the app is very nice. It has some nice smart features, but again, you don't have to use them if you don't want. You can literally plug it in and turn it on and go. I also like the fact that the filters are cheaper than what I have been used to buying and they last longer! So more efficient, longer lasting, cheaper filters, covers more space, WIN-WIN!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been considering getting some air purifiers for our home. So glad I got these ones. I got 2, one for our main living space and bedroom. Have them running in auto mode all the time. They work! I’ve noticed a huge difference in our home’s air quality, definitely removed odor. I just switched the filters for the first time. I waited two months. Just because our area experienced a really bad fire reason. So I wanted to wait until the fires were out before changing them. Easy to change filters and wash screen. Very happy 12/10 recommend. We live in the country with lots of animals, doors always opening and closing."
    },
    {
        "review": "Pros: - Reduces dust in the room a little. Cons: - Does not fit the 1875 square feet (174m2) indicated in its advertising. In practical terms it only serves 388 square feet (36m2) as indicated in the last photo of the publication. More than four air changes per hour are required for an air filter to be effective and that amount is only reached in a 36m2 room and at MAXIMUM SPEED (important point).- It is only HEPA grade at MINIMUM SPEED. You can check it on the official product page. It is not a certified HEPA filter. They even removed the HEPA filter legend from the filter itself, as seen in the image. They were forced to remove something that, basically, was false advertising.- AT MAXIMUM SPEED, in addition to not being HEPA, it easily reaches 60db of noise, plus less, as heard in the video. It is extremely quiet in first speed for sleeping, but in third and fourth it is not so that you are in the same room. - The sensor is always in blue, \"optimal\" air quality. Even if you lock it in a room where there is mold, it is unable to detect these particles. It only turns red when you sweep the room where the filter is located, it only detects really large particles. Even cooking in front of it does not lower the \"air quality\", even if your food is burning. So auto mode basically doesn't do much good. This is assuming that the sensor was cleaned and calibrated as indicated in the instructions. You almost have to turn a match on and off in front of the sensor so that it detects the smoke and the light goes from blue to red. - Bring very little carbon, if your problem is odors, you will use up this filter in weeks or a few months, not in 1 year. - Cheap plastic of very poor quality. The panel was scratched on the first pass of a microfiber cloth. In the photos you can see details of how cheap all the materials look."
    },
    {
        "review": "Honestly I've been eyeing a levoit air purifier for about a year. I thought it was a tad expensive but I finally bit the bullet. When I say I've put this to the test it's no joke! I've been learning acrylic nails and if anyone has been around monomer you know it's extremely potent and it smells my house up for about 2 days! I was starting to worry about the effects it may have on my children so this is what made me ultimately spend the money on one. When I first plugged it in it said air quality was \"moderate\" so i busted out the monomer and within 5 seconds my air quality went to \"bad\" It kicked in immediately (I had already set it up to wifi) and I kid you not within 10-15 minutes my air quality was up to \"good\" I left the monomer out to test it as I went for a walk and when I came home I was expecting the monomer smell to hit me in the face but it didnt!!! I was gone for about a half hour and I could only smell it once I went up to my room and stood beside it and it wasnt strong at all. To keep testing it I've left the monomer out all day and evening and my air purifier will kick in when the air quality goes below \"good\" which i love as it only comes on when needed. The monomers been out for about 8.5 hrs and i am just blown away. I forgot to mention the purifier is about 5 feet from it and i just checked the air quality and it's \"very good\" and i can't even smell it when i am beside it now! There is no better test than this! I also love that there is a setting so it'll detect light and if it's night time and dark (your sleeping) the displays lights won't shine, they stay dark. I should also mention i bought a chemical filter (green) one for it but wanted to see the power of the filter it came with so that's what I've used. Another great thing is even on high it's not super loud and like I said doesn't run consistently. I got the 200s so it does up to 1900 sq ft and is the larger model but it's very sleek and modern so I don't mind! I can feel the quality in my air now. It's so odd. I HIGHLY recommend Levoit air purifiers. You won't regret it! Oh it also has a pet mode!! I should also mention the filters do not need to be changed often. They recommend once every 9 months. I also love how it connects directly to my phone and my alexa so I can use voice control or control it when i am not home!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It arrived ahead of schedule, 5 days early. It came well packaged, with a manual in English. Very quiet, up to speed 2 you hear absolutely nothing, from 3 above, very comfortable sound. Control and pet mode via the app. The result and benefit, time will tell."
    },
    {
        "review": "It arrived on the agreed date, at an excellent price, it fulfills all the functions mentioned, I had an allergy to placeerin since they were working with wood, the allergy slowly subsided in one day, I would definitely buy it again"
    }
]

[
