    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using the Coway Airmega AP-1512HH for several weeks, and it's easy to see why this model has been recommended for so many years.**Setup & First Impressions**Setup took less than 10 minutes. The filters come pre-installed in protective packaging, so make sure to remove the plastic before turning it on. The purifier feels well-built without taking up much floor space.**Noise**One of my biggest concerns was noise since I use it in my living space. On the lowest setting it's quiet enough that I barely notice it's running. Medium is still comfortable for everyday use, while High moves a lot of air but is noticeably louder—which is expected when you need maximum filtration.**Air Quality Sensor & Auto Mode**The air quality indicator is surprisingly responsive. It increases the fan speed automatically when cooking odours or dust are detected, then returns to a quieter setting once the air clears. I rarely need to adjust it manually because Auto mode works so well.**Air Quality**I noticed less lingering cooking smells and the room feels fresher overall. Dust also seems to accumulate more slowly on nearby furniture. While I can't measure microscopic particles at home, it has made a noticeable difference in day-to-day air quality.**Maintenance**The washable pre-filter is easy to remove and clean, which should help extend the life of the HEPA and carbon filters. The filter replacement indicator is also a nice reminder instead of trying to remember the schedule yourself.**Pros*** Quiet on low speed* Excellent Auto mode with responsive air quality sensor* Compact footprint* Easy filter maintenance* Eco mode helps reduce power consumption when the air is clean**Cons*** High speed is fairly loud (although it moves a lot of air).* Replacement filters are an ongoing cost, so it's worth factoring that into long-term ownership.Overall, this has been a reliable air purifier that balances performance, ease of use, and noise very well. If you're looking for a purifier for a bedroom, office, or medium-sized living area, I'd have no hesitation recommending this model."
    },
    {
        "review": "The delivery was very fast, it arrived a day earlier than expected, first positive point. The purifier is made of very good materials second positive point. As for the noise at level 1 the noise is not perceptible and at level 2 it is almost imperceptible, at level 3 you can hear a lot but there are very few occasions and for a very short time in which it has to be used at level 3 so it is also a positive point. Another positive point in my opinion is its size, which is more compact than others of the same capacity. I live in an area where there are many building constructions in the surroundings which has meant that in the last two years there has been a lot of dust in the environment, in addition the air quality in the city where I live has also dropped a lot which has caused me to have allergic reactions that occur mostly at night causing my airways to become congested and I have trouble breathing. The 3 nights that I have been using it so far, the level of dust in the room has dropped by almost 90%, I have not had any allergic reactions and my nose does not get congested at night, I have it on 24 hours a day at speed level 1. It is still early to see if I will have good results in the long term but until today it has been very good. For those who are investigating the purchase of an air purifier, I recommend that you carefully analyze your particular situation. This purifier has been very useful to me since it eliminates dust, odors and the vast majority of contaminants, also from what I researched it eliminates only part of the gases emitted by cars in traffic areas but be careful, it does not eliminate them completely, if you live in an area with a lot of vehicular traffic and you need to eliminate the gases produced by traffic you need another type of purifier. In my particular case it has been an excellent purchase and if I recommend it, I am about to buy the second one for my children's bedroom."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this air purifier that I liked at first, it is really very quiet, only after using it for only 2 months it already tells me to change the filter. Because? You're supposed to change it after 6 months...and we only use it at night...really disappointing..."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this as we have pets and I have asthma and I am allergic to dust, spores, scents e.g. It came very carefully wrapped from the boxing of the product to the individual filters all in protective packaging. I turned it on and straight away it detected cooking smells and on Auto it started up and turned itself off when air went from red to blue. For those saying it doesnt work … did you take all the wrapping off the filters? Its a modern design and fits nicely against a wall. The air felt so much fresher this morning ( we live near to the sea so home has a sort of beach hut smell generally and close by trees blow pollen in)  It clearly removes spores as I didnt have my usual sneezing fit this morning having left it on auto over night."
    },
    {
        "review": "Opened the box a and followed all the instructions to remove packaging etc but it never worked. After switching on the power butter the speed buttons flash and then I’m not able to click on anything else. It doesn’t turn on at all. And very unhelpful customer service so have not been able to return the item!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I wasn’t sure how much of a difference such a small air purifier would make, but I have to say, I’m really impressed with this one. It does exactly what I wanted it to do, and I’ve been very happy with it.First of all, it’s really quiet. That was important to me because I didn’t want something that sounded like a fan running all day and night. I can have this going while I’m working, watching TV, or sleeping and barely notice it.It’s also the perfect size. It doesn’t take up much room at all, but it still feels like it’s doing a great job keeping the air fresher. I love that I can just put it on a nightstand, desk, or dresser and pretty much forget it’s there.The controls are super simple, and having three different fan speeds is nice depending on how much airflow I want. I also really like the aromatherapy feature. Adding a little essential oil is such a nice touch and makes the room smell fresh and relaxing.Another thing I appreciate is that it doesn’t feel cheap or flimsy. It has a nice clean design, works exactly like it should, and there really isn’t anything complicated about using it.For me, this is one of those purchases where I thought, \"why didn’t I get one of these sooner?\". If you’re looking for a small air purifier for your bedroom, office, or another smaller space, I would definitely recommend this one.It’s quiet, easy to use, doesn’t take up much space, and does exactly what it says it will do.Very happy with my purchase. Definitely 5 stars!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really happy with this little air purifier. It’s compact enough to sit on a nightstand or dresser without taking up much space, and it runs quietly, especially at night. I’ve noticed the room smells fresher and there seems to be less dust floating around. Simple to use and works well for a smaller room."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this air purifier for my bedroom. My dog has a very severe dust mite allergy. He was literally disintegrating. His hair was falling out and his dandruff was like a blizzard. He had full body yeast and it smelled like a dirty gym sock on steroids.Despite having no carpet, rugs and bedding that are washed weekly, and dust mite covers on both of our beds, he was still miserable.  He is so allergic that out of desperation I'm trying everything I possibly can to minimize his exposure while his immunotherapy does its job.The vet said that short of having hospital level air purification I would never get rid of all the dust mites, but I can limit his exposure with air purifiers, so we are giving it a try. There's no way I can accurately gauge how much this air purifier is reducing the dust mites, but it has to be better than it was before I got it.My dog gets 3 medicated baths a week and is about to start immunotherapy, so I can't really credit any progress to the air purifier alone, but there is no doubt it will help reduce the total number of dust mites he is exposed to.I also got a larger air purifier for my living room/kitchen. I live in a camper currently as I recently moved and am building a home. Since we live in cramped quarters with less ventilation than a sticks and bricks home, the dust mites and other allergens are far more concentrated.I've noticed since having these two purifiers running that our home smells fresher and cleaner, any smells do not linger. I've tried my hardest to deep clean any dust collected around the house in all the little nooks and crannies that you can't see and hopefully the purifiers will help keep that to a minimum. For some reason even in the dead of winter we seem to have a lot of dust. Again, probably because the space is so small. It seems the smaller the space, the bigger the mess! Thankfully it doesn't take as long to clean a smaller space.I'm not sure if I'll ever really know how effective these are, but I can say I've noticed a big difference since I got them in the quality of the air. We have wood heat so there's not a furnace constantly blowing air around. They provide air flow in what used to be pretty stagnant areas in the winter when the a/c isn't running.The stinky sock yeasty dog smell has been reduced quite a bit, and any other lingering smells like cooking or flatulence from my gassy teenager don't tend to hang around as long lol. So they have been a win-win! They seem to work very well.I don't use the timer features because I let them both run 24/7, but it's nice to have that as an option if it's ever needed. I really appreciate the small footprint of this purifier because there's not much room in a camper. I have it on my bedside table. You can see in the picture about how big it is next to my 40oz swig.Even on high it's very quiet, but I'm one of those \"can't sleep without a fan\" people so I enjoy the sound lol. Between this and the fan at the foot of my bed pushing air towards it, our air in the bedroom ought to be squeaky clean!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Seems to do what its designed to do - suck air in the sides, filter out dust etc. and blow the clean air out the top. Good airflow and three speeds. Quiet operation. We use it in a 10x10 closet to keep dust down. But I think it'd be quiet enough in a bedroom too. Comes with a plug-in transformer and a 5 foot cord which powers the unit. Very low wattage, so you can leave it run continuously. the filter can be easily cleaned out every month, and could be replaced if needed. Nice looking well-made unit. Recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m really happy with this air purifier. It’s compact, simple, and looks nice in the room without taking up much space. I’ve been using it in the bedroom and I like how quiet it is, especially at night. The air feels fresher, and I also like that it’s very easy to use."
    },
    {
        "review": "The air purifier gives me peace of mind as the air quality index numbers are rising.  My best friend,  my pup, is very sensitive to the particulates from the Canadian widfire smoke.  This levoit has change the air in my bedroom. And my pup is clearly no longer suffering.  The bedroom sanctuary is purified. Thank you!  Also, quiet and takes up very little space.  Just make sure you don't stack things next to it so the air flows and the machine can do its job."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve had this air purifier for about a year now, and it has worked great. Even with a newborn in the house, it gives us extra peace of mind knowing we can keep the air feeling fresh and clean. It’s been reliable, quiet, and easy to use, and it’s held up really well over the past year. Definitely a great addition to our home!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Quiet white noise and clean air, reduces dust, perfect for smaller bedrooms. It does not control odors because it doesn’t have a carbon filter, for that you have to spend a lot more money. (We have two gassy frenchies and a cat with smelly poo. We got the Levoit Everest to control pet emissions)."
    },
    {
        "review": "The design, price, and effectiveness are perfect. This season too, I had a sudden outbreak and couldn't stop my runny nose and tears while I was sleeping, so I immediately bought this for my bedroom! I'm glad it was a time sale. It's very quiet. On the first day, it smelled like the inside of a new car, but on the second day it didn't bother me. I haven't had any symptoms since installing it."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's a great find❤️❤️❤️"
    },
    {
        "review": "Without power cord"
    },
    {
        "review": "Although the room is very clean, there are no windows and no air circulation so when I was there for a long time my head started to hurt a little due to smells like humidity or storage, but after having it for a few months it has been more comfortable to be in my room even with fewer allergies now, the difference was noticeable from the first day, the first few days I had it on speed 3 but now I almost always have it on speed 1, this one is clearly of good quality, because there are also some that claim to be air filters but do not have them. no type of certificate and they do not have the appropriate filtration system"
    },
    {
        "review": "It is small, so miracles cannot be expected, but if the manufacturer's instructions are respected by using it in rooms of adequate size, it works very well, and purifies the air correctly. Everything seems to be built with excellent quality: plastics, joints, fan motor etc... Even the filter seems to be well built and of higher quality than others in the same price range. It has a 3-speed adjustment of which only the maximum is noisy but not very annoying, in fact the intermediate speed is barely audible (equal to a breath) and never annoying even if you are nearby. At first speed it is practically impossible to hear anything and this is a HUGE advantage compared to other purifiers on the market in the same category. This speed is perfect for night sleep. No hum or noise. This, perhaps, I believe is also possible thanks to the direct current motor/fan, in fact the purifier is supplied with a small power supply which is found in the package. It also includes 3 \"felts\" for the diffusion of natural essences to be inserted in a special almost invisible side drawer. Overall therefore an excellent, compact purifier, with a good quality/price ratio and above all not very noisy and worth buying."
    }
