    {
        "review": "Review is for the 6 Quart Instant Pot Pro. I love this thing and plan to use it for every single thing that I can!Setup was easy and next to no effort other than cleaning out the pot to start. Thought I had to take the white rubber 'cap' off the red popup pressure indicator under the lid as it looked like some sort of cover but I did not try - thankfully. I tried the 3 cups of water test and let it run through 5 min. Everything worked fine and showed me what to expect! I highly recommend doing this.Made Red Beans to start and they came out great. I tried it on the Bean setting but it ran it for 20 min. Even with overnight soak it wasn't enough to be done but wow , they got soft already - would have taken an HOUR in the pot to get to this point! Ran another 20 min and the quick steam release let me check progress and the powerful nature of this PRO let me going again quickly! Even with all of the stopping, testing, checking, I still cooked the red beans faster than the pot!Finally the interface is simple and intuitive - did not even need the manual. The presets are just that and you can customize your times. It will flash BURN and freak out requiring to unplug - if anything goes wrong. Yes I tried to re-warm the beans the next night and - yeah don't do that if they're thick. Nice safety feature because you can't exactly SEE what's going on in the pot with the lid on under pressure! Also it's heavy and seems durable. The rubber handles for the pot - love love love!"
