        "review": "I’ve been using this Instant Pot Pro for over 4 months, and it has become one of the most useful appliances in my kitchen. The 6-quart size is perfect for a family of four — enough space for stews, soups, and batch cooking, but not too bulky on the counter.Cooking results:• Pork and beef come out incredibly tender — the meat literally falls apart.• Potatoes with meat turn out soft and perfectly cooked.• Homemade beef stew cooks in about 30 minutes, which still surprises me.• I also made beef “tushonka” and it turned out excellent.• I tried making pilaf once — the rice overcooked and the bottom browned slightly, so this recipe needs some adjusting.Ease of use:• Very simple controls, intuitive interface.• I really like that the exterior has no physical buttons — it makes wiping the surface quick and easy.• The inner pot handled the dishwasher perfectly.What could be improved:• The lid is not very convenient to wash, especially around the silicone parts.• An extra sealing ring is included, but it doesn’t completely prevent the pot from absorbing strong smells from previous dishes (paprika, curry, etc.). I haven’t tested sweet or dairy recipes yet because of this — I’m sure the aroma would transfer.• The steam release is very hot and can splash, so you need to stand back when depressurizing.Overall, it’s a great appliance that saves a lot of time and consistently delivers delicious results. I rate it 4 stars, mainly because of the lid cleaning and lingering smells, but I’m still very satisfied with how well it cooks."
