    {
        "review": "I’m really happy with this Cosori 6QT pressure cooker. It has made cooking much easier, especially on busy days. I love that it can do different functions in one appliance, so it saves space in my kitchen.The size is perfect for my family, it’s easy to use, and the food comes out tender and full of flavor. I’ve made different meals with it and the results have been great. The cleanup is also simple.I like the quality and how convenient it is for everyday cooking. It’s definitely a useful appliance to have, and I would recommend it to anyone looking for a good multi-use pressure cooker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really happy with this pressure cooker! It’s super easy to use and cooks food much faster than I expected. The 9-in-1 functions are very useful, especially rice, slow cook, and sauté. It feels solid and safe, and the inner pot is easy to clean. Perfect size for my family and great value for the price!"
    },
    {
        "review": "First experience with a 9 in 1 ever, and I love it! This 6 QT appliance is a dinner saver when one has no time or not enough for a meal preparation. It is very easy to use, very intuitive, and there are plenty of recipes on the net. I have made already a lot of soups, stews, and brown basmati rice cooking (20 min).The last dish was a mongolian chicken in the pressure cooker for 5 min high pressure (no keep warm function) with 10 min NPR (letting sit the presdure cooker to release the steam \"naturally\"). I love its big capacity when I make soup or goulash, etc. The 9 in 1 means it this appliance can replace 9 of them:pressure cook, rice cooker, steamer, sterilizer, sous-vide, slow-cooker, instant cooker, yogurt maker and chauffe-assiettes. One can saute the ingredients first. Very easy to use, and it is also a big space saver on the counter. Presets include porridge, oat, stew/broth, ferment (if you make surdough bread)...To be honest, it is the first appliance I enjoy washing. No risks of elbow grease wasted thanks to the ceramic pot. I wash by hand though.For the price it costs, one should buy it, even I f like me, you have always felt a bit scared by pressure cooker. This one is electric and safe. If something wrong, it stops. The Seal/Vent button is away from the steam release valve so no risk to burn your fingers when releasing the steam which is angled released to prevent burns. That being said, always be vigileant, never open the lid of a pressure cooker full of steam without activating the steam release button!!! The included booklet must be read before use, it is great for instructions, recipes and safety.Great appliance, functionality and price! Do not hesitate, it is a steam steal!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m not one for giving 5 stars but this multi cooker is a very versatile little unit that turns out perfect every time and complements every kitchen space. All its functions including my favourite the slow cooking turns out brilliant every time. Very easy to operate, the built, locking arrangement and looks feels and gives a sense of security and durability. The pressure cooking function when compared to traditional cookers is way much better and faster without the constant lost any steam during the cooking process, IT IS STEAM FREE - that is energy efficiency if you ask me, and best of all I never had food drying out or burnt and the cleanup is always easy. I don’t regret making this purchase and you wouldn’t either."
    },
