[
    {
        "review": "Honestly, I was a bit worried because of the analysis of price vs features vs brand.  I was mostly satisfied with my previous one of a \"big brand,\" but my wife was not happy because it did not come with a metal insert.  And, of course, we all have our prejudices - and I have a wife with a crapload of those!Well, she went on a trip, and I had no cricket on my shoulder... so I took a chance!  he-he-he-he!!  (drumroll, please!)It honestly SEEMS a bit pricey, I will not deny that.  YET, when comparing features, its HUGE capacity, the \"stainless steel insert,\" it came very much cheaper than the main-brand ones.  Now, I am honestly not sure if it is stainless steel.  However, I have had this now for...  let me do math here...  the root square of...  add the cosene...  and dividied by Saturn's PI...  IDK...  2 months?  I am super impressed!I generally use it for rice.  but not just boring white rice.  I make rice with beans, rice with meat, sticky rice, basmati rice...  and I recently used the pressure-cooking feature.  It works just as, or better than, advertised!Only features that that are slightly annoying is that you have to press the one button a bunch of times until you get to the  function you desire, and that I still have not figured out how to change the time once I engage the function.  To be fair, for the latter, I have not opened the instructions manual (of course, I am a guy!), but I honestly have not needed it - it was mostly a curiosity.  I will just let the wife figure it out in...  4 weeks, when the peace is over in the house!  Sigh...Caution:  DO NOT leave it unattended.  IT WILL overcook your items!  Because of the metal insert, it conducts heat very well!  Its warming option is very, VERY effective.  Honestly, just shut it down and leave the lid closed if you want to keep the food warm for another hour or so, then reheat it as necessary.  You will also save on power.Lastly, something that never quite fit with the previous electric cooker we had.  I had obtained a third-party silicone cover/lid for it, and it never quite fit.  It FITS PERFECTLY for this!  I wish I remembered where the heck I got it, but it is great now, whereas it was just meh back then.Something I wish it had was a way to easily lift the insert while it was still hot.  I happen to have some hook-like thingys that easily attach to the insert sides, but I wish they came with it.  But that is it.  I love this!Anyway, GREAT purchase.  Obviously, I have used it quite enough."
    },
