    {
        "review": "I do not recommend this pressure cooker to anyone. Buying it was a big mistake, and I regret spending money on it.The baking function is terrible. No matter what I tried, cakes and other baked food always came out undercooked in the middle. Rice and other grains also cook poorly and often do not turn out properly. The only thing it does reasonably well is make soup.The biggest problem is the lid. It is very heavy and difficult to close correctly. We used this cooker for only a few months. One day we closed the lid, and now it is completely stuck. It will not turn or open no matter what we do. This is unacceptable for a product like this.I am very disappointed with this purchase and would never buy this product again. I hope my review helps others avoid making the same mistake."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my first pressure cooker. I researched many models and I love the capacity of this one. I was looking for something that would meal prep my favorite chili recipe with minimal cooking odor in my home. I have only made one batch so far but it turned out wonderful- just as good as in the CrockPot for seven hours. This unit took about 45 minutes. Total GAME CHANGER in the cooking odor dept. No more leftover onion smell throughout my home and the clothing that was in my closet.I love it and I am keeping it because I can’t wait to try it with other foods and experiment more.I give this unit four stars because the user manual is lackluster for a first time pressure cooker. It is also very hard to understand, the English language in it is not properly written. There are many misspelled words. Some of it doesn’t make sense at all. I managed to do some research and testing on my own and I ended up loving this unit.If I hadn’t had a lot of patience, I probably would have returned this item considering the instruction manual. However, with all the other great reviews, I had to give it my best shot and I’m so glad I did."
