        "review": "I read like 4 hours of reviews.  Spend more now less money at the dentist?  I dont think a more expensive electric toothbrush necessarily means better.  I have had exactly 3 electric toothbrushes in my life. One lasted me 10 years (they dont make it any more) and one made it 6 months (trash that rhymes with Noral Cee).  I decided to get this one based on reviews and price - I have had it for over 6 months now and I have to say, this is the best one I have had so far. Love it. Dont hesitate, get it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Sonicare 5900 Series toothbrush delivers an impressively powerful clean—so powerful, in fact, that I had to completely adjust my brushing style. My previous brush was much gentler, and with this one, if I’m not careful, it will fling toothpaste everywhere. Even after adapting, it still tends to get messy, and the brush head ends up covered in toothpaste after each use. I also need to watch and make sure i don't touch my lips with the toothbrush at all as the sensations can be a bit overwhelming sometimes.The pacing is also different from what I’m used to. My old brush gave 30‑second quadrant reminders, while this one bumps every 20 seconds. It’s not bad, just a change in rhythm. What I don’t love is that it shuts off automatically at the 2‑minute mark. It’s easy enough to turn back on, but I preferred being able to go a bit longer without interruption.One thing worth noting: the product image showing water spraying looks a bit misleading. In real use, the power is definitely there, but not in the way the marketing photo suggests.Despite these quirks, the cleaning performance is excellent. If you want a strong, effective brush and don’t mind adjusting your technique, this one does a very good job. I would say that you are getting your money's worth with this overall. As the clean is most likely a step up for most people.Here is how I rate items:5 stars – Exceptional, above expectations4 stars – Very good, meets expectations with minor issues3 stars – Acceptable, but with notable drawbacks2 stars – Poor, significant issues1 star – Unusable or fundamentally flawed"
