        "review": "This is a US product and has a US plug - you are expected to provide a plug adapter - should not be allowed to sell in Singapore"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using it for 3 days, the teeth are very clean, if something negative happens I will return to update this opinion. But so far I am very comfortable with this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent, arrived in excellent condition and exactly as described"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I've been using the Philips Sonicare DiamondClean 9500 for a while now, and I really like how clean it makes my teeth feel. It comes with three different brush heads, which is nice because I can switch depending on what I need. I've definitely noticed it removes more plaque than my old manual toothbrush.The design is sleek and feels comfortable in my hand. After using it, my teeth feel fresher and smoother, and I feel like my oral hygiene has improved. If you're looking for a reliable electric toothbrush that actually works, this one is worth trying."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have owned a few electric toothbrush over the years and prefer the Philips Sonicare. The 9500 was more expensive but it is a very high quality electric toothbrush with a lot of useful features I really like. It feels great in my hand and cleans better than my previous Sonicare. It can use the old style toothbrushes or the new ones. I was planning on using the 8 or so old toothbrushes I have. But after trying the new toothbrushes. I’ll stick with them. They are nice and soft and clean better. Yes they are a lot more expensive but I think they are worth it. If you are looking for a high end high quality Sonicare electric toothbrush this is definitely it !"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this toothbrush!!! There are so many settings you can’t go wrong. There is even a tongue clean setting. The battery life of great. I only charge maybe once every three weeks. The power can be more or less powerful and adjusted to your preference. There is even a pressure sensor that lights the bottom of the toothbrush if you are brushing too hard. This makes for a comfortable brush, and prevents you from encountering gum recession by brushing too hard."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the toothbrush however they aren’t made to last more then a year or two if your lucky. This is my third purchase of the same item, and has thankfully come down in price. All three times it’s been the same issue that destroys the toothbrush, a white gasket at the top of the toothbrush. I would remove the brush and dry the gasket clean after brushing and remove any toothpaste that surrounds the area. I like the light at the bottom of the brush which activates if I’m pushing too hard. As seen in the pictures, water got in and corroded the battery and the bottom light.This will be my last purchase, the quality build is poor and a well known issue with customer service and countless reviews I’ve read.  I have three packs of replacement brushes which are expensive and can’t be returned. I like the features the brush has and cleans my teeth very good and has a great gum care setting. The brush itself is super loud, and  annoying, I can tolerate it, but for whatever reason my wife always asks me a question while brushing, and it can be challenging to hear, (note)  I’m not hard or hearing, or while trying to listen to a video on my phone.  For 200.00 on Amazon, it’s also a high price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely love this toothbrush!Our dentist recommended we use Phillips Sonicare brushes and at first I was a bit skeptical.  I order this about 1 year ago and waited to see how much I liked it before writing a review.After using it for a year, I'm not sure why I never checked one of these out before.Ergonomically, the base of the unit fits well in my hand and is easy to maneuver.  The buttons are placed in great positions so I can change the brushing modes or intensity levels easily on the fly.I keep it on a shelf mounted in the battery charger at home, but I have travelled with it a few times and the battery holds a good charge for more than a few days easily.  I've never had a situation where I've taken it with me and had it run out of battery.It cleans very nicely and isn't too bulky to have any issue reaching the back molars and has great maneuverability while brushing.I like the fact that it's not very loud as far as noise, and it has convenient 30 second notifications to let you know how long you've been brushing.  I typically do one quadrant for 30 seconds for a total of 2 minutes, so it's nice to have the 30 second 'buzz' go off and let me know it's time to move.Two of the coolest features about this electronic toothbrush:  (1) - the pressure sensor that let's you know if you're brushing too hard.  It's easy to see the light come on when I tend to put too much pressure on the head.  (2) I use it in the shower so it's nice that it's mainly waterproof (even if it's not sold as that in the description) but I have been using it in the shower for a while and it's not had any issues.The travel case is nice to have when you need to pack it up and head out on the road.  I stay away from home about 4-5 times a year for work and it packs up really nicely and the case obviously keeps it protected.If I had one complaint it would be the unit cost and the replacement head cost.  When I first looked them up, I thought the price was crazy!!  But it's held up and continues to be my favorite toothbrush of my life, and I've had many in my 50 years on this planet.If you're thinking about getting an electronic toothbrush, this one definitely delivers."
    },
    {
        "review": "I used OralB for years, but it just wasn't cleaning anymore. The Sonicare is MUCH better. I was shocked. I did buy a softer Sonicare brush head, as my gums couldn't take the brushes that came with the toothbrush. So far, it's working great."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am writing this review for two reasons.First, if you're undecided about which version to get, I would recommend **not** getting this one. Even though I think it's a great toothbrush, I don't think it's worth the higher price unless you specifically care about the glass charging base.Second, the app is basically a guided visual tutorial rather than something that actually tracks your brushing in a meaningful way. It tells you where to brush, asks for your input, and then creates an oral health log based on what you tell it. There's nothing particularly smart or automatic about it.I can see myself using the app for the first week and then completely forgetting it exists. The cheaper version will give you essentially the same brushing experience, just without the app.That said, the toothbrush itself is excellent. The build quality is great, it feels great to use, and the brand's quality is undeniable. If I hadn't already tested this model, I would return it and buy the cheaper version of the same toothbrush instead. I'm just having a hard time justifying the higher price for what is essentially a faster vibration and a glass charging base."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great product at a great prime day price.Make sure you register it because these have a tendency to break at the base of the tooth brush applicator. My last two did exactly that, after a couple years.That said- my gums and teeth are so much better and cleaner because of these.I will continue to buy them."
    },
