[
    {
        "review": "I always forget to write reviews after I buy stuff on Amazon. I should try to do it more because it is helpful when you find a review that is real.So, I bought this toothbrush to replace another brand that I bought about a year and a half ago. The old toothbrush just wasn't doing a good job at cleaning my teeth. I have always had problems with cavities and plaque build-up. The only sure-fire way of getting all of the plaque for me was to use Plax prior to brushing. Still, I find myself in the dentist's office every six months with a hygienist jack-hammering my mouth with water pick to get my teeth clean. It's embarrassing and it makes me feel anxious about my gum health. I saw the Oral-B iO Series 3 here on Amazon and it was discounted. According to Oral-B it is really good at getting rid of plaque. I took the manufacturer at their word, and bought it. Holy crap, ya'll! This thing is amazing!The iO3 has a round brush head similar to the polishing tool your dental hygienist uses. I've used cheaper Oral-B electric toothbrushes that also have round heads, but they weren't as robust as the brush head on the iO3. The bristles aren't hard, but they are dense and arranged in a way that they can hug your teeth while brushing. You can get that brush on every surface of each tooth (except directly between the teeth, of course). The motorized handle has a pressure sensor that changes color based on how hard or soft you are pressing. If you get it just right, it lights up green.The iO3 also helps you time your brushing so that you the recommended two minutes. It pulses when it's time to change to a different quadrant. It doesn't automatically shut off when the two minutes are up, however. That's fine with me as I will just continue brushing other parts of my mouth like my tongue and the roof of my palette when I'm done with my teeth.There are supposedly three types of brushing settings to choose from, but I have only used the default cleaning setting. The other two setting are supposed to be for sensitive teeth and whitening. The default works just fine for me.The build is solid and feels good in my hands. I like that the handle comes with two brush heads, a travel case, and case for the brush heads. I like to take my brush head off and put it in the case after I'm finished just because I'm paranoid about having a toothbrush exposed in the bathroom. It's nice to have the option to shield it from germs.So, TLDR, this is a great electric toothbrush. My teeth haven't felt this clean since the last time I went to the dentist. Oral-B did a fantastic job of designing a product that makes brushing easy and will almost certainly result in you having a positive visit at the dentist, and may help reverse gum issues and prevent cavities. I definitely recommend you buy this product if you are in the market for an electric toothbrush."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is great!  Does a phenomenal job cleaning teeth and sensors work great as well.  Wish I'd have purchased it long time ago.  Was recommended by my dentist.  Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I recently upgraded from my old Oral-B Pro 100 to the Oral-B iO Series 3, and I can definitely tell the difference. The brushing experience feels much smoother and quieter, and my teeth feel noticeably cleaner after each use.One of my favorite improvements is the pressure sensor. It helps me avoid brushing too hard, which is something my old toothbrush didn't have. I also like the different cleaning modes they're simple to switch between and let me choose what feels best.The brush head glides comfortably over my teeth, and the handle feels solid and well-made. Battery life has also been great so far, lasting several days before needing a recharge.If you're still using an older Oral-B model like the Pro 100 and have been thinking about upgrading, I think the iO Series 3 is well worth it. It feels like a much more refined brushing experience, and I'm really happy with the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Oral-B iO Series 3 for a few weeks now, and the difference compared to a standard electric or manual toothbrush is night and day. It leaves your teeth feeling amazingly smooth, like you just stepped out of a dental cleaning.​What makes it great:​Unreal Cleaning Power: The round micro-vibrating brush head gets into every spot with zero effort. My teeth have never felt cleaner or fresher.​Smart Pressure Sensor: This is probably the best feature. The light indicator shows green when you're using the right amount of pressure, red if you're pressing too hard, and white if you're too soft. It takes all the guesswork out of brushing and protects your gums.​Built-in Timer & Modes: The built-in 2-minute timer pulses every 30 seconds to let you know when to switch quadrants, making it super easy to ensure a complete clean every single time.​Solid Battery Life: Holds a charge really well for daily morning and night use, and the charging base takes up very little counter space.​If you’re thinking about upgrading your oral care routine, this toothbrush is worth every penny. Highly recommended!"
