[
    {
        "review": "Takes a little while to get used to but it works great and you will use less toothpaste! Only had it a month but so far so good! Real makes your month feel clean!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been told by dentists for years that I should be using an electric toothbrush, but I have VERY sensitive teeth, and every time I used one it sent me through the roof! Well, a couple tooth cracks later and I decided to suck it up and try again. I bought this one because it has a lot of settings, including one for very sensitive teeth.Out of the box it was sleek and solid, and the display was easy to use and intuitive. It did take some getting used to, and I used it with warm water, but it did not hurt, which was thrilling for me! Now, several months later, I can say that I love this toothbrush and that it genuinely cleans my teeth really well!I am not one for pairing things with apps or my phone, so I can't comment on that side of the toothbrush, but it does have a pressure sensor that lights up red or green to let you know if you are bruising too hard or too lightly as you go.The battery lasts a long time, as do the heads, and it comes with a travel case as a bonus. Two thumbs up!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Oral-B iO5 series toothbrush is an exceptional product, renowned for its durability and quality construction. The toothbrush’s plastic components are robust, ensuring longevity and reliability. The entire unit is designed to withstand rigorous use, embodying the latest advancements in dental technology.One of the standout features of the iO5 series is its Bluetooth connectivity. This innovative feature allows users to sync their toothbrush with their smartphone, enabling them to track their brushing habits and receive personalized recommendations. The toothbrush also includes a range of essential features, such as pressure sensors and timers, to ensure optimal oral hygiene.Notably, the iO5 series is manufactured in Germany, as indicated on the packaging and the toothbrush itself. This commitment to German craftsmanship sets it apart from other brands, such as Philips, which is known for producing inferior products made in Vietnam. In contrast, the iO5 series has proven to be a reliable and effective replacement for my previous Philips toothbrush, which required frequent replacements due to its poor quality.Even my dentist recommended the iO5 series, further solidifying its reputation as a superior dental product. MADE IN GERMANY 🇩🇪"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this toothbrush, but it is important to know that it is extremely fragile. I accidentally dropped it in my sink (max approximately 1-2ft drop into a ceramic basin) and it broke immediately, meaning that it simply stopped working and wouldn't activate even though it was fully charged. Again this is a great toothbrush with great cleaning properties, but for the price it is extremely fragile and should be more robustly constructed. Very disappointing, but sadly as it is still one of the better electric toothbrushes on the market I had to buy a replacement. If that doesn't deter you, then go ahead and get it. It has great power and a reliable pressure sensor to help you from pressing too hard. Works great at keeping teeth white than a manual toothbrush. My dentist always comments that oral hygiene benefits from electric toothbrushes. If you have sensitive gums, I recommend buying the sensitive brush heads as they clean just as well but without as much damage. Oral b makes good gum sensitive replacement brushes but they are sold separately. The electrical component (the part you hold that the brush heads attach to) is a bit heavy but that's where the technology is right now. Battery life is okay, not great but if you charge regularly then you won't have an issue. Brush head size is good for adults but might be too large for children. I hope this review helps you make a decision that best works for your dental needs."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had the IO3 and that was really good but this one is even better. This one is so much stronger vibration wise. It also comes with an app with is really neat. I genuinely have never gotten a clean as good as I do with this oral B series. Hopefully this one doesn’t break when I drop it into my sink like the IO3 did.."
    },
    {
        "review": "ABSOLUTELY love this toothbrush, have always use the Phillips sonic and nothing is wrong with them!! But went to California for my 70th Bday/family reunion and purchased 2 battery operated Oral-B brushes for the wife and I. The first thing was the smaller brush head, and although it nothing like the iO I enjoyed being able to get to harder to reach areas without having to dislocate my jaws!! And soooo much more powerful (Phillips 3yrs old), but enjoy all the new features. Although I am having trouble downloading the brush app on my phone. Which was a selling feature I was looking forward too! The sale price was nice too as they are quit pricy, but planning on purchasing one for my wife's birthday next month.. I used my bday amazon cards for mine 😁"
    },
    {
        "review": "We had the oral B and thought we were getting great brushing.  Saw the ad in dentist office for the io.  We got TWO.  Price wise the 5 was more tgan needed!!  Started using them.  sufe and I agree that it enhances our brushing!! Both of us to our comfort level AND indicates our brushing level and time!  GREAT"
    },
    {
        "review": "I had the old style Oral-B before and was ready for a new toothbrush. The IO5 was on sale so I bought it. I didn't think I'd use the app at all but it turns out that the gamification of my oral hygiene is a positive for me. I brush longer and use the guided brushing to make sure I'm getting full coverage. The only thing is that the zone identification is sketchy. On almost every brushing, it indicates the wrong active area of my teeth. I've tried Oral-B's recommendations- stand straight, do each tooth one at a time, move to different segments, repeat on inside and bite surfaces- but it still misdetects zones. What that does is make me brush even longer, so not terrible, but better accuracy would be much better and, frankly, I expected much better. Occasional it totally glitches and I need to restart the app and the brush. I also thought the battery would lastonger but it's about the same as my OG Oral-B electric that was around $40. Note that I am probably brushing longer, so maybe the battery is a little better but I hoped for 3 weeks and I'm getting less than 2 between charges. I still like the brush, but just know the app guidance doesn't work as well as you'd think. I do like that it reminds you to floss, brush your tongue, and use a mouth rinse. It also gives you a score for each session and a running score, which I like even though I thought I'd never use that.  In summary, it works well and my dentist noticed a difference and told me to keep it up. It is a bit expensive for an electric toothbrush, so I hope it lasts a long time."
