[
    {
        "review": "Decided it was time to switch the family back to a electric toothbrush rather then standard brush. With a wife and two kids (12 & 9yrs) the price of the big box brands is hefty. So we decided to try these out because of the value they seemed to bring for the price including so many brush heads. We selected four different colors to be able to distinguish which one as ours.The brushes come with plenty of brush heads, these could last us awhile for sure. After a few weeks of use on the first brush head they seem to be lasting quit well to the daily use. Each brush head came in its own small sealed packing to keep it protected. Only thing I wish was if each bag was labeled with what type of brush head it was, as the product comes with 2 styles.These are rechargeable and they come with their own charging cable (DC style plug not USB) When they arrived I plugged all 4 of the brushes in to fully charge them. After 2 weeks of usage they are still on the original charge and showing no signs of slowing down. I plan to throw all 4 of them back on the charger again this week to keep them all topped of. See if I can get a routine going where I charge the whole families all at once.In regards to the most important part, how does it brush? Fantastic, honestly leaves my mouth feeling way more clean then a standard toothbrush. Allow the brush to do all the work, no need to go back and forth with a scrub. Just slowly work the brush around your mouth works wonders. It has a built in feature where it does a brief pause on the brushing to remind you to rotate to a different part of your mouth. While this feature doesn't really help a adult much because we understand time, for our two pre-teen kids its very helpful. They have mentioned it helps remind them with the foggy morning mind to move onto another area.Overall happy with the product for such a great price, will they last years? That I do not have the answer for, but if I can get 1 year out of them for the price I'll be very happy."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great deal! It comes with several, easy change heads that have different color stripes on them so we each can identify which brush head is ours. It came fully charged and lasted 3 weeks before I had to charge it up. For this price, you cannot beat it. Replacement brush heads appear to be available from several sellers here. Cleans WAY better than a manual toothbrush. I highly recommend this toothbrush"
    },
    {
        "review": "--edited May 19, 2026I'm updating my review because this really is a good value electric toothbrush, and the seller responded to my review and offered me a replacement or refund! I had already purchased another toothbrush from them, so they refunded me. I was not expecting that since it was outside the refund window. Great customer service!--original (3 stars)I bought this toothbrush on Oct 5, and really liked it! I had no problem with it, and it held a charge well.But yesterday it randomly would not turn on. I know it’s charged, it shows green when I plug it in. And the button cycles through the various settings when I press it…it just doesn’t activate. For the low price, I got 6 months worth of use out of it, so I’m not going to leave a totally negative review. But I think it should have lasted longer…I haven’t even used all of the heads that came with it yet. It should last at least 3 months per head that comes with it, which would be 24 months."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this toothbrush because I noticed, along the gumline it appeared like I was collecting gunk debris and also yellowing. A manual toothbrush was not giving me the reach I needed. I needed an electronic round brush, and I got this one because it comes with replacement heads and its budget friendly. I love this toothbrush because it has a powerful motor, firm bristles and after just one cleaning I had removed the buildup around my gumline particularly noticeable in the front.I have braces so I use this product at night, after flossing and a manual toothbrush in the morning.I only had one issue with this product which might not be much of a problem since it gets the job done pretty nicely but this brush doesn't spin 360 degrees. It moves very quickly side to side which I learned is what oscillating means. I misunderstood. Nevertheless, love this product and all its features."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've never bought into the hype of \"electric toothbrushes,\" but I thought I would give this relatively-cheap one I saw discounted on Amazon a shot. Mainly because it came with 10 replacement heads and if the batteries ever went kaput, I could just use it as a normal, albeit bulky, toothbrush. After using it every day over the last month, I have to say that I have rather mixed feelings about this rechargeable toothbrush (words I thought I would never say).First, the positives, and there are some to be found here. The battery life, in my experience, has actually been fairly good. Though, that could likely be attributed to how low-tech this tech toothbrush actually is (we'll get to that later.) The brush is lightweight as well, allowing you to maneuver it easily. The three vibrating modes do work and offer some variation for you to test and see which you like best. The brush also has an internal timer that briefly stops the vibration every 30 seconds, ultimately shutting off after 2 minutes. I personally found this to be annoying at first, but now kind of like knowing how long I've been targeting a specific area for. And finally, yes, you could use this as a \"manual\" toothbrush if your forgot to charge the battery. Keep in mind that the bristles are incredibly soft, so if you like your normal toothbrushes with some tensile strength, this one might not be for you.Now for the \"bad,\" or mediocre I guess I should say. The Teetheory toothbrush is little more than a vibrating wand with a brush attachment affixed to it. The bristles don't move, sweep, rotate, or oscillate like a more premium electric toothbrush would, so leave that fantasy behind now. Yes, the bristles do technically move, but that's just because of the vibrating motor that your brush head is on. The bristle movements are incredibly fine and gentle, to the point that you question if it's really doing any good at all. In terms of cleaning power, this is probably far from dentist-recommended.Also, if you have sensitive teeth, I wouldn't recommend this toothbrush. The vibration is all along the top portion of the brush, so if you even graze your teeth, you'll get a rather uncomfortable sensation. I personally don't have very sensitive teeth, but every time I've used this brush, I make the mistake of touching my teeth with the plastic, non-brush portion and it doesn't feel pleasant.Now, with a product like this, you have to take into account the price you're paying, which is significantly less than that of a premium electric toothbrush. I'm aware of and totally understand that. But judging this product on merit alone, I can't really say that I would wholeheartedly recommend it. Does it clean your teeth well enough? Yeah. Does it do it so well that I'll never use a normal toothbrush again? Not really. If you're truly gung-ho about dental care, would suggest spending the extra cash for a premium electric toothbrush. Specifically, one of the electric toothbrushes that actually spins. If you absolutely must have an electric toothbrush for cheap and you don't really mind it being low-tech, this will do you just fine, I suppose. As for myself, I will continue to use this brush for the foreseeable future, and hope to see if the reviews others have posted about the brush not working after a few charges are anomalies or something everyone should expect."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am the sole caregiver for my senior mother with late stage dementia. Brushing her teeth has been a challenge since she stopped brushing her own teeth, but oral health is important, especially with her eating issues. I wanted to have a relatively inexpensive toothbrush with replacement heads, as she does bite the toothbrush often while I am using it. This toothbrush has done well! I do need to change the heads more frequently due to her biting the bristles sometimes, but they actually hold up well to this mistreatment. I also like the typical smaller round head with the rotating motion. This is the same size as my Oral B electric brush.I have to say that I am impressed that the brush does still work after a few months of using it for her, as often asked as hard as she sometimes bites it. It’s not a malicious bite, nor done from discomfort, it is misfiring of her brain. This toothbrush is actually very gentle, and she does not have any bleeding gums with care.I want to add that I find other features helpful, as well. The brush has a short pause every 30 seconds, which helps cue me to switch to a different part of her mouth and ensure I am spending enough time on each quadrant. After 2 minutes, the brush will automatically turn off. There are different functions, but to use them, you have to push the power button multiple times, and it resets each time it stops. This does not bother me, as I do not use any but the main function.Charging the unit is easy. It comes only with a cord, not a block, but I had a spare hanging around and keep it with her brushing supplies. I did not time how long it took to charge, but I have charged it twice, once when I got it 1 July, and once again 18 September. It did not stop working, but as I use it once a day for at least the 2 minutes, I thought I should charge it after all that time, and I did.I would definitely recommend this product, especially as a great back up, or a brush that may be abused a bit while in use."
    },
    {
        "review": "I honestly didn’t realize how much cleaner an electric toothbrush would make my teeth feel compared to a traditional toothbrush until I started using this one. After brushing, my teeth feel way smoother and cleaner, almost like that fresh feeling you get after a dental cleaning.I’ve been using it twice a day for about a month now, and I still haven’t had to recharge it, which really surprised me. The battery life is honestly impressive.The brush itself is lightweight and comfortable to hold, and I like that it comes with multiple brush heads and different cleaning modes. The bristles are soft enough that they don’t irritate my gums, but it still feels powerful enough to clean really well.I also love the pink color—it’s really pretty in person. For the price, I think this is a really good value, especially if you’ve been wanting to switch from a regular toothbrush to an electric one without spending a fortune.Overall, I’m really happy with it and definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this so far. My old toothbrush just vibrated, however I don't think this one actually spins, it says it rotates but that's better than just vibrating... My mouth feels much cleaner. I know a couple people said it stops when you press harder (that's a safety on some toothbrushes) but I'm thinking they just brush too hard, I haven't had that problem and you shouldn't brush hard anyway. I think it's great for the price. It's just gonna take some time to get in the groove, I can't tell if I'm on the gumline cause of the vibration."
    },
    {
        "review": "Please note this product is not guaranteed!"
    },
    {
        "review": "value for money"
    },
    {
        "review": "The toothbrush self operates after turning it off.Used only for 2 months."
    },
    {
        "review": "Will purchase againBattery charge lasts a long timeVery strong leaves teeth feeling really clean and fresh"
    }
