[
    {
        "review": "The Oral B iO-10 is the best Oral B electric toothbrush I have used, and I have been using their products for years. I have a few sensitive teeth & areas of gum recession.  Oral B has designed a sensitive toothbrush head and this handle has a sensitive setting.  For the first time, I am consistently doing a better job using less pressure while brushing.  I like the feedback from the Oral B app on my iPhone. I use the app every time I brush. Over several weeks, my technique has become consistently using less pressure and I get great feedback from the app.  My teeth feel like I have just had my teeth cleaned by a hygienist and over the weeks of using this product I am not showing any build up of plaque, which  an improvement.My daughter needed a new electric toothbrush, so I gifted her an Oral B iO 7.  She let us know she loved it, it was such an improvement over her previous Oral B handle, which was pre the iO version.  When I decided to purchase a new handle for me, I did more research and discovered the iO 10.  It was expensive compared to the iO 7, but I have been very happy with this product.  I purchased the iO 9 for my husband.  I consider the handle a personal care product, so i purchase a handle for each of us.  The iO 9 seems to have the same features as the iO 10, and does cost significantly less.  We are each happy with these 3 different models of the iO handles.The iO tooth brush heads are expensive, but I like them.  The battery life goes down quickly, so I keep it charging. It has a tongue brushing mode, and several other settings to individualize the handle to your preferences.  It is important to read the instructions and rinse the handle & tooth brush head as directed.  I always rinse them, as directed by the Oral B directions, and have not had any build up dried toothpaste that a YouTube reviewer had a problem with.  Overall, this is the best electric toothbrush I have ever used.  I am very careful and consistent with oral care.  I enjoy using this product and my oral health has improved."
    },
    {
        "review": "When my trusty Sonicare toothbrush finally decided to retire after nearly twenty years of loyal service, I embarked on an epic quest to find a worthy successor. My Sonicare was so old it probably had memories of the Y2K scare, so it was about time. Enter the Oral-B iO Series 10, a toothbrush that’s so advanced I’m half expecting it to start giving me stock tips and weather forecasts.The Price Tag Dilemma:I’ll admit, the price tag gave me pause. For a moment, I wondered if I’d mistakenly wandered into the luxury goods section. I mean, I was searching for a toothbrush, not a second mortgage. But then I thought, \"Hey, you only live once, and I’d rather invest in dental hygiene than in future dental bills.\"Unboxing the Future:Unboxing this toothbrush felt like opening a gadget from a sci-fi movie. It’s sleek, shiny, and has more lights than my Christmas tree. The magnetic charger is so cool, it could double as a prop in a superhero film. I half expected it to come with a button labeled \"Launch\" instead of \"Power.\"Features That Make You Go ‘Wow’:The Oral-B iO Series 10 is packed with more features than my smartphone. It has an interactive color display that gives me feedback on my brushing technique—finally, an audience for my oral hygiene skills! It even offers multiple brushing modes, including Daily Clean and Gum Care, and I’m pretty sure there’s one that translates to \"You’re doing amazing, sweetie!\"The AI technology is like having a tiny dental coach cheering me on. It tracks my brushing pattern and offers helpful advice, probably more than I get from my therapist. It’s like having a buddy that’s really into your oral health.Brushing Experience:Using this toothbrush is like giving my teeth a VIP spa treatment. The micro-vibrations and oscillating technology make my mouth feel so clean, I’m pretty sure it could pass a military inspection. My teeth have never felt this pampered. The smart pressure sensor is a lifesaver, gently reminding me to ease up when I’m brushing like I’m trying to scrub away my middle school yearbook photo.The App Adventure:Of course, there’s an app—because why not? Syncing my toothbrush with my phone felt like introducing it to the Internet of Things. The app provides feedback and tracks my progress, acting like a personal trainer for my teeth, minus the motivational shouting. The 3D tracking is so precise, I’m convinced it’s secretly plotting my dental future.Battery Life and Cost Justification:The battery life is impressive, lasting up to two weeks on a single charge. This is perfect because I often forget to charge things until they’re as lifeless as my houseplants. As for the price, it’s steep, but think of it as an investment in oral health and a potential savings plan for avoiding future dental nightmares. Plus, it’s cheaper than therapy, and this toothbrush actually gives feedback!Final Verdict:In conclusion, the Oral-B iO Series 10 is more than just a toothbrush; it’s a technological marvel that makes brushing my teeth the highlight of my day. It’s a blend of futuristic features and everyday dental care that has transformed my oral hygiene routine into a daily adventure. If you’re ready to splurge on your dental future—and maybe show off a little at your next dentist appointment—this toothbrush is worth every penny. Just don’t be surprised if it starts offering you unsolicited advice on your life choices."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using electric tooth brushes since dirt was new.  This is the finest cleaning, quietest, with so many useful features that to me this is perfect for my needs.  Cleaning modes (speed) is selectable and after use my teeth feel and look great. I’m still in shock for having spent over $230 for this but it is indeed worth every penny.  Battery life is good.  It’s been dropped with no signs of being for the worse for hitting marble shower floor.  Found that I just can leave it on the magnetic charging all the time and I never worry about battery life. It has a hard case that came with mine that also serves as a charger using the supplied wall wart and cable.  Like all Oral B products it is exceptionally well made, designed and uses quality material.  I enjoy the display on the base which shows brushing time, mode and lets you know battery status.  Very ergonomic.  Though pricey, I do highly recommend this toothbrush and charging system.  Mine came with four brush heads and packaged well."
    },
    {
        "review": "Update #4 - 6 months later: it has continued to work, has been taken on several trips with no problems, still fun to use, and probably brushes better than I would without the feedback from the app.Update #3 - it has kept working fine for a month.  Amazing that it can track which of the 16 zone is being brushed, not nearly perfect but good enough.  The app on the phone is useful enough to keep using every days, kind of tricky to finish the side and top zones, still gamelike and engaging.  Back to 5 stars.Update #2 - emailed the company a few times. Finally got the reset button to work right after about 20 attempts, and it works again for now.  No secret trick, except the button doesn’t move. So I'm back to enthused about the unique capabilities of this toothbrush.Update #1 - Loved it for 5 days, as described below, but then the software quit working.  Somehow the unit is no longer connected to the phone app.  I've spent an hour so far searching YouTube videos and the instructions, making no progress.  The reset button at the back is the worst input device I've encountered in a long time, and all the instructions are complicated and unclear.  I'll modify this review if I ever get this $350 device back to working as it should.Cost is outrageous, but performance is great.  A gyroscope allows the toothbrush to know which of 16 zones is being brushed (top or bottom, inside or outside, left right or middle, and the tops of the back zones) to track whether each zone gets its share of time.  The graphic on the app on the phone (which I hold in the other hand) shows the progress.The ability to track history of brushing performance effectively gamifies the experience - I actually look forward to brushing at the moment.  In six years, it will probably get 2000 uses, so 20 cents is not so frivolous, and tooth and gum work prevented has some value."
    },
    {
        "review": "This toothbrush was a replacement purchase after my daughter took my original handle and left me with just the brush heads, so I needed to replace it. I’m honestly glad it happened because this one works so well and feels like a professional cleaning every single time I use it.The brushing experience is smooth, powerful, and very effective without being harsh. The visible pressure sensor is one of my favorite features because it helps protect my gums while still delivering a deep clean. The two-minute timer keeps me on track, and the multiple cleaning settings allow me to adjust based on how my teeth and gums feel on any given day.The connectivity is wonderful and adds to the overall experience. It makes brushing feel more intentional and polished, almost like having guidance built into your routine. Everything works seamlessly, and the toothbrush consistently delivers the same high-quality results every time.The design feels premium and well thought out, and the included replacement brush heads and charging travel case are a big bonus. It’s convenient for everyday use and travel, and nothing about it feels cheap or flimsy.Overall, this was an excellent replacement and exceeded my expectations. It performs extremely well, feels professional with every use, and has quickly become something I truly enjoy using. I would absolutely recommend it to anyone looking for a top-tier electric toothbrush that delivers consistent, high-quality results."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent toothbrush with beyond cutting edge technology. It's process has improved my dental hygiene. Worth every penny!When my wife tried mine, she had to have one for herself. So we did that. She absolutely loves it!The only downside I see is that it's not perfect in following where the toothbrush is going. But they are working on that and the last update improved it quite a bit. Still a little ways to go.I highly recommend this for anyone who cares about their dental hygiene and can afford the price.UPDATE:  I've had this now for about 6 months, and I do have one gripe. His biggest selling point is its ability to track your brushing and show you where your missing so that you can brush better. However this does not work well. If you watch it on the app or even on the stand, you can see that when you're brushing especially the bottom left side or the top right side of your teeth, it's contributing your brushing to the wrong segment of your teeth. And it's very difficult to get 100%. They really need to fix this! I still recommend it because I think it's a great toothbrush and really well made, but this is a major problem."
    },
    {
        "review": "So... Before this purchase my \"main driver\" was a 1000 series Oral B. They were always much more effective than a fully static/manual toothbrush.I needed a second brush and caught this on sale for $250. I'll say... This is worthy of being considered the Next Generation of Oral B brushes. Somehow they have taken the Sonicare vibrating concept and channeled it into rotation. This feels so much better than the old style and seems more effective. I use half as much toothpaste with it and I still have to spit early because of the foaming it creates.  I didn't realize the damage O must've been doing to my gums before... It feels like massage now.OK, beyond the basic brushing experience, the stand is neat. I simply like the timer the most, but they determine which section of your teeth you're brushing based on the orientation for the brush to help guide you... But really the timer is perhaps the most useful. Also, the base is so much better than the 1000 series - It's magnetic with no protrusion to loghtnio, and doesnt hold water or develope the associated crust.Things I don't like... Wish they would just use USB C. This would make traveling so much easier. I'll see if there is a 3rd party adapter perhaps.The travel case is kinda cheap. It's not easy or fulfilling to open. It works though.I don't care for the speckled \"star\" paint job... It looks like I've got toothpaste on it perpetually.Battery life is fine. It runs well throughout its duration. I might be able to get a week of brushing on a charge.The minor things aside, the brushing experience itself takes the chore to a whole new level. It's impressive they managed to incorporate hypersonic movement while keeping the rotating head."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is the top of the Oral-B IO line. If you are on a budget, look at those which are more affordable for you.  The pressure sensor, the visible timer, the LED's that show how much of the mouth has been done all lead to an excellent brushing but also one that is gentle on the gums.  These features help to organize and evenly distribute the brushing experience.  That matters if you have perio issues, which I do.  Avoiding periodontal surgery makes the price more appealing.  I have had the older \"Triumph series\" Oral-B which also had the brush time and progress indicator.  This is a huge step up and I wish I had purchased it sooner.  The one \"issue\" is that Oral-B provides a dedicated charger when they could have provided a USB cable instead - less to pack on a trip.  With the nice case,  this is the one issue I have with the overall design."
    },
    {
        "review": "It was worth the purchase even though it was"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using this brush for about 2 years now and my experience has been very positive. So far it has served me very well and continues to work as it should. What stands out the most is the functionality of the pressure sensor. The lights are very intuitive: white if you are lacking strength, green if the pressure is correct and red if you are overdoing it. What I really like is that when it turns red, the brush not only alerts you visually, but it slows down the vibration and movement automatically; This is great for protecting your enamel and gums. Honestly, I really like it because it doesn't require you to put in too much attention or effort. You can be a little lazy when brushing your teeth and still get a great result; All you have to do is slowly move the brush through the 4 quadrants of your mouth and the device takes care of the rest. Regarding the battery, it has naturally degraded a little with continuous use, something realistic that will happen with any electronic product. However, it hasn't gotten to the point of being a legitimate problem, especially if you don't travel much and keep it in its charging dock regularly. That being said, the product would be perfect if they allowed you to change the battery manually; This would solve the problem of degradation, help minimize e-waste and obviously allow the product to last many more years. It is an expensive product, very expensive for a toothbrush, but if you have the money to spare I say: buy it. It is a quality tool that you are going to use every day and it is not something that you are going to have to repurchase every 6 months or every year. Recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "This electric toothbrush is the best of the best. What makes it far superior to any other one on the market is that it assists you with your brushing technique, indicating as you brush which surfaces of your teeth you have covered or not fully covered so that you are sure not to miss any areas. It also tracks brushing time and measures the pressure so that you can know you are brushing each area of your mouth for the right of amount of time and using the proper pressure to remove any plaque (without overbrushing or brushing too aggressively either). It also keeps track of your brushing habits, and gives you a score after each brushing session. It has different modes with varying speeds : daily clean, intense clean, sensitive, emphasis on gums tongue cleaning, etc. You can set different short and long-term oral hygiene goals as well. The battery lasts a fairly decent amount of time, and since the charging base is wireless, it can stand elegantly on the vanity without having to deal with wires all over the place.Not only does it have all these awesome features, it will leave your mouth feeling impeccably clean and fresh. As someone who has super tight teeth, I can say that I'm amazed by how well it eliminates plaque and prevents tartar from building. My dentist even told me that my dental hygiene improved and asked what I was doing differently! It's only thanks to this toothbrush!Seriously worth EVERY penny."
    },
    {
        "review": "I never liked a single electric toothbrush. My husband has always had one and I couldn't stand the sound or the feel of it and how it would leave my hand vibrating long after I brushed my teeth. I also hate brushing my teeth so I always dread it and sometimes skip it. This toothbrush makes my teeth feel so clean, like after a cleaning. And the vibration isn't too strong to bother my hand and sound isn't too loud either. It has many modes, so I'd suggest the extra sensitive first. The app also tracks your brushing so it motivates me to stay consistent. If you don't want to use the app, the stand it comes with that also shows the clock, will show you the parts of your mouth that you've cleaned and how long you cleaned for. I'll never go back to manual!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The only problem was the device manual which was printed in English and French."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This great quality toothbrush works perfect. I read the few negative reviews but have had no problem so far with it. It does an amazing job cleaning my teeth. Very strong motor. Actually my gums were a little sensitive at first because of the strong cleaning power. I am delighted with my purchase, & recommend it to others. I would buy again."
