        "review": "I tried the Oral-B Pro 100 3D White toothbrush, and while it’s simple and easy to use, the overall performance is pretty underwhelming. It runs on regular AA batteries, which makes it convenient, but you can definitely feel the difference compared to rechargeable models.The round brush head is nice and does a decent job cleaning tooth by tooth, and it’s compatible with other Oral-B heads, which is a plus. It also has a built-in timer to help with brushing time, so the basics are there.That said, the power is where it falls short. It feels weak, especially if you’re used to stronger electric toothbrushes. It gets the job done at a basic level, but it doesn’t give that deep clean feeling you might expect. Even reviews describe it as more of a “basic” option rather than a high-performance one.Overall, it’s fine as an entry-level or travel toothbrush, but if you’re looking for something with real power and a stronger clean, this probably won’t be enough."
