    },
    {
        "review": "Short summary - looks good, excellent battery life, cleans better than any of my previous toothbrushes.It comes with - a travel case; 8 replaceable brush heads;  the electric tooth brush ; a wireless charging stand with a usb-A connectorIt does not come with a usb power supply,It cleans very well. I occasionally get a build up of hard plaque or tartar on a back molar - this is the only brush I have owned able to remove it, even if it takes 2-3 days of brushing.It has two buttons. The first controls the 5 modes, clean, sensitive, gums and polishx2. they just seem to control the power level and I only use clean.  The second button selects 1 of 3 power levels. I just use #3 the most powerful, but I used #1 when I first got the brush as my teeth were a bit sensitive.Value: It is not the cheapest brush but price is comparable to entry level name brand brushes bought at my local supermarkets . However, in my opinion/experience  it works much better than those with more features. I am happy with the value.ProsBattery: the battery is excellent. It claims 30 days use per charge, but I have used for 6 weeks so far and still has 3 of  3 bars of power.Cleaning performance is excellent.You can purchases additional brushes  if needed.  A lot of brushes do not have this and are basically disposable when the original  brushes wear out.comes with travel caseCons.Does not come with a usb A charger. So, if you don't have a spare floating around you may be up for an extra $5"
