[
    {
        "review": "We previously had a different model brush which we handed down to the kids after 3 years. https://a.co/d/bouL1w9  We thought that older model was great. I hadn’t had any cavities since I started using a Sonicare brush 10 years ago. I don’t floss my teeth and yet when I go to the dentist they always comment on how awesome I do at flossing.Due to eating ice I cracked a tooth. After using this brush for 3 days all the rest of the teeth in my mouth feel as slick as that brand new crown they just put in.I really like how this has 2 buttons, one for mode and one for power, the older models this was kind of frustrating to change modes while it was in your mouth.The ability to connect it to your phone so far for me has been less functional that it sounded. It sounds really cool and it does work awesome, but all it tells me so far is that I do great job brushing. It does tell my wife she doesn’t use enough pressure."
    },
    {
        "review": "I never write reviews but I’m making time for this one!!First off I spent hours researching and watching reviews on “the best electric toothbrush”. And it lead me to this one. It’s not too expensive like the diamond clean being $300+- it’s right in the middle for the price point and looks good, not too outdated and comes with a travel case, also it has all the features I’d really need. This is my first electric toothbrush coming from your regular target brand toothbrush’s ranging from $5-$20. What made me think of getting this over an oral B was the “sonic technology” which seems to be specific to the Phillips Sonicare brand, whereas oral b and others just rotate or whatever. Overall though it’s the best toothbrush I’ve ever owned and I’ll probably never go back to a regular toothbrush. My first concerns were reading other reviews that it broke in a year or 2 because of whatever faulty reason. But honestly if it breaks I’ll probably just get another one again because it’s worth it !! The clean is next level compared to a regular toothbrush and it’s a clean you’ll never experience without one of these toothbrushes. Once you realize what the vibrations mean you don’t need to use the app too, I never use the app and I know I’m gonna get a perfect clean each brush. As sad as it is to say but I look forward to brushing my teeth now every day knowing how clean and perfect my teeth are gonna feel afterwards lol.If you’re worried about the money then these types of toothbrushes aren’t for you. But if you can look past the price it’s 100% worth it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great quality Sonicare toothbrush left my teeth feeling super clean in an instant! I really like the different modes and speeds that I can adjust accordingly. Love the pink and white color — so aesthetically pleasing. It also feels good in my hand. Although the charger looks nice, it’s plastic and doesn’t feel as sturdy as the toothbrush. Same goes for the case but I’m not making a big deal out it. As for the features of the app, I really don’t care for it. I just wanted a nice toothbrush that did the job and this did!"
    },
    {
        "review": "this toothbrush is not worth the money.  Within 4 months , the charger died and I had to buy a new one because it was out of warranty.  The tooth brush head does not fit tightly on the the unit and shakes abnormally.  I have had the unit for one year, and it is starting to not turn on it also sounds louder than when I first bought it.  I have taken very good care of this unit, it's manufacture is faulty or this unit was a lemon.  I had my last Phillips Sonicare toothbrush for at least 8 years without any problems.  I don't recommend this unit it wasn't made well."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my third Sonicare brush. The first one was a 1000 second was a 7000. I always assumed the series # were just marketing tactics and the handles were all the same. This is not the case. The 1000 is basically a manual brush, I would never recommend it. The 7000 was outstanding, I used it for four years before I decided to buy my girlfriend her own and decided to upgrade slightly to the 9000. I order two, not because my 7000 needed to be replaced but so I could connect to the app which Ive heard was pretty great. Needless to say Im very pleased with the app although Im sure it's a luxury Ill use for a month then completely forget about. However the handle itself feels like a sledgehammer compared to the 7000. My teeth feel like I just left the dentist everytime I brush. I took the next step and linked my account to my Alexa which reorders brush heads when due. About every 85 days. I'll be buying these for my entire family come Xmas. Remarkable product"
