    {
        "review": "Outs true that only after a week of brushing with this 9000, made my teeth seem whiter.  But I didn’t give it 5 stars since I couldn’t get the app to work as described."
    },
    {
        "review": "So far very great. Great packaging, zero damage. Hopefully it last almost a decade like my last one i purchased from Philips. Love the multiple settings and speed/intensity changes. Been almost 2 weeks. Looks great feels great, easy to use.I'll try to remember to update later down line."
    },
    {
        "review": "the sonic toothbrush works good this is my 2nd one of this model and I enjoy both of them I now they are costly but so worth it for all the adjustments from telling you when you need to change the brush head to 3 speeds and lets you know when your pressing to hard against your teeth I will recommend this to anyone"
    },
    {
        "review": "The brand is security"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good tool for teeth cleaning, my dentist recommended it to me, easy to use and the program helps you manage the days you use it"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really happy with this Philips Sonicare toothbrush! It feels powerful without being harsh, and my teeth feel noticeably cleaner after brushing. The handle is comfortable to hold, the brush is easy to use, and the battery life is great for daily use and travel. I also like that it helps me brush more consistently. It is definitely worth the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been a loyal Philips Sonicare user for over two decades, and they’ve consistently improved their products over time in the following ways:🪥 Sleek handles that are light and easy to manoeuvre during brushing🪥 Elegant materials and finishes like glass, textiles for the travel case, chrome, and matte/metallic plastic🪥 Improved brush head designs for folks with more sensitive teeth and gums🪥 More attractive charging bases and accessories, like travel cases🪥 Charging tech to match what consumers have around the house or travel with, eliminating the need to carry a dedicated toothbrush chargerThis 💎DiamondClean 9000💎 model is no exception. It exudes premium quality.Here’s what stood out for me:🦷 Quiet Operation:  The toothbrush runs smoothly and quietly. The sonic vibrations on the high setting stimulate the gums and make your mouth feel like it just had both a massage and a hygiene appointment at the same time. Folks coming from a manual toothbrush will notice this after the very first brush.🦷 Light, Slim Design:  The handle is slender and lightweight, with modern gradient colours that enhance its aesthetic appeal.🦷 Slender Brush Heads:  A key advantage over Oral-B brushes. The slim design allows for better reach into back teeth and more precise cleaning. It’s ideal for those with gum recession and/or sensitive areas. The snap-on heads are easy to attach and resist buildup of old toothpaste around the connection point. I tried the Oral-B option with the bigger heads, and while it is a very slick product with a cool screen and functions, it was just too big and clumsy in my mouth.🦷 Customizable Vibration Level:  The power button lets you select vibration intensity. I’ve noticed the highest level is much more powerful than my previous Sonicare model. This thoughtful upgrade lets you boost agitation of the toothpaste, create more foam, and make your toothpaste go further.🦷 Stylish Charging Base:  The included black chrome charging base integrates seamlessly with premium glass charger cups from older Sonicare models, adding a touch of elegance.What Needs Improvement:⚠️ **Power Button Buildup:** I had this issue with my previous model to the point where it impacted button operation and made it difficult to use. While the buttons move freely on a new unit, the gap between the body and buttons remains and can accumulate hardened toothpaste over time, potentially causing them to stick. Philips needs to look at ways to address this, as my current solution is to use a pin and scrape around the button every few months under warm water to clear out the dried toothpaste gunk and get the button moving freely again. This was not an issue with the Oral-B.⚠️ **Brush Head Cap Design:** The updated cap for premium brush heads is cumbersome compared to the old slide-on design. Attaching it often catches and bends the outer bristles, which can be frustrating. The older design was quicker and more user-friendly. So, put on the cap carefully so you don’t ruin the bristles on the edge.Overall, this toothbrush still gets top marks from me, with just a few minor items noted for improvement. Philips, keep up the great work, and never stop innovating!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I have been using this COSLUS electric toothbrush for theee months now and I’m genuinely impressed with what you get for the price. Best of all when you register the product you get a two-year warranty.First off, the cleaning performance is solid. It has a strong sonic vibration that leaves my teeth feeling smooth and clean, comparable to other higher end electric toothbrushes I have purchased in the past. It’s noticeably more effective than manual brushing, especially around the gumline.The battery life is another BIG win. I only charged it every 3-4 weeks. For travel or everyday use, that’s really convenient.It also comes with multiple brushing modes, which is nice to have depending on whether you want a deeper clean or something more gentle for sensitive gums. The build feels lightweight but not cheap and it’s easy to hold even when wet.The included 6 brush heads are a good bonus and they seem easy enough to replace when needed. Charging is simple with the included base and everything feels straightforward with no complicated setup or app required.If I had one minor complaint, it’s that it doesn’t have the “smart” features or premium feel of much more expensive brands like Sonicare or Oral-B. But honestly, at this price point, that’s expected and not a dealbreaker for me.Overall, If you are looking for an affordable electric toothbrush that does the job well without unnecessary extras, this is a great pick. It’s an excellent balance of performance and value and with a two-year warranty, why not?"
    },
    {
        "review": "This sonic toothbrush arrived in a sleek, well-designed travel case that immediately stood out. The case holds two brush heads (one for current use and one individually wrapped spare), and what really impressed me is the built-in ventilation. If you’re someone who brushes in the shower (🙋🏽‍♀️), this detail is huge. Bonus: the toothbrush itself is fully waterproof, so no concerns there.The toothbrush is lightweight, slim, and comfortable to hold, making it feel more premium than bulkier electric brushes I’ve used. It features a 2-minute smart timer with 30-second quadrant pauses, which helps ensure even cleaning throughout the mouth. One feature I genuinely appreciate: if you stop mid-cycle—say, to sign for a delivery—the brush resumes exactly where you left off when you turn it back on. That level of thoughtful design doesn’t go unnoticed.There are 5 distinct cleaning modes, and with each mode change there is a noticeable change in brushing pattern, particularly through the blue bristles and angled top bristles. The toothbrush overall is well designed and aligns comfortably with both teeth and gums, providing a thorough yet gentle clean. The brush head shape feels intentional, not generic.COSLUS includes 6 brush heads, which equals approximately 18 months of use based on the recommended 3-month replacement schedule—an excellent value and a big plus for long-term ownership.I’ve only just started using this toothbrush, so I can’t yet speak to battery longevity or how the blue indicator bristles fade over time. That said, I’ll be more than happy to provide an update after extended use.Overall, this toothbrush checks all the boxes: smart design, strong performance, thoughtful features, and great value. I’m excited to continue using it and would absolutely recommend it to anyone looking to upgrade their oral care routine.  Great value and works WELL!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I don’t often leave reviews; however, this toothbrush works so well I am compelled to. I’ve had the more expensive brand tooth brushes and this works as well or better for much less money.  Quite, good battery life solid brushes."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for myself and fell in love immediately. The sonic vibration is no joke — my teeth feel genuinely clean after every use, not just brushed. There’s a difference and this toothbrush makes you feel it every single time.But let me tell you what really sold me. The bristles are soft. Like genuinely soft, not that medium-firm nonsense that has you questioning your enamel after every brush. Soft bristles AND somehow getting my teeth cleaner than any toothbrush I have ever used in my life. I don’t know how they pulled that off but they did and my mouth has never been happier.The multiple brushing modes are actually useful too — not just gimmicks. Polishing, whitening, clean — I rotate through them depending on what my teeth need that day and the difference is noticeable.BUT HERE is the real testimony. My fiancé has an Oral-B electric toothbrush. A NICE one. The kind that costs real money and comes with the fancy charging dock and all that. You know what he’s been using instead? This one. Every single day. Voluntarily. He put his Oral-B DOWN and has not looked back.That is not a small thing. That is a man admitting something works better than what he already had. That’s the whole review right there.For less than $15 this toothbrush is overdelivering at this price point by a MILE. Chef’s kiss doesn’t even cover it. And the multiple extra brush heads included means you’re not running back to Amazon every few months desperately searching for compatible replacements. Everything you need is in the box.Dentist visit about to be boring in the best way possible. Get this for yourself. Get it for whoever you live with. You’re welcome in advance.​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my 1st experience with vibrating toothbrush.Lemne tell you it's powerful. I have to keep mine on the soft setting. It tickled the gell outta me tikl I figured out leaving my mouth opened was the way to go.My teeth feel super clean after I use this. I love that it came with so many heads and the fact that you can order more later on when needed. I split the heads between my son and i so could try it out. I love that it comes with a case to store both ut and the brush head in. My son just uses a toothbrush cover from walmart since hes testing it out. Id definitely suggest using this. If at 1st you dont like ut give it more time to see if you can figure out a setting that worked better.If youre planning on getting this for a younger child have them test it out with one of the extra heads like I did with my teenager. It may be too strong for the littlest ones.My overall review is a 10/10There is a bit of a learning curve, its powerful so it may not be for everyone if you have sensative teeth, comes with storage, charging cord and extra brush heads."
    },
