[
    {
        "review": "Before using this product I would use toothbrushes that you could find at the convenience store or dollar store. After using this product I have no plans of returning to my original toothbrushes.The Phillips Sonicare is a great product. There are three settings on the toothbrush. They are clean, white, and gum care. These settings are self explanatory as their name and their function is the same. Each of these functions works well. You can really feel the effectiveness of each of these settings with its first use.The Sonicare toothbrush has a timer function. It is useful if you want to brush a certain segment of your mouth for a specific interval. Personally for me I brush each section of mouth simeotaneously.I have not traveled with the toothbrush yet. The carrying case makes it very convenient to pack it up and take it with you. I have not tested the battery life because it is more convient to place my toothbrush on the charging base  instead of leaving it off of the base.One drawback is that you will have to replace the brush head every three months or so. One benefit to this is that you can replace the brush head with a specialized head that helps a specific aspect of your mouth such as your gums, teeth  etc. Some of the packs are quite pricey but I believe that it is worth the investment but, be sure you are buying the official Phillips brand from a reputable seller. I have read reports of counterfeiting online, where people pay for a premium brand and ended up getting the bargain brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "Intro and things I like:I had the Sonicare E-series toothbrush for over a decade, and it started to not hold charge so well anymore, so I decided to upgrade to this toothbrush. The head on the 5100 is a bit smaller which I like, and the handle is also nice and slim as well. It's a fairly quiet toothbrush compared to my boyfriend's Oral-B toothbrush, which I love because I tend to be a night owl. The charging is perfectly fine and it lasts about 14 days without a charge, and will take 24 hours to charge if it's completely dead. The quality of this toothbrush is pristine, and this is why I decided to go with the 5100 instead of the 4100 because I head concerns about the newer 4100 model's build quality. There are no issues with quality for the 5100 as far as I know. I also love that it comes with a travel case as I am constantly on the go for vet school rotations. Some toothbrush brands come with a USB plug in style charger, but this style is much better because you can just sit it on the charger base without having to worry about plugging in a USB C cable or something like that.Using it:There are three different modes for this toothbrush, clean, whitening, and gum care. I use the traditional clean mode, and sometimes the gum care because it feels good on my gums. I love that the toothbrush has a very slight pause every 30 seconds indicating that it's time to switch quadrants, and turns off automatically at 2 minutes for \"clean\" mode. Apparently \"whitening\" mode goes for 2:30, but I prefer the \"clean\" mode. There is also a really awesome feature that you can set on the toothbrush letting you know when it's time to change the toothbrush head, indicated by the light near the bottom of the toothbrush. This is great for customers who don't always keep track of when to change their toothbrush heads.Cons I've encountered so far:The only con really would be that it comes with one toothbrush head. There is a little slip of paper that shows you how to register your product with Philips for discounted heads, but it would be nice if it came with at least two. Another thing that is probably just me, is that the black base for the toothbrush doesn't come with black heads. I think it would look pretty cool if the heads matched the base for a nice, sleek look. You can get matching colors if you opt for the white, but I just picked the option that would be delivered to me faster because I'm impatient.Overall:As someone who has always been pretty anal about her oral hygiene, I would highly recommend this to anyone who is looking for a  first time or new toothbrush to up their oral hygiene game."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Philips Sonicare ProtectiveClean 5100 since September 2024, and it’s still performing as expected. I usually charge it about once every 10 days, and the battery easily holds up that long, possibly longer (I've just never tried).This toothbrush leaves my teeth feeling noticeably cleaner than a manual brush ever did. I’ve used round brush heads in the past, but I much prefer these longer, slim heads. They reach all the way to the back; yes, even around my wisdom teeth, without causing any discomfort.The pressure sensor is a great touch, helping me brush more gently and avoid gum irritation. I mostly use the Clean mode, but it's nice having other options like Gum Care and White depending on my needs. While the brush helps lift surface stains over time, I’ve found that your toothpaste choice plays a big role in how noticeable the whitening results are.On top of the performance, the sleek black design looks great on the counter, and the included travel case makes it easy to take on the go. FYI - There is no issue having this in a carry-on when traveling by plane.All in all, this is a great investment in your oral health: reliable, effective, and thoughtfully designed. For the quality, performance, and features you get, this toothbrush is worth the price. I'm sure they have released 3 to 4 new models, but you really don't need a better toothbrush than this."
    },
    {
        "review": "I. LOVE. THIS. TOOTHBRUSH. This particular purchase I bought for a gift because I already own one. Within the first week of using it, OTHER PEOPLE noticed me with whiter teeth. It is well worth it. The battery feels endless to me. I honestly forget that it is rechargeable because the battery never dies for me. Forewarning: If it is your first time using one of these brushes, you will feel a little discomfort because it is different. Also, the vibration may cause just a little bit of discomfort, but after many uses, you get used to it. No bleeding at all though. It isn't like that. It's just an awkward feeling."
    },
    {
        "review": "It does the job.  I use the cleaning mode and whitening mode the most. Actually, I think the white mode might be a little bit stronger for cleaning my teeth.  Sometimes I use the gum setting but find brushing my gums with the clean and white mode okay. It is a bit noisy but not too bad while brushing teeth.  However, when you just put it under the faucet to rinse off it sounds really awful.  The last Philips Sonicare I bought in 2021 last until 2024 when the handle got hot and had a very loud screeching sound so unusable.  I’d recommend this toothbrush as it does clean my teeth satisfactorily. It holds a charge really well."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using this toothbrush for 3 years now.Was suggested to me by a dentist who told me that it’s more efficient and that it causes less gum recession due to you not over brushing manually.Ever since using it, I have had cleaner teeth and is also great if you have a post braces permanent chain behind your teeth.I even got sooo lazy during pandemic and wfh that I skipped a lot of teeth brushing. I moved across the country and was behind on my last cleaning as well. I was CONVINCED I had a cavity and my teeth were in bad shape but was told my teeth were in great shape and 0 cavities. I’m not recommending you not brush your teeth but the performance is so good that even with a lack of consistent use, the brush still gets the job done!Is also easy to wipe down with running alcohol every so often when it gets kinda icky under the head. You can also buy generic brand compatible heads which saves a lot of money in that area.Battery life is pretty good, although I will say it does sometimes die quicker with age but is still not that often that it’s a bother."
    },
    {
        "review": "If all you've used is a manual toothbrush for the past 30 something years, this sonic toothbrush will take some getting used to. There's a lot of vibration going on in your mouth basically, which feels abnormal for a while. Outside of that, I absolutely love this toothbrush. It gives you a very noticeable cleaning difference. Your mouth just feels much cleaner."
    },
    {
