[
    {
        "review": "I bought this laptop as a gift for my kid, and he absolutely loves it. We had no issues getting everything set up, and he was able to start using it for school pretty much right away.Having Windows 11 and Office 365 already included was a big plus for us. He can work on his school assignments, presentations, research, and other everyday activities without needing anything extra.The 12GB of RAM is more than enough for what he needs. He can have multiple browser tabs open, work on documents, and switch between his school applications without any problems. The 15.6-inch screen is also a nice size for homework and watching videos.I also like that the laptop is thin and lightweight, so it’s easy for him to carry around when needed.Overall, I think it offers very good value for the money. For a student who needs a computer for school, browsing, Office, and everyday use, this has been a great choice. Most importantly, my kid is happy with it! Definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great laptop! It’s fast, easy to use, and has a nice screen. Perfect for everyday work, browsing, and streaming. Very happy with my purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Incredible product. Much more solidly built than I had expected.I purchased this because my 2017 MacBook Pro I-7 would warm up considerably during heavy work (I am a data scientist and push the machine to crunch very large sets before I move a project over to AWS for its computing power). This product was more than I expected. It is light weight, strong, and folds conveniently into a size that fits in an outer pocket of my backpack, thus I carry it with me wherever I go. Even when I am not crunching numbers, I place my Mac on it. The typing angle is perfect for long coding sessions and makes my hands feel much better.The item does adjust for the size of the laptop. My MacBook Pro is a 15 inch, but my ASUS laptop is a 17 inch. With a quick turn of the pressure dial on two of the legs, the X-stand adjusts between my Mac and ASUS so that each has a SOLID platform to rest on. And the room below the machines is ample to provide good airflow to keep the machines cooler.I wholeheartedly and enthusiastically recommend the X-Stand, especially if your \"office\" is more often on your back and your workstation is any desk surface you can find like mine tends to be. It conveniently folds into a small size and provides an adjustable, solid platform to air your laptop. I may purchase additional ones so for when (as too often happens) this great product is discontinued - should it every be - or for holiday gifts for my other geek friends."
    },
    {
        "review": "Product: Steklo Laptop RiserUsed for: 1 year and 4 monthsKey Features:– Extremely portable and lightweight design– High-quality materials that feel durable– Good stability for various laptop sizesRatings:Quality:The build quality is excellent, with a strong and durable design that has held up perfectly after more than a year of regular use.Rating: 5/5Performance:Stability is very good, and it fits a wide range of laptop sizes. However, it lacks any real height adjustability, so you’re locked into one angle. That said, it still works well for improving airflow and keeping the laptop from sitting flat.Rating: 4/5Value:A bit on the pricey side, but it performs well and is built to last, so the investment feels justified.Rating: 4/5Pros:– Highly portable and travel-friendly– Solid and durable build qualityCons:– No height adjustment optionsSummary:The Steklo Laptop Riser is an excellent choice if you value portability and durability. While it lacks height adjustment, it still improves airflow and provides a stable platform for your laptop. A bit expensive for what it offers, but it’s a reliable, long-lasting option.Overall Rating: 4/5Disclaimer: This review is based on my personal experience using the product. I'm not an expert—just sharing my honest thoughts to help others make an informed decision."
    },
    {
        "review": "Got this for my daughter starting middle school and honestly its been better then I expected for the price. Comes with office already on it which saved me the subscription hassle, she was typing her book report the first nite.Its light enough she carries it in her backpack no problem, and the screen is bigger than the chromebook her school loaned out so less squinting. Battery gets her thru homework and a couple youtube videos easy.Dont expect a gaming machine, it takes a beat opening bigger programs, but for schoolwork and netflix its exactly what we needed."
    },
    {
        "review": "So since the iPad Pro release I've been on a mission to find a good stand to simple prop the iPad up a bit for sketching.  I'm a product designer by trade so I'm not doing insanely intricate work (mostly concept sketching) and after years of sketching a Cintiq, I'm used to sketching at somewhat of an angle.  I originally purchased a stand that was marketed as an iPad Pro/Macbook Air Stand from a much more expensive (almost triple the cost) and well-known brand, but it fell short in more ways than one.  THIS, however, is perfect for iPad Pro sketching.  It works so well that in fact, I'm going to also write the seller to make sure they add it to the description.The problem with the \"other\" stand(s) is they simply aren't portable.  Why would you want to buy a huge clunky stand (yes it might be pretty and textured aluminum and Apple make it more appealing by offering it in their online store) and not be able to just throw it in your bag?  The Steklo X-Stand features very well thought out design and construction along with the portability you want for the products it supports.  I do have one small gripe however, and that is the \"feet\" at the bottom that stabilize the laptop (by your wrists if you were typing) are a bit long.  They stick out above the edge of the iPad Pro but for MacBook Pro customers this probably wouldn't be a huge deal depending on what model/how you type.  For me personally I will probably Dremel them down a hair shorter so they're flush with the screen (I'm on the fence though as they do offer a good place to rest the Pencil) and still do their job of holding the unit in place.  In all reality the feet haven't really bothered me yet on a physical level (I've only been using it for a few days) so I guess it's more of an OCD thing.  The feet and back supports are soft polymer that provide plenty of grip/stability and I don't see them scratching any type of metal, but I use a case regardless.If you're looking for a great way to prop up your iPad Pro for sketching/drawing/painting whatever, you've found it!  Don't go blowing all kinds of money on a more expensive stand when it's simply not necessary and lacks portability.  I've added some customer images for anyone who'd like to see it modeled with an iPad Pro."
    },
    {
        "review": "Worst laptop I ever purchasedI couldn’t get this to work at all.It took forever to setup and did not work properly, slow, crashed and when I tried to delete the info to return it I was not able to.I wasted like 4 hrs trying to make this work and trying to clear my info before returning.I am very disappointed I wasted my time with this."
    },
    {
        "review": "Durable aluminum construction. Adjustable for multiple laptop sizes. No big bulky cheap plastic cooling pad to lug around, which effectively defeats the purpose of the portability of the device I need it for. This stand folds up into a very compact form factor that fits perfectly into one of the pockets in my laptop bag, no fuss, no problem. No useless fans that generally never improve temperatures in any meaningful way that the fans in the laptop don't already accomplish themselves if they have ample room to breathe, not to mention promoting more dust and dirt getting pushed into the laptop vents, all at the expense of more fan noise and using up one of the already scarce USB ports on the laptop to power them, therefore no mechanical moving parts that will inevitably break or die.This is getting use with a 17.3\" MSI Stealth GS76 laptop sporting a Core i7 11800H and a 16 GB RTX 3080 - This laptop gets mighty hot during gaming sessions, and sometimes even during general tasks when sitting flat on a surface. I already have to max the fans to 100% during gaming sessions so as it is. I'm always trying to prop something under the rear outer edge of the laptop to elevate it a little for better airflow, what a pain. This little stand has solved all my problems and really helps a lot to allow the fans in the laptop to work more effectively, pulling much more airflow through the vents underneath, as well as more room for hot air to exhaust away from it, and has such a small footprint where it makes contact with the underside so as not to block airflow into the vents. I get incredibly better cooling results with this stand.My only complaint related to this stand is directed at myself because I didn't get one sooner. It's exactly what I've had in mind and have been looking for."
    },
