        "review": "I had an earlier Lenovo Desk Top and was not real happy with it, so I was Leary about their laptop. But, it turned out to be a well made machine, I’m happy and surprised at the QC.I did notice the cover was stiff to open, probably due to not having a latch. One purchaser said the hinges were terrible, I can see his point, they are stiff for a reason! Just open it gently and not try to fling it open, it’s just stiff to keep it closed.I would recommend this PC to any and all persons."
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice light and thin with 16\" screen, video performance is good. Reasonably fast processor, with 32 GB RAM so it handles typical productivity application tasks easily. 1TB SSD will most likely meet my needs for life of the laptop. I have attached a USB-C docking station to enable a few extra USB-A ports for use with devices such as audio input from Yamaha mixer board, WYRESTORM 4K Webcam. external KB and Mouse. This unit is used daily for extended length Google MEET calls. BTW, product description said no backlight KB but the unit I received does have this feature."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent for the price. Fit our needs nicely."
    },
    {
        "review": "It pains me to give this Lenovo only three stars, since for the most part, it has good specs for a fairly budget-conscious laptop. It has an excellent, quiet AMD Ryzen processor and generous, upgradeable storage capacity, all of which contribute to smooth performance and speed for multi-tasking with more than one application open at once. So why three stars instead of four? Because this laptop's one fault, the one thing that the builders skimped on, is so major that it almost cancels out its good qualities. I'm talking about the poor quality of the display. It's described as full HD or FHD, backlit LED with 1920 x 1080 resolution. Unfortunately, these nice-sounding specs don't make up for the weak Radeon integrated graphics card, which delivers mediocre to poor images with washed-out, untrue colors. It's as if you're looking at old faded photographs, and the anti-glare matte finish doesn't help. The integrated graphics do not allow for enough manual adjustability to improve display quality. So try as the user might, there's only so much the built-in graphics card can do.All that said: This is a great laptop for business. Text documents are crisp, especially if you use the Windows text clarity function, where you can adjust the sharpness of the text according to your own eyesight. Also excellent for business or home-office use are all the different ports and slots. It even has an ethernet port, which is handy to have if you need reliable internet service but live or work in an area where internet strength can be spotty.  This laptop is also surprisingly light and thin, so another plus is that it has excellent portability.Conclusion: This is a handy, budget-conscious laptop for business use from the reliable and well-established Lenovo brand. But don't choose this laptop if streaming movies and seeing bright, vivid, true colors are also a priority. If you want an all-around workhorse that can double as a streaming device, you'll need to spend more money and get a laptop with a dedicated graphics card."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great laptop for 60 percent off too 👏"
    },
