[
    {
        "review": "I bought this laptop because I needed something reasonably priced for everyday use, mostly checking emails, browsing the internet, and doing some basic office and school work. I wasn’t looking for a high-end computer, just something dependable that wouldn’t be a pain to use.It arrived well packaged with the laptop protected nicely inside the box. The build feels solid enough for the price, and the 15.6 inch screen is a good size without making the laptop feel overly bulky. Setup was pretty straightforward and Windows 11 was easy to get going. I’ve been using it at my kitchen table for browsing, documents, video calls and streaming, and it handles those tasks without any problems. The keyboard is comfortable and the webcam works fine for normal calls. The 4GB RAM can feel a little limited when I have lots of tabs open, but I like that both the RAM and SSD can be upgraded. I’d recommend it for students or anyone needing a basic everyday laptop."
    },
