[
    {
        "review": "I looked and looked for a new PC for a while.  I love a bargain and this one fit the bill.  Has a great screen, good build, current hardware and Windows 11.I don't know what else to say about this PC other than I am impressed, especially at the price I paid which was $550.  Now price has dropped after a couple of weeks by about $75 with discount coupon.  I don't know if that means inventory is low or high, but if you are looking might want to make a move before is gone.The item I received I could not see anything that made it look less than new.  Then I realized there was a \"skin\" on the cover.  It was very close to the color of the PC and didn't notice until the edge started to curl.  Underneath were two areas of very small scuffs.  No way a deal breaker or enough to knock off any stars but the skin did seem to be kind of sneaky.  Close enough in color you won't notice at first, but not good enough quality to be much more than a temporary cover.The battery seems a little weak.  Once again not a deal breaker, but instead of around 10 hours I am getting about 5.  Granted I know the tests are designed to maximize battery life but I would have hoped for closer to 7 hours."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm impressed at the performance from such a tiny laptop. I'm a professional photographer and use this laptop almost daily. It fits perfectly in my camera bag when I'm traveling. The addition of the SD card reader eliminated the need for another piece of equipment to remember. Screen is bright enough for a bright studio but struggles in direct sunlight so I've ordered a screen hood for it and fixed that issue for $26. Battery last all day, touch screen is a huge plus too. The processor is plenty fast enough to edit on the go with light room and the ability to use it as a graphics tab for photos hop is a huge plus when I'm sitting on a plane for hours. If I had to gripe about anything, I'd say that the speakers are kinda crappy and the volume seems low but I bought this \"renewed\" so it could have been something the previous owner damaged.  Overall a great value for the $ and I will be buying the newer model eventually. Oh, the fingerprint access is a huge perk! One less password to remember!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This laptop arrived in excellent condition visibly. Works as it should for the most part. Having a bit of trouble with windows 11 update though. Could be something I'm not doing or a setting maybe? Not sure yet as I only had it a few days to play around with. Otherwise it works beautifully & the speed exceeds my expectations. The graphics are gorgeous. Love the ability to touch screen, 360° flip to tablet mode. Haven't tried the Bluetooth capability yet. The sound is awesome. Battery life is Okay. Power cord is long enough to plug in and continue use. My only gripe is the brightness has to be set very high in order to see well but again that could just be my eyeballs as I've gotten older. It was very easy to turn on & set up. This Lenovo flex 7i does have S pen capability but is sold separately. Excellent job on this one so far guys!!! Will update my review if anything changes. For now I'm very satisfied as I work out the small stuff."
    },
    {
        "review": "So far so good. College freshman just started using. Small adjustment from the school issued chromebooks but he is adjusting and navigating. Will come back to post any issues or positive feedback once classes begin."
    },
    {
        "review": "Okay, this is a BIG deal. Lenovo and I have a sordid past and mostly I couldn't stand the brand. All my Lenovos have failed pretty quickly and I didn't like they keyboard layout. But after having damaged my HP pavilion x360, I was in the market for a new convertible laptop that I could create digital art on and write with and that gave me similar if not better features. I was looking at HP spectre and Microsoft Surface and not only were they out of my price range, there were a lot of mixed reviews with an uncomfortable amount being bad.This laptop kept being forced on me in my searches and I finally caved and took a peak. Not only is it convertible/drawing friendly, its x360, POWERFUL, but its beautiful and sleek. It was an affordable laptop and imo rivals HP spectre/surface (which are $300-800 more). It came completely wear and tear free, so far works like magic with speeds faster than HP.I've been converted tp Lenovo this time. Love it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This review is mostly about the refurbish service, the computer itself is absolutely fantastic.  My expectations for a refurbished computer was that I would get something that would show very modest wear, but work perfectly. I was delighted when I first opened my new Lenovo computer. The screen, keyboard, and touchpad appeared like it was brand new had never been touched. I was initially delighted with my purchase and started loading software and restoring my data. On the second day however, I noticed some unusual indentations around the power button. As I explored it further, I found that the computer had probably been dropped on its side. It actually bent the case enough to make the SD card slot unusable. It also makes the USB connectors quite tight (which may not actually be a bad thing in and of itself - but it's not right). The bottom of the case shows a physical crack and I am moderately concerned about whether there's some hairline fractures or other damage that isn't immediately obvious. The bottom line is, I've decided to keep the computer since it seems to be working fine and I really appreciate the pristine screen and keyboard that I received. I don't use the SD card slot so it's not a big deal to me for that. But I guess I'm just a little disappointed to have received a laptop that was clearly dropped hard enough to bend the case.  I know this happed before shipping as the box it was delivered in showed no signs of any drop.  It is a bit of a testament to the high-quality build that Lenovo puts into their computers but not a great example of careful oversight on the Amazon reconditioning service.  I think they should have been more descriptive about this kind of damage on this particular item (maybe offered it with a bit more discount?)"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great laptop and a great price"
    },
    {
        "review": "Purchased this laptop. In less than 90 days, it completely fried/stopped working in the middle of my workday without any identifiable reason. Unable to reboot, or turn on to troubleshoot. It was fine beforehand. Not fantastic. No biometrics."
    }
]

