        "review": "Don't let the compact size fool you—this JBL mini speaker punches way above its weight class! The sound quality is remarkably clear with crisp highs and surprisingly punchy bass for something that fits right in the palm of your hand or pockets easily.​The rugged IP67 dustproof and waterproof rating means you can take it to the pool, beach, shower, or camping without worrying about water splashes, sand, or rain. The built-in durable loop/strap makes it super convenient to clip onto a backpack or belt loop with a carabiner. Battery life easily lasts through a full day of casual listening, and USB-C fast charging gets it back to 100% quickly. The ultimate portable speaker!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great little speaker.  Big sound in a little package.  Great for a road trip.  Was on a golf trip with some friends, and one of them brought the Go 4 with him.  We enjoyed it while winding down at the end of the day.  It does not come with a travel case, but is very sturdy and waterproof.  It's also small enough to carry in a shoe without the case. I bought the case anyway, which is attractive and adds a little more protection against the elements, if needed"
    },
    {
        "review": "Going on 3 months absolutely am loving this compact product. Not heavy but has a nice feel to it. I utilize this majority of the day in my CDL Truck. The clarity and volume is amazing. I really enjoy the red strobe lights especially at night. For the price you really can’t beat it at all. I was amazed how loud it reached. I use this also to watch movies along side w my table top notch sound. It also pairs quickly to my iPhone 14 Pro and my IPhone Tablet."
    },
    {
        "review": "This speaker is the cutest thing ever ! Small but great sound . Take it everywhere on the go . You'll want one in every color !!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I don't really consider myself an audiophile, though I do listen to quite a lot of music and can piece together where sounds are supposed to be on the equalizer. This speaker does it's job well for its size, it has great volume control, pretty good bass, the lights on it are pretty cute, and it connects flawlessly to my phone and mp3 player with Bluetooth. It's waterproof and weather proof which is great for when I go to the beach or out camping, and it is cool that it can become stereo if you connect another JBL speaker to it. However, this isn't a speaker to use for high quality listening, at least from what I've tried to do with it. There isn't a lot of depth to the equalizer quality, so you won't get audiophile level sound, and that probably isn't why you would buy this anyway, as it wasn't my reason either, I needed a speaker that was small for work. But sometimes in certain songs the mixture of certain frequencies will cause the speaker to play muddy, sometimes even strange sounding instruments which I have never heard from any other speaker. Crying by Bjork for example in the middle of the song there is a part with 2 synths playing which you can distinctly hear on regular speakers, but with this speaker it almost combines them and it sounds like a construction machine, and I know bjork does things like that but not in this song, I'm pretty sure. The midtones and the deep bass parts of songs seem to be this speaker's struggle, either it gets really really muddy or can't get to that frequency with the other sounds playing so it just doesn't play. It's really odd, but either way, this speaker doesn't have to do all that, it just needs to be small and play loud and pretty good, and it does a great job at that. I'm sure the more expensive and larger speakers don't have as much of an issue."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great sound, base and clarity in a package that feels almost as big as your phone. In my experience, it sounds almost as good as the JBL Flip 5 with around 1/4 the size.Taking it everywhere is easy in your pocket or backpack. Carrying it with one hand or even one finger is so easy to make sure everyone hears your music.It has a customizable eq, but the default sound is amazing.Battery life is relatively short. I have to remind myself to charge it every so often, but it lasts for more than 2 days with somewhat regular use."
    },
    {
        "review": "Can't believe the quality of sound coming out of this very small, lightweight, inexpensive speaker! Stunning. Set-up took a few minutes and love that I could pair it with another JBL speaker. Waterproof to boot and 10 hours between re-charges! Am a longtime Sonos and Bose speaker owner but this little thing is mind-blowing from classical to rock to hip-hop. Not sure why but also enjoy having this kind sound quality right next to me. Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "wonderful"
    },
    {
        "review": "I loved the JBL Go 5. Super compact but with a wonderful, fluid sound. It was worth it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "100000/10 I loved the product, the price-quality ratio is perfect, the design and color is beautiful, I am delighted with my purchase, it looks durable, it has very very good sound, I am surprised by how it sounds being small, I repeat, the color is beautiful I would buy it again a thousand times, highly recommended, I had previously bought JBL headphones and they were super resistant, good sound, in general they have very good quality. The only detail is that it does not come with a charging cable but in the images it mentions that they do not provide chargers, the input is type C, just to take it into account."
    },
    {
        "review": "This thing is amazing for the size. I had and older portable jbl that went MIA so needed to replace it. I tested a comparable sized bose and to be honest at most listened levels this was pretty much as good ... not exactly as good but it's like half the price for 90% of the boses performance. The lights on it are customized in the app, neat but really not a huge sell point to me but it may be for you. These are definitely a good buy for something small, portable and sound good."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wonderful product, I gave it as a gift and it was really liked."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this thing. First of all it is SO much smaller than I imagined it was going to be but don’t let the size fool you because this little thing JAMS 😂The retro look is probably what caught my attention in the first place. The wood finish and the little gold knobs are just really pretty and it looks like an actual piece of decor instead of another random plastic Bluetooth speaker sitting around.The sound is really good too. Obviously this isn’t my giant Bluetooth speaker that can basically shake the house but that’s actually the point. I have a massive portable speaker that is basically a shake the house down speaker lol. This one is more of my clean the house speaker and it does that job perfectly.I love being able to connect my phone and just walk around the house with it while I’m cleaning. It’s super portable and easy to move from room to room. It gets plenty loud for what it is and the sound is surprisingly full for such a tiny speaker.I also really like that you have all the different ways to use it. Bluetooth is obviously what I’ll use most but having FM radio AUX and TF card playback gives you a lot of options.And those knobs are just fun. There’s something about actually turning a knob instead of having to mess around with an app for everything that I really like.The build quality is honestly amazing. It feels solid and it looks even better in person. I really love this little thing and I think it would look good on a desk shelf nightstand or basically anywhere you want a little music without having a giant speaker taking up space.Amazing value for the money and definitely one of those products I’m just really happy I got."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wanted a small Bluetooth speaker that I could leave sitting around and use for background music, and I mainly picked this one because I thought the retro radio design looked cool. It’s even smaller in person than I pictured, which I actually like because it barely takes up any space on a shelf or table. I use it mostly for playing music for my plants. The sound quality is okay—not amazing, but honestly about what I expected from a speaker this small. It gets reasonably loud for its size and sounds perfectly fine at the lower and medium volumes I normally use for background music. I haven’t had any problems getting my phone connected to it, and it reconnects easily when I turn it back on. I usually just leave it plugged in, so I can’t say much about the full battery life, but I have used it unplugged for a few hours before and it kept playing. I also like the actual knobs on the front. They fit the whole old-radio look and are more fun to use than tiny buttons. I mostly bought this because it was compact and looked interesting, and that’s pretty much exactly what I got."
    },
    {
        "review": "Look, I'm no audiophile—my usual jam is just blasting Spotify from my phone's tinny little speaker while I cook. But I saw this wooden retro speaker and it gave me major vintage vibes, so I figured why not roll the dice? Priced at $42 at the time of this review (with a coupon that shaves off a couple bucks), it's sitting pretty in that sweet spot between cheap plastic junk and those eye-watering $200 wooden units that make you question your life choices. The walnut shell feels surprisingly substantial in the hand, and the golden knobs? Absolute chef's kiss—they turn with this satisfying click that feels like you're tuning into a 1950s broadcast. Pairing via Bluetooth 5.4 was stupid easy, and the FM radio actually pulled in stations without me having to wrestle with a janky antenna. Battery life seems decent—I got about six hours of mixed use before it crapped out.Pros:Gorgeous retro design that doubles as desktop decor.FM radio works well with the built-in antenna.Bluetooth pairing is fast and stable.Cons:Bass is pretty anemic; don't expect thumping lows.The volume knob is a little stiff to turn.No USB-C charging—still uses micro-USB."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the retro design of this speaker. The wood-grain finish, front grille, and old-school knobs give it a cool vintage radio look. Bluetooth connected without any issues, and I also like having the option to use FM radio, AUX, or a TF card.My biggest surprise was the size. This thing is a LOT smaller than it appears in the product pictures. It's truly a mini speaker and fits easily in your hand. The sound is decent considering how small it is, but I was definitely expecting something larger based on the listing photos.Overall, it's a neat little speaker and I like the design and features, but at almost $45, I'm not sure I would personally buy it. If you specifically want a very small retro-style speaker, though, it does the job well."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the combination of vintage style and modern functionality on this little speaker. The black wood-grain finish, classic grille, and gold-colored knobs give it the look of an old-fashioned radio, and its compact size makes it easy to place on a desk, bookshelf, or nightstand. It looks great even when it’s not being used.The FM radio is a fun feature and brings back that nostalgic feeling. The large tuning knob makes finding stations simple, and I really enjoy having a physical control instead of having to navigate through menus on a screen.Bluetooth 5.4 makes wireless playback from my phone easy and reliable, but I also appreciate having multiple connection options. The AUX input is useful for older devices, and the TF card support is convenient when I want to play music without relying on a phone or internet connection.The mechanical knobs are probably my favorite part. The volume and tuning controls have a nice tactile feel and make the speaker enjoyable to operate. Everything is straightforward without complicated setup or unnecessary buttons."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is more of a really good looking bluetooth speaker that has as secondary function the ability to accept other wireless broadcast (FM etc) transmissions, so if that if what you are looking for you won't be disappointed. (it's basically made for desk use)  However if you want a portable radio to listen to the radio while you work in the garage you might have some minor issues.The first one of these is there's no FM antenna, it still works without an antenna and if you want better reception you can use the \"aux\" port with a 1/8\" cable as antenna, and this does work.  But it'd be annoying if you are carrying this places and so on, again another reason why it's a great desk radio but perhaps not portable.Weighs a bit over 10 ounces"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love the classic wooden appearance. Bluetooth connects fast, volume knob is smooth. Nice sound for its size. Very satisfied."
    },
    {
        "review": "This little retro Bluetooth stereo definitely has the right vibe. It brings up memories of 1940s Philco-style radios, or at least the modern decorative version of that idea, and it looks great as a desk accent piece.Audio quality is about what I expected. Not terrible, not spectacular. I think it has two speakers with one firing toward the wall, or maybe just one speaker doing its best in there. Either way, this is not audiophile equipment, and the volume is not exactly room-shaking.Pairing was simple and quick, and the controls are straightforward. The volume knob also works as the on/off and mode button, which keeps things simple enough.Overall, I like it for what it is. Nice retro look, easy Bluetooth pairing, acceptable sound, and enough charm to make up for the fact that it is more decorative radio than serious stereo. If it was about fifteen bucks cheaper it would be an easy five stars. At nearly 50, it's a harder sell."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I didn't expect much for this price point but I was pleasantly surprised! The audio quality on this JBL speaker is top notch. It was very easy to setup and it also has an app that allows you to change the colors on the speaker, adjust the equalizer, and connect to other JBL speakers so you can really have a party.Battery life is very solid - I didn't even charge it fully when I first opened it and that hour of charge gave me several hours of music. It doesn't come with a charging cord for the USB-c but I had plenty lying around so it wasn't a big deal to me.It is small and compact, perfect for pool days or bringing along to enjoy music on the go. I also adore the pink color - perfect for me!It's so good that I might buy a second one for my husband. Definitely don't hesitate to make this purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The JBL Grip is an impressive little Bluetooth speaker that delivers much bigger sound than its compact size suggests. The JBL Pro Sound is clear, crisp, and has surprisingly deep bass, making it perfect for listening to music at home, outdoors, or on the go.The ambient light feature is a nice touch and adds a fun atmosphere without being distracting. Pairing with my phone was quick and easy, and the Bluetooth connection has been reliable. The orange color also stands out and gives the speaker a unique, stylish look.Overall, this is a well-built, portable speaker with excellent sound quality, easy connectivity, and a fun design. If you're looking for a compact Bluetooth speaker that's easy to carry and sounds great, the JBL Grip is definitely worth considering."
    },
    {
        "review": "I LOVE this speaker. I typically don't purchase higher-end products (because I'm quite the cheapskate) but I am SO glad I chose to indulge in this JBL Grip. It is totally worth the extra money spent. I got the red design, and it has a very sleek and clean design. The buttons on it are straightforward and responsive. Also, this thing is LOUD. I had it on about half volume, and it had my music loud enough to fill my entire bedroom, and even loud enough to make my family hear it from outside my room. Not only is it loud, but the sound quality is super rich and incredibly clear. This speaker is the perfect weight and is small enough to fit in a cup-holder, but still has such a strong enough speaker to pack a big punch! Also, it has about 4 different light-settings for the back of the speaker, which I love! This speaker is perfect for me, and totally worth it. The only downside is that it does NOT come with its own USB-c charger which is a little unfortunate since this speaker only has around a 12-hour battery life, but for how good of a speaker this is, I honestly can't complain that much."
    },
    {
        "review": "Easy to hook up to phones. Sound is clear and good volume. Love it and not to big to care around."
    },
    {
        "review": "Prior to this purchase, I had owned three other Bluetooth speakers.The first was Anker. A cheap speaker that sounded meh and became tinny.And, TWO PulseSound speakers that tore after a bit of base.This JBL speaker sounds AMAZING but the battery life SUCKS. While I was waiting for this to arrive, I was using my Anker speaker, which I didn’t have a charger for, and it played for about three days straight with no charge. The JBL barely lasts 12 hours before it needs a charge.It’s a small price to pay for a quality Bluetooth speaker that sounds as good as this one does."
    },
    {
        "review": "This JBL Grip speaker is a solid little portable unit. The sound is clean, the waterproof build makes it easy to take anywhere, and the ambient light adds a nice touch. The battery life holds up well, and the size makes it perfect for quick grab‑and‑go use. Just a dependable mini speaker that does exactly what it should."
