        "review": "I picked up the JBL Charge 6 on discount and it ended up being well worth it. I use it daily in a busy garage, and for its size, the speaker gets impressively loud while still keeping the sound clear. The bass is solid at lower volumes, and although it drops slightly as you push the volume higher, it never sounds distorted — JBL clearly prioritized sound quality over forcing too much low end.One thing I really like is the auto-shutoff feature. If no music plays for about 20–30 minutes, the speaker turns itself off to save battery. Since I often get distracted at work, this is actually super convenient.Battery life is excellent. At higher volume with decent bass, I get around 7 hours of playback. At normal listening levels, it easily lasts my entire 10-hour shift without needing a recharge.Overall, the Charge 6 is a great portable speaker with strong sound, good clarity, and impressive durability. Perfect for workspaces or anyone needing reliable all-day music."
