        "review": "I had a complicated issue with an older TV needing a Bluetooth transmitter. I chose the DUDGSIS Portable Bluetooth Speaker for its reliability in Bluetooth connection and its small size. After sorting out the TV and Bluetooth Transmitter, I was rewarded for my choice in DUDGSIS because it connected immediately. I was further rewarded in finding that it has a great sound and good volume (especially for a smaller unit). This is a great unit and a solution for use of a remote speaker that is simple to set up and works the first time. Lastly, it’s a great price for what you are getting."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m a group fitness instructor at a busy gym, and I teach high-energy classes like HIIT and bootcamp. My speaker is on for about four hours straight every morning, and it needs to handle a room full of wireless interference: Apple Watches, wireless earbuds, fitness trackers, even other small Bluetooth speakers. The X2 cuts through all of that like it’s nothing. I leave my phone at the front of the studio, then walk to the back row to check squat form, grab weights by the windows, step outside to get water. The music never skips, never stutters, never drops. Not once in over 30 classes. The sound quality matters too. I need the beat to be crisp so my class can follow along, and the bass needs to punch through without getting muddy. The X2 delivers. My students can hear every count clearly even at the back of the room. And the IPX7 waterproofing has been a lifesaver: sweat, spilled water bottles, even a rogue splash from someone’s hydro flask. Just wipe and go. For any fitness instructor or personal trainer working in a busy wireless environment, the X2’s Bluetooth is a workhorse. It doesn’t get overwhelmed. And the sound and waterproofing make it perfect for the gym. Class after class, it just delivers without any drama."
    },
    {
        "review": "Surprisingly good sound in a small package for a great price. This has surprising richness to the sound and gets fairly loud. I don't need earth shattering decibels so for me, it's perfect. I can hear it over the vacuum. I also love that it has aux input since I try to reduce my exposure to Bluetooth. Although, it does have Bluetooth too should I want it. It's got good battery life, charges fast, and is small so I can easily bring it around with me."
    },
    {
        "review": "Surprisingly good sound quality considering the pint sized speaker. Unfortunately the size really limits the size of the battery you can get inside so the battery life is pretty terrible. In my case thats not a big deal because I am usually using them indoors and plugged in all the time. but if you are looking for a portable battery powered solution this might not be your answer because I generally get less than an hour or run time out of a full charge. Even when the battery is still showing 2 of 4 bars of battery and you should theoretically still have 50% battery life...I find by this point the bluetooth struggles to stay connected and I either have to plug it in or constantly reconnect the bluetooth. I am giving 4 stars because it suits my needs and the sound quality os good for the price and size. but if I were using this as my primary portable speaker I would probably give it 3 stars or possibly even less."
    },
    {
        "review": "I do livestreams on Twitch and YouTube ,mostly gaming, sometimes just chatting with my audience. I like to use a Bluetooth speaker for background music and sound alerts so I don’t have to wear headphones for four hours straight. The X2 has been perfect. I’ve done over 20 streams with it, each 3-4 hours long, and the Bluetooth has never dropped once. It connects to my streaming PC in about two seconds every time. No noticeable audio delay either. But here’s something I didn’t expect , the RGB lights are actually great for streams. I placed it behind the monitor, and viewers keep commenting on how cool the setup looks. It adds a little something to the visual without being distracting. I’ve also spilled energy drink on it twice during late-night streams, and the IPX7 waterproofing meant I just wiped it off and kept going. No damage. Battery easily lasts through my longest streams. For any streamer, podcaster, or content creator who needs reliable wireless audio, the X2 is a hidden gem."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this little unit to replace my other bluetooth speaker I got years ago after the battery couldn't hold a charge anymore. But the one I had didn't exist anymore.This one works decently. It's sound quality is decent. It has pretty good volume and clarity, but is a little lacking in bass in the genres I listen to. (Rock, Metal, Alternative) It's hard to describe, because the bass is still audible, but it just is as full to be perfect. But for it's small size and price, I think it's still decent.The bluetooth has worked flawlessly so far, and the LED light is cool. It has two modes where it's just on, or it tries to react and animate to music, which is cool for more rhythmic songs. Or you can just turn it off. I would have liked to have been able to just change the color to a single color, but it's forced to be rainbow. Just a small feature I would have preferred, but that doesn't affect it functionally.I mainly use this in the bathroom while I shower. And that hasn't been an issue. I haven't gotten too much water on it, but it seems fine in that area.Overall I really like this unit, and still give it five starts, even if it could have some minor improvements."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m a professional gardener. I work outdoors in all kinds of conditions: full sun, light rain, high humidity, wind — you name it. I use this speaker around six to seven hours a day, five days a week, in a pretty harsh environment. Before getting the X2, I went through two other “durable” speakers in less than a year. I bought the X2 five months ago mainly because it was affordable, and it’s still going strong.It has been splashed with water countless times, fallen off my truck tailgate onto gravel, dropped in mud twice, knocked off workbenches onto concrete pavers, and left in a hot truck cab for entire afternoons. It’s also covered in potting soil and fertilizer dust on a regular basis.Thanks to its IPX7 waterproof rating, I never worry about rain or splashes from the hose. I simply rinse it off at the end of each day, and it works perfectly. For a speaker built for outdoor use, the sound quality is surprisingly good. I can hear my music clearly even over the noise from my leaf blower and hedge trimmer. There is no distortion or crackling, even at higher volumes.The battery still lasts a full workday. It easily runs for seven hours before I need to recharge it. The rubber casing has plenty of scuffs, but there are no cracks at all. The charging port cover still seals tightly after being opened hundreds of times with dirty, dusty hands.If you work outdoors — in landscaping, farming, construction or similar fields — the X2 is the real deal. It’s not fancy or pricey; it’s just reliable. Rain or shine, it holds up and gets the job done, and it sounds great while doing it. That’s exactly what I need."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wow! I’m genuinely impressed by both this speaker and the level of customer support I received. Easily a 5-star experience.My first unit unfortunately arrived with a defect. Right out of the box, it paired successfully with my devices, but within seconds of playback, the audio would begin skipping, produce static interference, and occasionally cut out completely before reconnecting. The speaker also became noticeably warm during use. After troubleshooting with multiple devices and confirming the issue wasn’t related to Bluetooth compatibility, I contacted Dudgsis support.Their response was prompt, professional, and solution-oriented. The support representative was incredibly understanding and efficient. There was no back-and-forth or unnecessary delays; they immediately arranged for a replacement unit and shipped it directly to me. The entire process was smooth and hassle-free. The replacement arrived just in time for my weekend gathering, and I’m grateful for how quickly they resolved the issue. Now that I’ve had the opportunity to use the replacement speaker, I can confidently say it performs exactly as expected.Pros: Excellent build quality with a sleek, modern design and attractive color finish. Compact and highly portable without feeling cheap or flimsy. The buttons provide good tactile feedback and are responsive without requiring excessive force. Bluetooth pairing is fast and seamless. My devices detect the speaker almost instantly, and the connection remains stable during use. The audio performance is impressive for a speaker of this size. The sound signature is well-balanced, vocals come through clearly, and the bass response is surprisingly powerful without overwhelming the mids. Even at maximum volume, the speaker maintains good clarity with minimal distortion. The RGB lighting effects are a nice touch and sync well with the music, adding to the overall experience. Battery life has been excellent so far. It charges quickly and provides hours of playback on a single charge. For such a compact speaker, the output and soundstage feel much larger than expected and easily compete with some larger portable speakers I’ve used.Cons: None so far.Overall, I’m extremely impressed with both the product and the company behind it. The replacement unit has exceeded my expectations, and the customer support experience gave me confidence in the brand. If you’re looking for a compact Bluetooth speaker with strong audio performance, solid battery life, and responsive customer service, this one is well worth considering.I look forward to using it for a long time, and hopefully it continues performing this well for years to come."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wasn't expecting much from a speaker this small — but the X2 surprised me right out of the box. After using it for over a week, here's the honest breakdown.Pros:Sound quality is genuinely impressive for the size. Clean vocals, balanced mids, and bass that actually exists (thank you, passive radiator).Gets plenty loud — I usually keep it around 60-70% and that fills the room.Battery lasts days. Charged it once when I got it, still going strong.Bluetooth 5.3 is rock solid. No drops, even when I leave my phone in another room.Lights are fun — colors cycle through at night and add a nice vibe without being tacky.Cons:The charging indicator stays on solid white when full — not a big deal, but if you want complete darkness, it's something to note.Bass definitely shows up more at higher volumes; at very low volume, it's less present (pretty standard for small speakers).Used it in the bathroom while showering, in the backyard while gardening, and on the patio for a small hangout. Handled everything. For $24, this thing is a steal. If you want portable sound that actually delivers, grab one."
    },
    {
        "review": "Has good sound and a cool light that flashes while your music plays. Took it on a fishing trip and worked great. Compact and battery lasted all day !"
    },
    {
        "review": "It's a wow!! wow!! as my impression of this small speaker. It paired with my Android phone immediately withput any hassles. Then I turned it on and was blown away with how loud it would go and still be crisp and clear . The bass is pretty impressive . I haven't played it long enough to see battery endurance but after 6 hours it was still p;saying strong. Every control is on 1 straight panel down one side with the charging port  there as well. When you press the power button ( 2 second press) it comes on and tells you what mode it is in. It lets ou pair 2 of them together to give a sterio effect. You can change the volume from the + - buttons on the front panel as well as a button to change songs . The front buttons also do other things with long presses that are explained in the included manual. It comes with a charge cable and a handy attached carry cord. If you want a small Bluetooth portable speaker with incredible sound and volume for its size and waterproof as well for a small price this is it."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "The Bose SoundLink Flex 2nd Gen puts out surprisingly rich sound for its size, and it’s tough enough to handle outdoor use without feeling delicate. Bluetooth connects fast, the battery lasts a good while, and the speaker has that clear Bose tone that works for music, podcasts, or just background noise while you’re working outside. I was looking for something portable that still sounded full, and this one delivers. For the price, it’s a solid pick if you want good audio in a small, easy‑to‑carry package."
    },
    {
        "review": "Solid purchase. About 1 month in since purchase.Pros: it’s compact, great sound quality, bass is a 4/5 and the battery life is great. It’s definitely bulky but that’s expected and there a decent heft to it which I like. It connects with my phone just fine.Cons: cord they give you is honestly short. This really isn’t much of a con cause I’m reaching but I can see why people don’t like the no-screen feature however, I personally like the fact the speaker states it’s battery life when you first turn it on."
    },
    {
        "review": "Best blue tooth speaker I've ever owned. Rivals my car stereo system (Bluetooth as well) which is also a Bose Soundsystem in my Hyundai Santa Fe. You can alter the predominance of sound in the app or on the device. Amazing dynamic range for such a small speaker system. I even like the response of the speaker to spoken audio tracks from Instagram or TikTok. Seems like it holds a charge forever. Of course the only improvement I'd make is a longer charging cord. But that seems to be the way of the world with shorter charging cables for everything. The first time I felt like I got my money's worth with this speaker's purchase. Virtually plug and play. As long as it's selling at a discount it makes it hard not to get another as a gift."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought the Bose SoundLink Flex (2nd Gen) to compare it directly against the JBL Flip 7 since they seem to be the two most popular speakers in this size category.For my ears, the Bose won.The biggest difference is the bass. The JBL has a little more punch in the mid-bass, but the Bose reaches noticeably deeper into the low end. It almost sounds like it has a tiny built-in subwoofer. That deeper bass gives music a fuller, richer sound that I really enjoy.Most of my listening is indoors in small to medium-sized rooms, and that's where the Bose really shines. Vocals are clear, instruments sound natural, and everything sounds balanced without being harsh. I found myself enjoying the music instead of focusing on what the speaker was doing.The JBL Flip 7 definitely has its strengths. It's smaller, lighter, looks better in my opinion, and is easier to throw into a backpack or even a bike bottle holder. It also projects a little better in larger rooms. If portability is your top priority, I completely understand choosing the JBL.For outdoor use, though, I don't think either speaker has enough low-end to really impress in wide-open spaces. Since the JBL's slight advantage in volume and projection wasn't enough to make a big difference outside, I preferred the Bose because it sounded so much better indoors.For reference, I came from an old Anker Soundcore Boost that finally gave up. Oddly enough, I still think the Soundcore Boost has more outright \"thump\" than either the JBL or the Bose. However, both of these speakers are much cleaner, clearer, and more refined overall.If your primary use is listening around the house, in the garage, on the patio, or in a small to medium-sized room, I think the Bose SoundLink Flex (2nd Gen) is the better-sounding speaker. If you need maximum portability for bike rides, hiking, or travel, the JBL Flip 7 may be the better fit.Neither speaker is bad, they're just tuned differently. For my listening preferences, the Bose was the easy winner, and it's the one I'm keeping."
    },
    {
        "review": "Hands down the best portable speaker for this budget. Given its compact size and weight, the volume and deep, punchy bass it puts out are truly impressive. The sound profile is rich, clear, and well-balanced even when cranked up. The companion app is fantastic—fast, responsive, and easy to use. The overall build quality and materials are top-notch throughout. Extremely satisfied with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "It was so simple to Bluetooth it to my phone. And I was surprised how loud it was for it being so small. The sound was like it was coming from a huge speaker. In true sound the power is true."
    },
    {
        "review": "Note to Amazon: This is a different product than the Bose Soundlink Plus which I've reviewed also, not the same product.I have been a Bose fan for a long time and still use my Roommate speakers, now with a Bluetooth receiver. My Chromebook speakers need help, and a Bluetooth speaker is the solution I chose, trying, first with the Bose Plus model which does not work at all with Chromebook.The Flex stays connected to the laptop when the speaker is moved from room to room. The few times I've used it on the battery, it has used about half the battery in about 2 hours of listening with the volume moderately high.Although the sound is excellent overall at the highs and midrange, the bass is too deep or muddy, and has an echo quality. The official Bose equalizer app only works with selected devices, such as Android and Apple, not with Chromebook.Depending on how you use this speaker, you may want to get a USB C to A charging cord. I keep it plugged in near my laptop, and learned that on a C to C cord and C block, the unit will not refill without replugging it, but with a C to A cord and A block, it recharges as it is used."
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazing sound! Battery life lasts all day, about 12 to 14 hours. Easy to connect to Bluetooth and other Bose Flex speakers. Quick charging. I also like the skip functions, very reliable too. Enjoyed spending time outdoors with great music!"
