[
    {
        "review": "If you're on the fence and going to read a review, read this one. After 3 years of blasting this thing at full power on every bike ride I go on, it's finally started to....get a little quieter. But it still works fine. This thing is a beast. If you wanted to see how much this can handle look no further, I got you. Bike rides through downtown Detroit, the middle of the woods, mud and dirt, rain and snow. This thing was blasting. You'd hear me before you'd see me. Probably saved my life more than I can count. The Bluetooth never has issues. The volume is super loud. I've gotten caught in torrential rain and it was chugging along the whole time while I was biking through gale force winds and sideways rain. If you want a durable and LOUD speaker that will take most things you throw at it, THIS IS THE SPEAKER. I don't write reviews like this for most things. But this speaker was 100% worth the money. It finally started to get a little quiet for the bike, so I upgraded to their X10. But this thing STILL works. I'll be using it inside for the coming years. Looking forward to giving the X10 a good review too. I love when tech is built to last and not for planned obsolescence. They don't have to do it. But they do. And I hope they make more money because they decided to make the better product instead of making money by cutting corners. Shout out to my d8 man, this thing is awesome."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this speaker! Price is in point, sound is loud and clean. I have EXOGEAR which is bada$$ but I was tired of luggin it around to pool partys, beach, lake, and room to room in my house.This hits the spot!! I play ambient soundscapes/edm/rock/hip-hop/country/jazz/classical. Great sound!I also love that it plays while charging.The green color looks slick and I love that the strap is thick and durable. The whole thing is really solid. 10/10.  It was between this and JBL. Glad i went with this for sure. You'll love it. ;)"
    },
    {
        "review": "Such an awesome portable speaker. Easy to use, charge lasts a while (6+ hrs), Bluetooth compatibility, the speaker is loud and clear, and so far it can take a tumble and continue working with no issues. The speakers a good size, no too heavy but won't blow over in the wind or off a counter. The strap is perfect for easy carry.  Great versatility. Used all the time."
    },
    {
        "review": "Just received this cool mobile, bring anywhere, long battery life, bluetooth speaker. 4 stars but not because I’m being critical about anything. I purchased the X-20 (A pair) for when I need some serious sounds to take with me to outdoor trips. So, starting with its main feature - 40 hours of battery life (from a fresh charge). This functionality  gives this model speaker advantages over other Bluetooth speakers in its category. Durability- has good weight, does not feel cheap, instead it gives you that quality feel, and priced reasonably- it’s not a cheap speaker, but instead, the makers were thoughtful about giving the consumers an opportunity to rock quality more so over just branding. It’s definitely not meant to entertain a large party and expect to fill the room or space with big sounds, however, it’s perfect for 5-6 persons sitting in a bond fire, picnic, or in the kitchen while you’re cooking. Yes, it’s equalizer function also brings you a variety of sound output for folks who want easy listening, light bass, or mid-range tweets being the dominant sound- so that’s helpful for type of genre and people with a certain ear for sounds that makes it music to their ear. I won’t thru the other basic features as I want to just communicate and focus on sound quality and durability. Overall, I do recommend this speaker if your needing to upgrade your JBL3…this W-King model will be 3 times punchier bass wise- but not heart pounding as some would exaggerate on their tik-tok. I’ve also uploaded a video to display what it looks like and sounds like at 45 percent volume level. I didn’t really select this to want to buy, it just so happened to be a bundle purchase with the T12 and priced significantly lower than when just buying the T12, so I look at it like a bonus speaker but a nice bonus speaker I can use daily for showers, and quick sounds for the outdoors without worrying about having to charge after 4 hours…one charge should last the entire day I need it for. I hoped this review covered the basics, but if you’re trying to F@ around with harder and solid sounds, I think the X20 has to be in everyone’s speaker to have. Can’t wait to review the T12 when it arrives."
    },
    {
        "review": "Mainly use in our pottery (so system and moisture), but recently started bringing it with me in my UTV trail riding. Super impressed by the quality sound, ease of Bluetooth, and ruggedness. Oh, if you use your phone to stream, use the phones equalizer and you can get even more our of the speaker."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've owned this W-King for over a year now and it still works GREAT! Sound quality is EXCELLENT!It's much bigger than a popular and cheaper portable speaker on Amazon as shown in my picture.This W-King is so good that you can actually use it as a TV Speaker. If your TV has analog out (headphone jack) then you can simply connect the W-King with a headphone jack cable and voila! You will just need to have a USB charger nearby to supply power, yes it works while charging.It works great for watching movies or playing video games. The audio quality for the price is unbeatable. Like I said I've owned it for a year and it's worked great and have no doubt it will last a very long time.Hope this helps!"
