[
    {
        "review": "I was concerned they wouldn’t be that great after seeing the box they came in, but they’re actually beautiful and great quality! The rippled texture look is beautiful and eye catching, the wood grain on the handles feels great and luxury. And they’re super sharp! I haven’t used the sharpener yet but they seem like they’ll hold up. Overall it’s a great value."
    },
    {
        "review": "​I am really happy with this 15-piece knife set so far! I was looking for an upgrade for my kitchen, and this set has exceeded my expectations in both looks and performance.​Here is what stands out the most to me:​Distinctive Aesthetics: These knives look absolutely fantastic. I really enjoy the hammered finish on the blades—it gives them a unique, high-end look that stands out beautifully on the counter in the wooden block.​Perfect Weight and Feel: They don't just look nice; they feel great to hold. Every knife is nicely weighted and balanced, making them very comfortable and easy to control during prep work.​Excellent Sharpness: Out of the box, these are very sharp. The high-carbon stainless steel cuts effortlessly, and knowing the block has a self-sharpening feature gives me peace of mind that they'll stay that way. The included steak knives are also a fantastic addition.​Overall, this is a gorgeous and highly functional set. If you are looking for knives that are both visually striking and incredibly practical for everyday cooking, I highly recommend this collection!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Knife Block Set for Dummies! LOL 😂Beautiful knife block set and it's definitely idiot proof. I mean it's perfect! Each knife 🔪 is stamped with what type of knife it is as well as the top of the wooden block. Great idea. That way you will always know which knife goes into which slot, also, the font on the wooden block is very stylish. The blades are made of High German Carbon Stainless Steel 'Made in China' 😂.The other thing I love about it is that it matches the wooden handle of my coffee pot perfectly. I also like the straight, upright design, it gives you more room on the countertop and it won't block the view of my cute distressed nesting crate. As I always say \"It's all about the Looks\" LOL I also love the black blades. The packaging is amazing, each knife was individually wrapped in 2 plastic sleeves with a plastic protective cap on the tip of the knife. Like I said: \"Idiot proof!\" LOL 😂 Only drawback about the design is that I will either have to tilt it or move it out from under the cupboards in order to take them out. Unlike other blocks that have a slanted angle, however, they also take up more space. Tried the Chef's knife for the first time last night to slice some chicken tenders and you won't even have to slice the meat. Just push the knife down the meat falls apart. Be careful, they (at least the one I tried) are as sharp as a razor, if not sharper.I Love It!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like this knife set overall. The knives work well, look nice, and get the job done. My only real issue was with quality control. I received one too many of the same knife, and instead of getting the different knife that was supposed to be included, I ended up with seven of the same style instead of six. It’s not a huge problem, but it’s definitely something the company should pay more attention to.I also wish the color was a little deeper brown, and the spacing in the block/setup seems slightly off. That said, they’re still good knives and functional for everyday use. I do think they’re priced a little higher than they should be, but overall it’s still a nice set."
    },
