[
    {
        "review": "I have wanted these Henckels knives for a long time and finally got the opportunity during a Prime Day sale.I can't say enough good things about these knives. They are sharp so be careful! Compared to the dull knives I used before, there is no comparison. These knives easily slice through everything I use them for, mostly meat and veggies. This set contains every type of knife I need, including scissors and a sharpener.I will not allow these beautiful knives to sit in soapy water or the dishwasher, therefore I can't speak to how well they will hold up over time to rusting. I am relying exclusively on the well-regarded reputation of the manufacturer.Overall, I gave these knives 5-stars because of the quality, sharpness, and ease of handling. They are sturdy and I am not concerned about rusting or degrading of the metal. This is an excellent set for the price and I'm very pleased!"
    },
    {
        "review": "You should know that when they say razor sharp, they are not kidding, My husband and I both cook and we have had our new knives about a week. Our other knife set was so dull I think that that was part of our adjustment issue. We both love this set of knives. The wooden block is beautiful and so are the knives. We highly recommend this Henckel knife set."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm pretty sure that this set I just bought is the fourth set in my lifetime. No question of which is the best set and it's the Henckels.  My, what a beautiful set of knives, with one for every need in the kitchen or at dinner. The steel is high quality and the blades are thin, a combination which is ideal for ease of use. What strikes you is the hefty handle and the slender blade, providing a great balance in the hand. And, of course, they come razor sharp and also an excellent sharpener is provided with the set. I don't think there is a competing set of knives on the market which can compare."
    },
    {
        "review": "bought these knives to prep dinner. I wasn’t expecting to enter a committed relationship.The first time I used the chef’s knife, it slid through a tomato so effortlessly that I had to look around to make sure nobody saw me smiling. The sharpness is downright scandalous. Carrots? Paper-thin. Steak? Like butter. My old knives watched from the drawer in shame.The balance is incredible, the grip feels just right in your hand, and every slice is so smooth it should probably come with a warning label. Cooking has become dangerously enjoyable. I now volunteer to chop everything. “Need onions diced?” Say less.My spouse is starting to get jealous because I’ve been spending an awful lot of quality time with this knife block. Honestly, I haven’t felt this much excitement in the kitchen in years.If you’ve never whispered, “Oh… wow,” after slicing a bell pepper, you’re about to.Five stars. Sharp enough to cut vegetables… and dangerously close to stealing my heart. ❤️🔪"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am very happy with this knife set.They arrived razor sharp.  Unfortunately, the spine is also very sharp and I keep cutting my fingers on them, thus the four star rating.I still recommend them, just be careful."
    },
    {
        "review": "These knives are perfect. A little expensive, but exactly what we needed so it is worth it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The steel is arguably soft, but that is typical of european (particularly german) blades. The iron content of this stainless steel is high and the nickel content may be low. If left wet for long, it may develop rust spots. However, you should always clean and dry a knife after using it anyway. If taken care of, these blades will last many years. They will cut what you want and retain a nice shape.The chef's knife is great. It is the primary knife used in my kitchen. It is comfortable to use, slices through most anything with relative ease. After about ten to fifteen diced onions I like to hone the blade again to keep work quick and easy. A dull knife is much more dangerous than a sharp one they say. Despite frequent maintenance, it does an excellent job and doesn't fatigue me.The santokus are of decent quality, and feel excellent for everyday tasks. The larger one has a good weight and feeling allowing for prolonged veggie extermination, and the smaller one is light and maneuverable to really slice and shape whatever you need.The paring knife is a razor blade with a handle basically. If the chef knife is too big or unwieldy for a task, the lil guy will step up with no issue.The bread knife is sharp. It WILL cut bread. Cake too, I bet.There is another smaller serrated knife but I have yet to use it.The scissors are nothing special but provide you something to open any package of food.The steak knives are beautiful but have lesser quality steel than the bigger knives. These will straight up form rust spots if left in the sink overnight, esp along the handle and spine of the blade. Just clean them after use and they should stay pretty and sharp for ya.The included file is useful to keep my blades honed.I'd say this set is a pretty solid value for your money if you are looking for a good set of knives for the kitchen. If you don't sharpen your knives or prefer a cheap kitchenaid knife, this isn't for you. For the home cook who uses their knives for everything and appreciates them, I recommend them."
    },
    {
        "review": "great product. perfect cutting. nice heavy storage block for the knives. easy to wash i hand wash them. i love the handles."
    },
    {
        "review": "Meets all the situations we need, especially meat"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good value and quality. Sharp"
