[
    {
        "review": "Very nice. Sharp. Replacing my big wusthoff knife set I had for 30 years."
    },
    {
        "review": "The HOSHANHO 20-Piece Knife Set is a comprehensive kitchen collection designed to cover considerably more cutting tasks than a basic starter set. With multiple knife styles, a storage block, sharpening tool, and other commonly used pieces, the set is geared toward someone who wants a coordinated collection rather than purchasing individual knives separately. The large assortment provides plenty of versatility for everyday meal preparation, although not every household will necessarily need all 20 pieces.One of the first things that stands out is the presentation. Having the knives organized together in a dedicated block creates a clean, coordinated appearance on the countertop while keeping the blades stored more safely than leaving them loose in a drawer. The block also makes it convenient to see and access the different knives while cooking. Of course, a set this large requires a reasonable amount of counter space, so that is worth considering if you have a smaller kitchen.The variety of knives is one of the strongest aspects of the set. Rather than relying on a single chef's knife for nearly every task, having different blade sizes and shapes makes it easier to choose an appropriate tool for the job. A larger chef-style knife is useful for chopping vegetables and general food preparation, while smaller knives provide better control for peeling, trimming, and more detailed work. Specialized blades can also make tasks such as slicing bread or preparing meat easier and more efficient.Out of the box, the cutting edges feel sharp and perform well for normal kitchen preparation. Slicing vegetables, chopping herbs, cutting fruit, and preparing meat require relatively little pressure when using the appropriate knife. A sharp knife is generally easier to control than forcing a dull blade through food, but the sharpness also means these knives should be handled carefully, especially when washing and storing them.The handles are another important part of the overall experience. They have an ergonomic shape that provides a comfortable and reasonably secure grip during typical cutting tasks. Balance can feel different from one knife to another because of variations in blade length and weight, but the primary knives feel manageable during extended food preparation. Comfort is somewhat subjective, particularly for people with very large or small hands, but the overall design should work well for many users.Including a sharpener is a practical addition because even a good kitchen knife eventually requires maintenance. Initial sharpness is only part of evaluating a knife set; maintaining the cutting edge over time is equally important. Regular honing or sharpening when appropriate can help keep the knives performing consistently instead of waiting until they become noticeably dull.The large number of pieces is both an advantage and a potential drawback. For someone setting up a kitchen from scratch, having a broad assortment in one matching set is convenient. It eliminates the need to immediately purchase additional knives for different tasks. On the other hand, experienced cooks who already rely primarily on two or three favorite knives may find that some pieces receive very little use. Whether 20 pieces represents useful variety or unnecessary excess will depend largely on individual cooking habits.The storage block helps address organization by giving each piece a designated location. This protects the edges from contacting other utensils and reduces clutter in kitchen drawers. It is still important to insert and remove the knives carefully rather than dragging the cutting edges unnecessarily against the block.Maintenance is another area worth considering. Regardless of material claims, quality kitchen knives benefit from careful cleaning and drying. I prefer hand washing knives individually and drying them promptly rather than leaving them wet or allowing them to remain in a sink with other utensils. This also helps protect the cutting edges from unnecessary contact with harder objects. Following the manufacturer's specific care instructions should provide the best chance of maintaining both appearance and performance over time.Another positive aspect is the coordinated appearance of the complete set. Everything looks intentional when displayed together rather than appearing like a random collection accumulated over several years. This also makes the set potentially appealing as a housewarming, wedding, or holiday gift for someone who cooks regularly or is setting up a new kitchen.There are a few considerations before choosing such a large set. The knife block occupies permanent countertop space, and buyers with limited room should check the available area before deciding where to place it. A large assortment also does not automatically mean every knife will be equally useful to every cook. Additionally, the included sharpener is convenient, but proper sharpening technique still matters to avoid removing unnecessary material or changing the blade edge incorrectly.It is also worth setting realistic expectations regarding the term “professional.” While this set provides a broad selection and performs well for normal home food preparation, professional preferences vary considerably. Some experienced cooks prefer selecting individual knives based on specific blade geometry, weight, handle design, and steel characteristics rather than purchasing a complete matching set. For the average home kitchen, however, the convenience of having a wide selection readily available is likely to be the bigger advantage.Overall, the HOSHANHO 20-Piece Knife Set provides a comprehensive assortment for chopping, slicing, trimming, and other everyday food preparation tasks. The knives arrive with sharp cutting edges, the ergonomic handles are comfortable to use, and the included block keeps the collection organized and accessible. The sharpener is also a useful addition for ongoing maintenance.The main considerations are the amount of counter space required and whether you actually need such a large assortment of knives. For someone starting with very few kitchen knives or wanting to replace a mismatched collection with one coordinated set, the variety and organization are appealing. For cooks who already have several preferred knives, some pieces may be redundant. Taken as a complete package, however, this is a versatile kitchen knife set that offers plenty of options for everyday cooking while providing convenient storage and a consistent overall design."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is going to be a long review due to the number of items in this set, but I'll jump ahead and say this is an EXCELLENT knife set with many well-crafted knives and accessories that all fit in a great looking wood block. It is absolutely worth the price, and I would recommend this to anyone. It would make a great housewarming gift or a present for the budding chef.The set comes with a heavy wood block holder that fits on a kitchen counter. The block is pretty big, but it can hold all 19 items included in this kit. The wood is a dense laminated wood that has been stained a medium brown color. It is quite heavy and unlikely to move around, specially since there are four rubber pads on the bottom that keep it from sliding.I've reviewed many Hoshanho knives in the past and have found them to be nicely priced and well made. This set comes with 16 knives in their Loong series. The Loong knives are made with a matte finished stainless steel blades attached to dark colored Pakkawood handles. The transition from the blade to the handles are smooth, I cannot feel an edge in the transition. The heel has a metal cap and the transition from wood to cap is also very smooth. Each knife is super sharp and maintains their sharpness over time, I've had some Hoshanho knives for over a year now and I've not had to sharpen them at all, I just use a strop after every use and a steel every once in a while. Each knife is easy to clean and will last many years of normal use; I can easily see passing these knives to my children, they are that good.Each knife is individually wrapped in plastic with a thick paper sheath to prevent damage during shipping. All the knives are then bubble wrapped and placed in a cardboard box which is then encased in the outer box that is suitable for gifting. I like this extra touch because I've ordered other knives that have poked thru the outer box due to insufficient packaging causing a dangerous situation.There are six steak knives in the set. Each knife has serrations about two-thirds of the length of the blade, the back third of the blade is not serrated. The beveling is on one side only, that is true for the entire cutting surface, serrations and straight edge. Each has a nice weight to it and curvature of the handle makes it easy to handle and feels secure in your hand.There are eight straight edged knives in different lengths. There is an 8-inch chef knife, an 8-inch carving, a 7-inch Nakiri, a 7-inch Santoku, a 7-inch filet/boning knife, a 6-inch utility knife, a 3-3/4-inch paring knife and a 2-3/4-inch peeling knife. These are perfect for general kitchen use. Each is evenly weighted and feels very balanced in my hands.The Nakiri and Santoku knives are the perfect chopper and all-around cutting knives. There are small dimples on both sides, about one-third up from the blade edge, that keeps food from sticking to the knife. The curved blades allows for smooth rocking motion for chopping. It has a nice weight and balance, and I find I use the Santoku knife more than any others.The 7-inch filet knife is the weakest knife Hoshanho makes, IMO. It is too thick and therefore not flexible enough for fileting fish. It's more designed for deboning chicken or meat.There is an 8-inch serrated bread knife. Like the steak knives, the edge is a single bevel. It too is heavy, but a lot of the weight is toward the heel, which makes it super easy and comfortable to use. There is also a 5-inch serrated tomato knife that is perfect for slicing thin-skinned fruits and vegetables without crushing them.Also in the kit is a pair of kitchen scissors that are very strong and can cut through just about anything you are likely to encounter in a typical home kitchen. There is a large carving fork, perfect for holding turkeys or large pieces of meat while carving. Finally, there is a very nice steel for honing the knives back to super sharpness. If you are serious about maintaining the sharpness, I would recommend buying a leather strop as this keeps it sharper than the steel IMO. For those new to sharpening, do NOT use the steel on any of the serrated knives as it may damage the edge.BTW, the $500 price, as of the time of this review, may seem high but if you divide that by the 20 pieces in this set, that comes out to just $25 for each item, which is an excellent deal IMO."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm a huge fan of HOSHANHO products, and this set has impressed me more than than any of their other products. First off, just the quality of HOSHANHO knives is enough to justify the price. But they go the extra mile to ensure that these knives are as beautiful as they are useful. I've never seen a prettier knife set. Like all of the HOSHANHO knives I've owned, these came as sharp as I expected, which is to say they are one notch below using a lightsaber to cut your food. Maybe not even a full notch below.This set does a spectacular job of packing in a ridiculous amount of knives and tools to cover pretty much everything you would ever need in the kitchen, while keeping the footprint extremely small. Speaking of footprints, the block has feet and doesn't just sit directly on your countertop, which I like in case you spill something close to it you don't have to worry about the wood getting wet.Each one of these knives feels great in your hand. The weight and balance of these knives are perfect, and they are comfortable to use and easy to control, which is great because you need to be able to control a knives that are this crazy sharp.I'm not sure I've ever used any of these knives without laughing at how easily they cut through whatever it is I'm using them for. I thought I had good knives before these, but I was obviously wrong. The quality and durability of these knives is just outstanding.These knives are the only exception I make to the dishwasher rule that if it doesn't live through the dishwasher I don't want it in my kitchen. I enjoy using these knives so much that I have no problem washing them by hand and would do it that way even if they were dishwasher safe just to maintain the beauty.I really can't recommend this knife set or the HOSHANHO brand highly enough!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is an extraordinarily complete, high-quality kitchen knife set. The blades, handles, balance, fit and finish are all excellent, and the 20-piece collection provides a specialized knife for just about every cutting task you're likely to encounter.The high-carbon stainless steel blades are incredibly sharp. The 15-degree edges cut with remarkably little effort and provide the kind of precision normally associated with much more expensive individual knives.That sharpness does require some respect. These are substantially sharper than the typical household kitchen knife, so use good technique and don't become casual about handling them. Very little pressure is required to make a cut.What distinguishes this set from smaller collections is the selection. In addition to the expected chef, bread, utility, santoku and paring knives, you get carving, nakiri, fillet, tomato and fruit knives, six steak knives, a meat fork, kitchen shears and a sharpener. Everything stores neatly in the substantial wood block.The pakkawood handles are comfortable, attractive and well balanced, while the entire set has the appearance of professional-quality cutlery.At the full listed price this is a significant investment, although discounts can substantially change the value proposition. Comparable premium Japanese-style knives can cost hundreds of dollars individually, so getting such a comprehensive collection at a discounted price represents excellent value.Beautifully made, extraordinarily sharp, and about as complete a kitchen knife collection as anyone could reasonably need. Highly recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "These knives are really sharp, and that is what stands out immediately. I had never owned this type of knife set before, so I was expecting there to be a learning curve with care and maintenance, but the performance has been excellent so far.What impressed me most is how well they have held their sharpness after repeated use. I am getting ready to start maintaining them with a whetstone, but even before that, they have stayed sharp enough to make prep work feel much easier. Cutting through food feels cleaner and smoother than what I am used to with more basic kitchen knives.The main adjustment for me is the care. I am used to just throwing knives in the dishwasher, and that is not something I would do with these. They require more attention, hand washing, and proper handling if you want to keep them in good shape.That said, the tradeoff has been worth it. The blades are sharp, the set looks great, and the difference in cutting performance is noticeable. If you are willing to take better care of them, this is a really nice knife set."
    },
    {
        "review": "the top of their line will satisfy the most demanding kitchen knife nut (which is to say, me) and one of their knives has become my primary go-to knife every day, but this set is a lot less high end than that one ... it's much lighter weight, the handles are comfortable enough but the knives just have less heft and the blades are very very sharp (as all new knives are) but don't have the momentum in action to power through slicing resistant materials with ease the way their high end blades do...the balance is not what my favorite knife reflects, but again these aren;'t designed to compete with itstill, this is an incredibly complete set and we got it for our second home, for which it is a perfect match; and the block has a ton of knives in a very efficient footprint ... at the full listed price it's probably more than I'd ever think of spending for the use I'm putting these to, but at the coupon price of half price it's a very decent value"
    },
    {
        "review": "I already own many knives from HOSHANHO—including several from this specific line—and I love every single one of them. You can truly never have too many knives when prep work starts, and this 20-piece set filled in a lot of gaps for me. It includes several blades I didn't have yet, plus different variations of ones I did (for example, the steak knives in this set are serrated, whereas my previous set had straight edges).Beyond the impressive variety of specialty knives, you also get a serving fork, kitchen shears, and a sharpener all housed together. Performance-wise, these knives are ungodly sharp. They glide through food with zero effort.The handles are comfortable, well-balanced, and feel great in the hand during extended prep work.The wooden block itself is heavy, stable, and has two really smart design features:Pass-through slots: The knife holes go all the way through the bottom of the block, preventing crumbs or moisture from getting trapped inside, making it much cleaner and easier to maintain.Angled slot faces: The angled surfaces on the block line up flush with the bolsters on the knives, giving it a sleek, custom-fitted look on the counter.Another absolute home run from HOSHANHO!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "What can I say? I mean, I absolutely love these knives. I love everything Dalstrong. Ever since I purchased my first Dalstrong product, which I believe was a pair of cooking tweezers, I have been obsessed with their website & subsequently their knives & such. Yes, they are a bit on the pricey side, HOWEVER, they are MORE than WORTH every single DOLLAR you invest. Take the time to visit their website, look at their videos, YouTube, Instagram, etc.; do your research. See for yourselves just how much time, effort, and dedication they put into creating their products. Their knife series' are not only creative but aesthetically appealing & they actually get the job done. They are strong, durable beautiful knives. If I had enough space in my house, I would collect them all! They are sharp right out of the box & they work so smoothly & make life just so much easier in the kitchen. I love to cook. I enjoy all the chopping, cutting, etc. I can spend hours in the kitchen cooking & I would be in heaven & having Dalstrong products to help me along the way just makes it that much more enjoyable for me. Please do yourself a favor. If you love cooking as much as I do, invest in a set of good quality durable knives that will last you a lifetime. I am not done yet. I am still aiming for the Shogun collection. Luckily I have 2 kitchens in my house so I have an excuse to get a second set of high-quality knives. Dalstrong is my go-to & I highly recommend them to all you home cooks & professional chefs as well since some professional chefs are already taking advantage of these amazing quality knives. And lets not forget about the hunters, fishermen, butchers, etc., they have knives for everyone. I can't brag about their products enough. You just gotta go check out their website. But be prepared to spend hours on your computer because once I got on, I could not stop window shopping. My wish list just keeps growing every day. Yes, I visit their website at least once a day. I am not exaggerating... I give them 10 out of 10 stars THANK YOU FOR CARING DALSTRONG FAMILY!"
    },
    {
        "review": "So far I love this set. The packaging alone for this set was impressive. They are well balanced and solid. Comfortable in the hand just slid through the vegetables and meat I have done so far. Extremely sharp and they look great. I will update when I have used them longer but so far I am very happy. I dont think I could have done better in this price range."
    },
    {
        "review": "Since you're looking at this particular set, I'm going to guess you've probably set a limit to how much you want to spend on what's likely going to be your every day set of knives.You might own more expensive (and arguably better) knives, but you’d rather not see them used by anyone who is not as concerned as you are with their integrity and longevity.You’ve also seen first hand the difference between the Wusthof Gourmet series and the classic Wusthof, and you also know Henkel doesn’t quite cut it.If I guessed right and you’re considering buying this set for these or similar reasons, do not hesitate: buy it right now!These knives are a cut above your usual value knife sets. Cool, sexy looks, sharp blades that stay sharp, full tang, well balanced overall, sturdy but ergonomic handles with no sharp lines. They even sound great - you know, that tuning fork ring they make if you just give them a gentle tap - so it’s really easy to pick up the right knife with eyes closed if you have perfect pitch! :PEverything most knives in this price range aren’t.I actually ended up liking these knives so much I now use them more often than my Global set. This is not to say the Globals are not the superior knives, it’s just that these Dalstrong knives are *perfectly fine* for most things someone who cooks for pleasure and not for a living will find themselves using them for.I will say that one of the knives I received had a small flaw - a crack in the side of the handle that looks like it occurred on riveting. I contacted Dalstrong support. Three days later I had the replacement. No runaround, no BS. They looked at the pictures I sent and just replied asking for my shipping address. Honestly, how often does that happen?(Thanks Rachelle for the terrific customer support experience!)You may rest assured that whatever issue you have with the product, they’ll make it right. I believe other reviews mentioned the awesome customer support as well, and I can confirm these guys really stand by their product.After the very positive experience with this set, I do think I’ll try some of their more premium knives soon (they’re still not even close to premium-priced).In short: These are value-priced knives that have none (or close to none) of the shortcomings you’d expect for the price, while blowing some of the established choices out of the water in some regards. Certainly the modern, streamlined looks will strike some conversations (yes, I know, that’s highly subjective)."
    },
    {
        "review": "I received the Dalstrong Gladiator knife set a couple of weeks ago and I am very pleased with this purchase. I am not a professional chef, nor do I play one on TV, but I do enjoy cooking and good tools make the process that much more enjoyable.Whenever I see an item on line that interests me, I always read the reviews starting with the worst ratings first. There aren’t many for this product, which was a good sign, and those that were there didn’t appear to be major issues. The 85% of 5 star reviews should give a good indication of the level of customer satisfaction.I’ve used various knives from the set (not all yet) every day since getting them. My observations are they are very well designed with a pleasing appearance, they are well crafted and well balanced, they feel good in the hand and are easy to handle, and they are sharp. With the quality steel used in the design I imagine these knives should last a very long time with minimal maintenance.Some comments spoke of shoddy workmanship on the wood handles or fittings. I did not find this to be the case as all the handles match up to the metal tang of the blade perfectly. The mounting block is a fine piece of woodwork and I can see no issues with it. It is big and heavy, but I’ve received compliments on it from friends.I agree with one other post that recommended not using a green pad to clean the knives, or any knives for that matter. I also never put knives through the dishwasher and occasionally wipe them down with cooking oil to maintain the surface. But that’s me.I did not comment on durability as I have had this set for a minimal amount of time. I would be surprised if they failed to deliver over the long haul and will comment further should they not.Overall, this set is aesthetically pleasing and does very well what it is supposed to do. I highly recommend this Dalstrong set."
    },
    {
        "review": "First, we could not be more pleased with this 18 piece \"Gladiator\" set of knifes; across the board the appearance, craftsmanship, weight/balance, sharpness, and block (which is huge BTW) are all top shelf!  Further, I can honestly tell you all that I have never written a product review before so that should tell you that I am really impressed.  Disclaimer/Quality: I must admit I have never owned a high quality set of knives before (thought a Faberware Set in a block was high quality--NOT!), but I cannot imagine a better set of knives for the novice/wannabe Chef's like my Fiance' and I.  Until we got this set, we never really thought about using different types of knives for the various areas of cooking/prepping in the kitchen.  Our AHA moment came when we discovered/realized that using the right type of knife for the job, and the reasons why, make all the difference--I assure you it does!  So much so, that we now have the picture and description that Dalstrong provided taped up over the block and give each other a hard time if either of us use the wrong knife for the task.  :o)  Price/Value:  In my opinion, even at $399.00, it truly is an amazing price for a potentially lifetime set of knives.  So you know, we also ordered the Gladiator series Meat Cleaver with the set.  All I can say about this meat cleaver is Holy $#!%!  I took one look at this thing and immediately thought it should be registered as a lethal weapon!  Not only is it extremely well crafted and gorgeous, this thing is very big, razor sharp and weighs a ton--I told my Fiance' that I needed to start working out just to be able to wield it properly.  Bottom Line:  Great job Dalstrong--Keep up the great work and reasonable price points--I am already looking for more Gladiator Series knives."
    },
    {
        "review": "Received the set today. With that in mind, I’m writing the review about the individual set that I got, not the Dalstrong product line.Delivery:The knives came individually wrapped and tip-protected. The set split between 3 boxes, the block and 2 boxes packed with knives. All neatly packed. Each knife, as I said, with a plastic tip protector, sheathed in cardboard and wrapped in bubble wrap. In my case, observing the packaging that I received, it’s beyond me how could anyone cut their fingers to the bone unwrapping, as some reviewers said they did.Construction:Superb. Simply superb. No lose parts, no unfinished surfaces. I’m not sure where other reviewers found “sharp edges”, in mynindividual case - superb construction.Block: again, having read other reviews I was expecting sloppy glue job, cracks in the block etc. What I received is far from that - a superb block. Yes, the logo is plastic. I don’t care. The block is hard wood. Nicely finished. Period. The socket for the sharpening iron is a bit through - that’s what gives you the clue, it’s wood. Not plastic glued witn veneer. It is solid wood.Balance. I’m not a professional, rather an amateur chef, but I cook for the family of 5 a lot. And I mean it - a LOT. I love it and yo me working with a good tool in the kitchen is as important as cooking a lamb kabob to juiciest perfection. These knives are very well balanced. The 8” chef just asks to put it in action right away - the weight of the knife is right there, comfortably fit in your hand. I chopped up 3 onions with it just for the pleasure of the experience. Bagged the onion - will put it to a good use tomorrow. Again, right out of the box, the knives that matter are reasonably sharp (and not excessively), offer good balance and are nice looking tools all around.Bottom lime: great delivery. Great packaging. Awesome set. I cannot speak for the long term performance just yet. Having read some other reviews that claim that the blades developed rust, I resolved to hard washing and wiping the blades with a lightly oiled paper towel. Something I do anyway. Will update if detwct any issues going forward. That’s why I keep the “durability” section vacant our now."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this set 9 years ago. After using them thrice daily cooking for a family of five they're still great!I have obviously sharpened them, several times, over the years, but the handles and block still look good.The honing tool also works well between sharpening sessions.The knives are well balanced and the grips are a comfortable shape and size.No rust has ever occurred on the knives, but I always clean and dry them quickly after use.I wish this set came with a carving fork, but I didn't know that it I wanted that 9 years ago."
    },
    {
        "review": "OK guys hello! And welcome to my review!I will inform you that I purchased a white set 18 piece block and upon arrival it was like any other Amazon package. I read the reviews and was quite amazed at some reactions. I have only owned them for 3 weeks so far, no I have not ridden over them, jumped on them or thrown them off the roof and had them break.....I unpacked them and the block from the boxes and the knives were sharp enough to cut my arm hair with just grazing them. That was a pretty good start.The block itself is very smooth, nice wood cuts. Love the finish on it and fits on the counter with finesse.Once I set the block up I was eager to try out the knives. The ergonomics of the these knives are great, they fit well. Smooth, not bulky, and easy to adhere to. Tried the 🍅 test with the chef knife and it passed, the paper test needed some more testing but they are great.I have used the slicing knife for chicken and brisket, I have used the chef knife for all my general slicing, steak knives for steak and they are all.performing above the expectation for the price!.This set is a must have for your kitchen, seriously authentically pleasing, comfortable, and great to use.One con is they shouldn't go into the dishwasher and that they have to be cleaned and dried. They shouldn't be left in the sink for too long.So overall I would recommend these knives to intermediate/ expert level cooks just for daily house hold cooking and outings. Though you do need to sharpen them after a week of use. Easy to sharpen though. They recommend a whet stone from their shop, but the rod works fine."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this product (on promotion) and the quality of Gladiator knives is high with exceptional sharpness and hardness. I would never have spent the sum of €1000 requested at the start...The set of knives is homogeneous with 3 rivets on the handles and a magnificent finish. The maintenance of the knives and the quality of the handles is top of the range with a lifetime guarantee. The walnut block is also magnificent but we had to return the whole thing because the wooden block was split. Unfortunately, this is not a recurring problem with this type of block. We returned the product and took a Dalstrong set with 6 knives for a less imposing magnetic wooden storage for 12 knives. Besides, we can see the knives all the time, which is more practical and nicer. The knives are still of a higher range (Phantom). Too bad for the wooden block, well finished with a stamp underneath. The return was hassle-free. We are really looking at real durable knives, far from what can be offered in very “pretty” sets but with poor durability."
    },
    {
        "review": "The plastic handle cracks"
    },
    {
        "review": "The first set that arrived had a minor (and I mean minor) finishing flaw which niggled at me enough to make mention of it to the seller, wow! This seller goes above and beyond in satisfying their customers, this is the sort of customer service that major companies only dream about, they are truly top tier! As for the product itself even the one with the minor flaw was good, the replacement flawless. The knives themselves I have been using for a couple of weeks or so and they are showing no signs of wear and tear, keeping a sharp edge and haven’t even needed to see a steel let alone a sharpener yet. The weight and balance is all there plus slicing through my fillet steak like it was butter even shocked me, and I’m an ex Butcher by trade. On top of that the block looks great on the worktop, even the wife was impressed after whinging about the cost lol. I would highly recommend this product and I will purchase from this company for the rest of my life so long as they keep up their standards as I was so highly impressed with the care they gave me as a customer. In fact I have already lined up my next purchase ‘the Obliterator’ cleaver which is part of this range. Honestly I am so happy...of course if the knives start showing signs of rust or ruin within an unreasonable time frame I will update this review."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great quality they feel good to use retain their sharpness for ages!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "There's not much to say, very sharp knives with a great design. Nice workmanship with no optical defects. Knives feel very comfortable in the hand.  There is also a beautiful knife block that enhances the overall picture. Great value for money for me as a hobby chef. I can't say much about durability yet. I just got the knives new. Just a note to the manufacturer/shipper: It shouldn't be so obvious what is being shipped in the box. My box was opened and sloppily taped again. It's probably just that nothing was stolen because the knife packaging was still sealed in foil."
