[
    {
        "review": "ProsExcellent camera for beginners who want to move beyond a smartphone.The two included lenses provide a lot of versatility for different types of photography.Image quality is sharp and detailed, especially in good lighting.Easy-to-use controls with room to grow as your photography skills improve.Battery life is solid and lasts through long shooting sessions.Comfortable grip and lightweight enough to carry around.Great value for those looking to get started with a DSLR system.ConsAutofocus can feel a bit dated compared to newer cameras you gotta know how to play with it.The 75-300mm lens is useful for extra reach but may not produce the sharpest results in all situations.Performance in low light isn't as strong as more modern camera models.OverallI purchased this as an entry-level DSLR, and it has been a great way to learn photography. The included lenses make it easy to experiment with different styles, from everyday shots to zoomed-in subjects. While it isn't the newest camera on the market, it still delivers great image quality and is an excellent choice for beginners."
