[
    {
        "review": "Great find.  The T7 is a perfect camera for the hobbyist...and this used one is in good shape.  We have shot more than 1,000 pics with it...closeups, action shots, etc.  Fantastic results."
    },
    {
        "review": "Canon never disappoints. The camera quality is outstanding. On top of that, the seller was very reliable and took great care with the packaging to ensure the product arrived in perfect condition. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Beginning my photography career I needed a camera that had the most features for the least amount of money, this camera is exactly that. I've used DSLR's in the past but they dont equate to this camera. One of the best qualities, is the battery life. Getting through an hour and a half of shooting (about 300 photos) and still having many more hours left on the battery is impressive. Another strong suite this camera possesses is its 24MP sensor producing sharp images and high compatibility with Canons EF and EF-S lenses.The only downsides i've noticed while using this camera is poor low-light function. I notice a lot of noise or grain when the ISO is up past 400, which decreases the photo quality. Additionally, the auto focus seems to fall behind about 15% of the time, which isn't too bad given the price. The last downside is when using the built in flash, after 30 photos, i get a busy icon, restricting me from taking a photo for about 60 seconds which can be frustrating when the models are holding a pose.Overall this is a solid camera, and i will continue to buy cannon cameras while progressing into my photography career."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent starter DSLR body. I wasn't ready to commit to the big prices of photography equipment, but getting a T7 has been a perfect entry point. It turns out that good lenses are the real cost of the hobby, but EF-mount lenses compatible with this Rebel are more reasonable than others and they're everywhere!My only gripe with this model is the WiFi connectivity. Who knows how old the interface/protocol is, but for 2026 it's slow and inconsistent. I wish it had Bluetooth for easy camera-to-phone sharing, but it does have an NFC and direct WiFi mode. They're just clunky. Using a PC to transfer more than a few photos is recommended. Oh and you'll need a MINI-USB cable for that (like 2 gens of cable connectors ago), so dig one out of your old cord drawer.Overall the autofocus and function of the camera has been great. Only 3 shots/second is a little slow, but only shooting sports does that really bug me."
    },
    {
        "review": "Picked up the renewed Canon T7 with the 18–55mm lens, and it showed up looking basically new. Image quality is solid, the lens is versatile, and it’s super easy to use if you’re learning DSLR photography. For the price, it’s a really good deal."
