        "review": "This is a very basic coffee maker.  It doesn't have a control panel or a computer.  It doesn't think it's smarter than me and turn off when it thinks I've had enough or anything like that.It has an ON and OFF switch.  I used a 24 hour timer that I bought online for $6.99 so it turns on when I decide and off when I decide.  You can make up to 12 cups of coffee (which turns out to be 8 normal mugs) as weak or strong as you want and the only waste product is a bio-degradable paper filter that was made from recycled product in the first place.This is coffee like your fathers drank before then went to work building the skyscrapers and freeways and utility systems that are the foundation of our society - in Hollynut, Irish Wisk, Basil, Thyme and frillyBisk coffee in an environmentally destructive single serving cup before you shuffle back to the bedroom still in your PJs to continue your career as an \"influencer.\""
