[
    {
        "review": "Buy this!! I love waking up to the smell of coffee, and this machine does it right everytime. It is also is so common sense to use that you could program it without reading the instructions. Added bonus: no k-cups needed! A single cup is easily brewed with the environmentally friendly reusable single basket. This is the one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker works very well and has been a nice upgrade from my previous one. The single cup option is perfect for that quick cup on the go. It is programmable which I really love because I can set my coffee to brew before I wake up! It also has a bold option for those of you that like a stronger coffee. It stays hot even when adding fridgerated creamer and has an auto turn off after two hours. You will need your own filter/disposable filters for the main pot but the single cup side comes with its own little filter. The price is decent and got it for extra cheap during prime."
    },
    {
        "review": "So, like you all ,I've been a coffeeholic for many years. Like you ,I've struggled to have a decent maker in my kitchen. I recently finished up with my Cuisinart mod#CHW-12. Had it for 5yrs. It got to point of no longer producing a well tasting cup. We did the Vinigar cleaning etc. So, i spent MANY hours searching online for a decent Maker. Problem was the abundance of poor reviews encompassing many manufacturers!  It's  now 2018 and we have trouble creating a Kit Coffee Brewer thats decent!  I did a switch and desired a maker that will produce a single cup as wife n i both have coffee at different times and mostly need the one 16oz cup. In searching for the 12cup Carafe / or single cup Maker ,my choices became limited. Read the reviews and pulled the trigger on this. It's only been 1wk now but i can honestly state that it is the BEST maker I've ever used! I ran a full 12cup Carafe first off, thn dumped. Then did same for the single cup side. ( full 14oz). Then ran 12cups clean water through for both. Then did the Coffee that I'll drink. No issues. Had to play round wth the exact amount of grounds for the single side so to get the outcome i desired. Has clock, easy to pre prog., and, the single side will turn off when done. The Carafe side will stay on (hot plate) for 2hrs after brewing complete. You can simply press On/Off button to turn off anytime. For those who have an over-spilling issue with the grounds within the gold filter basket?, you are using TOO MANY grounds!  The single side comes with a gold reusable filter which also encompasses two - Level markers. One is min and the other is Max. If you fill above the Max level, WELL, overflow of grounds will prob. occur. On the Amazon site you'll see the Reusable filter for the Carafe side in \" frequently ordered with\". I also ordered that as i don't like paper filters. It performs well. Water level for Carafe is helpful. It's towards the right rear, on the side. It's accurate. Brew time for 12 cups was good. I've learned to warm up my Mug when using single side as it is not as hot as Carafe as no hot plate for the Mug. I use single side to run water for tea as well.  What would make this model perfect? If it sounded out a tone when brewing is complete. It also has No charcoal filter as with my Cuisinart. No biggie as i always have used filtered water to begin with. Coffee is better when there's no Chlorine in the H2O! Filling either the Carafe or single side is easy and Max level markers are visible enough to get it right. Carafe pours very well and i like that the Carafe lid stays attached as u simply press thumb to open but it's not required to pour. Single side grounds chamber pulls out easily. Single side has a bottom (under mug/cup) that reverses to then become a elevator to bring cup higher if you'd like. I brewed a cup at lowest level without any spill or splatter. It drips slow enough that i don't believe i need to elevate my mug. This model also looks fantastic, Beautiful!  Has a \"Bold\" brew mode for both Carafe n Sing. The brewing is slower, so u gt a richer brew. Light on clock only on when unit is ON. Has seperate green light that indicates you are using \"Program\" mode. I don't use \"Pods\" but if i did the manual states that \"Senseo\" Pods will work. Note that unit will only brew one side at a time. It cannot brew both sides at once. Very pleased so far. If any issues I'll update here. P.s. if Manufacturer reads this, you may want to consider modifying so to have an end of brew audible tone! Jst a thought.  Update!; 1/5/18. Jst did 2 Lg mugs for me ( nine- 8oz cups), using Carafe of course. Wife then needed to do her single 14oz using of course the Single serv side. When throwing the slide switch over to Single, it turns off the Carafe side. So, yeah, hot plate under Carafe is still hot, but, it's now off. So, in future, wife does her single, first, then i do Carafe. UPDATE ; 1/22/18-  3wks now and NO ISSUES!  When removing coffee filled Carafe, absolutely no spilling onto hot plate. The spring loaded valve above, performing well. Reviewers having the Hot plate discoloration or burning may be turning unit on with a Hot plate thats dirty. I make sure plate is clean /dry before and after ea. use. I make sure bottom of Carafe is clean/ dry as well. Wife using single serve ea. day and says \" best cup of Coffee ever\"!  Update; 4/17/21.  NO issues, all still good.  UPDATE!!! - 10/10/21-  So, finally I'm now considering buying a new one of these as this one is intermittently not pumping enough water up and into Coffee basket. About 12× now in past 6mon's I've had to pour out Carafe into another cup, place Carafe back, then pour my Coffee,(that looks like Tea), into the grinds basket and do a Double Drip, sometimes twice to get color I wish. I got roughly 3.5 years out of this Maker. I guess that's good considering Everything's made in Cheapo China. If/when I buy a new one, I'll post back. Have a good Coffee!  UPDATE: 11/14/21. So, I purchased this exact model once again on 10/12/21. After 1 month, I can honestly state that it's a great difference between original and new. New machine brews perfectly as did the original one up until the 3yr mark. No issues to report with this New Maker( Same model as first one). Pictures here are of 2nd maker,(2021)."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's about what you'd expect for a mid-range Hamilton Beach coffee maker. Normal price of $80 feels a bit steep, but I think it's worth what I paid for it on prime day. It does what it says on the box/product listing and it works better than the dollar store coffeemakers you'd find in an economy hotel room. Looks to be of quality from afar, is somewhat cheap and plastic feeling when you actually use it. Just sturdy enough that I'm not concerned that I'll break it. Single serve and full carafe functions do not share a water tank, and you fill the single serve reservoir with exactly as much water as you want to brew into coffee. Pretty intuitive and I guess pretty standard for this type of coffeemaker. But if you are used to filling the tank once a week and brewing a set 6oz or 8oz this is not that. \"Brew Options\" button toggles between bold and regular brew strength.... And that's it. There's no way to set brew temperature, but the default temperature is fine. It brews a single serve in about 3 minutes or so. Faster than a drip coffeemaker of yesteryear but if you're expecting it to be as fast as a pod system you're looking in the wrong place. The thing that matters most though is how the coffee comes out, and I have to say it's worth the extra hassle of using loose ground coffee and filters as it's much better than pod-brewed coffee. The slower brew speed results in a better coffee. Much more cost effective than pods too. The reusable single serve filter is surprisingly easy to rinse out. For $50 it's not bad. I would not pay $80 for this. At a price point of $80 I expect to at least be able to choose a brew temperature, even if there are a few pre-sets instead of by-degree. If you can get this for under $60 and you are specifically looking for a coffeemaker that doesn't use pods, then I can recommend it. Otherwise at full price, I don't think it offers enough to differentiate it from other $60 coffeemakers to justify the extra $20. It does have a clock in it and the ability to set a time to automatically start brewing at a set time, which is a feature I really don't use, but for some maybe this will make the $80 asking price worth it as I am not sure if this feature is commonly available in cheaper options."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice. And when you pour your coffee, NO DRIPS!!!!One side has the pot, other side, you can just make a single, ahhh, cup . That's a really BIG cup. If you use pods, just bust the top open and pour it in. No problem at all. Actually it's kinda nicer than a Keurig, you can mix it the way you want to. 👍👍"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am so happy with this dual coffee machine! Just FYI it doesn’t use pods. The one cup feature has its own small basket which you use your own coffee. Coffee temperature is perfect. Is is very easy to use, and I have not had any leaks. It has helped to make more space in my small kitchen by combining the two features and has saved me some serious money not having to buy pods! I would definitely recommend this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "Delighted with this coffee maker! It arrived on time and in good condition. I had a very expensive coffee maker that quit working and thought I would save some money and try this Hamilton Beach version. SO glad I did!The set up was easy and that first morning I was very happy with my hot delicious, coffee!The single serve option is important to me and it works perfectly. I LOVE having a single cup of coffee without using a k-cup!Highly recommend this machine!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like this Coffee maker.  It does not spill or leak water.  It is easy to use and clean.  I can get a cup of coffee when it is still brewing the pot.  If I only want one cup of coffee, I can use the single serve feature which is really nice.  It was worth the money, and I would recommend this coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wonderful coffee maker! I have one in use and bought another one just in case, before it goes out of production."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am so amazed the versality of this Hamilton Beach coffee maker of Single and full pot brew. The product output is awesome! Good brewed coffee every single morning is a heavens gift!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It works perfect, the scheduling option helps a lot in my busy mornings as does the option to only prepare a portion when needed."
    },
    {
        "review": "・Function: With the automatic drip 2-way mechanism, you can choose whether to make a large amount of coffee in the pot or make one cup.The only thing worth noting is these two functions, and the rest is no different from a regular coffee maker.When you press the coffee brewing button, it makes just the amount of water you put in the jug, so if you pour too much, it will overflow.The temperature of the coffee itself is piping hot, so I think it's good for people who don't like hot coffee. However, it was a negative product for me, who bought it expecting an auto-drip function with a timer. This is something that can be said about all overseas products, but the timer is definitely off, and it's off by hours, not minutes, so I have to make adjustments every half day for about 2 to 3 hours (Is it possible?) I wanted to wake up in the morning and find coffee poured into a mug...but my long-awaited dream didn't come true...There are very few coffee makers that pour coffee into a mug, so it was a big shock as I had high expectations."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Love the color and how easy it is to use!I just received my new Keurig, and I’m really happy with it so far! The dark green color is absolutely beautiful and looks even better in person. It fits perfectly on my coffee station without taking up too much space.Setup was quick and easy right out of the box. Within a few minutes, I had it ready to brew my first cup. I like that it has multiple cup-size options, and it fits my travel mug without any issues.The coffee brews quickly, is nice and hot, and the machine is much quieter than I expected. Overall, it feels well-made and is perfect for anyone who wants a simple, reliable coffee maker without a lot of extra buttons.If you’re looking for a compact Keurig that looks great and makes a good cup of coffee, I would definitely recommend this one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have owned many different Keurig models over the years and this unit is really awesome! The brewing time is very fast unlike older smaller sized models. The water reservoir is of decent size, the unit is narrow which also saves on countertop real estate and it brews a great cup of coffee as well. I always use the strong brew button and the flavour is just as good if not better than the bigger higher cost models. Highly recommend this unit!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Works as advertised. A full-functioning, smaller-sized brewer for K-cups. Green looks great. Has three brew sizes, but it does not have the 4 ounce size that is popular in many European countries.  Some cafés serve even smaller than 4 ounces. What's new to me is the strong setting. Great idea."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Keurig single-serve coffee maker has been great for everyday use, especially if you don’t want a large machine taking up counter space. I’ve had mine for over a year, use it every day, and it still works just as reliably as it did when I first got it.It brews incredibly quickly, usually in around 30 seconds or less, and it’s surprisingly quiet while running. I also love how small and lightweight it is. It’s easy to move around, pack up, or take somewhere else when needed, so portability is definitely one of its strongest features.I’ve had no issues using different pod options with it. It works with the regular coffee pods I buy, including Starbucks, as well as the reusable pod options I’ve tried. I like having the flexibility to use either prefilled pods or my own coffee without needing separate equipment.Pros:* Excellent space-saving design* Very quiet* Brews in around 30 seconds* Small and lightweight* Extremely portable* Works with multiple pod options* Compatible with reusable pods* Easy to use* Reliable for daily use* Still working great after more than a yearOverall: This has proven to be a really dependable little coffee maker. I use it every single day, it takes up barely any room, and I can have coffee ready incredibly quickly. After more than a year of regular use with no issues, I definitely think it’s a great value for the money."
    },
    {
        "review": "First, an introduction, this will take some going through, bear with me. First, I had refused for years to get a Keurig, as I did not feel the quality and richness of a good strong cup of coffee was possible. But I finally got tired of trying other methods of brewing, from using a regular single cup espresso maker, moka pot, pour over, French press... I finally opted for the ease of a Keurig mini-plus. Coffee was ...eh... I switched coffee brands, to what I feel has to be the best commercial brand. And the coffee was EXcellenT! About a year later, despite regular cleaning cycles, the thing just stopped working. I tried to take it apart, watched some youtube videos which just solidified the fact that the company made these non-serviceable. P.O.'d at this obvious tactic to sell more, I waited a few weeks, but went and got another one. Same deal a year later. Another one. This last one gave me signs before ending it's own life. I would have to run several cycles where nothing would come out... till finally something... drip... by drip... several hours later, the thing would start running again, only to stop again the next day or two. Finally, it just died.So I REFUSED to get another. These things are ridiculous, right? So I got a new French press. Coffee is great!! But... omg... what a pain cleaning that thing every.... single... time... I mean, really, it's no big deal. But, it CAn be. So I saw this thing on sale, I thought, well, it's HAlf the price of the other ones... and I def want something different this time. Cut to now....This thing has SEVERAL issues that I don't like. First of all, it is a thinner cheaper plastic, and has a cheap looking shine to it. Ok, I'm over it. The plastic... I mean, can't they make these things with glass reservoirs.... the plastic reservoir has screws on the inside of it. I don't care if they say it is food safe... Plastic is also considered food safe... but that doesn't mean it is.. those are just bureaucratic rhetoric lies. But I digress,...So this coffee maker has an adjustment for high altitude... is THAT what ruined my previous Keurigs? High altitude? Hmmm. Ok, so maybe that's a plus. It also has different sizes that you can choose -8,10, & 12 oz. With the mini-plus, you choose the size by the amount of water you pour in. That means that this one measures what it sucks in. Hmmm. The mini-plus had the controls on the top. Easy peasy. This one has the controls on the side. It also doesn't have rubber feet on the bottom. So when you try to push the buttons, the thing slides away from you. Impossible to push any buttons with one hand, you have to use two. Even with rubber feet, you have to use two hands. I'm not a paraplegic, but it's rather stupid to have to hold the thing to press a button or two, or three. Which is what you have to do. It's just really awkward because you really have to hold it in the back to keep it from moving when you press the button in front. And you have to do that without touching the reservoir, which will pop out if you tried that.But let's get to the coffee. So with the mini-plus, the first liquid out of the machine, was dark coffee. As it was finishing, the coffee would be a little more clear, but not pure water. With this machine, for the first few seconds, it is spewing out crystal clear WATER. I don't even know how that is possible. But this, it does. It also claims to be faster than the mini-cup. I hestitate to say \"brews faster\", because it doesn't brew, Keurigs simply spew water into and through the k-cup, it's a pressurized system, not a true brewing system. And it definitely IS faster. And that's a problem, as evidenced by the watery coffee that it spews out. Sure enough, the \"coffee\" tastes like water. This is the 8 oz brew, mind you, with the machine set to \"strong\". I first tried the 12oz, and ended up pouring it down the sink. The 8 oz wasn't much better. My next step is to switch out cups while it's pouring out the water at the beginning of the cycle and see if I can get a stronger \"brew\".All in all, it's convenient enough. But it will sit on my counter, mostly unused, for when I have those really lazy, sleepy, or sick days, when all I want to do is pop in a capsule, and deal with the rest of it... Very disappointed. Perhaps if you live in a low altitude area, the mini-plus would work for you. I really do recommend that one above this."
    },
    {
        "review": "I like this this coffee maker overall. It's sleek, easy to use and the coffee tastes great. However, the descale light came on after only one month and won't turn off no matter what I do. I use filtered water and a filter in the water reservoir, and only make 2 cups a day. I've cleaned it thoroughly with vinegar and distilled water several times but the descale light won't go away. Very frustrating!"
    },
    {
        "review": "So we have had this Keurig for two months now & I have nothing but good things to say about it. Let me address three issues I read a lot about in the comments, which almost held me back from getting this machine. First, thinness of the plastic. Yes, it is lightwieght, which helps my arthritic hands so much in the mornings when I need to pull it out to add the waater. Too lightweight? Flimsey? No, I definitely think not. Just right. Splashing & a lot of clean up? No. A little splatter. I take a damp paper towel to it after we have all had our morning coffee. It's barely visible. Two swipes. Voila. Lastly, the noise. It is much quicker & quieter than our last machine. It does this little farting noise when the water first comes out, which cracks us all up. It's not \"noisey\". Like it a lot. Glad I finally ordered it! It looks great. Works great. Happy. Oh, and FAST. Soo much faster thanour last machine."
    },
    {
        "review": "The perfect little treat to myself for moving into my new home. The pastel mint/pistacho green color adds a hint of color to my budding coffee station without being kitschy, and ties in with the teal accents in my family room. Works great.coffee brews in seconds and is good and hot. Choice of 3 brew sizes and, regular or strong brew. Loooooove this cute little machine. The only thing I miss about a regular coffee pot is it fills your whole home with the smell of coffee. This does not."
    },
