        "review": "Makes excellent coffee. Had it for about 2 months and working great"
    },
    {
        "review": "Wanted this machine, but on delivery has USA plug took forever to get it sorted and returned.  Definitely don’t order if you live outside the USA as this is shipped from there"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Arrived so quickly.  It arrived 2-3 hours after i ordered it which was great because my current coffee maker suddenly quit working that same morning.  It was a Mr. Coffee 12-cup that lasted for 13 years so I figured that i got my money's worth.  So I thought I would go with Mr. Coffee brand again.Anyway, this time I decided to try the 5-cup because I no longer need a 12-cup as I now live alone.  I've only had it for 3 days but so far I love it.  It works great.  I don't like warm coffee and this little coffee makes makes hot coffee, but not too hot to burn you.  It stays hot until you turn it off.  It is not programmable but that is not a feature that I'm crazy about anyway.  The handle on the carafe isn't too small, just the right size.  The carafe has a wide opening which makes it easy to clean and the glass carafe is just the same glass as a 12-cup, only smaller. The basket uses the 7\" filters which I was already using in my old unit so I didn't have to buy new ones.  I don't like the cone filters and I'm glad this one doesn't require them.  I especially like that it doesn't take up as much counter space because I have a small kitchen and don't have much counter space to spare.It doesn't brew as fast as a large coffee maker but that is no problem for me.  I turn it on when I get up, then go get dressed.  By the time i get back to the kitchen, it is finished.  It does have the pause feature if you are in a hurry.  So far, I'm very pleased with this little coffee maker and don't share any of the negative reviews.  I did run plain water through the unit before making my first pot of coffee to clean it through and through. There was no bad plastic smell, no smell of any kind, and no bad taste of any kind from my first brew of coffee as others have mentioned.  I don't grind my own coffee beans but I use Folgers pre-ground coffee, so i don't know anything about grinding your own beans and how this would be any different.  i know some people are really picky about that kind of stuff, but I am not.  I am more concerned about convenience.  If you like stronger coffee, just add more grounds or less water, or both as there is no adjustment on this unit to make the coffee stronger or weaker.As I have only had it for 3 days, I don't know anything about the lifespan of this unit, but so far, I am very pleased and loving the little coffee maker.  I will update the review if it doesn't last long.It is perfect for small kitchens, dorm rooms, etc., and is very light wright.  It looks just like a 12-cup coffee maker, only smaller, without lots of bells and whistles- just a basic coffee maker.  ( I've had 2 Keurigs in the past and neither one lasted more than a year- too expensive to keep replacing every year.  I won't buy anymore of those)  This little unit is perfect for me.  Glad I found it and hope it last a long time."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been a Mr. Coffee user for 40 years. I love the 4 cup makers. This is the second time since Feb. 2025 that the coffee maker has stopped working. The first time 7 months into using it, it was replaced. So what to do this time. I am 10 months into using the replacement item. It makes great coffee and makes sense for a one-person user that's why I gave it 5 stars. BUT, it is a disaster in terms of longevity. What has happened to the quality of the product.  QUALITY of things has gone down with the coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Works great, easy to use, and it's the perfect size since I'm the only one drinking coffee. Doesn't take up too much space."
    },
    {
        "review": "Initial impression - 4/5I bought the mini brew Mr. Coffee maker to replace a 15+ year-old Hamilton Beach model that had a burned-out heating element. My initial impression was that the Mr. Coffee unit felt rather cheaply made. This is probably because the other two 5-cup coffee makers I've had were more expensive programmable units made years ago when appliances were often built more robustly. But given that heating elements often burn out before plastic breaks, this inexpensive Mr. Coffee unit is probably robust enough for the price. Appearance-wise, the unit has clean lines and an attractive design that looks good on the counter.Size - 5/5I like that this unit is so compact and is shorter than my old coffee maker. After making coffee, I usually leave the lid open for a while to let the water tank dry. The mini Mr. Coffee fits under my kitchen cabinet, even with the lid open.Paper filters - 3/5I have a bunch of 8-12 cup paper filters, and was a little concerned that they wouldn’t work well in this unit. The filter basket is shorter than the basket in my old unit, so the 8-12 cup filters stick up a little above the basket and can get folded over when you close the lid and the sprinkler arm swings into place. But pushing the edge of the filter down a little, then swinging the arm into place manually before closing the lid solves that problem. I'm glad I don't need to buy a different size because I didn't see any smaller filters where I usually shop.Brew pause - 5/5I use a coffee maker’s brew pause feature to let the basket fill with water so the coffee grounds can bloom before the basket drains. This worked fine with the mini Mr. Coffee unit—no coffee leaked through even when the basket was nearly filled with water. I also tried pulling the pot out in the middle of brewing. The pause feature worked well there too, with zero to one or sometimes two drops falling onto the warming plate.Extraction - 4/5Even with a little blooming, I thought the extraction could be better, as the coffee tasted a bit sour. Perhaps the water temperature from the sprayer could be a little higher. So I tried a finer grind, and that produced the more robust flavor that I prefer.Temperature - 5/5After brewing a full pot, I measured the temperature of the coffee, and it was 162º F (72º C), which is good for a drip coffee maker.Pouring - 5/5The coffee poured cleanly from the carafe, without any drips or dribbles from the spout.So overall, I’m happy with this purchase and would recommend the mini brew Mr. Coffee to anyone wanting a small, simple drip-coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Sitting here with my fresh brewed coffee from my new Mr. Coffee maker. Since I'm the only one in the family that likes coffee, this mini brewer is great for two cups. It's a simple machine that does not have all the frills like a 12 cup maker i.e. no timer, smaller carafe, small size, no automatic off heating plate. BUT for two quick cups of good brewed coffee, it's perfect."
    },
    {
        "review": "For a long time I've searched for Mr. Coffee's 4 cup coffee maker but all I've found here and on eBay is one that's not used. That one is at a ridiculous price when you add in a highway-robbery price for delivery. What would show up in my searches on Amazon was this 5 cup version. I had resisted buying it for about a year, but finally ordered it a few nights ago -- then promptly cancelled the order because some reviews made me think I wouldn't like it. Fast-forward to last night shortly before midnight. I decided to give this maker a chance to prove it was worth buying, so I hit the buy button. It was here, waiting for me when I woke up today.I love it. The design differences between this model and the 4 cup one were things I thought I would hate, but I don't. Really, I have only one quibble. The filters don't fit nicely in the filter holder, but that doesn't affect how they perform. Over time I may be disappointed if the pot's lid gets coffee stains on it. Cleaning this 5 cup model is easier than the 4 cup one is. That's because my hand fits more easily in the pot for drying it, thanks to the bigger size. I also like the finish on this model. It's mostly a matte white which will go with the matte white toaster oven I'll be receiving tomorrow.I also like the on/off switch that is on both models. I use an Echo smart plug that I can turn on via my voice as soon as I wake up: \"Alexa, turn on coffee.\" The switch is always in the on position but the plug is off until I tell Alexa to turn on the coffee. When the maker is on, I appreciate the fact there is not automatic shut off after a certain length of time, like there is with other coffee makers. When having two mugs of coffee, I often don't get around to drinking the second mug till an hour or more later. I want it to be hot when I'm ready for it. Reheating coffee in the microwave is not the same as having the pot on the heat. There's a scientific reason for this.Now about the coffee: it tastes great with both models. I think it takes the 5 cup model longer to make the coffee but it's really not an issue. I will never brew 5 cups. Most often, I will use the 2-cup setting with 3 scoops of coffee. I like it strong. Someone needs to let Mr. Coffee know they are lousy at measuring cup sizes. My mug (which looks bigger in the photo than it actually is) holds 11 ounces. The 2 cup setting delivers a little less than 11 ounces. I think Mr. Coffee uses the usual cup size other coffee makers do: just 6 ounces per cup (not the expected 8 ounces for those of us who use a regular measuring cup for our cooking needs). But the 2 cup setting gives me less than 12 ounces. It's closer to 10.5 ounces. I doubt I'll ever use more than the 4 cup setting which will give me two mugs of coffee.The pot is easier to pour from versus the 4 cup version. Getting the last little bit out of the 4 cup version is difficult, but super easy with the 5 cup version.It's obvious I love this 5 cup model. I hope Mr. Coffee won't stop making it in the future like they did with the 4 cup version. When I need a new coffee maker, I want this model to be here, ready and waiting for me to hit the buy button again.UPDATE: After using the coffee maker for a while I noticed the lid on the pot has a faint stain that I can't wash off. I expect it to get worse over time so I ordered the black version so I could use the black pot in my white coffee maker (see photo). I know it'll get stained too, but I won't be able to see it. Totally worth it. I'm adding two photos to show how it looks if you want to avoid the coffee stains. You can just use the black pot or you can adapt the white pot to accomplish the same thing. Just remove the just the white lid and snap the black lid into the white pot. Photos show what I mean, I hope. This white pot/black lid is what I'm happiest with."
    },
    {
        "review": "A coffee maker that really works. Small, convenient and darn good for the money.Purchased in 2023 and made approximately 1,080 consistently dark brew pots of coffee for me and my friends. Unfortunately, I had a fall and took it out, breaking an internal piece and it's replacement, the newest version spits grounds everywhere. Not Brand. The search is continuing."
    },
    {
        "review": "My mother loves the wide mouth cup. Much easier for her to clean thoroughly, the way she likes. It brews coffee quickly and she loves it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I already knew the product and it met expectations"
    },
    {
        "review": "The latest update of my 5 star review I wrote 2 months ago is unfortunately down to 0 if I could give a zero star because the coffee maker just stopped working on the day when the so called return window closed! So basically the machine lasted for 2 months. On top of that a customer service agent on Amazon lied to me that I will receive a refund in 24 hours but I got no email stating that the refund was made so I wasted my time and money with the machine and the customer service agent. Avoid this seller!*******************************It is super simple, easy to operate reusable filter coffee maker that turned to be my best purchase! It makes up to 4 cups of coffee for less than 2 minutes and you just wash the filter under a rinsing water and ready you are for your next tasty cup of coffee! The only disadvantage is that the seller doesn't say you need to buy the reusable filter separately which was a bad aurptice for me expecting the filter to be included in my coffee maker purchase. This caused me to have my coffee maker unusable for 3 weeks at home while I was waiting for the filter to come by another seller. Once you have them joined, you can enjoy your coffee time."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great coffee maker just failed to mention its different voltage to UKNeeded to by a US To UK voltage converter hence 4 stars"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I just got my Keurig K-Duo today. I just gotta say I absolutely love this machine! The size is just right for countertop use. Everything is very easy to operate and I love all the brewing options. It cost more than I wanted to spend, but now I believe it was worth every dime."
    },
    {
        "review": "This shipped so quick and was easy to unpack and install.  I love that it’s not super bulky on my counter and I have the option to make a quick cup or make a pot on the days we have company or feel like it’s a multi cup morning.  IYKYK!! The KCups are easy to use and comes up a great brewed cup every time.  The brew is quick and hot!  To pot is easy to make.  The lid in the back comes off easily and I just pour water into the reservoir.  I would highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this on Jan 2 and have been using it for only 24 days. Today I continued to get a \"add water\" message (with a full tank) and \"error 8\" message followed by \"dry\". I cleaned the tank and re-filled several times and unplugged the machine to re-set it as online has indicated. I was finally able to get the machine to brew. Mind you this is a brand new machine and after 24 days has issues. I use filtered water so this should not be an issue. I have notified Keurig to see if there are solutions to fix these issues. I will keep this rating updated, but use caution when purchasing this machine.EDIT: So I have been able to get the coffee machine to work once again. After getting errors, I unplugged the machine for a period of time, flushed out the water tank, and plugged it back in with fresh water. I was able to get it to function normally for the past several days. I use the timer and it have brewed coffee without issue for a few days. The single use side is functioning normally. Don't know if unplugging it reset whatever chip is inside but it works for now. If it continues to function normally over the next few months I will change my star rating. For now, I am skeptical of long term use.02/08/25 UPDATE: DO NOT BUY THIS MACHINE!!!!!!!! I experienced same issues as listed about. Tried to repeat the \"fix\" three times without success. Contacted Keurig, but I am not optimistic I will receive a full refund. Amazon also closed my ability for a return on 02/01/2025, so I now can ONLY DEAL WITH KEURIG. If I could give zero stars I would.02/28/25 ANOTHER UPDATE: Was able to finally get Keurig to send me another machine on 02/16/25. On 02/28/25, I received the new machine. Unpacked and carefully followed the directions to the \"T\". Plugged in the machine as directed and it failed to turn on. Tried a different outlet, nothing. Tried another machine and it powered up without issues. Not an outlet problem. It was clearly a machine problem walked around the house trying the machine on various outlets, nothing. Called Keurig and they ran through troubleshooting, nothing. Machine DEAD ON ARRIVAL. They tried to tell me since this was a warranty replacement machine, it no longer was subject to warranty. EVEN THOUGH THIS MACHINE WAS DEAD ON ARRIVAL. I was able maintain my composure and convince Keurig to send me another machine, which will be here in 7-14 days. Stay tuned folks! BTW way, my first machine still has the above issues and continues to periodically stop working, then work, then not work... I would love to have my money back, but Keuring rather spend more money on shipping and returns than refund my purchase price. Come on Keurig, you can do better.EDIT: 04/20/25, ANOTHER UPDATE. Since my last update on 02/28/25, I received a third replacement machine from Keurig to replace the dead one. Got #3 all set up on 03/03/25 and ready to go and it worked until 03/28/25, exactly 25 days, then I got the dreaded \"add water\" and \"error 8\" message. Called Keuring and asked for a refund, but they still refuse since I bought it from Amazon. Asked to get another comparable machine, which they didn't have in stock (UGH). Ordered #4 replacement. On April 3, 2025, #4 replacement machine arrived. Got #4 all set up and on 04/20/25, it stopped working like the others. This one only lasted 17 days.EDIT: Keurig has started ignoring my calls. I was referred to a \"specialist\" who told me I needed to send my #4 machine in first BEFORE I could get sent a replacement. As I did not want to send them my machine without a replacement first, they started ignoring my emails and are now refusing to correspond with me at all. #4 machine continues to brew 2 cups then shut off reporting it is dry when there is a full water tank. I will never purchase another Keurig product and you should seriously consider doing the same. Four unusable machines in 8 months is ridiculous!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Keurig K-Duo Single Serve & Carafe Coffee Maker is an absolute game-changer for households that want both quick morning speed and full-pot brewing capability. By seamlessly combining single-serve K-Cup convenience with a classic 12-cup glass carafe, it replaces two separate appliances with one sleek, space-saving countertop setup.Brew speeds are impressive on both ends. Single-serve pods deliver a rich, flavorful cup in under a minute, while a full 12-cup pot brews in just a few minutes without over-extraction or bitterness. The control panel is intuitive, with clearly labeled buttons for cup size and carafe settings. Maintenance is equally straightforward, featuring accessible filter baskets and clear fill indicators.The Keurig K-Duo hits the sweet spot between weeknight simplicity and weekend batch brewing. For anyone seeking speed, versatility, and dependability without cluttering their kitchen counters, this coffee maker is an exceptional choice."
    },
    {
        "review": "My duel coffee maker (also Keurig) that I've had forever died.  I am a coffee all day / all night drinker  - so you can imagine my desperation to get a new coffee maker quickly.  This one was luckily on sale and was delivered overnight!! It make a perfect K-cup of coffee with a strong brew and a hot brew buttons!!  Something new to me and I love it.  Made a full 12 cup pot as well the first day and that was excellent too!! Thank you Amazon for the speedy delivery and thank you to Keurig for a wonderfully upgraded coffee maker!"
    },
