[
    {
        "review": "I’m Swedish and a coffee aficionado, so I am hard to please. This coffee maker is superior and outshines much more expensive coffeemakers. It is sleek and good looking on the counter, simple to use and makes a fantastic cup of coffee—hot and delicious! You can’t go wrong with this fine product."
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee pot has been my favorite so far, I don’t drink but a cup a day, therefore the size is more than enough for me. It’s perfect size to sit on my counter and not take up to much room. It matches the decor perfectly. It brews strong and quick. Keeps the coffee hot.  Easy to dump the old filters, and pours like a dream. No spillage. Easy to wash!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I loved this coffee pot as soon as I unboxed it. It was simple, yet elegant. I had always wanted to use the programmable features of being able to set up a time of when my coffee could be brewed in the morning without me, but I always got frustrated over all the buttons needed to press in order to set a simple time. I would get discouraged and instead of messing with it, I would just decide to turn my pot on as soon as I woke up. When I purchased this one I looked for 5 simple things.1. Was the coffee hot enough when it was brewed.2. When poured, did the coffee spill all over the place3. Did it have a clock and did have a programmable feature4. Was it reliable and sturdy5. Was the price rightAfter reading almost 90% of the comments, I decided to take a chance on this one. I will tell you, the coffee in my WHITE (I'm not sure about the black) coffee pot comes out extremely hot and I love my coffee to the point of burning. I add a significant amount of creamer and if my coffee is warm, my creamer will make it luke warm and by then, I no longer want to drink it. I have ABSOLUTELY no  issues with the temperature of the brewed coffee. Second, The carafe in this coffee pot pours water and coffee efficiently. Every other coffee pot I've owned, water would pour everywhere whenever I filled the water basin up in order to start a pot, but this one is fantastic. I haven't spilled any coffee or water while using this coffee pot. I read multiple comments about this issue and I'm not sure why they would have this problem unless they were in a rush and trying to pour all of the coffee out of the pot at once. Three, The clock and programmable function on this coffee pot are wonderful! Fast, Easy, and reliable. You push a button to program the time and push the hour and minute buttons to finish it. The programmable function, where you can set your coffee pot up the night before and it will start to brew at a specific time in the morning WITHOUT you needing to touch it, is just the BEST feature ever! Its so easy to program, so easy to set up, and it has yet to fail me. I set my coffee pot for 4 am and by 4:20 I'm walking into my kitchen, making my coffee to go and out my door by 4:30. Easy and efficient. Four, reliable and sturdy. As I stated above this coffee pot is VERY reliable, I've had it a little over 2 months and it's never once not functioned as promised. It's never overflowed, I've never had coffee grounds in my coffee, I've never had the stop and pour function release ANY coffee when I've had the coffee stopped mid pour, and my coffee has always been hot. The sturdy part is where I'm just a little disappointed. When my pot first came in the ONLY part I felt could've been improved, was the cheap feel of the carafe. The design is great, as I stated before. The water never drips for me, but the handle seemed weak and the glass was thin. I planned on ordering a second carafe, in the future just in case the handle broke off from my current one, but unfortunately I didn't even get a full three months before it broke. And the way it broke was not how I thought it would. This cold Sunday morning I was pouring myself a cup of newly brewed coffee and I put the carafe against my cold ceramic coffee mug. I usually pour my coffee into a metal travel mug and therefore I never touch the metal to the glass, but this morning was different and I am battling the flu and didn't have much energy to hold the carafe over my cup so I poured it with it against the mug and immediately I heard a crack. At first I thought it was my mug, but upon further inspection I noticed a crack along the lip of my coffee carafe. I was shocked to say the least and of course disappointed. I can't think of any other reason other than temperature change being the culprit. I wasn't pushing up against my mug, I wasn't forcing the lip into the cup, I wasn't forcibly leaning the pot against the rim of the cup, I was simply not holding the carafe away from my mug. I let it touch the cold cup and this I believe may be the reason it cracked. I have put in a request for a replacement carafe and I'm hoping they will be able to help me. My coffee pot is white and it's particularly hard to find white coffee pots, so I hope they have a white replacement part. When I hear back from them I will surely update my review. As for the right price, I couldn't have asked for a better price for a functional coffee pot. All other coffee pots are $40 and beyond and have so many features that most don't use. I am a simple person with simple needs. This pot gave me everything I needed without an outrageous price tag.Even though my carafe cracked, I would still recommend this coffee pot, that's how reliable and efficient it truly is. I will make sure in the future to watch out for temperature changes when it comes to the glass of my carafe. If I wash it and it's cold, I would make sure to warm the glass up with warm water before placing it in the pot to receive hot coffee. If your mornings are cold, pour the coffee over your cup and don't make contact with cold ceramic. I also have granite counter tops, so I would recommend putting a pot holder on your counter before placing your carafe down onto it if you don't plan on putting it back into the pot. Just a few suggestions that I myself will be doing for now on. I hope I helped anyone looking for some info and like I said, I will update you on my interactions regarding my replacement part.**I contacted this seller regarding my replacement and it was such a wonderful transaction that I HAD to make sure to update you. I have now had my NEW carafe for about 3 months after the first one cracked and to be honest, it's Wonderful! The first carafe I got felt weak and I was concerned it would give out and indeed it did. I called the manufacturer searching for a replacement carafe (one I would purchase myself) and they were fabulous. They informed me that there is no replacement carafe for this particular machine, so they would be replacing the WHOLE coffee pot for FREE. I was taken aback by this response and had to double check to make sure I heard correctly. Indeed I did, all I had to do was cut the plug off the old coffee pot and take a picture of the wire and plug. I had to make sure the numbers on the plug were visible in the picture. I double checked the photo and then sent the evidence. I didn't have to deal with shipping costs or long waits or any hassle. It was fast, efficient and absolutely stress free! The best part, I PAID FOR NOTHING! I received a brand new replacement for my cracked and broken carafe. This company was kind, respectful, and on the ball. I hope you try them out, I'm truly impressed and I recommend this coffee pot to anyone!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This black and decker coffee pot is superior for the price. It also makes a dam good cup of coffee. Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought a \"returned\" model, assuming it would be functional and cosmetically ok.  But it had a 1\" X 1\" gauge broken off the plastic.  Fortunately in the back, not the front.  I was disappointed because the sales into never said it was defective or even refurbished.  Just returned, which means like new.  Anyhow I put tape over the gap so insects can't get it. A couple months later, the spring broke on the \"swipe a cup\" feature so I lost the feature.  Black & Decker has always outlasted other brands so I was very surprised but maybe I'm using more grounds lately and weighed it down.  The last straw was when the maker quit working altogether less than a year in.  The on button stays on, can't turn it off, and nothing happens.  It doesn't brew at all.  Very disappointed.  I think this \"return\" was probably damaged before I bought it.  It must have been dropped, since the plastic casing broke off.  I won't buy returned items anymore."
