    },
    {
        "review": "We bought this to replace our dinosaur Keurig. We had the OG silver, bulky, heavy Keurig. It lasted us a lifetime then died a sudden death. We actually mourned! We have a camper now so I bought this new mini to be a space saver. I like it. I don’t love it yet but I like it. It’s small, lightweight and does the job. It splatters quite a bit, so we drape a lightweight kitchen rag over it while it brews. I’ve also noticed it doesn’t push out all the water every brew. After each brew we immediately remove the pod and toss it. Then randomly I open it later and find the pod area filled with water. Where does this water come from?? Tapping the brew button forces that water to be purged but I have to know why it’s there! It never seems like our cup of coffee is lacking a couple tablespoons so I just don’t know. Maybe a small bit is held back each brew until it creates enough to send it to the pod area. I’m perplexed. Also, if I brew plain water for tea after we have brewed coffee, I have to flush it out with 2 cycles of water or my tea is yucky, ashtray smelling tea. It really clings to that coffee smell!! That being said, love the size and weight, it brews really hot, pretty darn fast and the color is cute. So, 4 stars."
