[
    {
        "review": "I love this machine! After two years of researching, even trying out different machines, this one is perfect! I got the upgraded ES701 series and am glad I did. I am a big coffee ninja fan and this one replaced my Ninja Coffee Bar that I have used for years, but the water tank leaks when removed and it is harder to find parts now for that model.This machine grinds your beans, tamps the coffee by a lever, allows you to make expresso, double expresso to multiple size coffees or cold brews from 6 oz up to 18 oz large cups (remove the bottom plate for jumbo cups), froths and self rinses without disassembling. It is easy and amazing. In the video I walked my husband through the steps prior to filming and show him making his first cup of coffee.  He is NOT techy! You can grind your beans or use preground coffee. This morning I used mushroom coffee. Everyone can finally be a barista! The rubber mats in my photos are not included but you can find on Amazon. I love this has a removable water tank in case your overhead cabinets prevent you from getting a water pitcher under them to fill. Our coffee bar is not near sink and this was one of the problems we had with another unit we tried with a water tank that could not be removed. It also has a side storage door to store unused expresso equipment. This unit addressed all of our wishes!! Pricey yes, the most I have ever paid for a coffee maker, but worth it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m in my mid-40s and have used only standard simple drip coffee makers and basic Keurig machines my whole life. This Ninja Luxe Café Pro is a completely new experience, and its introduction to my family felt truly next-level.There is an initial learning curve to operating it, but the instructions include clear diagrams and are very easy to follow. You must patiently work through the instructions upon opening it. Once complete, you understand the mechanism, and the process becomes straightforward.This product was clearly engineered with cleanup in mind, as it's very easy to remove parts and put them in the sink or dishwasher. The best feature of the device is that it handles all the measuring for you. All you do is manually fill the water reservoir, pour in whole coffee beans, and set the grind dial. The machine then displays the optimal grind setting number for whatever you are brewing (espresso, americano, etc.). You then tamp the freshly ground coffee (a very simple process), install and twist on the portafilter containing the compressed grounds, select your desired brew if you haven't already, and hit start. The result is amazing coffee unlike anything I have ever made at home.The frothing milk function is also a breeze and simple to use. I made a cappuccino that was Starbucks-level quality; it had no added sugar, yet tasted incredibly fresh and naturally almost sweet.Upon initial impression, the machine is clearly well-designed, and I have no immediate complaints. I will update this review if I run into any issues later."
    },
    {
        "review": "After 8 months of personal use, we could not be happier with the Ninja Luxe Café Pro Series Espresso Machine. It makes amazing coffee, espressos, and lattes, and we have had absolutely no problems with it.The built-in grinder, integrated tamper, and hands-free frother make it so easy to create café-quality drinks at home. We have only had to descale it once in 8 months, which has been a pleasant surprise. It also has a beautiful appearance and looks great sitting on the counter.Overall, this machine has exceeded our expectations. We give it 5 stars plus!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm very happy with this machine and its ability to make different types of coffee. I don't intend to use it for drip at all, but I've been using it for espresso-type drinks with excellent results. The fact that it makes brewing easy, while still keeping you mostly in control, mostly means you're learning about WHY something is working or isn't working. This machine helps you tweak temperature, strength, and extraction separately. You get guidance, but it's up to you if you listen to it based on what you're trying to extract. Is it perfect? No. It's not meant to be, though. It's meant to be convenient for a beginner. That said, it's expensive, but you do get good functionality for that price.I wanted something that wouldn't take away my ability to tweak, in case I got more into espresso, but if I decided not to I could still get good coffee. This delivers."
    },
    {
