    },
    {
        "review": "I waited until I had this espresso machine for a while-I am VERY happy with it. It’s pretty good size but I luckily have the space. Brew speed and coffee temp are spot on. It’s durable-love the tamp feature. I’ve been experimenting with different brews, froths etc. I’ve had a spectrum of machines over the years and this rates right up with some of the more expensive. All in all am enjoying it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I researched extensively before buying this espresso machine. I came across a number of reports of defective machines but decided to take a chance based on Ninja’s reputation. I’m so glad I did! The machine is extremely solid and well built. It can make everything from regular coffee to espresso to iced coffees. This is a very sophisticated machine and reading the manual is essential for a good result.  The coffee produced smells and tastes amazing. The milk frother works better than any frother I’ve had before. The bean hopper holds a large amount of coffee beans which I appreciate. I find the speed of the machine to be good and comparable to other espresso machines I’ve had. I’ve seen reports of the coffee produced being too hot or too cold but mine has been perfect for me for each type of drink.  Given the many different types of coffee beverages this machine makes with ease, I highly recommend it. In fact, I went to stay with relatives for a month over the holidays and I took the machine with me!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It is the best coffee machine I’ve ever had and I’ve had a rainbow of them however it could do better on the Crema of the espresso as it is not very cream thick, but everything else is great especially the frother, it takes away that has work to make great cappuccinos and incredible chilled coffee drinks! The materials of it look really good even though it’s not stainless steel the whole thing and it does have several parts that are made out of PVC. I think the cost is a little high, but I guess with everything that it comes with, including the semi automatic tamper is also a super convenient feature,  you can see it’ll last you for years. The only downside to it is that the use of water is quite a lot so you have to be emptying the tray constantly after you make around to good drinks. I think ninja should look into integrating a rubber doing for discharging this water into your sink and that would solve the problem! The coffee quality depends on what coffee beans you use but as far as functionality with the beans, it’s great the brew speed, coffee, quality, and heat level of it are great as well. The capacity you get on each beverage is also great and especially by the fact that you can choose from Ristretto, espresso, Lungo and Americano among other to choose from. It also gives you automatically the number that you should match to the machines suggestion in order to have the perfect grind for your choice of drink. Last but not least it comes with Storage for your coffee, tools so they are entirely hidden from site inside the machine on the right side.  The only downside this machine has is the fact that it accumulates a lot of water as the byproduct of making the different coffee choices. It should come with a drain tube to go directly into the sink or spout! The counter space it takes is a little bit chunky but against having an espresso machine and a drip coffee machine it’s a win-win! I think it’s a great upgrade from the last Ninja, but the pro series is incredible!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The Ninja Luxe Café Pro Series exceeded all my expectations. The quality of the espresso is incredible: consistent extraction, full-bodied flavor and a crema that rivals many professional coffee shops. The Barista Assist system makes life much easier, automatically adjusting the grind and helping you find the ideal point for each bean. The machine is fast, intuitive and very stable — each drink comes out the same as the last, which shows the care taken in design and technology. The steam wand is powerful and produces creamy microfoam, perfect for cappuccinos and lattes. It's exactly the type of foam that I could only get in specialized coffee shops before. Another strong point is the ease of maintenance. The internal cleaning cycles are guided, the interface explains everything clearly and the process is very simple. I've never had problems with clogging or variation in flavor. In addition to all this, the design is beautiful, modern and robust. It really gives that feeling of a premium product — it looks like a professional barista's piece at home. After I bought it, I started to prefer making my coffee at home instead of buying it outside. Ninja has really raised my daily coffee standard. I highly recommend it. Worth every penny!"
