        "review": "A Beautiful aesthetic in my kitchen. And the dial helps keep track of the time I have left before it turns off. I love it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I wanted to love this coffee maker so much, I really did. It's definitely a fun design and looks great, and it worked like a charm for a couple of months, but then I started having the same issue that so many others started having when their pot wasn't very old. It started steaming up a storm (literally making the machine soaking wet with steam sweat as it tried to brew) and brewing very, very little coffee... and having a burnt taste to what actually did end up in the pot. On top of that, the carafe is incredibly thin and fragile. My first one cracked by the handle within weeks, and after some teeth pulling I managed to get a replacement from the company... but then, a little over a month later, the brewer itself stopped working.I know I've read about a 1-year warranty, but I honestly don't even think it's worth the hassle trying to get a replacement for a crappy coffee brewer that's just going to crap out on me again after a few months.For example, when I tried to get a replacement carafe...I first contacted Amazon and was told I had to go directly to Nostalgia, so I did. I emailed them first, but after many days did not hear back. I then found a phone number and called. After a looooooong hold time I finally spoke to someone and she was very nice and said she was sending me a new pot (despite their website saying they were out of stock). A day after I spoke to this lady on the phone someone else replied to my email and said they couldn't send me a new carafe. I told her that I spoke to someone who said they would send me a new carafe to which this person basically replied, \"so she did.\" It sounded like the person on the email didn't want to send me a replacement at all despite them actually having them in stock. I'm glad I got someone on the phone, because they did come through... but that's still a bit shady - hence why I don't even feel like dealing with trying to replace the whole crappy unit now that it's crapped out on me.I'm sadly tossing this in the trash and putting money towards a top rated and top notch coffee brewer.No fun nostalgia in my kitchen, design wise, but I'd rather have functionality any day of the week."
    },
    {
        "review": "Beautiful classic look, I love the beige color. It absolutely matches my aesthetic. It is super easy to use, just one button ! I love the reusable filter because save the environment 🌍 Easy to clean, dishwasher safe parts ✅ This retro vintage vibe is gorgeous in person and if it matches your space you should totally get it ! I'm usually a Percolator gal but I decided to try this Drip style coffee maker and I am happy with it. When looking I saw a lot of smaller options like only 4-5 cup brews and that would simply not work for me and my husband. We love our husband and got this 10 cup maker to fulfil our coffee needs ! ☕ I will say I don't understand the little clock thing on there but I haven't investigated that part yet, maybe I missed it in the manual. None the less it's stylish and makes good coffee. It also fit my budget. I didn't want the cheapest options like those $25 ones from Walmart but I didn't want to spend $200 either because yeesh. I think this is a great price for a durable appliance."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really beautiful and effective. Fast and the coffee is delicious."
    },
    {
        "review": "It looks great with its vintage style."
    },
    {
        "review": "Looks exactly as advertised.  So far has worked perfectly but I'm only 2 weeks in. I recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It makes a great pot of coffee and stays hot for 2.5 hours. We use it daily. Glad we bought it, it looks good on our counter."
    },
    {
        "review": "Just over a year old and won't pump water through.I clean often.Unit does not last.for the price, not a good buy."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "The twomeow coffee and tea maker makes single serving coffee or tea. It uses kcups, grounds, or tea bags which is convenient. It is very simple to operate.  The machine has settings for the amount you want to fill and for cold or warm drinks.  The machine is very lightweight, so it is easy to store in the pantry or cabinet. It looks nice, so you could keep it out since you may use this everyday.  This is a great value for the money. Well worth the investment."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this to replace an older single serve brewer and have been running it two or three times a day for about three weeks, mostly pods in the morning and loose grounds in the afternoon.The iced setting is the feature that justifies the machine. It brews hot but at a lower volume and higher concentration, so when it lands on a glass of ice you get coffee rather than the watery mess most brewers produce when you just pour a normal cup over cubes. I use the 6 ounce iced setting over a full tumbler of ice and it comes out at drinking strength with the ice still mostly intact.Bold mode does something measurable. It slows the water down and the difference in the cup is obvious, not a marketing distinction. With a medium roast pod on bold at 8 ounces I get a cup I would call properly strong. On standard at 12 or 14 ounces the same pod thins out noticeably, which is true of every machine in this class but worth knowing before you default to the big sizes.The reusable grounds basket is decent. It holds enough for a 10 ounce cup, the mesh is fine enough that I get no silt in the cup, and it rinses clean under the tap. The drip tray lifts out and my 6 inch travel mug fits underneath with room to spare.Two things kept it at four stars. The 52 ounce tank sounds generous but if you brew 12 or 14 ounce cups you are refilling every fourth cup, and the tank has to come off the base to fill, so it is not a walk by top off. Second, the touch panel needs a deliberate press. Wet fingers or a glancing tap does nothing, and a couple of times I walked away thinking I had started a brew when I had not.Good machine if you drink iced coffee regularly and want strength control. If you brew large cups for a household, plan on filling the tank often."
    },
    {
        "review": "For the most part I really like this coffee maker. I like the water tank that holds enough water for me to make about four fourteen ounce cups of coffee. You are able to choose the size and strength of coffee. For size it goes from six to fourteen ounces in two ounce increments. Strength is regular or bold. They also have the choice of capsule or ground. You can use pre measured coffee pods that start with a k. The other option is a reusable filter which does come with the machine along with a scoop to measure out the grounds. This does fit a tall glass, or my larger mugs, though even with the drip tray removed it doesn't fit my 20+ ounce vacuum insulated mugs. That is fine since I usually use those for cold brew. This doesn't do cold brew but it does brew over ice brewing at a cooler temperature. Drip tray is removable and easy to clean. Hold the cold brew button for three seconds to put the machine into descale mode, fill the tank with baking soda water solution or citric acid solution to descale, then run full tank of fresh water to remove cleaning solution. I am hopeful that this machine will last a good long time if properly maintained. The cord is about two foot."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the flexibility built into this coffee maker. Being able to use both K-Cup-style pods and ground coffee makes it much more versatile than a machine that only accepts one type of coffee.The different cup-size options are also convenient because you’re not locked into making the exact same size every time. I especially like that it includes a bold setting for people who prefer a stronger cup.Another feature that stands out is the ability to make iced coffee. That’s something I would definitely use, especially during warmer weather. Having hot and iced options in one machine saves having to keep a separate appliance just for cold coffee drinks.The larger water reservoir is also a nice feature for a single-serve machine because you’re not constantly having to refill it every time you want another cup.I appreciate that it includes a reusable filter for ground coffee as well. That gives you the option of using your own coffee instead of being completely dependent on pods.Overall, this is a very flexible machine for someone who likes having choices. The combination of pods, grounds, multiple sizes, bold brewing, and iced coffee makes it much more versatile than a basic single-cup brewer."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a good coffee maker with great accessories. My only issue was the residual coffee in the machine after use.K-Cups work great. These machines are very simple for serving single-serve drinks. This machine was really easy to use with the cups. Just load them and water, and it brewed well.This also comes with a cup for coffee grounds. I didn't use it, but it looks like it would work just as well. I imagine that this is a great substitute for the disposable K-Cups.This does have 5 different sizes. That is a good way to control the volume of beverage dispensed. My big concern with this is that when I dispensed a 6-ounce drink, there was still residue in the machine after I ran the cycle. This is fine if you continue to use the same beverage (only coffee, for example), but I drink tea, hot chocolate, and such. So, this would be really unpleasant.The cycle is very quick. It heats and brews very quickly.The reservoir was good, but if you are using this in a setting outside a home (like an office), it would feel small. The markings on the reservoir"
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker is simple to use and makes a good‑tasting cup, whether hot or iced. The controls are straightforward, and the different brew sizes give you flexibility depending on how strong you want your coffee. The bold option adds a nice boost in flavor without making it bitter.The water tank is a convenient size and the machine doesn’t take up much counter space. I also like that it works with both K‑cups and ground coffee, which makes it more versatile.The only drawback is that it brews on the slower side compared to other single‑serve machines I’ve used. It’s not a deal‑breaker, but it’s noticeable if you’re in a hurry.Overall, it’s a solid coffee maker with good results—just expect a slightly longer wait for your cup."
    },
    {
        "review": "We got this to replace an older name brand k-cup machine that was acting up. We like that this has so many options like the size of the cup, stronger or standard strength, and if it’s a k-cup, ground coffee or iced coffee. It’s very slim and fits nicely in a smaller kitchen. We do have to keep filling the water reservoir more often but it’s smaller so that’s to be expected. It feels more lightweight than our old one so we are not expecting it to be too durable. The handle you pull to open the lid for the pod feels like it’s not going to hold up to daily use. It’s difficult for us to remove the used pod, it fits tightly into the holder, which is good, it’s just more difficult to remove. What I really like about this is the ability to use ground coffee, that’s a game changer for me because there are so many more flavor options. The current price for this is in the mid 50’s and I definitely think it’s worth that price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Compact single serve brewers are convenient until the reservoir needs refilling every other cup. The 52 ounce tank on this version gives the machine more breathing room while still keeping the convenience of making one drink at a time.The choice between K Cup pods and grounds is useful because mornings are not always the same. Sometimes convenience wins, and sometimes I want to use whatever coffee is already open in the cabinet.The 6 to 14 ounce brew sizes add flexibility, while hot, iced, and bold options give more control over the finished drink than a basic one button brewer.A larger reservoir takes up more space than the smaller TWOMEOW machines, so this version makes more sense when fewer refills matter more than having the tiniest footprint possible. Actual brew strength and temperature will still depend on settings, coffee, and serving size.For daily use, the larger water capacity is the feature that makes this version easier to live with."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I have been using the Keurig K-Compact Single-Serve K-Cup for about 5 years, and it is still working well. However, lately, I have noticed that my coffee is not as hot as I would like, so it was time to get a new one.It arrived yesterday, and I love it. I'm a coffee addict. I make 3-4 coffees a day using organic beans, filtered water, and stainless steel reusable K-Cups for Keurig, also purchased on Amazon, and my coffee tastes great. I love this unit because it's very easy to use, nothing fancy, it is compact, it doesn't take up much space on the countertop, and it looks good. Brews coffee quicker than my old one. Hopefully, this one will last as long as the previous one. Great value for money."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've owned two Keurig coffee makers over the last 10 years. They do not die! I moved and because this kitchen is small I decided to go with this smaller compact one which is perfect as it takes up little counter space, but gives me a delicious cup of coffee every morning. It is quiet and easy to use."
    },
    {
        "review": "Keurig always rain true to their brand, I am grateful for my buy and will always buy with Keurig brand of products. It’s super nice to make my cup of coffee at home to enjoy on my ride to work or in the morning on the weekend with my husband, where we both can enjoy a cup of coffee while  out on the patio😋"
    },
    {
        "review": "I got this because I need a replacement because I had the elite version. This thing is amazing, it saves on countertop space if you have a small kitchen. It's easier to clean, has a pretty small tank if you want to make one or two cups put anything more you constantly have to fill it. Load functionality is pretty easy and smooth. It's really easy to clean as always keurigs do. And their parents if you have a small kitchen as well as not the much counter space this is the perfect thing for you"
    },
    {
        "review": "Received this Keurig same day delivery.  Very happy with it and it is quieter than my previous machine like it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve really enjoyed using this Keurig K-Compact coffee maker. It fits perfectly on my counter without taking up too much space, which is exactly what I needed for my kitchen. The coffee brews quickly, and I like having the option to choose between different cup sizes depending on how much coffee I want.The Smart Start feature is really convenient because it heats and brews in one simple process, saving time in the mornings. The removable water reservoir also makes refilling and cleaning easy. It’s simple to use and perfect for busy mornings when I need coffee fast. The only small downside is that the water reservoir could be a little bigger since I find myself refilling it more often than expected, especially if multiple people are using it. Other than that, it’s been a reliable coffee maker and works great for everyday use."
    },
    {
        "review": "Update:Despite loving this coffee maker, I am returning it for what is probably a rare reason. It triggers my asthma. It took me a lot of time to find the cause of the asthma attacks.  I looked at my purchases from the time when the attacks started. At first I thought it was a prescription eye drop I use. I picked it up from the pharmacy the day the attacks started, but it was an Rx I've used for months with no ill-effects. I experimented with the Rx: I took it and found the attacks continued. I stopped using it and the attacks continued. My doctor put me on a Prednisone burst for 5 days and I had no attacks on those days. But as soon as the burst ran out, the attacks started again. Then a couple days ago I checked my Amazon purchases. Turns out I received the coffee maker on the day the attacks started.  Yesterday I made coffee in my Mr. Coffee and there was no attack. Ditto for today. I Googled, looking to see if others have had Keurig's that triggered attacks. Mostly, what I found was that it was possible because hot water interacting with the plastic and foil in K cups might activate chemicals, or there could be mold in the Keurig. I doubt there's mold in the one I bought because it showed no sign of having been used. I know nothing about chemistry, so I can't really weigh in on whether the potential interaction with plastic and foil is true or false. I just know that since I stopped using the Keurig, the asthma has stopped.I'm leaving the five stars from my original review because the Keurig is so pretty, so much fun to use, and so solidly built -- and I think my issue is probably extremely rare.  Just one more thing: when Googling the issue, I got a lot of links that warned about mold forming and the need for regular cleaning. Passing that along because when I bought the Keurig I saw nothing about mold -- just the info that regular descaling is necessary.Original review:I have a lot of green and turquoise/teal in my kitchen but black seemed like the safer choice. To settle the matter, i ordered both colors. In the end, I chose the turquoise one because it's so cheerful-looking. I'm giving the black one to a friend.By the way, my choice surprised me. The black one arrived a day before the turquoise one and I was quite happy with it. Almost decided to just return the turquoise one without opening it. But curiosity won out and I'm glad it did because the difference is dramatic and the choice is a lot more fun.For k cups, I ordered what has been my everyday coffee for many years: Folger's Colombian medium. Tastes exactly the same as what I had been making in my Mr. Coffee. I had worried needlessly that the k cup wouldn't brew to my preference, but it did in the medium-size mug setting."
    },
    {
        "review": "I grabbed this when I moved into my own apartment so that I could enjoy coffee without having to make a whole pot of it. As a single-serving coffee maker, it makes the grade.The three brew sizes is great for variability, since some mornings I'll want to make a larger cup than usual. Other users have complained about how the cups it brews are inadequate; I think that's more a consistency issue, as it definitely feels like there are times when the medium-size button produces 10 oz and other times it's only 6 oz for whatever reason. The other minor complaints I have are that the machine doesn't stay powered on, so you have turn it on THEN put in the grounds and select a cup size, when there doesn't seem to be any reason to turn it off between brews. The other issue is the reservoir: it's kind of in this no-man's-land where it's a bit too small to go more than 2-3 days between refilling but also big enough to make a rather substantial footprint on the counter. If you have multiple coffee drinkers in the household, I'd suggest picking a Keurig with a much larger water tank so you're not refilling every other day. (I'd also suggest buying some mesh filters so you're not overpaying for K-Cups!) Overall, a fine product with just a few design quirks that don't detract that much from the final score."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great machine, easy to use and good selection of coffee pods available."
    },
    {
        "review": "I like the simple older style Keurig.It was just what I ordered. Had no problem getting the Keurig.It did take awhile and they stated that up front."
    },
    {
        "review": "Beautiful turquoise coffee maker. It works well. As it is not digital, it is very easy to operate. It heats up and brews quickly.Update…this coffee maker stopped working just a few days after 3 months so can’t return it. Very  disappointed as it was a gift. Have bought a similar one before that that has lasted a few years."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is probably the 5th one I have bought over the years! Only because we drink ALOT of coffee! They’re affordable and super easy to use.Different options for cups sizes. Perfect for on the go! Small and portable enough to take to the trailer or cottage!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Compact.  Fast brew. Makes a good cup of hot coffee (haven't tried the iced setting). Unit will be easy to keep clean. Filter basket let's you decide how much ground coffee to use, which is nice. I started with 3 heaping teaspoons for a 12 oz cup. There was room in the filter basket for more if I wanted to make a 16 oz cup or a smaller strong cup. If you prefer using k-cups, there is an adaptor."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this iced tea maker"
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker is supposed to be versatile single cup brewer but definitely need some improvement. The slim profile let you tuck it into tight spaces.  It is very easy to use and you really don't have to read the manual if you have used single cup brewers before. The water tank is a plus so you don't have to fill a cup at a time. It is good enough to hold a few cups for brewing but not large enough to leave water in there for days if you only do a couple cups everyday.  Brewing size seems to be on par. I tested the brewing size by selecting the 16oz of hot water. It filled up my 16oz mug to the rim. Selecting 8oz with grinds also roughly filled up 2/3 of my 12 oz tumbler. As with other single cup brewers that let you use your own grind, some fine grounds will pass thru and I use a separate paper filter to make sure I get clear coffee.  The k-cup tray works as it should but the puncture point is on the side instead of bottom. The basket inside holding the ground filter or k-cup does retain water a bit. Therefore, when you swap between ground filter or k-cup, there is water dripping out to the cup tray.The \"Ice\" feature is kind of moot as it only restrict brewing size to 6/8 oz. I can probably select 6/8 oz by myself. My biggest complain is the brewing temperature. The coffee does not seem to be hot enough at the cup so I use a temperature gun to measure right after brewing at the pod. It was showing no more than 178F. Given other factors, I estimate the brewing temperature to be no more than 185F. They should actually change the \"Ice\" feature to \"High heat brewing\" feature.  If you want very hot coffee to the cup, this is not the machine for you."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m sitting here sipping a great cup of coffee brewed with my new Horavie Single Serve Coffee Maker. The main features are that it works with K-cups or grounds and has settings for hot or iced coffee. You can choose the amount from 6oz through 16oz. It doesn't have a strong or bold setting but has \"over ice” instead. It shuts off automatically after five minutes.The coffee maker is a cheerful fire engine red. The red and black plastic panels have a classy satin matte finish. The only parts that are glossy are the silver trim and the display panel. Instead of a touch screen, the display features actual buttons that click when you press them, which I prefer.The coffee maker parts are all removable and the unit itself is wide enough to insert your hand for wiping it down inside.  It comes with a funnel that holds either the k-cup attachment or the filter attachment for ground coffee. The set includes a coffee scoop and brush, as well as a user manual. The power cord is short, approximately 2 feet long.It’s small and thin, under a foot in length and height, and less than 5 inches wide, so it fits pretty much anywhere. The opening for the mug is 6.5” high to fit a tall container for iced coffee. The only disadvantage to the tall unrestricted opening is that when using a normal size 12 oz mug, the coffee splatters onto the counter a bit when it drips into the cup. The grill is removable and has its own removable drip tray, which makes cleaning up under the mug so much easier.This is my second Horavie coffee maker, so I have something to compare. This new red one produces hotter coffee, and doesn’t push as much clear water through initially. My old coffee maker expels almost 2 ounces of plain tepid water when brewing the first cup of the day. I’ve been catching it and tossing it out so it doesn’t cool down and dilute the fresh coffee. I’ve also been preheating my mug with boiling water from the kettle. It adds a good bit of trouble for that first cup of the day.As a work around for the lukewarm coffee problem, which seems to be inherent in most single serve machines, I’m now running a 6oz cycle of plain water through first to get the old cold water out of the internal tubing and prime the machine with hot water. At the same time this process preheats the mug into which it drips. Then the first cup of the day drips piping hot coffee into a preheated mug.I measured the temperature of the drip from my new red coffee maker at 190F and the resulting coffee at 170.8F, which is ideal. It took about a minute and 15 seconds to brew (see my video). This coffee maker is perfect for tall insulated containers to grab and go, whether hot or iced coffee is your pleasure. It’s quick and easy to use, with removable parts facilitating the cleanup.The fact that I can use my extra dark roast ground coffee in the large filter attachment makes this machine worth it for that reason alone. I can put as much ground coffee in there as I like and get a seriously strong cup of coffee when I want it, or I can go for a quick and effortless k-cup.  Works great!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This replaces another single serve model that does both ground and k-cup style coffees, and I find it even easier to use.  First of all, I probably won't go back to bigger carafe coffeemakers because I'm the only coffee-drinker here and I only really need one or two cups a day, max.  So I often waste too much coffee in the larger carafes.  Additionally, I love that I can do either k-cup style or ground coffee, it couldn't be easier to choose between the two.  And with this model (unlike my previous other brand model), I am given options for cup size, which is great because I have some larger 20oz cups I like to use when I'm drinking ground coffee (k-cups would get pretty weak in those larger cups, though - better for the 8oz cups).  The water tank is big enough to keep me going three or four days without needing a refill.  And to top it all off I love the color!  My kitchen is black and white with red accents so I love the red color, really pops.  No issues at all so far.  Loving the product."
    },
    {
        "review": "This thing takes up almost no space, which I love. The reusable pod filter fits right inside and I can use pre‑made pods or fill it with my own grounds — which saves money.The water tank is removable and holds a full 47oz, so I don't have to keep refilling it throughout the day. I just pop it out, fill it up, and pop it back in — super convenient.Coffee comes out really hot — actually hotter than my old machine. Or hit the iced button and it comes out a little cooler, perfect for over ice.Super happy with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked this coffee maker up for my RV where space is limited, and it works great. The compact size is perfect for a small counter, but it still has enough features to make it feel like a full-size coffee maker.I like that it works with both coffee pods and ground coffee, which gives some flexibility depending on what I have on hand. The removable water tank is a nice size, and the different brew options make it easy to choose the right cup size without wasting coffee. It also cleans easily, which is a big plus in an RV where I do not want a lot of extra cleanup.Overall, this is a great little coffee maker for an RV, office, dorm, or any small space. It is easy to use, does not take up much room, cleans up quickly, and makes it convenient to have a good cup of coffee without needing a bulky machine."
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker has been easy to use and, most importantly, consistent. It brews the same way each time, without me having to fiddle with settings or wonder if the next cup is going to come out differently. The controls are straightforward, and I haven’t had any issues with it.The larger water tank is also nice because I’m not constantly refilling it between cups.TLDR: Easy to use, brews consistently, and has been reliable so far."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Great little coffee maker at a great price.  I bought this to replace my Keurig slim that failed me. I have replaced too many of them with the same brand and feel I’ve given them too much of my money for an inferior product. I have used this machine daily for one day shy of a week and it is great.Pros: hot coffee (Keurig is hot for the first several uses then it seems to  decrease over time) this machine also seems to extract the great flavor of the coffee. Some reviews complained that it takes too long to brew, but I’ll take a slower brew for a hotter and better tasting  cup  of coffee. I appreciate that it comes with the tea brewing basket and the loose coffee ground basket without making you spend more money to get those things. It fits nicely on my counter without taking up too much space. The machine use is pretty straightforward. Fill your desired amount of water in the reservoir and put your coffee pod or ground coffee basket in and close the lid and press whatever button you prefer. There is the option for iced coffee but I’m not a big iced coffee fan. I also appreciate the riser to avoid splashes but I don’t really think it would be needed because it doesn’t seem to splash much like the keurig did. It’s a great looking machine without being bulky.Con: which was my own fault for not fully reading the directions. I filled the reservoir all the way to the max for the first cleaning and didn’t realize I had purchased the one cup machine because I had looked at so many and compared. I thought I bought the one that had the size selection options and I nearly overflowed my cup. Other than that. I don’t have any cons."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this coffee maker. It has a very small footprint on my counter. It is very simple to operate. I don’t have to program a computer every time I want to change the amount of ounces. It looks modern and nice in my kitchen. I love the hot brew, bold and over Ice functions as well. The noise level is not offensive, and the brew time is quick."
    },
    {
        "review": "Edit:I was finally able to send a message through to the company via Amazon. I had to do some shenanigans to do so as there was limited options to contact the company. They were really nice and immediately offered a refund or to replace the unit. Since I really loved the machine, I opted for a replacement. My original was out of stock so they are sending me the T model instead.I'm going to increase the stars for the customer service and will update again if the replacement dies within a year again.-----------Original reviewI bought the item in March, and it no longer pulls water from the reservoir. It also seems to be overheating the water to the point that the lid that fits down over the pod compartment has warped and emits large quantities of steam. I descale monthly and keep it clean, but it only lasted five months.It is supposed to have a 1-year warranty, but I can't find my paperwork nor how to contact the seller/company."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have a Nespresso as well, and I was looking for another easy-to-use item that makes strong coffee.  What I really love about this is the 'bold' setting for the brew and the various sizes setting.  I have not used the iced coffee setting, but I will absolutely try it.  I have had lower-end Keurig makers before, and they didn't come up to the quality brew this does.  I am honestly blown away; for the price, there is likely nothing better."
    },
    {
        "review": "I needed a small coffee maker for work, and didn’t want to spend $80 on the name brand one. But I think that would’ve been the better option overall. This one is just OK. Will it make a cup of coffee? Yes. Though you do have to run a LOT of water through it first, to remove the plastic taste…like, a LOT. But you can only put in the amount of water you expect to use for your cup. No filling the reservoir completely for multiple cups. So it was annoying to have to go back and forth to get water each time I needed to use it. And inevitably someone was going to be “helpful” and try to fill it completely, only for it to use ALL the water and make a huge mess. That led to having to tape instructions to the top, which just looked messy. This one will be donated and I’ll just spend the money on the better one."
    },
    {
        "review": "This coffee maker brew coffee very quickly. It’s small and space saving very easy to use. Looks good and is very reliable.The company is also very reliable. Should something go wrong with your coffee machine. They are quick to help you or replace it. Definitely worth the five star rating."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased it for use while traveling so I could enjoy my favorite coffee pods. Worked great for the first 3 uses...It provided a nice hot cup of coffee. I generally brew a 12 oz. cup, but starting with the 4th brew it only provided a 16 oz. cup of brew. I reread the instructions and tried a few things to no avail. It had the potential of being a good coffee maker, but when one of the functions fails it becomes a piece of crap."
    },
    {
        "review": "We grabbed a box of inexpensive pods to try the coffee maker functions. The foil top blew out about half the pods. We were going to return it but then tried some Peet’s and they have worked fine. There is enough pressure that the foil will blow off and make a huge mess if they aren’t glued on well.Ground coffee basket works fine but for RV travel the grounds are more mess than we wanted. There are filters made for the basket but I just started making my own by slightly trimming some small cone filters I had along. Still a little messy since the grounds get blown up on the top due to the pressure. If you’re at home without clean up considerations, then no big dealWe have 20 oz Yetis and the height (6.5”) is no problem.  We like strong coffee and find the bold button and water to the “max” level will make a decent 20 oz cup from one Peet’s pod.All in all a good product, 4.5. We are satisfied and it makes decent coffee, but it comes out VERY hot. ( too hot for my taste)."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "This is a nice coffee pot with the features that I want. I'm the only coffee drinker in my home, so this smaller pot is just what I wanted. It functions well and looks very nice sitting on my counter! Don't hesitate to purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've only used this coffee maker a few times, but it seems to work fine. The price was decent.For the life of me, I don't get what size cup, 10 cups mean. I get a good three cups in my slightly oversized mug (which is enough for me)."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this exact coffee maker about 3 months ago and I haven’t had any issues or problems with it so I decided to get a second one for my vacation home. The coffee maker is compact and looks nice on my counter. The instruction manual has straightforward step by step instructions for first time use and for normal coffee brewing. However, there are a couple of things in the instruction manual that I disagree with. First, it says “the appliance can be used by children 8 years old and above if they’ve been given supervision or instruction.” I can’t imagine letting my 8 year old grandson use my coffee maker or why I would want him to. Also, it says you should unplug and thoroughly clean all parts of the coffee maker daily. That’s probably a good thing to do but I have only been cleaning mine periodically. And for clarification, #3 under Normal Brewing says to use one level spoon of coffee for each cup. This should say one level Tablespoon for each cup of coffee. Other than those things I found the instruction manual to be helpful and clear.The coffee maker has all the common features found in coffee makers. It can be programmed to go on automatically at a specified time which is convenient for people who work or are in a hurry in the morning. We tried this function and it was easy to do, however, since we are retired we like to prepare the coffee the night before but then press the on/off button when we get up in the morning. The coffee maker has a pause and serve function so you can grab a cup of coffee before the brewing stops. It also has an automatic shut off that turns the coffee maker off two hours after it was turned on. I find this feature to be very important because I often forget to turn it off. There are two other features on this coffee pot that I really like. First, it has a button to make the coffee a little stronger. You just press the “strength” button and a little coffee bean symbol shows up under the time. This slows down the drip and gives the coffee a bolder flavor without making it bitter or too strong. The second thing that I really like is that this machine makes HOT coffee which is the way I like it."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a terrible product which has no brand name. The instructions say to unplug it after every use. So then all settings, including the clock, have to be reset.  Therefore I don’t feel safe leaving it plugged in and I will be throwing it away after I get a trusted brand replacement. DO NOT BUY THIS ITEM!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This machine is great standard coffee maker. Came with its own reusable filter cone, unlike other brands that make you purchase it separately. Style is inline with other stainless steel black combos. The font is the spoiler for the look, I can’t quite put my finger on what would be a better font, but I feel the one that was used does detract from the look. There is also no cable storage or management on this machine so there is just rouge cable, simple fix for me since I had an extra cable winder, but just something to keep in mind."
    },
    {
        "review": "10 Cup Programmable Coffee Maker, Regular & Strong Brew Drip Coffee MachinePause & Serve, Keep Warm, Heat Resistant Glass Carafe, Permanent Filter, Auto Shut Off, Compact Coffee Maker for Home OfficeWe are a Keurig family but when we have parties or guests, sometimes, it best and more affordable to brew a whole pot. At the time of order, this 10 cup coffee maker was listed at a discount from $60 to $40. I love the simple black and stainless steel look that blends with our other kitchen appliances. We appreciate that it has a reusable filter so it eliminates the need to buy paper filters. It's fairly easy to dump out the grounds and rinse it. We haven't had to use the programable feature, but I can see that as being very useful if this was something you use daily and want fresh and ready to go first thing in the morning. There is a strength button that makes the brew stronger but not bitter. What we like a lot is the fact that you can remove the carafe before it's done brewing in case you're antsy and just need your coffee already and the coffee machine will pause the brew. It keeps it hot for 2 hours and then auto shuts off, which is a great safety feature. Overall, this machine is excellent for entertaining our family gatherings."
    },
    {
        "review": "We haven't had a drop coffee maker in quite some time. I'm usually more into French press or espresso but I occasionally find myself just wanting drip coffee. It's also really nice to have coffee waiting for me when I wake up which is kind of impossible with a French press. The filter basket works really well and is easy to clean. I'm really happy with this!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Sometimes I want a whole pot of coffee and not just 1 cup so this works great for me.  It is very asthetic looking and goes very will with my Stainless Steel and Black Kitchen appliances.  I really like that this coffee maker is programmable and I can set the time that I want it to brew my coffee so that when I get up in the morning my coffee is waiting on me instead of me waiting on my coffee to brew.  This has a \"strength\" feature to it and I couldn't really tell much difference in taste but I already use a very dark - strong french roast to begin with.  The touch controls on this are very sensitive and just the slightest touch of the buttons will change the time or the programming so be careful with that.  I set it for 10 cups and I get 10 cups, not 8 or 9 cups but actually 10 cups so that is great.  The price really makes this a good value too.  I really like how well this coffee maker works."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "We just received the SimplyGood coffee brewer. Did a water only run for clean up and followed with a one cup batch coffee brew. So here are our impressions:• unit came well packed with excellent protection• confirmed water path is all metal/glass including glass reservoir• the unit is much more streamlined and visually pleasing.• Design avoided a enclosed architecture.• Metal parts are easy to access for cleaning• brewing cone has a positive shut off lever* First brew was distinctly much better than old coffe makerIn conclusion we are very satisfied with this purchase. I suppose in the future it might be cheaper as sales volume increases."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent coffee maker. easy to use, looks great, I use it every day and brews great tasting coffee, good temperature, brews quick, no leaks, and great value for price. Love the no plastic where water touches.  will buy the newer model also with the timer.  i have 1st gen. still great."
    },
    {
        "review": "FINALLY A CHEMICALLY CLEAN AUTOMATIC COFFEE MAKER!I have shopped for years for an automatic glass/food grade stainless steel coffee maker and Simply Good Coffee came through. As far as I know, this is the ONLY company that has met the public demand for a clean coffee maker. All parts that touch the water and coffee are either food grade glass or high quality food grade stainless steel!!!All other coffee and espresso machine manufacturers use plastics along with cheaper grades of stainless. You may not want to publicly admit it but deep down inside you know the damage daily high heat does to plastic. Even the flavor of our coffee is affected, but worse the daily caustic toxins injested. I just can't do that to my and my families bodies. No wonder so many suffer health problems!We have been using the pour method over a glass double wall insulated Bodium carafe with a food grade stainless steel filter. The Simply Good Coffee brewer makes much better coffee than my prior clean method.  The hot water drips wide and slowly over the ground beans creating a wonderful frothy bloom in the grounds  bringing out the deep smooth and sweet tones.The machine is quite simple, which I like. Fewer things to break later on. I did not spend the extra on the programable coffee machine. The base model quickly brews in like 5 or 6 minutes. No mess, no fuss.I waited for my Simply Good Coffee machine to come on sale...$80 off. Still it is much more than I have ever spent on an automatic coffee machine but now I know the process is as clean as my Bodium and french press methods, but much better tasting!!!!Give Simply Good Coffee a try! Through Amazon, they offer a free 30 day trial with free return shipping. I purchased Amazon's 4 year additional warrentee which provdes me some relief since I spent so much on the machine.Enjoy knowing now when you drink your morning coffee, if you use the Simply Good Coffee brewer and quality organic coffee, like Purity Coffee beans, you are getting all those great antioxidents from the coffee without all the contaminates from inferior machines."
    },
    {
        "review": "Don’t buy the hype, yes it’s glass and stainless, no plastic.NO, it does not heat to 195 degrees, using my therma pen I’m only measuring 175 degrees, and that was after running 2 pots back to back.Definitely not worth the price tag.  Unless you are into Luke warm coffee.Brew time with bloom is 5 minutes.  Not bad, but definitely not Bunn quality."
    },
    {
        "review": "We're really enjoying the coffee maker.  I would have rated 5-stars if the water reservoir were removable.Features I like:-One-button start (non-programmable version)-Materials - high quality stainless or plated metal parts, glass carafe & water reservoir (although the glass is thinner than expected).  Plastics seem high quality and are not in the water/coffee flow-Ability to EASILY dissasemble and clean the components to assure good tasting coffee.  I have medium sized hands and can get my hand into the carafe for easy washing.Tips & Tricks:The mixing tube/carafe lid fits snugly on the carafe.  When removing or installing the lid/mixing tube, the rear of the lid should be seated, then pry up or push down near the spout.  This will keep the mixing tube from accidentally hitting the side of the carafe.Not as Expected:-the coffeemaker's website said the water reservoir is removable.  It is not, as confirmed with their customer service.  They will be changing the reference on their site."
    },
    {
        "review": "It was pricey and took a while to ship but it’s all I hoped it would be and I'm happy with the purchase.  Well made, looks good on the counter and the coffee tastes great.  I bought stainless filters #4 so I don’t have to use paper filters—if it helps anyone here’s a link to the ones I bought that are working great!2Pk #4 Cone Reusable... https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D3HPBDY7?ref=ppx_pop_mob_ap_share"
    },
    {
        "review": "Works great. Comes with 30 paper filters and will otherwise need more or require buying a stainless steel mesh filter, so my only preference with them making this for a leaching-avoiding audience is that they should have included a choice with purchase: permanent mesh filter or 200 paper filters. That would be a nice touch to make bundle sales like that in the future.My only other critique is a bigger one: The roof of the glass water container is plastic, and while the heated water comes up and out through steel tubing and thus the water never touches that plastic directly, it may cause that roof to heat enough and leach plastic into the steam droplets that touch that roof. The glass walls show trapped evaporate after making coffee, so surely some gets on the roof as well.I get that it both looks better and is cheaper to have black for that piece, but it undermines the concept, and the opening of it isn't even great plastic, as mine has an imperfection. The other plastic is purely casing and is fine, but this makes it feel less than 100% plastic-free.Still, this is the most plastic-free coffee maker available and they pulled it off and in a way it can survive shipping well without glass breaking. They deserve 5 stars for that still, because I finally feel like I can make coffee for my wife without causing her to drink little microplastics over time, and it's a genuinely good and good-looking machine as well."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is sad that this seems to be the only non-toxic coffee maker out there. It is nothing special otherwise, and shouldn't be as expensive as it is. The coffee it makes is fine, but the maker does not seem that sturdy. Not sure how long it will last. The glass carafe seems very fragile, so I will be very careful, because it is $40 to replace it. It should have been stainless and not had the hot plate. The coffee maker leaves quite a bit of water inside it after the brew, so I am concerned that it might start molding."
    }
]

