    {
        "review": "This coffee maker works well and brews a good cup of coffee. I like that it can use both K-Cups and ground coffee, and it includes a reusable filter for ground coffee, which is a nice bonus. It also offers different brew sizes and has a compact design that doesn’t take up much counter space.However, I think $99 is simply too expensive for such a basic machine. It’s made almost entirely of lightweight plastic and doesn’t feel particularly premium. Since it’s a single-serve brewer, it’s also not practical if you’re making coffee for multiple people.One thing I was disappointed by is that while it includes a reusable filter for ground coffee, it does not come with a reusable K-Cup pod, so you’ll need to buy one separately if you want a reusable option for K-Cups.Overall, it performs as advertised, but considering the simple build quality and limited features, I don’t think the price reflects the value. If it were significantly less expensive, it would be much easier to recommend."
