[
    {
        "review": "We initially purchased the coffee maker in March 2024 and rated it 2 stars because it worked well and then it completely failed within about three months. We're updating the rating and giving it 5 stars because Black & Decker was really great about replacing it for us and the new one has been working exactly as it should for at least a year since then. In the past, we've purchased much pricier coffeemakers, but now that we're retired and far more budget conscious, this coffee maker is perfectly fine -- even for total bougie coffee snobs. Our coffee tastes pretty great! It's a standard 12-cup model, reasonably quiet, the brewing time is reasonable, the coffee stays hot in the pot and we've had no leakage problems or any other issues. This coffeemaker really is a pretty great value for the money."
    },
    {
        "review": "Basic coffee pot capable of making a large, hot pot of black goodness that helps me 'get through this thing called life'. I am going all the way (5 star) for this basic drip maker. Obviously you can spend $400 and get a superior machine but in the basic coffee pot category? This one is great. Our last machine was so bad we celebrated when it died.Our last pot went through paper towels and cuss words like they were in competition with each other. Trying to pour from the carafe was a bloody nightmare with coffee dribbling off the pot mid pour. I hated that friggn thing. So did my hubs. This pot is so easy to pour from. It makes NO MESS.This one is easy to pour water into the back. There is no missing the pour area unless maybe you are drunk. (Note: Resulting cup of coffee may vary if/when there is alcohol involved.)It has a standard reusable basket for grounds right in the front that is super easy to clean, etcThe auto shut-off works TOO GOOD for all day drinkers. I appreciate the safety feature regardless. It does it's job. I just have to keep turning it on. That is a personal preference that has more to do with my addiction than it does the integrity of the coffee pot.It has a timer so you can have that baby cooking up your first morning pot while you are still drooling on your pillow.Anyways, Good pot, good coffee. I really hope his one lasts longer than the last one. If it doesn't, I will probably look for an upgraded pot with the same carafe.Good luck!"
    },
    {
        "review": "arrived on time & packet very well.  This was a replacement for an old Black & Decker, so i went with the newer basic model since it lasted so long.  This is the classic coffee maker style thats been around for ever. PROS: makes HOT coffee, the donut shape hot water dispenser does very well, no paper filters have fallen over with this design, still has the timer,  and the best new feature is the STRONG setting thats for making 1 to 2 cups at a time, plus it save coffee too, also when 30+/- brews happen it tells u its time for cleaning & has a built in cleaning mode. CONS: the lighted buttons glow are very dim & are especially hard to see in a bright room, the carafe or pot lid that one usually uses the thumb to push down to open the lid, your thumb has to go down into the side handle a little & its unconformable tight area especially with big thumbs.  All in all its a great basic automatic drip coffee maker and i hope this one last as long as its predecessor B&D model.  Would buy again."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's a coffee maker. Works great. less filling! Ha Good buy!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I debated over getting this. I didn't really 'need' a sneak a pot feature or a programmable timer, but I love the features now that I have them. Glad I spent a few dollars more to go with this coffee maker."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have had Mr. Coffee drip makers for many years and have loved them.  But when I needed to replace my old one, I decided to try this Black and Decker.  It is simple which is what I wanted.  I love the strong brew feature which is what I always use.  And the spray water head is great because it gets water throughout the coffee grounds rather than just coming out through one little hole.  It makes a rich tasting cup of coffee.  The only thing that bugs me is that when I lift the lid to take out the filter basket, water drips down the back of the coffee maker.  But overall I am very happy with this coffee maker and highly recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "CHEAPER THAN MOST UNITS, BUT YOU GET WHAT YOU PAY FOR. I GOT THE UNIT TODAY AND RIGHT FROM THE START I GOT MY FIRST SIGN THAT I PROBABLY MADE A MISTAKE. I HAD TO USE KITCHEN SCISSORS TO GET THE COVER OFF THE POWER CORD PRONGS (strike 1). I WENT TO PUT WATER IN THE  CARAFE AND NOTICED THE WATER LEVEL MARKERS WERE SO THIN THEY WERE BARELY VISIBLE. I HAD TO KEEP TURNING THE CARAFE UNTIL THEY WERE READABLE (strike 2). THE MANUAL SAYS THE ON/FF BUTTON LIGHTS UP. ALL I SAW WAS A TINY PIN POINT SIZE LIGHT INDICATOR HARDLY NOTICEABLE. THE MANUAL ALSO SAID THE BREW BUTTONS LIGHT UP, IF THEY DID THE LIGHTS MUST BE ON THE INSIDE BOTTOM, I DID NOT SEE ANYTHING. WHEN I WENT TO PLACE THE BASKET INTO THE UNIT I HAD KEEP WIGGLING IT BEFORE IT FIT IN (strike 3- it is out) . WHEN I AM STRUGGLING IN THE MORNING TO GET MY FIRST COFFEE I DO NOT WANT TO FUSS WITH A CLUTSY COFFEE MAKER. I JUST GOT IT AND IT'S GOING TO THE  DUMPSTER."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this for the programmable feature, which works as advertised. Unfortunately, the taste is mediocre at best even on the strong setting, I end up having to use more coffee to get the Rich flavor I prefer. The cord is too short, so unless you have a plug close to the machine, it can be a pain. Filling it can be messy as well. I found myself spilling the water while pouring into the back and some of the water would go down into the carafe. It’s also light and will move around, especially when you pull the carafe . I’d give it a C+."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've spent decades spending absurd amounts of money trying to find the perfect coffee maker.  After spending nearly a month in a rental house that only had an inexpensive coffee maker - and LOVING the coffee I'd get from it - I finally shopped around for something like it.  I landed on this particular model and couldn't be happier.  I feel silly for having invested so much over the years on coffee makers that didn't last nearly as long as they should have (for those prices).  If this one breaks down after a year, who cares?  I'll get another!  At this price, I can afford to buy a new one more often.  (Have been using it for a couple of months now. Perfect coffee every time. Super easy to operate, program, and clean.) ***UPDATE JUNE 2025: Still going strong! Not a single thing has changed. Carafe and basket cleaned in dishwasher daily without issues. All features working perfectly.  Still very happy with my decision to go low-tech and basic."
    },
    {
        "review": "At first, I wasn’t too sure about this coffee maker, but now that I’ve gotten used to it and know how to use it. It’s actually a good coffee maker I like Black & Decker. And it makes pretty good coffee. At first, I didn’t give it a very good review. But it’s not the coffee maker. It was just the person who was trying to make the coffee. Now that I know how to use it it works good."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm happy with the functionality of this machine.  It brews my usual 8+ \"cups\" of coffee in 11 minutes and keeps it at a good temperature for the stated 2 hours.  Capacity is 12 5oz. \"cups\", which is consistent with other coffee makers.  It pours without dripping and the interrupt function works well.While the clock is easy to set and very visible the on/off light is difficult to see unless viewed straight-on from a high angle, as may be evident from the three photos I'm attaching.  This makes it easy to leave the heat on after the pot is empty.  Improving the light is the one and only change I'd ask for."
    },
    {
        "review": "New coffee maker for the hunting camp. Big hit."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good quality! Good price!"
    }
]

