[
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐I’m really happy with this chair! It looks even better in person and feels very comfortable to sit in. The cushioning is nice, the back support is great, and I especially love that it comes with a footrest. It’s perfect for sitting for long periods of time, whether I’m working, gaming, or just relaxing.The chair also feels sturdy and well-made, and the design looks stylish without taking up too much space. Assembly was pretty straightforward as well.Overall, I’m very satisfied with this purchase and would definitely recommend it to anyone looking for a comfortable and affordable chair! ❤️"
    },
    {
        "review": "This GTPLAYER e-sports chair really exceeded my expectations! The installation process is very simple. It takes about twenty to thirty minutes to install according to the instructions. The accessories are complete and there are no missing parts.The chair is very comfortable to sit on. The biggest highlight is the Pocket Spring cushion. It is not as hard as an ordinary sponge chair, and the support is very good. You will not feel tired after sitting for a long time in office and playing games. The backrest has a strong feeling of wrapping, and the position of the lumbar support and headrest is also suitable, which has good support for the waist and neck.I bought the black one, which is basically the same as the picture. It is very good-looking, and the fabric is comfortable to touch, and it will not be as sultry in summer like leather. The armrest is linked with the backrest, and the arm is also supported when lying down to rest, and it is very comfortable to pull out the footrest for a lunch break.The overall workmanship is solid, the chair is very stable, the wheels slide smoothly, and there is no abnormal sound. At this price, it is really cost-effective, which is more comfortable than many more expensive e-sports chairs.I am still very satisfied after using it for a few days. If I still need to buy a computer chair in the future, I will choose GTPLAYER and recommend it to my friends."
    },
    {
        "review": "The hardest part about putting this thing together is the legs. It says \"slap on floor\" or something to get the screw holes to line up. THEY WON'T! What you really need to do is get it as close as possible to lining up, then put the bolt in at an angle but DO NOT SCREW IT IN! Put the tool into the bolt and then use the two to press inwards and kinda pry back the leg piece until the bolt stands upright like it should. THEN screw it in! A screwdriver won't work because it tends to slide right back out if you aren't holding it in place when you start to screw in the bolt. So when you remove the screwdriver to put the bolt in, you'll lose the alignment anyway. And you need the tool (included with it) in the bolt to be able to apply enough pressure while at an angle to \"catch\" the screw hole before pulling it into line.HEAD. ACHE.Aside from that, here's my assessment of the chair's use compared to about 4 or 5 others that I've used in my lifetime:The assembly is easy and straightforward after you get those leg screw holes lined up. The arms seem to be shorter in length and height than some other chairs I've had. But that's a good thing for me because when the seat is at the correct height, the arms of other chairs were rubbing against the underside of my *GLASS* top desk. Occasionally that little bit of give in the chair when I get up or descent when I sit down would snap the arms against the glass of my desk, and it always sounded like I would break it. Thankfully, I didn't.Also, I love the fabric covering! I ordered this specifically for that one reason. The one I'm about to throw out now has the typical vinyl covering and as it aged, it cracked, especially on the arm rests, and my arms were getting torn up by it!  While this cloth will also wear over time (especially being microfiber), it shouldn't create sharp vinyl pieces to scratch up my arms, so that's a plus!The back of the chair has a really thick dense foam that isn't quite conforming to my spine just yet. It's going to take some wearing in to really feel comfy. My worry is that once it breaks down enough to wear in, the foam may deteriorate very quickly afterwards. That's something to watch for in the future though. The arms may have a lighter foam, or maybe the foam just conforms better to sharper points, like elbows. But they seem to have more give to them, for which ever reason. The back also doesn't lean back as far as some gaming chairs I have had. That could be bad for me as I sometimes get *very random* vertigo and need to lie flat for a few minutes until it goes away. With this chair, I'll probably have to stumble to a couch or bed to lie down if it happens.The seat itself is not too long or short either. I've had some that were short enough I felt like I would fall off the front of the chair. And others that were so long that when I saw back, my knees were ON the seat of the chair. This one is, thankfully, right in between. The foot rest isn't anything special nor bad, but it \"attaches\" in the slides with a bolt on the back of one side. That will make it easy to remove when it's time to buy another chair. With the exception of the gas lift, most of this will be easy to take apart to fit inside of a large trash collection container when it's time for that. (Yes, I've gone through enough chairs for that to be a concern now!)I never use the lumbar supports, so I can't give any information on that."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair is a great quality but what's even better is the customer service. The chair lives in my teenagers Game Room AKA bedroom. It has withstood 7 months of hard use. He has been known to sleep in it and to have his 60 lb dogs sitting in his lap. Seriously this chair has taking some abuse. Approximately 8 months after we got it one of the arms broke off.. probably because my son was leaning to heavily on it. I contacted the manufacturer, sent them pictures and they immediately sent us a new arm rest and back of the chair because the armrest had ripped the leather of the back when it broke. From the pictures they also noticed that the lumbar support was misshapen (because of abuse) and offered to send a new one of those as well. When the items shipped, free of charge, they sent us a tracking number and even followed up after we received it to make sure everything was okay. I will definitely be a repeat customer of this company!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This gaming chair is incredibly comfortable for long sessions. The lumbar support and adjustable armrests make a real difference, and the breathable mesh keeps me cool. Sturdy build, smooth recline, and easy assembly. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely love my new gaming chair! The adjustable headrest, lumbar support, and pull-out footrest provide incredible comfort. It feels ergonomic and sturdy for long gaming sessions or work. It also comes with head pillow and back pillows! Very easy to install !  Highly recommended for anyone seeking style and support!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Pros: pretty comfortable so far but I haven't sat on it for an extended period of time yet.There's a tiny bit of side to side wobble (not enough to really care about it) but it feels pretty solid. Especially the base.Easy to assemble.Looks pretty nice. Doesn't take up a lot of room. This chair is skinnier than my last one but still wide enough to contain my fat body lolThe fabric material feels pretty good even against bare skin. The padded fabric armrests are a huge upgrade from the hard plastic/rubber ones ony old chair.Cons: the footrest isn't very long and feels like the cheapest part of this chair.The lumbar/back pillow isn't adjustable like on other chairs. It's just a loose pillow that sits on the chair. It's not that important to me but this may bother some people.The neck pillow is a lot smaller than I expected but still pretty comfortable when reclining.The levers that recline the chair and raise and lower the seat are  not in the best location. You really have to reach for them. The angle of the seat cushion feels weird. It feels like it leans slightly forward so it's not the best seating position for me. This leads to slight discomfort in my tail bone area after sitting for long periods unless I'm leaning forward myself.All in all I like this chair so far but I'm sure there are better ones out there around the same price. I will update if things start breaking any time soon lol  this is definitely an upgrade from my old and busted chair. I just wish I was able to order the color I wanted (I wanted the grey one) but when I added to cart it switched back to the default black one and for some reason Amazon wouldn't let me cancel the order even though I requested to cancel it only 20 minutes after ordering it. And this was on a late Saturday night. I submitted 3 cancellation requests and they still shipped the wrong chair anyway. Good job Amazon! The chair still looks good though and I don't feel like going through the return process so I'm just going to keep it anyway. This is a decent budget gaming chair"
    },
    {
        "review": "To first start off the chair is very comfortable as a heavy set person myself, and the different color options for it’s appearance is nice to see as most just come as black or white, The back plate is made of steel as it feels so it’s very durable and stable, The cloth is really nice, the con with the cloth is that it’s prone to get any type of animal hair stuck to it very easily and it’s a little hard to get the hair/fur off, the seat is cushioned a good amount where you can go about 10hrs-12hrs in it with very minimal to no discomfort, the wheel base is very sturdy and strong, but 11months in a screw shaped in the screw hole where you’d screw the leg into the base of the chair, I got ahold of customer support through emailing them and I was shocked only cause how fast they respond(2-3 hours after your email/reply) and honestly it was great! I had to provide proof of damage and they responded with sending me a new base and also a gas piston lift cause mine has a very small leakage where it’ll slowly go down from max lift tell it’s at its lowest it can get and stop, the customer support is very reliable and helpful, I’d say better then other chair brands, to put it short your getting a really good chair for the value that it is and a 1 year warranty along side with it, so I’d say give it a try!"
    },
    {
        "review": "A full month of usage by my son and the chair still hold. Can't be bad for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have been using the GTPLAYER gaming chair in light blue for some time and am very satisfied. The assembly was easy and all parts were complete and well made. The comfortable spring seat cushion is particularly impressive, as it still offers a high level of seating comfort even after several hours. The fabric surface is pleasant and significantly better than artificial leather, especially when it is warm. The backrest can be easily adjusted and, together with the extendable footrest, you can lean back and relax. The moving armrests are also very practical. Visually, the chair looks modern and high-quality and fits well in the study. Overall, it offers a very good price-performance ratio. A clear purchase recommendation for anyone looking for a comfortable gaming or office chair."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very comfortable, beautiful, functional. Highly recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent, very comfortable"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’m not sure what more you can ask for out of a chair at this price. Easy to assemble, looks pretty good, easy to operate, cushion, lumbar, and neck support are all really good and better than I was expecting. I love the foot rest and the ability to set the exact recline with ease. I’m 5’10” 170 lbs and this chair is very comfortable and foot rest is perfect. For larger people this chair may not be perfect, but it would likely get the job done. If you want something that looks fancy, this isn’t your chair. It looks nice and it’s sturdy, but not fancy. All parts are heavy black plastic. Are there better chairs out there. Yep. Do they cost 3x to 10x more? Yep. I’d say you get 90% of the chair for half the price of name brand “budget” gaming chair options. I’d be surprised if anyone who bought this chair didn’t rate it 8 out of 10 or higher."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair is a lot nicer than I had anticipated after reading some reviews.  It was packed extremely well and the directions and assembly was super simple!  They pack all the hardware in an easy access package that's labeled for every step in the assembly process.  They also give you the tool, an Allen wrench, that works on each bolt and screw.The chair is well designed and comfortable.  The seat is firm and thick!  Don't get me wrong, it's not hard by no means.  It has great cushion.  It's just well built.  Should last for years.It's sturdy!  It's not a cheap chair.  I bought the textile version at an incredible price and that's great marketing because after putting this baby together, I'd have no hesitations about buying another in the faux leather because I now know the quality is really they from this manufacturer.  Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair has been a fantastic purchase! I thought I would have to get a super expensive chair to get the comfort and support I wanted but this one was very reasonably priced and I got it on sale too. It's extremely versatile and very comfortable even for all day gaming. The lumbar pillow is the perfect firmness. The seat width is such a breath of fresh air. I can change how I'm sitting regularly and comfortably with plenty of room. All of its movement is smooth, i.e hinges, support column, wheels. My favourite feature so far is locking the recline in the exact angle I want with a quick push of a lever. It was easy to put together (though it took a bit of hand strength for some spots, like the last screws on the sides, so it may not be very easy for anyone with dexterity concerns.)It's almost completely noise-free and what noises it does make are quiet. The fabric is holding up well so far (2 months at the time of review). As a seamstress, I had concerns since the faux suede types usually aren't, but it's doing well. And the temperature regulates great. No overheating or sweating. The only thing struggling occasionally are the zippers on the neck and lumbar pillows. Sometimes they slip open since the fabric is so tight over the inserts, but they can be closed again and the zippers aren't technically broken yet. The footrest is a nice addition but doesn't extend far enough out to fully stretch my legs out. An extender that collapses into the main bars for the footrest would be needed since the bars are exactly the depth of the seat when put away. It they were longer they would stick out the back underneath the seat.All-in-all, a fantastic purchase that my weary body is appreciating when I'm at my computer. I'll try to remember to update this on the durability in a few months!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is actually a pretty solid chair. Was easy to put together, I’d say it took me about 35-40ish mins to put it together. I like the color, was a bit lighter than I expected tho. The material is very soft and comfortable, I like how it feels and everything. The seat padding is pretty firm, but not uncomfortable, could be a tad softer tho. I might need to break it in more. It reclines well and the leg/foot rest is solid and sturdy. The neck rest pillow works well, but I do wish the lumbar pillow was a tad thicker and actually strapped to the chair. My only gripe is the left arm rest wiggles a bit, that’s it. Over all happy with my purchase, would get again in a different color just to have or would give one as a gift."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this chair on August 6th, and after a little over two weeks of regular use, I absolutely love it. It is much more comfortable than my previous chair, which I had been using for years, and I can sit in it for long periods without feeling uncomfortable. I also haven't noticed any degradation in the cushioning, materials, or overall comfort so far, which is a great sign.The only downside I had was the assembly. There wasn't really a clear manual included with the chair, so figuring out exactly how everything was supposed to go together was a little confusing. I had to rely on YouTube videos to figure out some of the assembly, and finding a useful video was a bit of a hassle. Once I figured everything out though, the chair went together fine.Overall, I am very happy with the chair. It has been a major comfort upgrade from my previous chair and after a little over two weeks of use, it still feels just as good as when I first put it together."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really happy with this gaming chair. The lumbar and neck support are fantastic—I can sit for hours working and gaming without my back aching. The build quality feels very solid and sturdy. I also really like the fabric; it’s soft, breathable, and much more comfortable than leather/PU leather, especially for long sessions. Definitely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair looks great. I bought it because it had pocket spring construction and the seat wasn't your typical \"chunk of foam on a piece of plywood\"...and it was red. I hate it. It creaks and wobbles every time you move in it. It took me a solid hour to get one of the arm rest bolts threaded, then the next day, the arm fell off. It's back on, but I have no faith that it will not say goodbye again. The fabric is so slippery that after you sit in it for 15 or 20 minutes, you start to slide forward, out of the chair. Microfiber. Yuck. Warning: Do *not* try to lean back when the chair is in the upright position or you'll end up sitting on the floor (after the seat scrapes your back on the way down.) The headrest is in the right position and is quite comfortable. The lumbar cushion is uncomfortable and, if you do give it a try, it helps in pushing you out of the chair. Sitting on it doesn't help. If you decide to recline, make sure you have a friend there to take a video...so you can post it in the 'funny videos' area of YouTube. It reclines, but the spring isn't adjustable and has so little tension on it that you may end up somewhere you don't want to be. (e.g., the floor)I don't know who this chair was made for but it certainly wasn't me. Maybe it was you. I'm not a gamer. I just wanted a decent (and fairly comfortable) chair for my desk. Maybe if I was a 16 year old gamer I'd be ecstatic. But I'm not. While I'm at it, how does that tubby guy in the picture get his hugeness on that seat and cross his legs? I'm probably half his size and fairly flexible and I can't do that. I tried. Didn't work. I can easily get one leg up on the foot rest though - two if you cross them.Finally, on top of all of this, the pneumatic cylinder seems to lose air on a random basis.As much as I thought I would like this chair I do not. In fact, as much as I hate to say it, this is probably one of the worst chairs that has ever been introduced to my rear end...and back...and arms. I have been in old, wooden office chairs devoid of all padding and/or adjustment that were more comfortable.Even though it says \"FREE RETURNS\", I would return this chair in a heartbeat - except that I'd have to disassemble it and get it back in the box in a satisfactory manner. You should buy this chair, but only if you want a nice-looking, fabric covered chair that you will never enjoy sitting in. For me, it's just money wasted."
    },
    {
        "review": "I didn’t think this chair would be as comfortable as it is. I’ve bought a few gaming chairs this year looking for a good one under $200 and this was the one! Nice feel and super easy to put together! Love it and bought the light purple one as well 😌"
    },
    {
        "review": "Super comfortable, but you have to get used to the chair for a week to find it comfortable. This is because of the pillows. At the beginning you think “how uncomfortable are the pillows”, but your body has to get used to the new sitting position for a while and then you just say “BABA!”. The gaming chair offers a lot of little extras, e.g. the adjustable backrests or the front footrest, which can be extended. ASSEMBLY: The whole thing took me almost an hour, but you have to keep in mind that I had never assembled any chair before and was a bit shocked by the instructions at first, but it turned out that the instructions were easy to understand. You can compare it with an Ikea assembly plan. CONCLUSION: My conclusion is that I can definitely recommend this chair because it offers many extras and is comfortable (once you get used to the shape of a gaming chair). Nevertheless, the price of this chair is of course a lot of money, but I would say it's worth it, because you'll definitely keep this chair for a few years and the company is world-famous for its good gaming chairs."
    },
    {
        "review": "its a very good very comfortable chair in + the fabric and very good quality very comfortable for long gaming sessions another + the chair and high very easy to assemble all the tools its in sight nothing to complain about very good chair very happy for the price it doesn't get any better."
    },
    {
        "review": "First of all, a 10 for delivery, it arrived 1 week earlier than initially expected. The quality of the materials is very high, the touch and precision of the pieces stands out. The assembly is very simple, following the instructions without a doubt (I recommend an electric screwdriver to tighten the screws or it is very tedious to keep turning the wrench). The operation, the comfort, the fact that it has everything (Bluetooth, speakers, the adjustable armrests (also a rotary little) and the footrest makes it great for intense computer sessions, whether for work, leisure or gaming. It is even comfortable to take a nap if you want. The only drawback, and I hope the seller or manufacturer resolves this question, is that the left speaker does not sound. I understand that these speakers are for an immersive experience and therefore do not have much volume, since the sound is very faint. But looking at the Bluetooth receiver, it seems that each speaker should have a separate jack cable. and connect both cables to the receiver. I only found one, and before opening the case (which involves disassembling it) I want to make sure that there must be a cable, and that it will be inside the case because it has slipped through the exit hole. Without a doubt, at the price it is, I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good product, robust and comfortable. Easy to assemble, just with the key it comes with. We'll see how it ages."
    }
]

