[
    {
        "review": "Amazing gaming chair. Firm seat, which I like. Highly adjustable back. You can literally lie down in it lol. Has a pull-out footrest too. Not noisy or squeaky or anything like that. Seems pretty durable and highly stable. I have never felt it would tip over at all. I use it for gaming and doing college homework, so I'm in it for hours on end lol. Super easy to put together; instructions were easy to understand. Great chair for a great price. Dang good deal! I can highly recommend this gaming chair."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like the feel of the cloth vs leather chairs, leather ones tent to crack over time and our cat would leave scratch marks. It was easy to put together. Customer service is great. My teen son is on the heavy side so when he broke off one of the legs I contacted customer service for a replacement part and had one sent out with in a week. Then my son broke the backrest. I had worries that they would not cover it since they already sent a replacement part in the past but customer service was so nice and understanding and sent a replacement backrest with in a few days. I would definitely purchase this chair again. Out of the 5 name brand gaming chairs my son has gone through this is by far the best one of with great quality, comfort and stability."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair is a replacement for another gaming chair I had for a number of years that had the fake leather on it and tore off over time, so I decided to get one with a cloth cover instead.  I'm happy with the quality of the chair and it looks like it will hold up well over time.  It also looks really good.One thing to be aware of is that the chair seat is very firm.  If you want a chair that is softer, this is probably not the best option for you.  It is still comfortable and I'd still recommend it for anyone who doesn't mind a more firm seat.Another thing to be aware of is that the width of the back between the raised sides is rather narrow.  If you have broad shoulders or are a bigger person, you may not be able to lean back comfortably in the chair.The chair can be put together pretty easily by one person and the only issue I had was the picture for attaching the seat back to the seat... the bar that attaches is shown in the picture backwards from what it is supposed to be.  If you watch the video that they provide, it's clear how to attach it, but if you're following the instruction images, it may be confusing.The reclining lever is the type that you can push or pull and let go while adjusting the back rather than the spring ones where you have to hold it while adjusting the back.  Either option is fine, but I find this style to be slightly more convenient."
    },
    {
        "review": "Like other reviews say theres something wrong with the armrests where something sharp stabs u, other then that its a perfectly fine chair and really comfortable. Looks really good and pretty durable id say"
    },
    {
        "review": "Probably the best economy chair on the market.I needed a second chair for guests and didn't want to spend for another SL chair. This one is surprising well made for the price.Pros:Metal frame. Definitely better than cheaper plastic options. Solid build.Easy assembly. I was able to put it together by myself in about 35 minutes.Material. Reminds me a bit of car seat material. Decently soft and seems fine for prolonged sitting.Cons.Leg rest is really short. Basically useless and I'm only 5'8, BUT it's a standard size and can be replaced with an alternative.Lumbar pillow is not attached. Also kind useless.Arm rests. Not adjustable. But they do move with the recline.Overall, I got it for $100 and worth every penny."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my first ever gaming chair and it makes a great first impression. As the title says, it's comfortable, it's sturdy, and the black and grey color combo looks really nice.the packaging was compact, the instructions were very easy to follow as everything is coded with numbers and letters to show where each hardware piece belongs to what part and how to install it properly.The foot rest is not necessarily a foot rest, it's more for your calves ( I'm 5'9\")The assembly took me roughly 30-45 minutes. Only complaint I have with it is assembling the arm rests, while yes they flex to adjust to the backrest, screwing them in can be tedious since the screws sometimes jump out and make you start over again. I suggest having a second person help out with the arm rests by pressing them into the chair while the other person screws the hardware in.otherwise, i've had this chair for now roughly 2 weeks and it feels great. it's helped with my back pain a bit from my old lounger chair.i highly recommend also to vacuum the fabric before assembly, and give everything a nice disinfectant spray before sitting down on it; let the spray sit for a few hours / a day. As with most warehouse items / packaged items, this will come with a smell. I used the Febreeze disinfectant / odor eliminator spray on everything as i assembled it, then gave it a nice vacuum clean. no more smell!if you're looking for a first time gaming chair, or a low-cost, good quality gaming chair, or even a gift for your grandkids, kids, nephew, niece, etc. this is a good buy for them.There's also no noise or squeaking when spinning around in it or moving it around on the wheels. Very smooth motion!"
    },
