[
    {
        "review": "Easy to assemble.  Comfy, though I have owned it about a week, we find it still as comfy.  Adjusting arm rests are useful. I'm 5' and it's a bit tall for me at the lowest setting, but my fiance is 6'2'' so at a higher height works for him.  I recommend it.  I'd buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very comfortable chair! Large seat area, comfortable arm rests, comfy back with good support. Smooth wheel action, easy assembly with good instructions and all parts clearly labeled. Only con would be that the seat height would probably be too high for someone with short legs, as I am 5'4\" and the seat's lowest setting is where my feet touch the floor. Glad I took a chance and purchased this chair."
    },
    {
        "review": "Seems to be solid built for the most part. Love that it came with extra screws and a T-handle allen wrench for the screws. But like most furniture that comes with allen screws/tools, by the end assembly, the tool starts stripping, so be careful or grab a socket like i did. The chair works great, if i had to complain about anything, the arms are solid built but the have some movement, that appears to be the only weak part of the chair. I love the all metal base, i just wish the casters were also metal. Im 6’2 and 279lbs, it supports me very well. Im sure the cushion could be better but for the price, its fine. Speaking of price, check other chairs from this company before buying, i think i paid $109 for this one, after looking i could have got a very similar chair for $59 or even the exact same chair as this one with a head rest for $79.  Overall a good chair"
    },
    {
        "review": "Arms do lift straight up in line with the back if you want them out of the way, seat does lower or rise depending on how you have it set. Does have slight give to it when you lean back, so that it is not stiff. It has been quality so far, was easy to assemble and looks nice next to my desk."
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect chair for my son’s room to go with his new desk for homework. It fits perfectly and is just the right size for him (teen, age 13). It holds up to 330# which he does not come even close to but it is still a great size for himSimple, comfortable, and exactly what we needed for his study space. Very happy with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "It functions as a chair and it is pretty comfortable.  That said, it squeaks every time I get up or sit down or move in it.  Also it does not roll very well.  I think this may be due to the fact that the wheels are not solid on the bottom, they look rather like two very thin wheels joined at a common axle. It's not bad enough for me to return it, but I regret the purchase and will definately not be buying another."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a fantastic chair that offers great value for money! It is easy to assemble, very comfortable to sit in, and fits perfectly at my computer desk."
    },
    {
        "review": "The chair is a much better quality than I expected for the price. Back lumbar support is not the best. However, since I only spend an hour or so at my desk, it's very comfortable. The seat has lots of padding and is a much larger than expected.A little trouble assembling the chair as the holes didn't easily match up. So some it took a little over an hour to get it together. But extra screws and the screwdriver are enclosed. Would definitely buy again!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "A great chair.  Exactly what I needed for a dual purpose result.  On the one hand a comfortable mobile chair with back support and armrests for attending to my computer and regular desk duties.  And second, with the arms flipped up I can strap on my guitar, have my usual prep workouts to loosen the fingers, and then get into \"playing mode\" and work through my song choices as part of my daily practice.  A little tricky to assemble but it only takes patience and following the provided guidelines to get through it, and then - Voila -  Assembled and customized to your exact needs."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a light and basic black office chair with synthetic seat upholstery and metal legs.  Assembly took me less than 30 minutes.  The seat is not perfectly horizontal, but is instead tilted back a little.  The back of this chair features rigid peace of plastic serving as lumbar support that may be adjusted up or down, depending on personal preferences.  It is able to tilt back in a limited range when I lean back, and the counteracting force may be adjusted by tightening or releasing a coil spring located under the seat.While in sitting position, the user will only be able to operate a single paddle lever that allows changing the height of the chair.  There is no provision to change/adjust neither the initial seat nor back inclination.  The armrests are not rigid enough imho.  They may be lifted upwards, which helps to push the chair deeper under the desk when not in use.  In my case, lifting one armrest also helps me to easier operate the computer mouse which is located on under-desk tray just above my knee height.Overall, I believe the quality of this chair corresponds to its modest price.  It will definitely serve well enough while on the budget."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great chair at a really good price point!  Easy to put together and very comfortable.  Would definitely buy again!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair arrived disassembled, but it was very easy to put together (it did require a bit of screwing in).  The first page in the manual has a QR code, you just go to that youtube link, and it made the simple assembly even easier.  The manual is fairly easy to follow too if you don't want to watch the video.  The chair is quite comfortable, the seat is large and padded, the meshwork fabric keeps it breathable and cool.  I like that the armrests are also padded, hydraulic height adjustable and rocker incline can be set.  The only difference to my existing chair is this one did not have an individual headrest, but I don't usually use the headrest anyway so it is more than fine without.  Rolls smoothly."
    },
    {
        "review": "Lightweight and lumbar support can be moved to adjust to your back height.  I like it for the price"
    }
