[
    {
        "review": "I really liked this chair. It's comfortable and feels quite sturdy and stable. The lumbar support is very helpful, especially when I spend a lot of time sitting. I also like that the armrests can be flipped up when I need more space. The mesh back allows for good airflow, and the design looks modern. Assembly was easy following the instructions. Overall, I think it's a good chair for the price, and I'm happy with my purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "These chairs are incredibly comfortable, and I highly recommend them. I would say they are the best desk chairs I’ve ever sat in from the cushioned seat, to the adjustable arm rest and everything in between, I'm very happy with this purchase.I sit at my desk all day for work, so I needed a new chair. The great reviews sold me on these, but I wasn’t sure whether I would want a headrest. I ended up getting two of their padded-armrest chairs, one with a headrest and one without so I could compare the two.The chairs are pretty much identical, except the one without the headrest has a slightly larger seat. I’m shorter than average, but even the larger seat was still very comfortable for me. The headrest is convenient because it allows me to lean my head back and relax instead of constantly leaning forward, which helps prevent tech neck. Since I’m on the shorter side, I’m still working on finding the perfect position for the headrest, but it’s still really nice to have.Both chairs were easy for one person to assemble, and the materials and overall quality feel very well made.However, the biggest praise I want to give is to their customer service. It is honestly the best customer service I have ever experienced from an online company. They provided a direct phone number with the packaging, and when I had a question, I called and was connected straight to a live person. She was extremely helpful and even called me back on a weekend, just as she had promised. I actually missed her call, but she called back later to make sure I received her voicemail.I will definitely continue shopping with this company. There truly wasn’t a single thing I was disappointed with. Great chairs, great quality, and exceptional customer service!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this TRALT chair to work several hours a day at the computer, and it has exceeded my expectations. The mesh back allows for good ventilation, preventing my back from getting too hot, and the lumbar support provides excellent support throughout the day. The adjustable headrest helps maintain a comfortable neck posture, while the fold-down armrests are very practical when I need to save space.The chair feels sturdy and stable, even with extended use. The seat is wide, padded, and comfortable, and the casters glide smoothly. Assembly was also easy thanks to the included instructions.Overall, it's an excellent option for its value. I recommend it for those who work from home, study, or spend many hours sitting at a desk. 👍🏻💺✨"
    },
    {
        "review": "I guess I misread the size this chair is intended for (description says 54”-62” - but I saw it as 5 foot 4 to 6 foot 2 because of the 300 lbs weight limit) - I mean, I guess that’s really my fault.. but seriously, WHO IS 300lbs and 4 foot 6? So needless to say the lumbar support is in the totally wrong place for me being 6 ft - but I’m sure it’s well placed if you’re a petite person for which it was intended.Anyway, I’m keeping it because it works for my daughter that is 5’ 6” (she says it’s “super comfy”) and the chair design looks really sharp and modern (we got the Gray on White frame).The reason I’m not giving it 5 stars is because there’s no way the seat cushion can handle 300lbs, I’m only 210 and my butt fell asleep after 2 hours of sitting in it.. also, the arms flex so much using them to get up out of the seat I’m afraid they will snap under my weight (again, I’m not even close to the 300lb weight limit it’s intended for).While the lumbar adjustment goes in and out towards or away from your back, it’s good to note that it does NOT adjust up or down.Props to the mfr for keeping the parts to a minimal and reusing the same screw sizes for most of the build, that was helpful so I didn’t have to worry if I was using the correct screw lengths or washers.. they also include a really nice T Allen wrench instead of the standard L style (which is a super nice touch) - so all this kept the assembly simple and I was done in less than 20 minutes.Putting my misunderstanding to the side, the reason this gets dinged a star is due to the seat having weak arms, thinner than expected seat padding, and the inability to adjust the lumbar support up/down.. other than that it’s actually a good solid and stylish chair for somebody in the 4 1/2 to 5 1/2 foot, sub 200lb demographic."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’m really impressed with this TRALT ergonomic office chair. It has a comfortable, supportive design that makes a big difference when sitting at a desk for several hours. The lumbar support is one of my favorite features because it provides good support for the lower back without feeling too stiff.The chair is also very adjustable. I like being able to adjust the seat height, headrest, backrest, and armrests to find a comfortable position. The flip-up armrests are especially convenient when I need more space around my desk.The breathable mesh seat and back are another great feature. They help keep the chair comfortable during longer work or study sessions, and the cushioning provides a nice balance between softness and support. The reclining function is also great when I want to lean back and relax for a few minutes.The wheels roll smoothly, and the 360-degree swivel makes it easy to move around my workspace. The chair feels sturdy and well made, and I really like the overall modern look.Assembly was straightforward and the instructions were easy to follow. Once assembled, the chair felt stable and solid.Overall, this is a great ergonomic chair for working from home, studying, gaming, or simply spending a lot of time at a desk. It offers a lot of adjustable features and comfort for the price. I’m very happy with it and would definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this chair for my daughter and she loves it.  I was skeptical about whether it would be good because it was so much cheaper than the fancy ones, but my daughter says it is very supportive for her back even after hours of summer gaming.  It has been about 7 months and no complaints with this chair so far.  We purchased all black.  It's nice looking, was easy to put together.  The height adjusts so you don't have to worry about what size desk you have.  I did have to call customer service once and i got 2 beeps and then the line disconnected.  I thought- well that stinks...but they called me back.  They were super pleasant and easy to deal with.  I'm thinking of getting the smaller tralt chair for myself.  I wouldn't hesitate to buy from them again"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really wanted to like this chair but, while there are things I do like about it, there are too many things I find fault with.For context, I am 73 years old, am 6’3” and weigh in around 265lbs. My last chair was designed for big and tall people and it fit me to a tee. I worked from home for two years during the apocalypse and that chair was super comfortable and I could spend over 8 hours a day in it with no problems. Unfortunately the faux leather wore off so I needed a replacement. I retired a couple of years ago and now only spend a few hours a week in front of the computer so I really don’t need anything too fancy or expensive.After researching a bunch of chairs, I settled on the Tralt Mesh Back Ergonomic Computer / Gamer Chair. I’ve never had a mesh chair before so I expected it to feel a lot different from my old all faux leather chair and it does feel a lot different but it’s what I expected.The good:1. Price. For $130.00, I think this is a pretty good deal.2. Assembly. Fairly quick. It took me about 30 minutes to unbox and assemble but I took my time so you could probably do it in 15-20 minutes easy. All parts lined up correctly and all bolts screwed in without any problems.3. Weight. This chair is at least 50% lighter than my old chair so carrying it fully assembled upstairs was easy for me.4. Appearance. Very nice.5. Adjustments. Raising and lowering the chair is smooth and easy. Control lever and hydraulic piston work well. Tilting mechanism is also smooth and easy.The not so good.1. IMO, this chair is NOT for anyone over 6’ if you are going to spend any time in it. The Amazon description says this will fit people who are 5’2” - 6’4”. Nope. The measurements shown in the description PHOTOS says 5’3” - 6’2”. Also nope. The front of the seat cushion hits my legs about half way up the thigh. It should hit closer to the knees. This makes me feel like I’m sitting on the edge of the chair. If the seat cushion was 24” in depth instead of 19-1/2” this would solve that problem. Also, if the lumbar support was positioned correctly, it might fit and feel better as well.2. Lumbar support. As other reviewers have stated, the lumbar is too low and hits your tailbone, not the lumbar area of your back. This setup might be acceptable for someone shorter but for anyone 6’ or taller this is a problem. The lumbar is adjustable but it’s kind of a moot point in my case.3. Arm rests. They are adjustable and slide forward but for taller people, even if fully adjusted forward, the arm rests still sit too far back and are not comfortable.4. Stability. When I sit in the chair it doesn’t feel super solid. I don’t know how to explain it but I feel like I am going to tilt off to the side. It’s just a weird feeling. The chair doesn’t actually tip side to side but it’s just this odd feeling I get when I sit and even when rolling forward.5. Weight capacity. The description says the chair has a weight capacity of 330lbs. This is probably true but, after using the chair for a while, I wonder about the longevity of the chair for someone heavier like me.Look, as I said earlier, for the price this is a good deal. I only use the chair once or twice a week so decided to keep it as returning it was more of a problem than I wanted to deal with. If the seat cushion was 3-4” longer, it would fit my legs much better and I would be a lot happier.My advise: if you are big and tall like me, pass on this chair. Spend a little more money and get something that fits you."
