    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent product comfortable chair took about 20 minutes to put together much better than my experience trying to purchase one from eBay would purchase from this seller again"
    },
    {
        "review": "Not recommended.  Buy something else .  I should have paid a little more and gotten a much better chair/experience.Comfort: Fail.  Bottom line is that chair is just uncomfortable.- The seat cushion does not feel good on my but after just 15 minutes of sitting in it.  I had to put a bed pillow on it to make it somewhat useable for more than an hour.- Lumbar support is very disruptive and just feels horrible, would prefer to take it off.- Headrest is horrible.  I am not tall (5 foot 8) and the headrest was so low on my shoulders which is very uncomfortable and clearly a design flaw.  The tippy top of the head rest is below my ears, so literally no head support.  It would be even worse for anyone taller than 5 foot 8.  which would be most people.- Arm rests are not height adjustable and are incorrectly height designed compared to low head rest.- Last time, I bought a slightly more expensive chair and it was significantly more comfortable.- Better than a $20 folding chair... which isn't saying much.Building it: Fail- I followed the directions and also did it a second time in a different order.  Either way, the alignment was very difficult to get into the screw holes.Quality: Fail- Feels cheap"
    },
    {
        "review": "I waited 16 months to write this review. I’m at the top end of this chairs capacity, I’m 340lbs and 6’6” tall. I use this chair as my 44hr a week office chair. It took 16 months for something to finally give out. A wheel caster finally collapsed. I ordered new ones next day and was back up and rolling. I bought this chair for $99.00, a great investment. It’s hard to find office chairs for larger people so I wasn’t expecting a long life for such a lower price item, let alone be comfortable. From my experience, this was a great find."
