        "review": "Good chair definitely not big and tall but found another use for it so it kinda worked out."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great chair! Received it on time. It took me a little over an hour to put it together on my own. I was missing an arm rest & contacted the company.  They responded quickly & are sending out the arm rest. I've been using it the last couple days & it's comfortable. The footrest is a little tricky to pull out, but once it's out it's nice. I'm only 5'4\" so the foot rest fits nice.  All in all I'm happy & would recommend.Only downside is that I wish there was velcro or a strap on the lumbar pillow, whenever I get up I have to readjust it as it doesn't stay in place.  But it is nice to have!"
    },
    {
        "review": "All in all, good chair for the price. I bought it on sale for $120. It has pros and cons. Pros first: Very comfortable, super soft, it looks nice and I can sit in it for hours. It's sturdy and has good padding in the butt area, head pillow and lumbar support pillow are nice. The footrest is nice and can support my legs. Arm rests are comfy and soft. I could definitely fall asleep in this chair.Cons: You cannot adjust the armrests. I find my hands falling asleep unless I bring the chair higher up, which makes me bring my monitor higher. This is not a rocker, meaning you have to lock and unlock it whenever you want to change the lean position. I will keep this chair as it is much comfier than the one I'm coming from. Also a piece of my McDonald's hash brown fell and bounced off one of the arm rests and landed clean on my desk so that makes this chair awesome and raised it a star."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair took 2 adults, one who works in the furniture industry about an hour to build from start to finish. The directions are very straight forward and clear, however the screw packs are incredibly difficult to understand. There are overlapping number and letters and there were times we opened up the wrong package. Be sure to take a picture of the hardware before you begin as the instructions tell you to!!! It was a lifesaver when we had to go back and figure out where we went wrong.The foot rest has only one rail to it so that it can swing out easily, just do not over tighten it. We did find the foot rest much too short for my 6'10\" daughter, so she doesn't use it much. It does stay tucked underneath well when not in use.The only thing we had difficulty with is the arm rests not staying secured. The both fell off within days of assembling the final product and were very difficult to attach. The screws are just shy of being long enough to secure them properly and I did worry about stripping them after trying to secure them multiple times.Overall, the chair has not wiggled or wobbled since assembly, with the user weight of 290lbs. We did choose not to install the casters on our chair due to being on hardwood floors and the chair sits flush with the floor without harm.The fabric of the chair is a gorgeous lavender purple and very soft to the touch. The seat is firm and the backrest is high enough to support your upper and lower back.Perfect in every way."
