        "review": "I don't often write product reviews. But this chair is worth the price.COMFORTABLE"
    },
    {
        "review": "First of all I would like to compliment the assistance from the seller. The product ships in two packages and, initially, I thought one of the two was missing. Only a few hours later I discovered in my email that the seller had provided me with the tracking of the second package. I ordered the product on Sunday and, although there was talk of a 9 or 11 day wait, in just 4 days I already found it at home with a notice from the courier (the second package arrived the next day). Assembly was somewhat cumbersome at the beginning but not impossible, it took me a long time (almost two hours with the necessary breaks due to the heat) but the instructions (in English and German) are very intuitive (in case of difficulty you can find several very good tutorials on YouTube!) and each bolt, nut and screw is packaged and identified in an orderly manner, complete with extra fixings to secure the steering wheel, pedals and gearbox. Despite the low price, the station is quite solid, the seat is quite comfortable, which can move forwards and backwards and is also reclining. The steering wheel and pedals, G29, can be placed in different positions and angles thanks to the available support grids. Despite my robust build (almost 100 kg) and my height (almost 190 cm) I find myself quite comfortable and the possibility of moving the seat, positioning the pedals forwards or backwards or even tilting the steering wheel, allows me to put myself at ease. The only flaw, which however does not influence my entire positive opinion of the product, was that one of the tubulars had a small bump on the inside, a scraper, and a slightly scraped cut point (which could be solved with a nice rubber seal). Surely the product may have suffered a shock during transport but honestly it doesn't seem right to lower the review to 4 stars for these little things. At the end of all I recommend this seat, especially to those who don't have one and would like to start with something solid and economical while approaching sim racing. PS: The seat also has two speakers, which connect via Bluetooth, but I can't tell you much because I only play video games with headphones so I'm not interested in knowing if they work well or badly."
