    {
        "review": "If you are not comfortable with this chair, it is because you have a problem with your body... It is comfortable, spacious, the components are resistant and the head cushion is wonderful for working many hours. Recommended without a doubt"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am a transfer from AK●cing. I'm an engineer so I'm sitting there all the time, but the current situation is good and I'm satisfied. However, if you are big and short, you will need a footrest (otherwise it will put pressure on the backs of your thighs). ●Good points: Easy to assemble ★: Incredibly easy texture ◎: Smooth even though it's made of cloth. This is the perfect solution if you don't like the durability of PU leather, but you also like the texture of fabric. Lumbar support 〇: For a built-in type, it protrudes quite a bit. Armrest ◎: Feels solid. The top is really chewy. Seat/Back 〇: For someone who is used to the fluffy type of AK, this is quite a hard type. It doesn't have a semi-bucket type rise like common gaming chairs, so it's easy to sit cross-legged. Rocking ◎: A nice feeling where you can sink in and relax (loss of vocabulary). Pillow ◎: This pillow is soft against the seat surface and does not hurt the back of your head. ●Bad points (I knew this from research so I can accept it) Size △: Cylinder is high, too big for someone 165cm tall, as expected from a foreign country. It seems to be perfect for people of 175-180cm. *This is not a problem because I prepared a separate footrest. Caster △: I use it on the ground like an office mat, but it doesn't roll around much so it takes a lot of force to move it a little. On the other hand, it feels solid and stable."
    }
