        "review": "I purchased this chair for my husband’s home office, and it has been a great choice.The height and angle can be adjusted very easily, making it comfortable to customize. Assembly was also simple and straightforward.The size is just right, and it remains comfortable even after sitting for long periods of time without causing fatigue.Overall, the quality exceeded my expectations for the price. If it ever breaks, I would definitely purchase the same one again."
    },
    {
        "review": "This chair offers good lumbar support and a well-padded seat. It has a very nice and smooth rocking motion, you can loosen the tight/loose knob for reclining, and it is very comfortable to sit in while working on the computer or relaxing to watch TV. The back of the chair hits just above my neck, so the back of my head rests comfortably on the top of the chair. The color, brown, is exactly what I expected and looks professional. The height adjustment works well, it sits higher than my old chair, and I like that. It seems sturdy for the 300-pound weight recommended. I got it on Prime Day, so it was a good value for the money.  It came packed well and quicker than expected. The pictures are a comparison to my 20-year-old office chair.Assembling the chair was easy, however, be sure to attach the bottom part of the chair with the tight/loose knob facing the front of the chair. It's not clearly marked on the instructions.  When it came time to put the back of the chair on it would be good to have another person to hold the chair back for you to align the chair arm holes and screw in, then you should be OK but I did discover that if I had attached the arms to the back of the chair first, it would be so much easier to align them for attachment. The wheels glide very easily and will take you across the room after one push. It swivels at 360 degrees easily, almost making me dizzy.I am writing this review the same day I got the chair so I will update if I run into any issues. Otherwise, I recommend this chair."
