    },
    {
        "review": "This is a very high build-quality chair from Razer. As others have pointed out, the build quality is top notch. The problem is, it's not very comfortable. For the amount I spent on it, I was expecting extreme comfort when I sat down in this chair the first time. I was surprised that felt quite stiff and not really comfortable. It may soften up in time, but - again, for the price of this chair, I think it's reasonable to expect comfort from the get go. Also, the only adjustments you can make are to the height of the seat and how far back the back goes. You can't even recline without manually adjusting the position of the back of the seat.Pros:- It looks cool- Very high build quality- Lumbar support is very goodCons:- Not very comfortable- No place to put your feet up- Limited adjustabilityI'm going to return this one and look at some of the gaming chairs with more features and a lower price."
