        "review": "The price is enough to scare you into looking elsewhere, but trust me, THIS is the chair for you! Unique styling unmatched quality put this gaming chair in a completely different bracket than its counterparts. Are there cheaper options? Absolutely, can you finder a chair with better looks? maybe...(Secret Labs) better construction? I seriously doubt...This is the APEX of gaming chairs! Everything else is just chair with wheels."
    },
    {
        "review": "It's not awful but just hear me out. I'm a rather tall fellow, I'm 6'5 and its majority legs so I have a shorter torso. The maximum height specified for this chair is 6'4 if I am correct. I didn't inherently think too much of it...to any ladies reading that one inch makes a difference.As a preface, I have never bought into the fad of racing or bucket seat style gamer chairs. I just never saw the point when most chairs I've had were just office chairs but more often than not fit my height. I got this one a few months ago and really sat with it, pun intended, to decided if I liked it or not. I reeeeeeeaaaaaallllllyyyyy want to like this stupid chair, but it is just so ridiculously uncomfortable. I'm a massage therapist so I'm on my feet and actively leaning over for my work days, I don't need a chair that exacerbates those issues when I'm sitting down. The built in lumbar curve is a neat idea but for me it presses into my spine so firmly that I can't find a spot to sit comfortably leaning back because I can't rest my head either. To anyone that is reading that is of a normal height that wants this chair, get the Enki Pro, it still comes with the magnetic headrest that is the same color as the chair. I don't know why, but Razer doesn't sell the headrest independently, so if you're like me and got the Enki X you're only options are something off brand, ebay, or Hello Kitty themed. To build on that, I've gotten stuff an attempt to make this chair more comfy. I got an actual lumbar support for chronic back problems a headrest and even as far as to replace the 2d arm rests for 4d ones to maybe see if that would help. No, it didn't. The chair isn't so bad when I'm playing something that I use a keyboard and mouse for which I feel like this chair is meant for that type of gamer. Where as, I just play with a controller for most games and try to kick my feet up. And the seat, the seat. I thought it would just take a little bit to break in...no it's still stiff as a board. I'm maybe like 200 or 210 so nothing crazy but I would atleast assume that after 3 months of relatively active long game sessions, it would be broken in.All in all, I probably spent about $650+ on my comfort which was the exact sentiment I had when browsing for chairs and now here I am, browsing for cheaper office chairs that will be infinitely more comfortable. This could just be a case of skill issue and I'm simply not the target for this chair because I really want to like it. I've been a looooooooong time Razer user and I love their accessories and thought why not give their chairs a shot. I'm not terribly dissapointed as all my other Razer stuff has done pretty right by me and this was just a circumstantial thing."
