[
    {
        "review": "I grew up in the days of using paper bags as book covers, and the era of the basically indestructible Jansport backpacks. But now that we live in the internet age, it was time to get a backpack that could safely hold my laptop among other things.The first thing that caught my attention is the color - the sage green shade is one of my favorites and I was thrilled to get a backpack in this hue. The second thing I noticed was how light it is. It doesn't take up much space, but it has plenty of padding and makes me feel secure enough to trust that it'll protect my laptop and other items.There is a padded pouch in the back that can fit my MacBook Air, my iPad, or any of my other electronic device securely. It has padding on both sides, and the back of the backpack is mesh and breathable. There are pockets throughout - one for a laptop, one opposite that to secure items, and two separate pockets on the front, one of which has two inner pockets for pens, styluses, or other items you might want to keep apart from the rest of your things.The back is padded with a mesh overlay, keeping my back cool when I use this, and it has a stretchy pocket on the side for a water bottle. The straps are padded as well, and I love that a strap comes all the way around from the back and snaps to secure the backpack and prevent anyone from sneaking anything out of it.I will absolutely be using this to carry my laptop around and for short excursions. I love that I can safely store my laptop or tablet and still have room to put clothes, papers, books, or anything I need to bring when getting away for a day or two."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a better backpack for the price than I'd imagined! When I saw mention of a 15.6\" laptop I thought the bag would be slimmer, and was completely wrong - I misunderstood one of the images in the product listing. If you put a laptop in the main compartment instead I think it will fit a 16\" easily even if the laptop is in it's own lightweight sleeve to protect it. One of the photos shows a 15.6\" that I carry a lot in the main compartment and there is a lot more room for books, notes, food and so on. It's also roomy enough for spare clothes, and for use as an overnight bag.The sewing is good, and the zippers are securely inserted. They're not particularly heavyweight or rugged, like a backpack you might take on expeditions and adventures, but it's not that type of backpack and I don't think they're an issue for everyday use. There were a few loose threads, but if you were holding it in a store you might pull them out and buy it anyway.There is a care label sewn inside indicating that it can be machine washed and hung in the shade to dry, great for a bag that will probably get a lot of use.The bottom doesn't have any reinforcement or feet to protect it against wet or dirty surfaces, and in the end that's the reason for removing one star from the rating. So if you're travelling on trains or subways, or through wet or snowy weather, you might need to watch where you set it down. Otherwise, it looks durable, the color is perfect and easy to spot, and it's a great buy around 30$."
    },
    {
        "review": "This review is for Bagstellar Laptop Backpack for Women, Puffer, selling for $32.99 at the time of my review.I am quickly becoming a huge fan of Bagstellar products! This is my third or fourth. I've lost count. Each is well constructed. Each is ample. Each is awesome. Each is both beautiful AND functional ... it's a one, two punch.This back-pack is no exception. I love it and I haven't even used it for it's true function ... yet ... and will when I return to college. How do I love it? Let me count the ways ...1) Padded wide straps2) Five zippered compartments, one is hidden, one is inside3) Five non-zippered compartments and/or pockets, one deep and large and on the inside, two on the outside for bottles (both bottle compartment have a strap to securely fasten bottles into place), and two cell-phone size inside one of the zippered compartments4) All the lining in all of the compartments are water resistant for easy cleaning5) The sage color is gorgeous6) It's really roomy7) It's well constructed and it's sturdy.What I do not like in any design of any product is if the designer never really used them in real life. Like some vacuum cleaners have awkward placing of the cords, or my iPhone has a button on the side where I keep inadvertently turning the thing off. It should be placed on the top!Anyhoo, I feel as this backpack was designed by a student who understands the specific needs of students who use backpacks regularly.BRAVO Bagstellar for another job well done!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am absolutely in love with this backpack! The quilted puffer material is super soft, trendy, and gives it a chic, high-end look without feeling bulky.Here is why it’s easily a 5-star bag for me:Insanely Lightweight: At just over a pound, it adds virtually no weight on its own. Even when loaded up with my 15.6\" laptop, notebooks, chargers, and a pouch, it feels comfortable to carry all day thanks to the padded straps.The Side Pocket Actually Fits Giant Tumblers: If you carry a 30oz or 40oz tumbler everywhere like I do, you know how hard it is to find a backpack pocket that fits it. The elastic side pocket with the adjustable buckle strap holds my large cup completely secure with zero risk of tipping out!Smart Storage & Easy Access: The double zipper on the main compartment makes grabbing things super convenient. Everything has its place—my laptop stays safe in its sleeve, and there are plenty of organized pockets for small items like my keys, phone, and lip balm.Travel-Ready: The luggage strap on the back made navigating the airport a breeze on my last trip, and it slipped right under the seat in front of me with no issue. Plus, the water-resistant material is super easy to wipe clean if anything spills.Whether you're a student, teacher, nurse, or just need a stylish work/travel bag, this puffer backpack hits the spot. Function meets fashion—10/10 recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Little things really do impress me.This company wrapped this puffer backpack in a dust cover. The backpack totally deserves that. It's great marketing but it also shows me the company takes pride in their products.Puffer backpacks have become wildly popular not only amoung students but professionals as well. They vary just as wildly in price and quality . This Bagstellar Laptop Backpak checks all the boxes without breaking the bank.It falls into the feather weight category weighing in at slightly more than 1lb. Backpack is large enough to hold a 15\" laptop and a few changes of clothes in the main compartment.  There are 3 additional varying sized zippered compartments. All hardware is black and blends in nicely.The bag features horizontal quilted channels giving it the puffer esthetic.Material is a strong lightweight polyester with reinforced stitching. Zippers glide easily making additions or removals quick and efficient. I almost forgot to mention there are side pockets large enough to accommodate that giant eco-friendly water bottle.I really can't say enough about it. It's attractive,  well made, affordable and extremely functional.  It also adapts to travel excursions fitting nicely on a luggage handle and under seats. Adjustable back straps are well padded for comfort.  Job well done Bagstellar!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a very nice, well made backpack. Each pocket is big and roomy and easy to access. This would be a great bag for a student to carry books and school stuff. This is also roomy enough to use as a weekend bag or overnight bag. There are not really any smaller interior pockets. There are two slip pockets in the smaller front compartment, and there is a larger zip pocket in the large compartment. There is no security pocket. The hidden pocket is on the very front so if the pack is on your back, that pocket is one of the easiest to open. Not secure. I like to use backpacks as a purse/Mom Bag for big outings, and there are not enough smaller interior pockets for me to use this bag in that manner. The laptop pocket is somewhat padded but not really enough to be doing much protecting. I can fit a 32 oz. water bottle in the side pockets. It is still a good, sturdy bag for books or larger items. Nice standard backpack."
    },
    {
        "review": "We lost all of our backpacks during a house move and had to replace them for a lot of travel that we do.  I got my wife a really nice full sized pack that holds lots of stuff and has many pockets and features.  Only problem was it became too heavy and big for her ( yeah, she puts too much in it).  I saw this medium sized light weight model and she loves it.  A nice shade of green happens to match her luggage, these come in lots of colors.  It doesn't have all the hooks, loops, straps etc. of many travel bags, but the light weight is perfect for my older wife. It looks great.  The quilted, puffer style really looks like a professionals backpack.  The extra large beverage holder with the strap are a plus.  Our bottles constantly roll out.  She plans to take this one on our next trip."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Puffer 15.6\" Computer Back Pack is an absolute gem! From the moment I got it, I was impressed by its overall design. It's not just stylish, but incredibly comfortable to wear, making it perfect for daily use.— WHAT I LIKED —DESIGN AND COMFORT: The \"puffy\" aesthetic is fantastic, and the backpack is super comfy to wear. It looks great and feels even better.ZIPPERS AND COMPARTMENTS: The double zippers are smooth and make accessing compartments a breeze. I particularly appreciate the large number of compartments, which are incredibly helpful for keeping everything organized.TUMBLER HOLDER: The giant tumbler holder is a standout feature. It securely holds my 30oz water bottle without any issues.LAPTOP COMPARTMENT: My laptop fits perfectly and is held well, providing peace of mind when I'm on the go.CAPACITY: This backpack holds so much! It's surprisingly spacious and easily accommodates all my work and school essentials."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I’m really happy with the SwissGear Merlot backpack. It’s stylish without being too flashy, and the merlot color is even nicer in person. There’s plenty of room for my everyday essentials, with enough compartments to keep everything organized. The straps are comfortable, and the backpack feels sturdy and well-made. It’s a great choice for work, school, travel, or everyday use. Definitely a good value for the quality!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I spent more time than I would care to admit looking for a solid backpack, but good ones are expensive and I didn't feel like buying a few to try then return. I wanted a backpack for my office job to carry my tablet, laptop, work binders/folders, blender shaker bottles, and small knick-knacks to and from work and between different offices. These were my requirements:- Holds my laptop in a sleeve (preferably padded/protected)- Tablet sleeve big enough to hold my Kindle Scribe Colorsoft- Stylish and slim with plenty of room- Good quality without breaking the bank- Side water bottle cup holders with straps to hold down my insulated blender bottle shakers- Plenty of pockets for smaller items (gum, chargers, charging blocks, pens, etc.)- Something I could use for an overnight or couple day tripI hated it for the first 20 minutes I owned it because I thought it did not have a general large interior compartment area with folder dividers as shown in the product images. However, I quickly realized the zipper track blended in too well with the bag and I simply missed it (it's right in front of the larger top handle).This backpack nailed it. Even the tablet compartment hold my kindle scribe securely, though I'll likely only use that when traveling as it's a tad too snug. The only thing I don't care for is how the laptop compartment is only a side entrance zip and the \"sleeve\" is a plush arm that secures the laptop in place with velcro that you have to remove and reattach every time you move your laptop in it. That seems a bit odd and is slightly tedious to do, but I assume it's for easy access; they should really include that in the pictures of the product. Also, I understand that the backpack essentially zips in half to open up 180 degrees for quick airport security laptop checks, but I almost never fly, so that may be useless to me. I've read other reviews that claim the bag opens up on its own because of this feature. I've only had it a week so far but that hasn't happened to me yet and I don't see how it would unless the bag was packed full and only partially zipped shut.Overall I love this bag, it meets all of my requirements and then some. It also redistributes the weight well due to its longer size, so more weight in the bag somewhat feels like less. Highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "My work laptop was upgraded from a 15\" to a 17\" model which just wouldn't fit in my current SwissGear pack which I've had for over a decade. The brand is high quality, well produced, and durable. Never had an issue with my current one that I've used both for my work commute and travel, so when it came time to look for something that could carry the new laptop, I looked to SwissGear. The only real issue I had was the pocket arragnement having an exclusive laptop carry section to make travel through TSA checkpoints easier, but as I don't intend to take my worklaptop on trips (vacation) I didn't need that - but all their existing bags are designed this way it seems. No biggie as there's ample room in the bag for the stuff I noramally carry to/from work and added side pockets are nice as are the very well padded straps and back. Highly recommennd the brand as a whole."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is an absolutely solid backpack I bought for my son replacing an old one. The durability on here is incredible from the stitching to the zippers.  Much better than I expected to be honest.  The size of this is ideal he is in medical school and carries a lot of gear and it holds everything from the laptop to the lab books.  The color is neutral, he picked it, so that is a plus.  He has been using it since he got it and said that the straps are also super comfortable on his shoulders a big improvement from what he had. I will update with photos later."
    },
    {
        "review": "I like this alot. A few months of use and I don't see alot of wear and tear. It looks good and the material quality on the handles are great. Still, I have some complaints. The pockets on the side are too small for larger water bottles. The \"smart scan pocket\" is a waste of space that could have made the middle pocket(s) larger. The middle pocket has an \"inner pocket\" (like for folders) that doesn't reach the bottom of the bag. Other than that, I don't mind using this."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have used this bad boy since 2015.  It has flown I don't know how many miles for typically weekend trips.  No, I don't take anything but essentials, but this pack is strong and it holds more than you can imagine.  It has holders on both sides for water or whatever else.  I like using the front pocket for my cell phone, keys and wallet when going through TSA lines.  It's really good for experienced business travelers, as the laptop portion is pretty good.  I take a cushioned mousepad along and wrap it along whatever part of the pc is on the bottom to protect it from damage.  Highly recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my favorite brand of computer backpack. My household has been using this brand for over 20 years.  For many years they were used daily. The inner liner on the tiny pocket of my previous 20 year old backpack finally tore so I purchase this one as a replacement. Mainly used for travel and anyplace I have to tote a laptop too. So far, things are going well. I will update if that changes.Material and workmanship: Sturdy and quality. I understand sometimes there can be defects and I would hope they stand by their warranty. So far all is good.Size: This is a good size. Small enough to fit under an airline seat, big enough to hold the essentials. I use mainly for all types of travel. I can fit a change of clothes, medications, umbrella, bose headphones, airpods, water bottle, snacks, wipes, tissues, etc. I travel with a macbook air always and sometimes  a heavy lenovo laptop. It holds both.Pockets and design: This is a slightly different design than my last one. I went with this one because it was on sale. For the overall purpose ( to haul all my stuff around,) it serves the purpose. I kinda wish I spent a little more and got the similar model I had before.-The laptop compartment has a padded velcro adjustable strap. I do not know if this is necessary but it is there. It is removable. Compartment is roomy enough to hold 2 laptops. This compartment only has a \"one side\" zipper. It does not zip all the way around. I found this a little annoying since my last one had a zip around. I am sure I will adjust to it but I prefer to pull my laptop out of the top instead of out the side. The downfall of one zipper, you can not zip tie or put a lock on the zippers. Depending on where we were traveling, we would zip tie the zippers. It does have a tiny pocket on the top. Not quite sure what I would use that for.- Next compartment for a tablet. It is padded around the sides and has mesh in the middle. This one unzips all the way around.  TSA friendly design. Have not tried this out with two laptops yet so I don't know how that will go with tsa. The tablet pocket is small so maybe ipad mini size? The ipad pro would not fit. They could have designed this to be bigger.  I was thinking of getting a laptop sleeve and using this compartment for my macbook air when I travel with 2 laptops.- main compartment: has a mini pocket for phone but I use for my airpods. Has a divider for books, papers or whatever. I actually use it for wipes.  Can fit a change of clothes in a packing cube, medications, headphones,  snacks and everything I need.  There is a mesh zipper pouch on the top. This is great for cords or whatever.- top front pocket- I have a love hate relationship with this one. Easy to empty your pockets and phone into when going through tsa but a pain to get stuff back out. You have to dig around a little. I will probably need to separate things in little bags to make this pocket work for my needs. I miss having a small top pocket for things like chapstick and eye drops. Making two pockets, iphone sized and a small one for little things,  would have been my ideal solution.- bottom front pocket: this one is fine. Big enough for epipen, inhaler, key hook,  hand sanitizer, tissues, gum, some toiletries, misc stuff. Also has some loops on outer part of pocket.- side zipper pockets: there are small size zipper pockets on each side that are deep. These are ok. Weird shape. Can fit a small umbrella or a standard plastic water bottle. Space for other things but I don't have that many skinny long things going in a backpack. Pocket is deep so if you wanted to put money or something way down at the bottom of this pocket, this would be hard for anyone to just grab out of your bag. You can not fit a water bottle or similar item in the mesh pockets on the outside of these ones if there is stuff in the pockets.- mesh stretchy water bottle pockets: The pockets are a little small. These can hold a smaller sized water bottle. There is a strap to help secure. It would be better if there was a loop at the top to hook a carabiner on it, to secure a water bottle. I have lost a water bottle before out of this pocket. Sometimes I use the strap to tie a sweatshirt or raincoat to it.Backpack Straps: padded, thick work well. Have a few loops for whatever. Back is padded enough. Comfortable enough to carry around for a few hours.Overall, a good backpack. When shopping for a backpack, think of your purpose and what you want to put in it. Does it have the right sized pockets for your needs? The price was right for this one and I will use it until it breaks."
    },
    {
        "review": "This backpack is amazing and feels very sturdy and durable. It has great support, and the compartments are fantastic, especially for my daughter, who needs to carry several books and school supplies. Everything fits perfectly, and there’s still room left. I highly recommend it for school or travel."
    },
    {
        "review": "he liked the bag"
    },
    {
        "review": "Super comfortable, large size, strategic compartments and resistant material. I loved it"
    },
    {
        "review": "The backpack is large, resistant, adjustable, and has multiple compartments for laptop and tablet. The only flaw is that in one of the compartments the zipper can open the entire backpack, from then on it is very nice."
    },
    {
        "review": "I came across this SwissGear backpack at De Gaulle Airport and this is my fourth one. My first impression was that a 17\" Mac could fit easily. I bought some more expensive bags along the way, but I ended up hating them as soon as I carried them on my back. This manufacturer's bag is by far the most comfortable to carry. When I walk around carrying it on my back, this is the only one that provides a stable fit on my back. Shoulder strap system and Airflow back It's because of the system. I'm convinced that this is the only manufacturer that suits me. However, I don't like that it's too big and falls forward when I put it on the floor."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Great build overall. This is a fraction of the cost of the big name tactical backpacks while looking and feeling great. I use it for everyday office commute, for the gym, rucking, overnight trips - you name it! It is significantly more stable than my old backpack. I like the sleek black appearance and padding on the straps. Lots of places to attach things to. 10/10"
    },
    {
        "review": "Lots of space. Comfortable to wear. The material seems decent. Laptop pocket is padded well. There are two main compartments. The front doesn’t expand very wide, and seems good for books/flatter items or rolling and stacking clothes. The 2nd main area has the laptop pocket and stretches pretty wide to fit a number of things with some sleeves and a zipper/web divider.A very small piece of stitching was coming off a handle after only a little use.  We’ll see how it holds up long term, but for the price, the amount of space and general quality seems well worth it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Been using this as my everyday carry for a while now and it’s held up really well. Fits comfortably on my back even fully loaded — the straps are padded enough that I don’t notice it after a few hours out. Zippers feel sturdy, no snagging or sticking so far, which I was a little worried about given some tactical bags skimp there. Plenty of compartments for organizing smaller stuff (keys, wallet, cables) separately from bigger items, and it doesn’t feel bulky or oversized for everyday use despite how much it can hold. It’s also easy to throw in a car or take on the go without feeling like overkill. For the price, this feels like solid value — good build quality without the markup you’d pay for similar “tactical” branded bags. Would recommend if you want something durable that doesn’t feel like a chore to wear daily."
    },
    {
        "review": "This backpack has served me incredibly well. I use it everyday for work and then the gym.I use one pocket to keep my laptop, lunch bag and other work items and the other pocket to carry all of my gym straps, preworkout and creatine.This backpack has held everything so well and even holds up and doesn’t unzip when going 130 mph on a motorcycle.It’s been through the rain and has stayed dry and the color has never faded from the original black."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great backpack overall! Pockets and storage galore, feels well made (time will tell), and very comfortable to wear. Only downside is the waistband strap and chest strap are not long enough to go around a well built American."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this for my son who is a welder & he absolutely loves this to carry all of his work supplies & tools. He loves that it has a pouch for his water bottle, many pockets, padding, & finds the zippers are actually great quality.  He says it's very sturdy for the price I paid. The straps are adjustable & the color is great for what he is using it for. He also likes he can organize his stuff and find what he needs with ease."
    },
    {
        "review": "The back pack is well made and designed.  After a couple of rugged hikes I was pleased with its performance.  Well worth the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this backpack as a gift for my husband and he absolutely loved it. The quality is excellent, the material feels strong and durable, perfect for daily use, travel, work, or outdoor activities. It has plenty of compartments and pockets, making it easy to keep everything organized.The straps are comfortable and adjustable, even when the backpack is fully loaded it feels good on the back. The tactical design looks great and matches the photos exactly. After several uses, it still looks like new. This was a great purchase and I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very good backpack, lasted over a year of daily use and abuse. Work tools in main compartment, survival and overnight kits in second (middle) compartment, pills, vitamins, salts, caffeine in top small pocket, the back lower pocket writing, charging supplies and memory media. Can put water bottles, umbrella, jacket in pockets. Can hook up almost anything with carabineers or reusable zip ties to the many loops. Has all important adjustment straps.Very strong fabric.In the end I destroyed the main zipper and it got rained on brutally. I was sad to find out it's over 10k yen now, but I think that's a reasonable cost for the quality, especially if you live out of a backpack as I do as traveling salaryman. Dry zipper area for military patches is amazing."
