    {
        "review": "For the price, this is a good backpack. Lots of room and different sized pockets for things. I can fit a LOT in here. There are some downsides though. After 3 semesters of hard use, the side mesh pockets were stretched out and the bottom of the bag had hole ripped in the outer layer. I sewed the pockets tighter and it was still usable. The mesh where it sits on my back is pilling now after 5 semesters of use and I want to get a new backpack now, it’s looking too worn for my tastes. Not too bad for the price! I will say the mesh water bottle pockets are on the shorter side and taller/bigger water bottle will fall out frequently. Definitely didn’t work for my 30oz Owala. But my 18oz Yeti was fine. If you just wanna use it for a year or two, this is a great choice!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent bag for computers.  I used it on my recent 3 plane trips and it worked great.  What I like the most is not feeling the computer on my back because of the padding.  It is not a heavy bag, but still built with a lot of protective cushion.  There are 4 main compartments with lots of several compartments, even some mesh so you can see thru them for stuff.  The stitching is strong and will not fall apart at the seems.  Excellent quality workmanship.  It is a bag suitable for kids or adults.  I am using it as a computer, travel, all purpose bag.  Its large enough that it fits my gaming system with room for controllers, plugs, etc.  Great bag to have."
