[
    {
        "review": "I’m not going to lie, I am a backpack snob. 😂 I’ve always felt like you get what you pay for, and in the past we’ve used Simple Modern and Pottery Barn backpacks. I couldn’t find the colors or designs my kids liked this year, so I decided to take a gamble on this one for my daughter.I was honestly shocked by the quality for the price! It’s very large, has several compartments, and feels much more substantial than I expected. There’s plenty of room for everything she needs without feeling cheaply made.Hopefully it holds up well throughout the school year, but so far I’m very impressed and would definitely consider buying another one!"
    },
    {
        "review": "We stumbled across this brand when my kid was in 7th grade after the Walmart bag ripped at the seams mid year. This brand was still going strong end of year and through the summer so we purchased another one for 8th grade. My kid uses these bags all year, and then for traveling between states during the summer- with definite overstuffed pockets.Now here we are heading into 9th, and both bags are still going strong- and we’re grabbing another for this school year. The laptop pocket is perfect for the school issued chrome books with room for the power cords etc too.Between the budget friendly price, and the premium quality- we keep coming back!There’s plenty of space, organization, it’s sturdy, and the padding helps when the days are long and the bags are heavy."
    },
    {
        "review": "Loved it. Sturdy. Big enough.  Easy to use. Black is perfect."
