[
    {
        "review": "Fantastic monitor, great resolution. Love the curve effect on it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using the Samsung 27\" Essential S3 (S36GD) for a couple of weeks now, mainly with my Xbox, and it’s been a really solid upgrade from my older 24\" screen.Setup was easy I just plugged it into my Xbox and it worked right away with no issues. The jump to 27 inches is definitely noticeable. Everything feels more immersive when gaming, and even smaller details are easier to pick up.I’ve been playing a lot of Fortnite on it, and it’s been a good experience. The colors look nice and the image stays clear, even during fast movement. It’s easier to spot things in the distance compared to my old monitor, which actually makes a difference when playing.The picture quality overall is solid for what I need. It’s not a high-end gaming monitor, but for casual gaming and everyday use it does the job well. I didn’t notice any major lag or issues while playing. One thing I liked more than I expected is how slim it is. It doesn’t take up much space on my desk and has a clean look. The stand is basic but stable. The only small downside is there’s not much adjustability, so you have to work around that a bit. I’ve also used it for YouTube and general browsing, and it works perfectly fine there too. No eye strain even after longer sessions. I honestly think this is a great value if you want a bigger screen for gaming and everyday use without spending a lot. It’s simple, reliable, and does exactly what I needed."
    },
    {
        "review": "I snagged one of these along with one of the flat monitors for a new system recently.  The flat model was $149, while this one was $119, and yet this one is worlds nicer than the flat model.  The colors are more even, the blacks are darker, the menu has more options, and as someone that has never had a curved model before I think it looks amazing.  If it weren't such a pain to return the flat model and get a second one of these, I would do it in a heartbeat. The only thing I could see might be an issue for some people, is the stand on this model isn't adjustable almost at all. It is very stable, and if you plan to put it on a mounting arm it wont matter, but if you need to constantly adjust the angle of the monitor you might have an issue on some desks with this stand.  However everything else is fantastic.  If you are looking for a good budget monitor I can't recommend this one enough, even over other models in the same product line.  If you are looking at the flat models, save yourself the disappointment and the $30 and go for this one instead."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Samsung 27” Essential S3 (S36GD) Curved Monitor is an excellent choice for both work and entertainment. The setup was quick and straightforward — plug it in, connect the HDMI cable, and it was ready to go. The 1800R curve creates an immersive viewing experience that feels natural and easy on the eyes, especially during long sessions at the computer.The picture quality is crisp and vibrant, with rich colors and great contrast for an FHD display. At 100Hz, the motion is smooth and fluid whether you’re scrolling through spreadsheets, editing photos, or streaming videos. The slim, modern design looks sleek on the desk, and the stand is sturdy with just the right amount of tilt adjustment.For the price, this monitor delivers outstanding value — sharp image quality, smooth refresh rate, and that signature Samsung reliability. If you want a curved screen that enhances both productivity and enjoyment, the Samsung Essential S3 is a fantastic pick."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Samsung 27” Essential s3 is a great addition to my office. I love the curve design and screen quality!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Lightweight, the base that holds it takes up a lot if space so I go a mounting rack that attaches to a desk, so much space saved. Picture quality varies, especially during video games. Make sure to change the screen refresh rate to 100hz, otherwise games will look terrible. And even at 100hz, they’re still kinda of iffy.I bought two and both screens are different colors even when all the settings are the same. One is much more vibrant than the other. Mounting was pretty easy so that was nice. Compatible with pc, Mac and gaming consoles. I used with hdmi to hdmi, hdmi to usb c and hdmi to DisplayPort. All worked fine except the pc to display port when the monitor is set to 100hz, for some reason if the pc would go to sleep, the monitor would begin to flash in and off once the pc was woken up. Only way to solve it is to restart the computer. It’s not the cable or of as even when the ports are switched, the same monitor turns off and on.Seems kind of durable. As durable as a 130 buck tv can be. As long as you don’t throw anything at it or drop it you’ll be fine. Worth it’s value, gold entry level tv/minitor."
