    },
    {
        "review": "OVERALL: This is a decent curved monitor, screen looks nice, easy to assemble, some minor drawbacks. Good Value.Background: I am using this monitor to hook up to my mini computer and my Nintendo Switch. This is my second curved monitor that I have owned. Both have been Samsung monitors as my first one was wonderful but got damaged in a flood. So when I was going to set up a new workstation I default went to Samsung to replace my old Samsung. I found this monitor and ordered it quickly. Shipping was fast and it came in undamaged.The Good:Monitor was easy to set up.It is a good size.Screen looks good.The Neutral/Bad:Monitor boasts a 100 hrtz refresh rate. While this is fine for my needs (switch and basic computing) this is probably not good enough for a heavy gamer or someone dealing with advanced graphics.The monitor only has 01 HDMI input. I find this annoying and I have to buy a HDMI switch in order to switch between my nintendo and my computer.The Monitor does not have built in speakers. My last one had built in speakers and I was spoiled with that simple feature.Overall if you are looking for a basic curved monitor with decent specs, I believe this is a good candidate. However if you are looking for something with the most advanced refresh rates and multiple HDMI inputs, you may want to look a tier or two up.I have included pictures of monitor front and the back (so you can see the inputs)."
