[
    {
        "review": "The AOC 27 Inch QHD Gaming Monitor 240Hz 0.3ms has been fantastic so far. Before buying it, I had never owned a monitor above 60Hz, so I honestly didn’t think I would notice much of a difference. At first, I was a little skeptical because some reviews mentioned that the blacks were not very deep and that some units arrived with dead pixels or lines on the screen. However, my personal experience has been excellent.My monitor arrived in perfect condition with no damage, dead pixels, or display issues, and the setup process was very simple. When I first started using it, I couldn’t immediately tell the difference between 60Hz and 240Hz. But after moving my mouse around and comparing it to my old monitor, the difference became very noticeable. The smoothness is honestly amazing.The monitor also includes a lot of useful and fun features. It has a sniper mode, a built-in crosshair option that places a dot in the center of the screen, and even a timer feature. Another great feature is the ability to overclock the monitor up to 260Hz. There are also many ways to customize the display colors, including detailed manual adjustments.One small downside is that the stand is not very adjustable. However, if adjustability is important to you, a monitor mount would work great with this setup and would easily solve that issue.One thing I was initially worried about was the HDR performance because some reviews said it was not “true HDR.” In my experience, though, that concern ended up being overrated. The colors look vibrant and impressive, and overall the display quality has exceeded my expectations.If you’re looking for an affordable 1440p gaming monitor with a high refresh rate and plenty of features, this is definitely a great choice."
    },
