        "review": "Amazing picture quality & the stand it comes with works very well & is not bulky. Picture is clear, colors look great & gaming is a breeze at 240mhz!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I like this monitor a lot , it’s quick it was easy to setup and get working the way I wanted it. I think the panel is good quality. The stand is a bit lacking but I guess it’s ok because the panel itself is good especially for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "The screen itself is pretty great. Size, color and options are nice. I didn't realize Audio out only meant it has a headphone jack. Pretty bummed it doesn't have its own audio. Most likely returning."
    },
    {
        "review": "WOW, just wow.  My old ASUS 1920x1200 finally (9+ years) went bye-bye, so I saw this monitor, and my nephew said to get an AOC as he liked the brand.  Done.  It just arrived and its HDR is jaw dropping.  No bad pixels (deadpixelbuddy tested).The bads.  Stand is okay, but I purchased a new stand for it, knowing it (I didn't want a clamp on).Screen is darker on the edges than I like (as one reviewer said you have to sit directly in the middle of the monitor) or my previous IPS monitors.Going from a 60hz 1920x1200p IPS to a 240hz, adaptive-sync, 2560x1440p IPS beast will take getting used to (I actually feel a bit overwhelmed, but will get used to it I am sure).I purchased a DP cable for this because the write up was all kinds of messed up on Amazon.  Acted as if it were a TV, which it is not, so it came with an HDMI and a DP cable.I don't regret this purchased in the least (and I always fear pixel issues when I buy one).Hopefully it will last as long as my previous monitors did which was about 7-10 years."
