[
    {
        "review": "I attached this screen to a VESA stand over my work desk, so I could connect my Firecube and watch a live game, anime, movies, Youtube vids, etc, while I work.The picture quality is actually pretty good after messing with the settings. Colors are quite vibrant and HD anime shows look especially fantastic on it. This screen doesn't get hot after hours of use, either.For the price, this monitor is pretty darn good. Nothing about it looks or feels chintzy. If you're looking for a secondary monitor or for the purpose of using it to watch media, like I am, it's actually pretty great.I'll report back if this unit starts to fail.  If I don't return to edit my review, it's because the screen is still functioning well."
    },
    {
        "review": "For just over a hundred bucks these are the best monitors I've used. You get a nice bit of gear here for not a lot of money.Pros;+Cost is lower than low+Build of monitor itself is great (I'll mention the stand in the cons below)+has AMD Freesync+75Hz is not bad for people that don't need to go nuts with gaming. I play casually and don't want to spend a lot for a feature I don't need.+Has vesa mounts built in to the monitor, Very convenient (especially at this price)+Fast shipping, with NO dead pixels(I bought 2 for myself, and a third for a friend, and had no damage whatsoever). People writing bad reviews must've gotten unlucky I suppose.+Bezels are surprisingly very discrete.+27 inches of screen are the sweet spot for me, any bigger and you're turning your head to look. Any smaller and you run out of space to work with.Cons;-The stand is awful, wobbly as heck, but if you have a sturdy desk, or plan to mount them it's not even an issue.-5ms response is a bit lackluster with all the rest of the features it has, but for the price I Still can't complain.-Not really sure why they have a vga input instead of a Dvi input... I haven't used vga in over a decade. But glad they included two Hdmi's to make up for it.-screen bleeds quite a bit when black, but I personally don't care but it's a con to most so I'm including it.-Don't use the built in speakers unless you have too, they are exactly how bad you'd expect. I tested them just for kicks. No bueno.Overall this is is worth the money, chances are if you're looking at budget monitors, you don't truly need anything more. This will work for everyday use. From basic photo editing, gaming, and watching movies, to just having a bigger screen for all your tasks. Either way. I like it. Hope this helps!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've only had the monitor for a day but I'm happy with the purchase. I initially tried to cancel the order but the seller had already shipped. I figured I would give it a try and send it back if it wasn't up to spec. I'm coming from a 12 year old Samsung T260HD monitor that is 25.5 inches, 1920x1200 @60hz. This was top of the line at the time and paid $329 while this was one was only $109. The old monitor had screen tearing in games (no g-sync or freesync) and FPS play wasn't ideal, especially in COD Warzone. If you've never played on a higher refresh rate monitor before, it makes a difference. I tried overclocking the monitor to 85hz and then 80hz but neither took so I tried out the rated spec of 75hz with freesync and let me say.. I could notice the difference right away and even picked up my first Warzone Solo victory. Aiming was much more smooth and I could keep my reticle glued on other players. If you're using this for light gaming and you're coming from a 60hz panel, you'll be pleasantly surprised. This appears to be a TN panel because the viewing angles are poor. They're completely fine when viewed straight ahead - since this is being used as a computer monitor, it's not a problem for me but buyer beware. No dead pixels or edge bleeding to speak of. Blacks aren't super dark but decent and the factory setting was ok as far as brightness and contrast was concerned. I configured to my liking and I'm satisfied. The stand is wobbly as others have stated and I didn't even bother with speakers, nor should you. I'm not expecting this thing to last but I'm hoping to get 2-3 years out of it. I was looking to get a higher refresh rate monitor (144-165hz) but after doing research, you can't take advantage of the higher refresh rate unless your frames per second average is just as high (144+fps). With a Ryzen 5 2600 and an aging Rx 570, I'm getting an average of 75fps in COD Warzone with the settings at high. In this case, the monitor is a perfect pairing for the 75hz refresh rate.In order to take advantage of the higher refresh rate you will need to open up your AMD or Nvidia software and create a profile that is set @75hz. Once this is created, go into display settings on your computer -> advanced settings -> monitor and then select the new 75hz profile from the drop down. Last, you will need to enable freesync from the monitor control panel (it's in the menu options) and then enable it in the AMD software (not sure about Nvidia). If you're lucky, you may be able to overclock the monitor to a higher refresh rate. Just create a profile for 80 or 85hz, select it in display settings and see if it takes. If it doesn't, the monitor will revert back to the previous refresh rate in 10 seconds. From what I've read, this doesn't harm your monitor and it depends on the manufacturer as to how far you can overclock it. Don't expect much from this panel, however. All-in-all, it's an upgrade for me in just about every way. Some people say a 27\" screen at 1080p for gaming isn't ideal. I beg to differ. The pixel density isn't superb by any means but I didn't notice any difference from a slightly smaller screen (25.5 vs 27) and less pixels (old monitor was 1920x1200). If I had to choose, I'd take the extra real-estate over pixel density which I think only amounts to 6ppi. There's pixel density calculators out there if you're curious. If you can afford it and your GPU/CPU can achieve 100+fps, I would go with a higher refresh rate monitor. For lower end specs, general use or a second monitor and for the low price, I don't see why not."
    },
    {
        "review": "excellency"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great value. I bought this to use for Xbox One and PS4 online gaming (most people know now that the higher frame rates on monitors give you a significant advantage) and have to say it does this perfectly. No issues out of the box and very easy to set up. As other reviews state the speakers on the monitor are absolutely terrible, but given what I bought this item for that is irrelevant as I will be using headphones anyway. Will see how it holds up the next few months, but starting off this was exactly want I was looking for and I couldn't be happier. Highly recommend this monitor for any consol gamers out there looking for a way to stop getting shot around corners or dying from \"lag.\"Picture quality - 5/5, I notice so much more in games now compared to TVs it is so clearSound - 1/5, do not buy this if sound quality is a factor the speakers are uselessFrame rate - 5/5, as advertised has very high frame rateConstruction quality - 4/5, the stand feels sturdy but is all plastic so if you aren't careful I could see it breakingAgain, exactly what I was looking for and so far very happy with my investment!"
    },
    {
        "review": "The monitor is easily one of the best for this price point.( its off in the video because I have my Oculus plugged into the the DisplayPort currently, didn't want to get back down there and plug it back in at the moment :D )-The image/video is clean and clear with true 1080p 60hz with HDMI and 75hz with DisplayPort.-It is the best side/2nd monitor for my setup for tasks like web browsing, discord, youtube, twitch or anything else you would want for a second monitor while you are putting your main focus on your main monitor, mine being for gaming, video editing, audio editing.-By all means if you are looking for a gaming monitor this is not it as it only goes to 75hz, you would want 120/144/165+ monitor for gaming, maybe even throw in a curve in there for a main gaming monitor. So I am not reviewing this as a monitor for gaming.-Though if this fits your price budget and there isnt a 120+ hz monitor with or without curve at 27inches than seriously grab this one.DO NOT BE PUT OFF BY THE \"wobble\" or \"shaking\" of this monitor, if its sitting on your desk and you are not touching it like you shouldn't be than this is a non issue. People giving it bad ratings for that have no business giving a serious review. I have a direct drive sim racing wheel mounted to my desk and when it vibrates and shakes from the forcefeedback this monitor does not wiggle or shake.Solid 4.5 out of 5 for what I use it for. Sadly can only give whole numbers in the star rating."
    },
    {
        "review": "It works"
    },
    {
        "review": "I needed a monitor because my more expensive Acer monitor died after a little more than 2 years (purchased August 6, 2023) and cost $129.99. Needed something fast and good. Saw the reviews on this monitor, purchased it. Set up was a breeze and the picture is sharp and crisp. This monitor costs less and I hope that it lasts longer than the Acer.  No more Acers for me although my tower is one...gulp!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "For the money, I can’t believe it looks as good as it does. The built in speakers are also much better than you would expect for this price point. Would absolutely buy again. Months later and still going strong"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great size and picture quality for the price. Easy to set up and adjustable to support seat height and viewing. Well crafted and great monitor for the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Absolutely awesome picture for the price.  Is it the be all end all of gaming monitors.  No.  It's a low cost 27\" 1080p monitor.  Yet the color, clarity, and build quality are on par with more expensive monitors.  Compared to my daily used work monitors built by LG it's just as good, or better. Actually it's oddly very very similar."
    },
    {
        "review": "I work a hybrid job and I’m a grad student. I look at spreadsheets and often toggle between screens. I’m not a tech person or a gamer; I have dual monitors at work and simply wanted a similar set up at home for ease. With that being said, I’m giving it 5 starts because of the ease and functionality. I purchased two of the 27 inch monitors. They worked right out of the box. My significant other assembled them quickly with no complaints. They have built in speakers with nice, clear sound, and they came with hdmi cords. The screens don’t move up and down, but they do move forward and backward which is just fine with me. It’s a great product for the price. If you don’t need anything special or super high tech, I definitely recommend these monitors. They also look very sleek and they came overnight. Can’t beat it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good things:1. Image is good. I bought two monitors and they're both connected to my laptop hub via HDMI. An HDMI cable comes with the monitor.2. Connectivity is very good. I like the rear USB connections, which have allowed me to declutter my hub.3. I like these monitors and they price is right for what you're getting. (I'm not a gamer. I use them for documents, spreadsheets, and graphics.  They're perfect for that.)What you need to know:1. You'll need to connect the monitor to USB. You'll need a cable with a USB type-B connector at one end and USB type A at the other.  (I also bought two from Amazon, $6.44 each.)2. Attaching the base went smoothly on one, but on the other it wouldn't go.  If that happens, you need to depress the tab while pushing the monitor in. (See the picture for where the tab is.)  I did that, and it went in and connected.  When it connects you hear a click.3. The button for on/off and control, in the back, is not intuitive, but once you understand it, it's ok.  I think front controls would be better.  But it adjusts everything you'd need to adjust.4. There's no information about registering the product for a the one-year warranty. I guess the fact that you can review your purchases on the Amazon site is proof of purchase.5. You'd better have lots of room on your desk.  That's a good thing though.6. The quality of the speakers is low, but can be improved with a free graphic equalizer tool that you can download.  But I use external speakers, so I didn't care.7. I'll never change the tilt.  It makes me nervous."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good value and quality"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is exactly what I was looking for. I have two HP Series 3 Pro 324ph 24 inch (23.8) FHD monitors but I had to order my own third monitor for work. This Amazon Basics monitor looks and functions exactly like the two HP monitors, for a fraction of the price. The only difference I've noticed is the size of the monitor. It says 24 inch (23.8) but it's just a hair smaller than the HP monitors. It's not super noticeable, but I am kind of OCD about things like that. Most people probably wouldn't notice, honestly. It was super simple to set up. The base is plastic and felt like it wasn't going to support the monitor, but then I picked up the monitor and it's super light, so it works exactly as it should. I was going to knock off one star (since I can't do half a star) because the monitor tilts slightly forward and I feel like I'm looking down at the screen instead of straight forward, but I didn't because it's possible that it's just my OCD.  It's not adjustable, so I'll have to get another monitor mount, but that's just my preference. Overall, this is a perfect monitor for office work. I would most definitely purchase it again.*Edit* I actually used my paperclip holder to kind of prop up the monitor so it’s not tilted downward."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought 2 to replace my work monitors, easy set up, almost too easy. The quality of the screen is wonderful. You can adjust the tilt of the screens. Came with all the cords needed, took me less than 10 minutes to set everything up"
    },
    {
        "review": "An incredible 27\" IPS monitor that bridges the gap between old-school hardware and modern PCs.Features VGA, HDMI, and DisplayPort, a built-in 4-port USB hub, and crisp 100Hz performance. Absolute hidden gem for retro enthusiasts and daily users alike!I am absolutely thrilled with this Amazon Basics monitor. It delivers outstanding value and serves as the perfect display solution if you want to connect both classic hardware and modern systems to a single screen.A Holy Grail for Retro Enthusiasts (Amiga 2000 / 1200 + PiStorm)I mainly bought this to use with my vintage setups, specifically an Amiga 2000 and an Amiga 1200 equipped with a PiStorm expansion. Finding a modern display that plays nicely with legacy signals is getting harder every day. The VGA connection on this monitor is fantastic. Combined with the PiStorm, it outputs a crystal-clear, rock-solid picture. The Amiga Workbench and classic games look incredibly sharp, without any of the typical sync issues you find on other modern panels.Unbeatable Connectivity Across Generations.The port selection is a massive selling point. It effortlessly accommodates multiple computer generations at the same time:VGA: Perfect for classic retro computers and legacy systems.HDMI: Great for modern consoles, laptops, or streaming devices.DisplayPort: Ideal to hook up a modern desktop gaming rig.You can leave all your systems plugged in simultaneously and simply switch inputs via the monitor menu—no more annoying cable swapping!Smooth Modern PerformanceThis monitor doesn't just shine with vintage hardware; it is equally impressive as a modern daily driver. The 1080p FHD resolution on the 27-inch IPS panel ensures excellent color reproduction and wide viewing angles. With a 100Hz refresh rate and a 4ms response time, modern PC gaming feels incredibly smooth and responsive, with absolutely no noticeable ghosting or motion blur.Great Bonus Features:Built-in USB Hub: The 4 extra USB 2.0 ports are a lifesaver. I can connect my mouse, keyboard, or flash drives directly to the monitor, which keeps my desk clutter-free.Integrated Speakers: The built-in speakers provide clean and clear audio performance. It’s perfect for hearing those classic retro sound chips without needing bulky external speakers.Eye Care: Thanks to the flicker-free technology, my eyes don't feel strained even after hours of tinkering on the Workbench or playing games.Verdict:Finding a display with a 100Hz IPS panel, built-in speakers, a USB hub, and modern ports alongside a legacy VGA input is extremely rare at this price point. Whether you are a retro gamer, a multi-generation collector, or just need a solid everyday monitor, this is a highly recommended buy.It’s worth every penny!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent basic monitor including 2 speakers, 4 USB ports, 2 video inputs. The refresh rate and video capabilities amply do the job for everyday use (not purchased for gaming), screen size that allows you to comfortably work on two documents displayed. Very good value for money having been able to take advantage of a Black Friday discountAlmost perfect but: I bought this monitor to connect a mini PC with Windows 11 and a desktop computer with Linux Mint, two HDMI inputs would have been more relevant today than a VGA, especially on a monitor. One of the characteristics that appealed to me was the 4 USB ports included, I plugged my mouse and my keyboard into two of these and I use a USB switch to the USB-B power supply via the computer used, but there you go, I sometimes lose contact with these ports in the middle of a session, not very reliable for working with a device plugged into one of the two other remaining USB ports of the monitor. The on/off button which is also used to activate other elements such as brightness, contrast, etc. is rear mounted and difficult to handle. Control buttons on the front would have been more user-friendly. Small drawbacks that do not deserve to lose a star, I would have given it 4.5 if the options would have allowed it."
    },
    {
        "review": "At this price point, the monitor exceeds expectations. The built in speaker is a bonus."
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice unit. Picture is great, sound is ok for video conferencing or teams. Not sure about the on/off joystick combo, it makes it a bit hard to turn the unit on."
    },
    {
        "review": "A fabulous monitor. Easy to assemble. Painless to set up with your computer. Excellent color and clarity. Well worth the price ."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I honestly wasn't expecting to be this impressed. I've used monitors that cost significantly more, and this Sceptre delivers an excellent experience for both work and entertainment.The 27-inch curved screen feels immersive without being overwhelming, and the 100Hz refresh rate makes everything look noticeably smoother, from everyday browsing to gaming. Colors are vibrant, text is sharp, and the display has been easy on my eyes during long work sessions. Setup was quick, and I appreciated having multiple connection options available right out of the box.What really stands out is the value. For the price, you're getting a large curved display, smooth performance, solid image quality, and a sleek design that looks great on a desk. It's rare to find a monitor that exceeds expectations these days. Most products seem determined to disappoint us in increasingly creative ways.Whether you're working from home, streaming content, or gaming, this monitor does exactly what it promises and does it well. I would absolutely buy it again and have already recommended it to friends and family."
    },
    {
        "review": "Larger than advertised... great for me! Most monitors are measured from lower corner to upper corner but this one for some reason is measured from one side to the other. The rim around the monitor is almost non-existent making the screen larger and easier to see. I wish the stand was adjustable so that I can raise the monitor the the height I want but it's fine for the price. All of the ports allow me to add devices so no more switching cables for each system.When I power up my computer I find it comes on faster than my other monitors and is brighter. The clarity of the image is top quality and the colors are vivid and accurate, more so than my HP monitor.I wish I could tell you about gaming but I'm an audio engineer and video editor so I don't know the gaming capabilities. I can say that set up was easy, and using this monitor for one day had me rushing to buy a second so I can wrap it around and have a dual screen set up.I worried that the curved screen would be an issue but I found it to be easier on my eyes when I'm writing books in MS Word and when I'm editing videos the clarity is top notch. I'm almost glad that my old HP died and went to monitor heaven, this Sceptre 1500R monitor is surprisingly better!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great monitor for the price! The screen quality is excellent, with sharp images and vibrant, accurate colors. Everything looks clear and crisp, making it perfect for work, gaming, or watching videos. I’m very happy with this purchase and would definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this for my pc to play video games, and the refresh rate is SO SMOOTH, the colors are beautiful, the quality is amazing, the setup is super easy, easy to adjust, and I have never seen any lag from the moniter ever. You can also even control the contrast, brightness, and so much more with the power of one button on the back. I have had the monitor for around 2 years or so."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great monitor! I bought 2 for a dual monitor setup. I work at the computer and this has worked wonderfully for my work and was well worth the investment. The display picture is perfect and I am very happy with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "I picked up two Sceptre curved monitors for a dual-monitor upgrade, and overall it’s been a great addition to my setup. I need the extra screen space for work-related multitasking, and it’s also been really helpful for my YouTube content creation. The display looks good, and for the price, it definitely delivers solid value.There are a couple of minor downsides. The built-in speakers aren’t very impressive, so you’ll probably want external speakers or headphones. Also, the monitor takes a little longer than expected to power on. Neither issue is a dealbreaker, but they’re worth noting.Overall, I’m very satisfied with this purchase. If you’re looking for an affordable curved monitor that gets the job done, this is a strong option."
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice! Easy to set up - attach cords. Great pixels, clarity, awesome / perfect size! Con - turn on button is a push button that is a little tricky to get right.... but we leave on. Positive - everything else. ❤️💕🤙"
    },
    {
        "review": "Don't listen to the negative comments about things not working or the quality being bad. This monitor is genuinely amazing for the price. I've experienced 0 issues that other comments have stated. The screen refreshes great, the color quality is absolutely brilliant. This made my setup so much better for work. I actually plan on buying another soon to expand my setup!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent for playing or working"
    },
    {
        "review": "The monitor has defects, interference appears when connecting, I requested a return but they have not yet picked up the equipment"
    }
