[
    {
        "review": "Owala water bottles will absolutely ALWAYS be my favorite hydration bottle! Keeps my drinks cold ALL day long, comes in the cutest colors, high quality and durable, and the sip straw lid makes drinking out of it super convenient. This specific size is also perfect for bringing with me in my tote bag – plus it can fit in my car cup holder!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I don't know what kind of mad scientist they have working for Owala, but can we get this guy working on improving other things, like those gas pumps that always shut off every $.05 cents, or maybe invent a cell phone screen protector that doesn't crack a week after you put it on?  Seriously, what an amazing design they have.  I love the Owala spouts.  I detest water bottles with straws, except for Owala.  These things are so pleasant to drink out of.  Also, this lid is fantastic, it's leak proof, easy to remove (Stanley, take a look, this is better), and that little string loop thing goes great over your middle finger.  That's the strongest point, and if someone messes with you swing that thing like a club!  Seriously, don't go around just hitting people, but as a self-defense item this will work!  It kept my ice water nice and cold today.  They claim you can put other stuff in here, but really, why would you?  It's such a fantastic water bottle.  I guess if you wanted to load it up with coffee, tea, soda, or any number of adult beverages that's up to you.  I just don't want to stain up the inside.  The 18 ounce fits perfectly in my backpack's water bottle pocket.  I have the Bellroy Transit Workpack Pro 28L.  I bought this to take with me when I fly.  Empty water bottles are allowed thru security, then fill it up after going through security.  It'll save you a bunch on bottled water.  If you want something easy to carry, fits any cup holder, and can hold enough water to quench your thirst for a reasonable amount of time the 18 ounce is perfect.  If you're one of those people that likes to carry enough water for a full day of hiking on the AT this probably isn't for you.  For the rest of us it's perfect!  Great job Owala!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love my Owala FreeSip Twist water bottle! First, I love that it’s cup holder-friendly, lightweight, and easy to carry around without feeling bulky. It’s perfect for everyday use.One of my favorite features is that you can either sip or chug from the same bottle. I personally prefer sipping because it’s so refreshing, especially with ice-cold water. The insulation is amazing—my ice stays frozen for hours, even on hot California days, so I always have a cold drink when I need one.I also think it’s reasonably priced for the quality you get. The denim color is simple, clean, and goes with everything. I use it every single day, and it has quickly become one of my favorite water bottles.As much as I like my Stanley, I honestly reach for my Owala more often. My Stanley is great for certain occasions and the aesthetic, but the Owala wins when it comes to everyday practicality and functionality. I would absolutely buy another one if I ever needed to."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my second one. I love that it has a hidden straw and gives you the ability to either use the straw or drink it out of the spout. Great colors! Temperature retention is really good and stays cold for a long time even out in the heat of the sun at the beach.  It is the perfect size and has a finger handle to carry it with at the top of the cap."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm a big fan of Owala especially their FreeSip spout bottles. I already have the original design in the 24oz and 32oz, I also have the Sway in 40oz and now I was looking for a smaller bottle that is easier to travel with and this FreeSip Twist 18oz is the one! I do have to get used to the twist off cap that's not attached to the bottle since it's not as quick or easy to use as a push button attached lid. It is leak proof as advertised but beware that if you have ice water in your bottle and you have it laying on its side, the cap and right at the fill to area will form condensation (just like the other Owala bottles). I also like how this bottle can carry carbonated or hot liquids (the other Owalas do not recommend it). It is fairly easy to take apart and clean but coming from larger bottles where I can usually fit my hand in it to clean, this one you definitely need to invest in a bottle cleaning brush if you don't have one already. I hope Owala doesn't come out with other styles of FreeSip bottles because I'm just going to keep growing my collection! I love this Dreamy Fields color which seems to only be available through Amazon, it's a very subtle pink to the point where it looks almost white online but when placed next to my Shy Marshmallow (white bottle), you can clearly see the difference. I do wish Owala made a bottle boot that would fit this bottle, I ordered a generic one but it is just slightly too loose but it is still better than nothing since I don't want to scratch or dent the bottom of the bottle (btw, the Owala boots are the best quality ones you can get). The thin shape of this bottle is easy to grab and it does fit in the side pocket of my Baggallini Securetex Vacation backpack purse (you can look it up for reference) and it fits inside of that bag too (that's why I opted for the 18oz vs the 24oz one). The quality is great as usual and it does keep ice water cold for a long time. I do think that Amazon should improve the packaging on this type of item because it was shipped in the brown paper bag that no longer has any type of cushioning and this is a stainless steel bottle so I'm surprised and grateful that there were no dents or scratches when I received it (especially when I saw the delivery guy just throw the package onto my cement stairs). I did order multiple items hoping it would ship in 1 box but it was shipped separately on its own (my other items did come in a box)."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Owala has to be the best, so far, in terms or water bottles that I have tried. Nice to not have to tip the water bottle up to drink it. Someone else in my house swears by this water bottle and carries it everywhere including hikes, traveling, and everyday use. After using theirs I knew I had to get one of my own. She showed me how she takes hers apart to clean which is fairly simple and an easy hand-washing job (tons of videos online from Owala on how to do this). Did I mention that it fits in my car's cup holder and hiking pack? Great price during Prime Days. Lid does not leak and is an easy twist on and off. Feels extremely durable but not too bulky/heavy. Highly Recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this Owala for almost a year, and it has held up really well. As I mentioned in my video, my partner uses it every day for work in construction. When we add ice, it stays cold for a long time, and the ice can last up to around 10 hours without completely melting.The outside has gotten a little scratched and worn from regular use, but the bottle itself still works perfectly. I really like how well it keeps drinks cold.The only thing that took some getting used to was closing the lid. At first, it can be a little tricky to close when you’re in a hurry. Also, sometimes the drinking opening ends up facing the opposite direction when you open it. There is a small marking that shows you the correct position, so once you get used to it, it’s not really an issue.Overall, I really like this bottle, especially for its insulation and durability. After almost a year of regular use, I’m still happy with it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am absolutely in love with this water bottle. I go through water bottles way too often because they either break, get gross, or start leaking, but this one has been amazing so far. It feels heavy-duty and very durable, which immediately set it apart from others I’ve owned.I was originally drawn to the different color options (I got Dreamy Field), but what really sold me was the two drinking options - you can sip through the straw or take a regular swig. It’s such a simple feature, but it makes a big difference depending on what you’re doing. Plus, I've found it makes drinking water so much more enjoyable lol!Another thing I really appreciate is the rubber seal. It’s much thicker and more heavy-duty than the thin seals on most bottles, so I don’t have to worry about spills or leaks at all. It feels very secure. It’s also easy to take apart for cleaning, which is huge for me since bottles can get gross fast if they’re hard to wash.The size is perfect - not too big and not too small - and I love that it comes with a built-in strap at the top for carrying. A lot of similar bottles don’t include that, and it’s surprisingly annoying when they don’t.I haven’t tested it with ice yet, so I can’t speak to that specifically, but my cold water does stay cold for a long time. Overall, this is a great bottle that looks good, feels high quality, and is very practical for everyday use. It's totally worth the money and definitely one of my favorite water bottles I’ve owned."
    },
    {
        "review": "It feels of very good quality, the color is beautiful and the size is perfect to carry everywhere, without details."
    },
    {
        "review": "It is very practical, you can take it everywhere. It doesn't waste water at all and keeps it fresh for hours, plus it's very nice. The straw is incredible. I lost the rubber band and it has been a problem but it is an excellent purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bottle seems to be a rejected item but sold at a premium price. That's what I felt it was when I first received it. Gotta be careful when opening the package, take a video to document the whole process, otherwise you're stucked with it."
    }
