[
    {
        "review": "Absolutely a great buy! Highly impressed for only $21.50. Very well made! Equal, if not better, than all the popular name brands like Swig, Yeti, Brumate, etc. High quality design/print that is slightly textured to the touch. Rubber/nonslip bottom, removable lid and straw, flexible zip spout, easy to attach the water bottle to a backpack, purse, etc. Super cute navy gingham! Keeps drinks cold, hand wash recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm super picky about my water bottles.This one is my new favorite!+ The chug spout is great!+ also comes with a straw insert (if you're into that sort of thing).I like that you can go chug or straw without having a separate lid. It's really easy to change from one to the other.+ flip top for refilling is super easy. I only need to unscrew the lid for cleaning.+ cleaning is easy.+ keeps my water cold all day.+ the handle is easy to grab.+ grippy bottom stays where you put it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this waterbottle its so perfect and easy for me to keep track of how much water I'm taking in. I did read the reviews on the spilling it can cause and it is true, I found if you fill just before the actual twisting part you should be fine and they're won't be any spillage. With that being said I wouldn't say its a true 32oz just because of the underfilling but thats no problem for me because I tend to have a little sip and refill it again lol. The handle for now is good it does seem like the little bolt holding might fall off but for now its good. The taste and temperature retention is SOOOO GOOD. I have filled this waterbottle up at work with cold water and I have come back to it late at night and the water is still cold like if I just filled it up. From experience I would say 5+ hours I cant really say more than that because the water doesnt last as long lol. Overall very happy with this purchase I highly recommend to anyone needing a waterbottle, I myself have been looking at their bigger bottles because I'm drinking alot more water and I want to better keep track of my daily intake. Again solid purchase and highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "My new FAVORITE drink tumbler. The size is just right for a full 16 oz water drink with lots of ice. I love the grip on the bottom. The temperature inside keeps my ice frozen all day long. It’s versatile and durable. The handle is great and I LOVE that I don’t need the straw! I was looking for a spout and this is it. I’ve wasted so much money looking for this and I’m so happy I finally found the perfect one for me! And I Love Love the purple. Perfect!  Everything tastes great!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I saw this at Walmart, but I checked Amazon in case there were more, and better, options. The one at Walmart had one similar to this, and it had a removable bottomed section for easier cleaning. I didn't need that feature and went with this one instead.I got the black color, and I hope I never drop it. It kept my water cold on one of the hottest days we had in our crazy weather, and the pop-off lid did its job in keeping the water from spilling out.The reason for the 4 stars? The smaller mouth piece that allows you to use the straw doesn’t draw water consistently. When i try to draw water, it isn’t sealed around the straw, so I end up drinking air and very little water. Think of when you drank from a straw that had a hole in it. It feels like that.I had to switch to the gulp mouth piece and liked that one better. It just flows out easier.The top lid pop off feature is nice so you don’t have to remove the entire lid to refill but if you’re refilling at home, it’ll usually hit the area the holds the straw, splashing water everywhere. Be careful when refilling this way. I got tired of it, so I just remove the cap altogether now.The carry handle has some rubber in the middle ring, making it comfortable to carry for long periods.My main concern is dropping this and breaking the top plastic cover, but until then, I’m satisfied with this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "My absolute favorite water bottle to use! It's super cute and easy to use. The seal on top doesn't completely stop water from dripping out so I wouldn't suggest leaving it in a bag with books but for everyday work/life use this bottle with get the job done and help you definitly get in water and keeps is nice and cool for hours!!!My only quam is that rubber mouse piece  tends to grow mold but if you're on top about washing the bottle every week at least (and I just chuck the rubber mouth piece in the washing machine ) you should be good!"
    },
    {
        "review": "this water bottle kept ice in it in 117 degree arizona heat! the lid give you a peace of mind that no germs get on the mouth piece. the size is perfect and can fit most cup holders and not too bulky that its annoying to carry. this is 100% worth the money in my opinion and i recommend to everyone i know because i love it that much!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This has become my new favorite water bottle. I have been a Contigo fan for their Autopop lid for a while. I hate straws or lids with mechanisms that harbor bacteria and I'm too impatient to unscrew a cap. I also want to be able to chug my water as well as keep it ice cold for hours. So yeah, I may be a bit high maintenance when it comes to water bottle selection.I take my water bottle everywhere with me and as such, may drop it on occasion. This has been the downfall of my Contigo bottles as they inevitably get dented on the bottom and then don't sit straight. Plus, the autopop lids are getting harder to find! I've been through 3 Contigo bottles - one I broke the lid and the other two have so many dents on their bottom that neither sit properly. So this led me to search for another option.Enter Zulu. I was first attracted to the rubber base as that was my most recent issue with my Contigos. I liked that it advertised a chug option - although I could care less that a straw option was also included.The lid: like the Contigo, it has a button to press that pops the lid for a quick guzzle. While the opening isn't as big as the Contigo which does limit the flow a bit, there is a vent hole that actually helps keep the water flowing at a good rate. I also love that the mouthpiece comes off for quick washing and sanitizing. A bonus for me is the fact that the lid itself can be popped open for refilling and adding ice. This is super convenient as you don't have to unscrew the whole lid to refill! The drinking part does have a lock feature to prevent the button from accidentally being pressed and popped open in a bag or something. I did worry a bit about the big lid popping open unintentionally but that hasn't happened yet.Chill power - this has kept my water cold for a full day. Perhaps not quite the staying power of the contigo but really close. I usually fill my bottle with ice and water at night before bed and there is still plenty of ice left in the morning.The durability has been great. The rubber bottom has protected it through a couple drops and I love the brushed matte finish on the bottle itself. Nice feel in the hand.I've retired my Contigo autopop and am now a full-fledged Zulu girl! Very happy with the switch!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Ordered this bottle after trying the 40oz zulu which had no issues, I received this 64oz bottle in the wrong shade of white described in the ad also the bottles top cap keeps opening whenever I fill it up i do not recommend anyone to purchase this bottle since you will face many problems with the cover coming off and spilling everywhere."
