[
    {
        "review": "This insulated water bottle is great! I specifically purchased it for my son to use during his Youth football practice/games. It has proven to be an excellent purchase. While it is a little higher on the purchase price it is definitely worth it. The water bottle is very easy to use and clean. It requires very little maintenance. The 1 gallon capacity has ensured he doesn't run out of water during practice or games. The insulated water bottle keeps the water cold long after he's finished with practice regardless of the 100°F plus, temperature days. The material it is made out of has proven to be very tough and durable while still remaining light weight. It also comes with some very handy accessories such as a heavy duty custom sewn hand carrying strap, straws and straw/water spout cleaning brushes. Just to mention a few. It also comes in several different custom color options. I was forced to purchase the Raymylo 128oz insulated water bottle to quickly replace the first water bottle I purchased (Underarmour) for my son which suddenly and without warning started to profusely leak between the cap and bottle after only a few uses. The RAYMYLO Water bottle I purchased has resulted in an unexpected upgrade that has turned out to be the best replacement I could have asked for. It has proven time and time again that regardless of what activity it's being used in conjunction with, temperature altitude and environment it's subjected to, or position it's stored in it will continue to provide an extremely durable, reliable, leak proof light weight water bottle that keeps its liquid contents cool for long periods of time. I highly recommend it and I will only be purchasing the RAYMYLO brand water bottles in the future!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve accumulated quite a few water bottles over the years, but this RAYMYLO 20 oz insulated bottle has become one of my daily favorites. I’ve been using it regularly, and it has held up extremely well.The powder-coated exterior is durable and still looks great even after several accidental drops. I also really like that it comes with both a comfortable handheld strap and a shoulder strap, making it easy to carry whether I’m running errands, hiking, or just on the go.It keeps my drinks cold for hours, doesn’t leak, and the overall build quality feels solid. If you’re looking for a well-made insulated bottle that’s built for everyday use, I highly recommend this one."
    },
    {
        "review": "These are great bottles at a great price! I usually use a much more expensive water bottle, but needed a backup so I gave this a shot. I'm so glad I did! They don't leak, they look great, they keep my drinks super cold, they seem durable, and they aren't too overpriced so if something happens to it I won't feel like I lost an expensive EDC item, I can just buy another and keep it moving. I love that they have the outside cover and paracord handle too, what a nice touch! They are fairly easy to clean as well, which is one of the most important features for me."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been really impressed with this water bottle. The insulation is outstanding—it easily keeps my water ice cold for a full day, and I've even had ice left after 24 hours. The 64 oz size is perfect because I'm not constantly refilling it throughout the day.The build quality feels premium. It's durable, the powder-coated finish provides a good grip, and it doesn't sweat. I also really like that it comes with both a straw lid and a spout lid, so I can switch depending on whether I'm at work, traveling, or at the gym. The paracord handle is a nice touch and makes it much easier to carry than I expected.Most importantly, it doesn't leak. I've tossed it in my truck, carried it around the house, and traveled with it without any issues.If I had one suggestion, it would be to make it fit more vehicle cup holders, but that's a tradeoff with any half-gallon bottle.Overall, this is one of the best insulated water bottles I've owned. If you're looking for something that keeps water cold for a long time and helps you stay hydrated throughout the day, I highly recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "I first ordered the 24oz since i just needed something for my 2hr afternoon  walks.  I liked how this comes with a sleeve 2 lids 2 straws bottle and straw cleaning brushes as well as a paracord handle. Dont need the whistle or compass but its there.  I put ice and chilled water at 10am and by 12:30 am it still had ice.  By the next morning no ice but still super cold.  So it passed the insulation test easily.  Btw most of the time it was in an 85° environment and 95° for a few hrs.  I like this cup so much i just placed an order for the 64oz for keeping the rest of my water for the day nice and cold.  Its 100% leak proof too btw. Im sure as with any product defects are possible but that aside this is a very well designed product."
    },
    {
        "review": "It held water & didn’t leak, but def did not keep it cold for very long. Filled bottle halfway w ice & cold water in the morning before going to work. Not sure if the sleeve is counted in the “triple insulated” or not, but working in house w ambient temp in the 90’s it stayed cold for a couple of hours max. Ice melted so quickly I’m not sure filling the whole thing w ice would have netted much longer. It’s built well tho.Edit: I didn’t put enough ice in it in the 1st place. After filling jug 3/4 w ice, water stayed cold all day in 90 degree+ weather. Ice remained chunky as well. Nice product."
    },
    {
        "review": "Okay Day 2 of ownership and I’m in love, I work 8-12 blue collar shifts and sweat To a concerning degree, I was running through cases upon cases of water bottles and hundreds of lbs of ice a week. Now I toss a large polar pop worth of ice in this bad boy in the morning and it really does stay cold for a long time. Atleast long enough to be filled again, which is what really matters. It comes with a nice padded protection sleeve and has 3 different handle options+ a carabeaner. Multiple lids (the straw being my preference) and they all feel of solid quality. If you want an enormous Stanley like I wanted (a full gallon specifically) then this right here is what you’re looking for, the straw comes with a replacement aswell, standard reusable straws that clip into the bottom of the lid and also comes with a cleaner for them. No leaks so far, it’s a little difficult to store in the truck so I’ve been seatbelting it in place🤣"
    },
    {
        "review": "My absolute favorite purchase from Amazon this water bottle is amazing and is true to the description. It stays cold for hours even when left in the car in the sun (on accident) it also comes with either the straw or the drinking cap as well as brush to clean both the bottle and straws. Another thing I like about it is the clip and the paracord handle it makes it very easy to carry around. It is Leak-proof but you have to make sure it’s sealed on tightly I learned the hard way lol. Besides that it’s honestly a really solid bottle for the price I’ve had it a few months and use it everyday only thing that I don’t like is the fact it doesn’t fit in a cup holder but what can you expect for that size."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very happy with the bottle. It keeps drinks cold, exactly as advertised. I think the best thing is that you can get by without the annoying straw. A lid with a straw is included, but the alternative screw top lid is the better solution for me. Workmanship is very good, the bottle is tight."
    },
    {
        "review": "Easily breakable"
    },
    {
        "review": "Quality, durability, hardness, practical and all sizes."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great product. Well insulated. Price is good. Strap and carrying case are great and surprisingly comfortable when adjusted. I bought this in the summer of 2024. The carrying case broke in the summer two years later, but the bottle is still in good condition. I would recommend this for adventures outdoors but expect the straps themselves to be fair to the price. Invest a little more if you want the straps to be more comfortable and durable to carry long distances.The option between a straw and chug cap is brilliant, though keep in mind that the bottle’s large size can make it hard to suck from. I think I got the biggest size at the time because I only wanted to have to fill it up once a day. Turns out that it sometimes can go multiple days without refilling but it is awkward to carry because of its size, so I personally would only usey particular size bottle for hikes with multiple people or long trips in heat (safaris, etc). That being said, I am still using this every day partially filled for work until I get another small bottle.My only suggestion to the manufacturer would be to offer a model with a higher quality strap (fake leather or something of the sort) that will do better in harsh environments."
