[
    {
        "review": "This has been one of the best purchases we’ve made. I bought the 64 oz Yeti Rambler for my teenage son, who spends long days outside at marching band rehearsals and competitions. It gets used for hours in the heat and direct sun, and I’m honestly amazed at how well it performs.Even after being outside all day, there is still ice left in the bottle. It keeps his water ice cold all day long.The 64 oz size means he isn’t constantly looking for a refill.  It’s a little heavy when it’s full, but that’s expected with this much water.If you’re a band parent, coach, athlete, or anyone who spends long days outdoors, I highly recommend the 64 oz Yeti Rambler. After seeing how well it keeps drinks cold, I’d absolutely buy it again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Do not be thrown off by the price - Yeti quality is unmatched. I’ve had several other brands of water bottles - Hydroflask, Camelback & Owala, but nothing beats the construction and simplicity of design when it comes to Yeti.I previously had a 46oz rambler, and while it was amazing, I realized I was running out of water quickly, so I needed a size upgrade. This 64oz is perfect if you are on-the-go, at work, needing something to get you through the entire day. And let me tell you, this thing keeps water COLD! I rarely ever put ice in mine and get my water really cold instead before filling up, and even sitting out in the sun or in a hot car, it holds up.10/10 recommend this bottle. The only complaint I have is I wish it was taller and had less width, similar to the 46oz, but it’s not too bulky to where you can’t still grip it with one hand. If you’re on the fence about it, just buy it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great water bottle, I have to drink a gallon a day, so I drink 2 of these a day, mission complete. Ice and water stays cold the entire day in any weather. It seals great and fits perfect, no leaks. Highly recommend"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a fantastic water bottle and due to the high altitude where I live I use this everyday as its insulation, stylish color and, unbreakable metal no matter how many times I have dropped it is unbeatable, it has never leaked and even though it carry’s lots of water the weight is easy to handle thanks to the handle built into the lid. Like I said the material is unbreakable and if you are even considering buying this just get it you won’t be disappointed. This water bottle literally stays insulated all day."
    },
    {
        "review": "Super fast shipping! Very good product quality at a fair and just price. This thing is huge. I had no idea. Even better than described. A perfect seal. Very nice design. Holds exactly 1/2 gallon of liquid. I just purchased the Yeti Gallon Jug as well. Can’t wait to drink plenty of water during these extremely hot days in New Mexico. Thank You Amazon for yet another pleasant buying experience."
    },
    {
        "review": "The hole is bigger than most 64oz bottles and it makes it much easier to add ice to the container. It’s leakproof and keeps ice cold for hours. Zero cons and worth the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Honestly, such a great water bottle. In the middle of summer my bf left it in his car and 18 hours later it still had ice and was super cold!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great yeti, perfect size for working outdoors. Leak proof, kind of hard to clean inside, but nothing hot water and soap can do, solid material, holds my ice and water all day even in hot conditions."
    },
    {
        "review": "Have the 18oz version of this but paid out for the larger version which I now fill up every night and place in the fridge so I have cold water all day long. Keeps everything cold for hours when out and about. Pricey but overall worth the money"
    },
    {
        "review": "Let’s get the worst bit over with first, Yeti is expensive.  However, as my Granny used to say, you get what you pay for and this is a case in point.  It is a gorgeous and vibrant red colour, really stands out so hopefully I won’t leave it behind anywhere!  The top screws on really tight, I fill it and put it in the fridge on its side without my leaks.  The chug spout is good to drink from and pour from.  This isn’t a one handed drinking bottle - it’s big and when full, it’s heavy.  I use it to make sure I drink about 2L of water a day and it is brilliant for that. Love it."
    },
    {
        "review": "It came beaten and with hard scratches"
    },
    {
        "review": "If you don’t wanna carry its not for you,  it’s bulky but very good"
    },
    {
        "review": "Huge, keeps water cold and over engineered. Great quality, better than Chillys or Hydro Flow bottles"
    }
