    {
        "review": "Love the insulation on this and the tight fitting lid for carrying in my work bag. This stays cold even when the lid is off, remarkably!! I prefer and love the sipping attachment!! This is the only water bottle I want or need!! I replaced one I lost.I didn’t get a color and stuck to stainless steel so the color wouldn’t rub off in the dishwasher. I’m happy with this decision! The size is perfect for all day. If I want one for a short trip, I use a smaller one."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased the YETI 26 oz bottle and it has been a wonderful addition to my hydration habits. The size is perfect - I add ice and water two to three times a day. The water stays cold, which encourages me to keep sipping away at it. The Moon Dust is a great color and I love the texture of the bottle - it makes it easy to grab and hold onto. The chug cap is also nice - it makes it very easy to drink from. Honestly, I have begun to carry this bottle with me everywhere. It has become my go-to and my first pick for hydration every day."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love it! I seem to drink more water using a chug bottle vs a sip bottle.  This is durable, however,I do recommend getting a Yeti rubber boot to put on the bottom. I scratched mine up a bit when out walking. I put in down in a rocky area a few times.  Otherwise,  this is my new go to bottle that I take everywhere! Easy to clean, doesn't leak, keeps water cold for hours.  I am definitely a fan of this design."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this YETI as a gift for my boyfriend and he absolutely loves it! It keeps his water cold all day, and when he adds ice in the morning, there’s still ice in it around 12 hours later. The quality is amazing and it has become something he uses all the time. Definitely worth it and such a great gift!"
    },
    {
        "review": "My old water bottle has been a source of annoyance to my husband pretty much since it arrived. He hated washing it. It was one of those with a very narrow neck which required a special brush. I liked it fine, but after I replaced my coffee mug he suggested (with not much subtlety) that I should grab one of these without delay. Iced coffee won. I tried my best to object. It was a good show. Really. But I couldn’t get that in my old bottle and I certainly could in this.I wish I’d have gotten it in black, or even navy or dark green and I got the alternate lid right away. The local Ace hardware said they can’t keep that item in stock it’s so popular.Properly outfitted, except for the colour, I’m one happy camper. My husband is even happier. He’s our resident dishwasher. He says that this is as easy to clean as anyone could wish for. Even the fancy new lid breaks all the way down and goes back together without any instructions needed. Neither nooks nor crannies where stuff hides from washing.So far, it is every bit as durable as I’d hoped but it’s way too early to say much. It’s easily handled everything I’ve thrown at it, which nothing else has. Not so much as a ding. I don’t mean to sound like I treat stuff badly. I don’t. But when you spend time in a wheelchair things will occasionally roll off, get too close to the wheels or whatever. The truth is this is the first one to still look anywhere near new after this much time, little as it’s been. It may not sound impressive, but it is. Stuff that stripped my old bottle(s) down to stainless just make a little mark on this. Wipe it down with a microfibre towel and it’s gone. I’m adjusting to the new way as best I can. This is my new jugs’ personality. Tidy, just like me. I like it better than what’s passed for personality in the past.From a practical standpoint it does everything just as it should. It holds temperature incredibly well. Yesterdays ice is still there in morning and I tend to imagine it would do just as well with hot drinks. Not that I’m likely to test that out in a cup this size. But my husband may try this bottle with the alternate cap for his coffee in an 18oz. Someday. When his Zojirushi is ready for replacement.Which brings us to:Gifting: to me this seems like it would make a nice gift. Unless the person is one of those that doesn’t like practical gifts in which case my heart goes out to you. I’ll find out when it’s time. Little caveat. It didn’t arrive in the whole Yeti package. It came in bubble wrap and would need dressing up.I fully expect I’ll be back to upgrade this to 5 stars in a few months. I don’t like to do that until at least a year. Durability is hard to address sooner than that. It’s too soon, really, but this is the Internet.I hope this is helpful to someone. Thank you."
    },
