[
    {
        "review": "I have always trusted Amazon for offering top-notch products, and their own brand, Happy Belly, is no exception. From my experience, I can confidently say that the Happy Belly Purified Water delivers exceptional quality and has become a staple in my household.First and foremost, the taste of this purified water is clean and refreshing. It lacks any unpleasant aftertaste, making it perfect for drinking on its own or using as a base for beverages like tea, coffee, or smoothies. The water is crystal clear and has a pleasant mouthfeel, leaving me feeling hydrated and satisfied.One of the aspects that impressed me the most about Happy Belly Purified Water is its commitment to quality and safety. The bottle is made from durable and 100% recyclable plastic, ensuring the water remains uncontaminated until consumed. Additionally, the water undergoes a meticulous purification process, removing any impurities and leaving behind a pure, crisp taste.The pack size, containing 24 bottles, is ideal for my household needs, and the compact design allows for easy storage in my pantry or refrigerator. The bottles are also convenient to grab and go, making it perfect for keeping hydrated while on the move or during outdoor activities.Moreover, I greatly appreciate the affordability of Happy Belly Purified Water compared to other brands in the market. It offers exceptional value for money without compromising on quality. The subscription option offered by Amazon also ensures that I never run out of water, as it can be conveniently delivered right to my doorstep.Lastly, I commend Amazon for their commitment to sustainability. The Happy Belly Purified Water bottles are easily recyclable, and Amazon actively encourages customers to recycle them responsibly.In conclusion, I highly recommend Happy Belly Purified Water to anyone seeking a reliable and refreshing source of hydration. With its excellent taste, commitment to quality, and affordability, this Amazon brand has become my go-to choice for purified water. Stay hydrated with Happy Belly and enjoy the convenience of having it delivered right to your doorstep!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Time and time again a continued purchase. No need for fancy water. Or toted as best. This water which is just water is straight forward and has a refreshing and clean taste in the mouth. Our family uses this for refreshing taste and reliability in exceptional pricing."
    },
    {
        "review": "If you want no-drama drinking water for the house, car, gym bag, or emergencies, Amazon’s purified water bottles do exactly what they should: taste clean, stay sealed, and not cost a fortune. It’s the kind of neutral, crisp water you don’t think about—which is the whole point.What I notice (and why I keep rebuying)Clean, neutral taste: Chilled, it’s refreshing with no plasticky aftertaste. Because it’s purified (typically reverse osmosis) with a touch of minerals added for taste, it doesn’t have the “salty” edge some spring waters do.Grab-and-go size: The 16.9-oz (500 mL) bottles fit cup holders, treadmill holders, and backpack side pockets perfectly.Consistent seals: Caps twist off with a clean pop; I haven’t hit leakers or half-sealed bottles.Value: Case price per bottle is hard to beat, especially for keeping a few packs on hand for guests or a go-bag.Where it shinesDaily hydration: Easy way to track intake—four bottles gets most adults near their daily goal.Workouts & errands: Neutral flavor is ideal when you’re sweaty; it doesn’t fight with electrolytes or mixes.Coffee machine/steamer safe: Purified water reduces mineral build-up vs. hard tap (still descale on schedule).Emergency stash: Two cases on a shelf = peace of mind for outages/boil advisories.The honest nits (no sugar-coating)Bottle thinness: They’re lightweight by design. Great for portability, not meant for multiple refills. If you squeeze hard, they’ll crinkle.Shrink-wrap case: The plastic wrap can tear if you grab from the side—lift from the bottom to avoid the cascade-of-bottles moment.Taste preference: If you love the mineral “snap” of spring water, purified can feel a bit “flat.” That’s normal—this aims for neutral, not terroir.Tips to get the best out of themChill them. Purified water tastes best cold; keep a rotation in the fridge.Store smart. Keep sealed cases in a cool, odor-free spot—water can absorb nearby smells.Freeze hack: Half-drain a bottle, freeze it upright, then top with fresh water before heading out for a long day—instant ice pack + cold water for hours.Recycle everything your local program accepts (bottle + cap + label where allowed). Day-to-day, use a reusable bottle and lean on these for travel/emergencies.Bottom lineIf you’re after clean taste, reliable packaging, and real value, Amazon’s purified water bottles deliver. They’re an easy “set it and forget it” staple—perfect for stocking the pantry without overthinking it."
    },
    {
        "review": "What a deal! The price is right. There is a “purified” water taste to these found in all purified bottled water no matter the cost. I’ve been mixing in propel powder and xtend powder and even drinking them with no enhancement. They’re a bargain and make adding water easy to my hydration  strategy. I photographed a bottle with 3 other 16.9 oz bottles to see the size differences."
    },
    {
        "review": "Amazon Grocery Purified Water is honestly a solid and affordable option for everyday drinking water. The water tastes clean, purified, and refreshing, and I haven’t had any issues drinking it regularly. It does not leave a strange aftertaste, and overall it feels like a reliable product for daily use.One thing I would like Amazon Grocery and Amazon to improve is making the plastic bottles a little stronger and more durable, especially during delivery and carrying multiple packs.I would also love to see more quantity options available, such as 30+ bottle boxes, along with larger bottle sizes like 1L purified water options for people who drink a lot of water throughout the day.Another great improvement would be expanding the variety of water choices, including spring water, alkaline water, flavored zero sugar water, and specialty water options designed for people managing diabetes or healthier lifestyles.It would also be nice to see Amazon Grocery continue expanding affordable water options for SNAP users, low-income individuals, and families who rely on grocery delivery and budget-friendly products.Overall, this is still a really good purified water product, and I appreciate Amazon Grocery continuing to improve and expand their grocery selections."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been really impressed with the Amazon Grocery brand bottled water. It tastes great—clean and refreshing—and honestly we prefer it over several of the name-brand waters we’ve tried. It’s also priced really reasonably, which helps a lot for a busy household.I have several kids who are involved in sports, and while we do our best to remember reusable water bottles, that doesn’t always happen when everyone is rushing out the door. I like keeping a case of these on hand for practices, games, and last-minute needs.It’s a simple product, but the quality and value make it a great staple to keep around. Definitely one we’ll keep buying."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ran out of water a couple days ago and being that I live in Arizona it was 107 out. I didn’t feel like trying to carry a case or two of water in so I decided to try Amazon fresh and they delivered the four cases to me and the size I wish they had it in 40 bottles, but the 24 works good too. I like that they let you know exactly when it’s there so that you know in 107° weather to go get your delivery at your door and I haven’t sit outside very long drink ability. It’s water I mean to me it’s the same as any brand name. It just has Amazon on it. I would order again from them, especially if it’s 107°. I just feel like it’s better to order in bulk."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Ello Cooper stainless steel bottlesOne of the best designed stainless steel bottles.  We’ve been testing and using this product on a daily basis for over a month now and so far so good.The Outside:The Ello Cooper Stainless Steel Water Bottle is aesthetically well-made, featuring a sleek design with various color options as well as various capacity sizes.  The design includes a soft silicone spout and a one-touch locking flip lid, which adds to its modern appeal as well as providing added protection to the mouth spout. This lid is designed to keep the drink surface fully covered during transport, ensuring cleanliness and preventing spills.  It’s definitely a terrific feature.  As long as the lid/cap that secures the bottle is turned snug enough, and the locking flip lid is closed, there has been no leakage even when the bottle is turned upside down.  Note:  Not to overfill the bottle, maintaining a good level at approximately 90%-95% full.  The integrated carry loop enhances its portability and style, making it suitable for both casual and active lifestyles.The Inside:The interior has the classic stainless steel appearance, its vacuum insulation keeps cold beverages cold for many hours, easily up to a day.  We’ve been exclusively using the bottle to hold water only.  Included is a durable straw made of silicone, designed for easy sipping.  Another great feature is that we can elect to achieve a steady flow of water from the bottle without actually sipping, using a technique that involves tilting the bottle carefully above the mouth and drinking this way.Sizes:The Ello bottle comes in a variety of sizes.  We’ve enjoyed having the bottle quite a bit so we’ve picked up a variety of colors and sizes: 2x 32oz (at home and on the go use for 2 people); 1x 22oz (short distance on the go use for 1 person); 1x 40oz (at home use) and 1x 64oz (at home use for extra water storage).Cost:The price seems to be competitive, if not better, relative to other brands of stainless steel bottles but I’d argue that it’s a much better value for the quality and features.In summary, The Ello Cooper stainless steel water bottle is both well-made and well-designed, offering excellent functionality."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great water bottle and color. Easy to fill, clean and carry. Keeps water cold and holds ice cubes for hours at a time. My daughter said it stayed cold to long 😂 less ice. Great for hot days spent at the pool or beach and then transition back to school. I bought water bottle stickers to let them personalize and the bottles took them well and continue stay put.The 20/22oz size is perfect for my kids."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is one of my most favourite water bottles I have ever owned. Doesn’t leak, the lid has a safety lock, soft straw, not a slippery body, keeps water ice cold even overnight, and the colour looks amazing! I lost the first one but ended up buying the exact same one after a while because I couldn’t replace it. The only thing is, it’s not cup holder compatible. But other than that, it’s amazing, absolutely worth the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ello is my favorite brand of water bottle. I actually never buy any other ones! It hold cold forever, even if you’re outside in 90°+ weather! They aren’t thick very sturdy as well and have never dented. My husband ran his over with a forklift at work and it only scratched off some paint, didn’t dent at all! They are very easy to clean and help with getting your daily amount of water in because it’s convenient! They are also only leakproof if you ensure the lid is closed, doesn’t have to be locked but definitely has to be closed! I discovered Ello years ago and have never gone back! Definitely recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I recently purchased the 22oz Ello Cooper bottle in Lilac to use for carrying water with me to campus, and I've been genuinely impressed with its performance and design.Great Lid Security! (A Major Pro) -The lid is the key reason I chose this bottle. There is absolutely zero leakage when the cap is closed. I especially love the security features:Fully Covered Spout: The cap completely covers the drinking spout, which is fantastic for keeping the surface clean when the bottle is in a gym bag or sitting on a desk.Easy Locking Mechanism: The lock is effortless and fast to use (it's super easy to engage and disengage), ensuring the cap remains locked and guarantees leak-proof security when tossed into a bag with electronics.Portability and Size Recommendation -The 22-ounce size is portable and fits easily into my backpack's side pocket. I chose this smaller size specifically because I was concerned that the larger-capacity bottles would not fit in my car cup holder. While the 22oz fits perfectly, with some room to spare even (in a 2026 Corolla), I've found I need more water capacity throughout the day. For my next purchase, I would definitely order the larger size and would recommend others check the dimensions against their own cup holders.Design and Durability Considerations -I have a few points about the construction that potential buyers should be aware of:Cap Alignment Issue: The screw mechanism inside the lid, which is crucial for preventing leaks, can be tricky. It sometimes takes a few tries to line up evenly and screw on properly. It's a minor frustration, but worth noting for daily use.Exterior Scuffing: While I love the sleek look, I was disappointed that the exterior finish already shows small scuff marks after less than a week of daily use. It seems the painted finish may be prone to minor wear and tear quickly.Cold Performance, Cleaning, and Drinking Experience -This bottle excels at keeping drinks cold all day. The water is still cold well into the evening.Cleaning is Very Convenient: The lid is easy to fully disassemble for deep cleaning, and both the bottle and lid can be safely put into the dishwasher, which saves significant time.A Note on the Drinking Experience: The silicone spout is comfortable, but the drinking experience is a personal preference point. It requires slightly more suction, and the rate of water flow is a little less than I am used to (in comparison to my Owala bottle, for example).Important buyer awareness- this bottle is for cold use only!!Please be aware that this specific bottle is not designed for use with hot liquids, which was disappointing to discover after my purchase.Overall Recommendation:The Ello Cooper is a fantastic choice if your priority is a securely leak-proof, fully covered spout design with excellent cold-temperature retention. I recommend it highly, and based on my experience, I'd suggest considering the larger size if you need more volume, even if you were initially hesitant about fit."
    },
    {
        "review": "I had the lilac one for about two years and the little rubber ring by the flip lid hinge just broke the other day, so I decided to get another one and I ordered the dark blue green color 22 ounce. The first one I got was a gift from target. keeps cold and long time as long as you have ice. Great product 👌"
