[
    {
        "review": "I bought the 36 Oz version for coffee to take to work. (Yes, I love coffee that much!) I work 12-hour shifts, and this keeps my coffee hot for 7 to 8 hours. I've had this for 2 years now, and it's even survived a couple of hard drops onto concrete. I stick it in the dishwasher on high heat after every use, and the only place that the paint is showing any wear at all is on the bottom where it is in constant contact with the table. It doesn't leak at all. The lid lock stays in place great. Just make sure to use the lid lock before you place it in a bag. I forgot once, and made a mess! The cup and lid are very easy to clean, because you don't have to take anything apart to access the inside of the lid. This is slightly more expensive than other options, but it's worth it because it's outlasted every other option I've ever owned."
    },
    {
        "review": "This Stanley-style tumbler has become my favorite for daily use. It keeps drinks cold for hours, and the ice lasts a long time—perfect for hot days.I love its practical design, with a comfortable handle and the perfect size to take anywhere, whether it’s in the car, at work, or at the gym. It’s also very sturdy and feels high quality.It’s easy to clean, and the lid helps prevent spills, making it even more convenient. Definitely a great investment if you want to keep your drinks at the perfect temperature all day. Highly recommended! 🧊💧✨"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been using this Hydro Flask water bottle for a few weeks now, and it has quickly become my go-to for daily hydration. The insulation performance is outstanding—my water stays ice-cold for a full day, even when I leave the bottle in my car or take it outdoors. It also keeps hot drinks warm for hours, which is a huge bonus.The build quality is top-notch. The stainless steel feels durable and premium, and I love that it doesn’t retain any flavors from previous drinks. Everything tastes fresh every time.Another big plus is the leakproof design. I’ve tossed it into my backpack multiple times without worrying about spills. The wide mouth also makes it easy to add ice cubes and clean thoroughly.I also appreciate the sleek design and powder-coated finish, which gives it a great grip and prevents condensation on the outside. It’s both functional and stylish.If I had to mention one small downside, it’s that the bottle can feel a bit heavy when full—but that’s expected with high-quality insulated steel.Overall, this is a reliable, durable, and high-performing water bottle that’s absolutely worth the price. Highly recommend for anyone looking for a long-lasting insulated bottle!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I can't believe how much I love this water bottle. I mean, it's a water bottle. For the record, I did NOT jump on the Stanley fan wagon when there was all the crazy hype about Stanley cups. I recently started replacing my plastic water bottles with stainless steel double-walled bottles and I have four requirements. I'm picky.1. It must have a way to lock it closed in case I want to throw it in a bag.2. It needs to have a way to carry it (loop of some sort).3. It needs to have a decent opening for drinking (NOT a straw I have to clean)!4. It needs to have a good threaded top I can take off to add ice to my water if I want to.This bottle is perfect! I have some bottles we got at Costco several years ago, as well as another name brand, and the mouthpiece/opening on this is just amazing! It sounds silly, but I can gulp and take big drinks much easier with this one, and I swear it keeps drinks colder longer than my other bottles. It doesn't leak, it's extremely well made (I mean, c'mon - Stanley has been making thermoses since 1913), and it looks nice (if that matters). This is hands down my favorite bottle. I wish they weren't so expensive because I really want another one! My husband wasn't used to it and his only complaint was that because the mouthpiece isn't just a round tube-like opening, you do have to make sure you drink from it straight on (not with the bottle turned sideways or you will spill water). Also, the hinged lid is sturdy and doesn't try to close on your face while you're drinking. :)"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this water bottle! Keeps water cold. Right size. VERY EASY TO USE LID that has a secure latch, but when unlatched pops open at the push of a button. Easily my favorite water bottle of the 4 or 5 I've owned"
    },
    {
        "review": "The cup is pretty good overall. I really like it, but the lid is a little too tall and doesn’t look as nice as I expected."
    },
    {
        "review": "Is this it, the water bottle that doesn't have any annoying quirks or defects and I actually like drinking out of it? Gosh I sure hope so.I had not wanted to go past 32 oz because I was worried about it being heavy and wide but this one is shaped just tall enough to not be too bad, the outside feels nice to grip, and it has a handle which I means I don't need a separate bottle for home and hiking. I can even fit my hand in it to wash. I have other bottles that are smaller, slipperier, handle-less, not insulating, using silicone parts that mold, other parts that smell bad. This bottle hits all the right features.My partner has the 24 oz Bubba Trailblazer which I like everything about except the size and that one goes from 24 oz with auto lid to 40 oz with no auto lid. My most recent fail was Iron Flask which even with 3 different lid types didn't meet my expectations. I far far prefer this type of spout lid, and I don't chug, but I'm not interested in the Owala style lids that have a straw and more silicone and more nooks and crannies for developing mold.I searched for this lid style a lot, which I had originally only seen on Zojirishi and Tiger bottles, but somehow overlooked this model through many sessions. My next stop would have been spending a lot more on a Zojirishi or Tiger and creating a DIY handle or keeping it in a carry bag. I'm glad the algorithms decided to finally feed me this result and the light pink color is so pleasant in person as a bonus.I have not experienced leaks. I hope Stanley as a company honors their warranty if something comes up."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wanted a bottle that could do hot or cold, minimum or no leakage and fit car cup holder.  This bottle checked all the boxes.  Extra plus for metal clip handle.  Some people irritated that cap cover doesn't hold open by itself when bottle tipped all the way back, but I think this is not a big issue.  I got a bunch of these in different colors as Christmas gifts for tweens and \"sporty\" friends and family.  Everyone said they love bottle and diverse functionality. Big bonus was getting most of them brand new for $15 to $19.  Only negative was not with bottle but was how bottles shipped to me.  1st...most were just wrapped in tissue paper or plastic bag and put in brown envelope.  If I ordered 3+ bottles at same time then those put in cardboard box with some brown paper for protection (?).  I had to return 3 of 20 because of denting and scratches. But overall great bottle. (Also bought two 36 oz size which were great but buyer beware,  it does NOT fit most car cup holders vs. 24 oz does)."
