[
    {
        "review": "I’ve gone through a lot of water bottles over the years, and this one from CamelBak is hands-down one of the best I’ve owned. First off, the build quality is unreal—this thing feels solid, durable, and ready to take a beating. Whether it’s riding around in the truck, getting knocked over, or going with me on long days, it holds up without a problem.The insulation is legit too. Keeps my water cold for hours, even sitting out, which is huge for me. No weird taste, no sweating on the outside—just does exactly what you want it to do. No joke I've left ice in this thing and left it at work came back the next day still with ice in it.The handle is a game changer. Makes it easy to carry around without worrying about dropping it, and it feels sturdy, not flimsy like some other bottles. The lid seals tight, no leaks at all, and it’s easy to open and close without fighting it.And honestly, the look? Clean. Simple. That matte green finish looks great and doesn’t feel cheap at all.If you want a bottle that’s reliable, tough, and actually looks good doing it—this is it. Worth every penny."
    },
    {
        "review": "It was exactly what I was looking for - smaller chug and no straw. I love that the chug/spout is made of silicone and not hard plastic. Fairly easy to clean, not a lot of crevices. It fell a couple of times and it held up great. The water stays cold for a long time even when in the sun.The only \"con\" for me, is the lid that \"forces/springs\" open instead of moving freely."
    },
    {
        "review": "CamelBak Thrive Chug Stainless Steel Water Bottle 40oz, Black - CamelBakI purchased this forty-ounce insulated stainless steel water bottle to keep cold water handy during long days out without needing constant refills.Pulling it out of the thin paper shipping bag, the matte black powder-coat finish gives it a sleek look, and the integrated rubber bumper on the bottom keeps it firmly grounded.Filling it up with cold tap water and a few ice cubes is easy thanks to the wide neck opening.The double-wall vacuum insulation does a fantastic job holding temperature. I filled it up in the morning, and the water stayed ice-cold all day long without sweating on the outside or leaving wet rings on my wooden desk. Even the next day, both the ice and water were still in the bottle.The chug-style spout cap unscrews smoothly and tethered out of the way, making it easy to take quick, large gulps without fighting a narrow straw or a clunky latch.Carrying forty ounces of liquid has some weight, but the soft-grip handle built into the lid makes it comfortable to haul around. The screw-on lid seals down tight against the mouth rim, so I can toss it onto the passenger seat of my car without worrying about slow leaks dripping onto the upholstery.The silicone boot on the base is a great touch—it dampens noise whenever I set it down on a hard countertop and protects the steel bottom from getting dented if it takes a hard knock.Paying around thirty-eight dollars for a solid daily water bottle feels reasonable given the heavy stainless steel construction and reliable thermal performance. Running the whole assembly through the dishwasher after a long day makes cleanup completely effortless without ruining the outer finish.The forty-ounce body is definitely on the bulkier side, so it won't fit into standard automotive cup holders, but the extra capacity is worth the trade-off. It holds plenty of water to get through an entire afternoon without stopping for top-offs.Pros:✅ Double-wall vacuum insulation keeps drinks cold all day without sweating✅ Rubber bumper base prevents clanking and protects against bottom dents✅ High-flow chug spout makes drinking fast and mess-free✅ Built-in carry handle feels sturdy and comfortable in hand✅ A reasonable valueCons:❌ Large 40-ounce diameter is too wide to fit standard car cup holders❌ Metal exterior can dent if roughly handled❌ Tall thin profile reduces stability and can lead to tips/spills -- keep it closed and away from electronics"
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using this bottle daily for a few months, and it still doesn't leak!  I prefer to chug rather than use a straw and this bottle has a great top for chugging.  It keeps my water cold for a long time and is very easy to carry and clean.  I like that it has a rubber bottom and is very quiet when placed on a hard surface.  I would definitely recommend and would buy again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice and cute water bottle, as well love its soft color. Not heavy. Has soft  silicone bottom pad, carry on handle and silicone bottle neck. Leakproof - checked. Overall liked this bottle and would recommend it for purchase.Did not expect and was a bit surprised. Just be ready if you choose this item::1) I expected 32oz to be smaller, than actual size turned out similar to 50oz bottle. I believe it explains by insulated body.2) Weld seam is inside that may rust over time."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm a huge fan of the Thermos Funtainers, but we needed something bigger. Daughter loves this for sports days. Large enough to last all day and into sports practice at school. She loves the softness of the silicone mouth spout. It's easy to open and close tight so that it doesn't leak. It's slim enough and fits well in the outside pocket of her backpack, but large enough to easily fit under the refrigerator ice dispenser. Water stays cold all day and there is still ice in there at the end of the day - never sweats. The base is too large to put on the top rack of the dishwasher, but we always put the in the dishwasher. No mold so far! The only thing is, the spring loaded cap no longer works after 3 months of use twice a week. Doesn't affect anything else, though. We bought this on sale but daughter loves it so much, we'd pay the normal price if she needs another. Highly recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Just received my new water bottle and it's fantastic!* Keeps water cold, even after many hours* Is lighter in weight than my previous stainless steel water bottle, not sure how that's possible at the same size* Love that the cap snaps open and stays open after unscrewing it* Nice features: silicone mouthpiece, rubberized bottom built in, comfy silicone carrying handle* Beautiful color"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this bottle! It keeps drinks cold for a long time, doesn't leak, and is easy to carry. The chug lid provides great water flow, making it perfect for workouts, hiking, or everyday use. The Sky Blue color is beautiful, and the quality is exactly what I expect from CamelBak.My only complaint is the shipping time. It took a full 25 days to arrive, which was much longer than expected. Other than that, the product itself is excellent."
    },
    {
        "review": "This brand of bottles looks very durable and keeps the cold very well."
    },
    {
        "review": "Well worth the cost, this is a quality item that’s going to last for years.  Pleasant tactile experience, leakproof, perfect size for a 1 hour workout.  The handle is useful, the spout feels nice to drink from, and there is no germy internal straw to get lost in the dishwasher!The insulation is terrific too.  I pour in a hydration tablet and cold filtered water from the fridge when I pack my gym bag.  Hours later when I use it, it’s still refreshing and cool throughout the session.Cannot fault.  I have had so many different flasks and bottles over the years, but this one ticks every box.  Delivery cost/time from the US stock was pretty quick too, only a few days in my case."
