[
    {
        "review": "It's hard not to compare this to the one I originally bought. This does everything I want it to. I want a bottle by my bedside that is spill proof but not hard to squeeze. I don't want metal. I know it's not going to insulate well at all. I just want to be able to sip water during the night. If the cat knocks it over it's fine. If I knock it with my pretty ring, my ring isn't scratched up. I just wanted a plastic bottle that sports water. This one squirts water. And it doesn't leak. And I don't know about the projectile style squirting that some people mentioned. Mine doesn't do that. I'm weak in my hands and I give it a medium squeeze to get what I need out of it and it doesn't attack me with water. I would buy this again. I don't know if I would buy it as a gift because it's very simple. It's definitely not worth what the price was but it looks okay not that anybody is going to see it next to my bed. I might take it with me on a walk because it's easy to drink out of and if somebody stole it I wouldn't cry over it like I would if I lost one of my yetis. It's a nice little bottle and I could totally see getting these if they cost a little bit less for kids and Little League or other sports because they're just the right size not too big not too small and you could stick a bunch of them in a cooler with ice and they'd be refreshing. I like the ideas that I read on some people's reviews where they had different colors and stickers and stuff. Mine condensates a lot so I guess everybody's does so I'm not going to be putting stickers on mine but the sharpie idea is a decent one and they come in lots of sharpie colors these days. I'm really happy with this it seems easy to clean to. One thing I forgot to mention is that the spout is no frills. And I really like that. If I were to clean the spout it's not like there's five different parts that I'm going to have to remember how to put back together. It's simple just like I like"
    },
    {
        "review": "Super easy to use, have measurements scale, fits to most of cup holders, sealing is great, didn’t have any single drop in my bag. Drinking is ok, comes back in shape after squeeze. Materials that is made also good for grip."
    },
    {
        "review": "I utilize this squeeze bottle extensively for both work and gym, finding it perfectly suited for everyday use. Cleaning was straightforward when I first obtained it, and while it's dishwasher safe, I prefer the personal touch of hand washing it. The bottle's capacity is equivalent to standard water bottles, but I advise keeping additional water bottles on hand due to its rapid drainage. Its spill-proof design design provides a peace of mind against accidental knocks, and the clear side panel allows you to track your water level. Although the bottle was initially stiff and required a bit of force to dispense water, it has become remarkably easy to use with one hand after one month of regular use. Also it's perfect for travel since it can fit perfectly into the side pockets of bags. Honestly you can't go wrong with this bottle and it's an absolute must have."
    },
    {
        "review": "Overall great cup that's held up well through the first sports season. I got 1 for each of my daughters (age 3 and 5) and it took them both a little bit to figure out how to drink it-- you have to squeeze the sides and drink the top at the same time to get it to work. It worked great after they got the hang of it. (There's no straw, so it all works off suction.)It's great about not leaking, the lid is easy to get on and off, and it is also  super easy to wash. (I hate having to take apart all the small pieces of kids' cups and clean them. This is literally 2 parts- the cup, and the lid. Yay!) It holds a lot of water and keeps it decently cold, at least enough to last through a sports practice. It fits in all the normal size cupholders in our car seats and SUV.My only \"complaint\" would be that it's a little big for my 3 year old's hands, but that's on me for buying it for her. She can carry it just fine and it's perfect for my 5 year old and would be for older kids too. It won't keep water super cold in a hot car, direct sunshine, etc. for hours and hours, but as stated, it works great for a sports practice or taking around on an average day!"
    },
    {
        "review": "It isn't super explicitly spelled out, but this can be used for a bike. I just used these to ride the 160 mile in one day RAIN ride and I'm so glad I got these. I ordered 2 of these and thankfully my bike frame easily accommodated both of them. If you have a newer frame it might not work as well. Before I ordered these I checked the dimensions and would suggest you do as well to make sure it will fit. From the Under Armour Website, you can see the dimensions are: 10\"H x 3.25\"W x 3.25\"D.I drink a ton of water even when I'm not exerting myself and so I was worried about getting dehydrated during my bike ride. I have a CamelBak, but didn't want to have anything extra trapping heat or weighing me down for my 160 mile ride. I looked around for a while and 26 oz seemed to be about the max size for cycling water bottles. I actually ordered 2 Schwinn 26 oz water bottles, but one of them quickly broke after falling out of its included cage, and so I decided to go looking for something else. I had seen some mention of 32 oz biking water bottles earlier, but I couldn't determine for certain that they could fit well in any cage I found, so I hadn't ordered them the first time around. Now that I had the Schwinn water bottles, though, I was able to compare dimensions and determined that I probably could get the 32 oz Under Armour water bottles to fit on my bike, so I ordered them plus a 2 pack of UShake water bottle cages.The water bottles and the holders did great for me and I'm very glad it worked out. Thanks to having two 32 oz water bottles I was able to stay well hydrated between the 30 miles between rest stops. I even managed to test their durability some by crashing. They have some tire marks or something on them possibly from me half running them over, but they are still working great.I should add one con: When you squeeze them, they can sometimes stay in a semi-compressed state. This didn't cause an issue for me thankfully, but I was a little worried it might make it a little easier for them to fall out of the cage. You can get them to re-inflate some if you squeeze the sides from a different angle (rotate your hand position 90 degrees)."
    },
    {
        "review": "It was a little tough for my 6 year old to use at first.  But now that he has it figured out these are perfect. They wash nicely, easy to label.  Great value."
    },
    {
        "review": "Ordered it because we needed a replacement for one that was lost. This one came the next day. It is not the easiest to sure for younger kids. Water doesn’t stay as cold as other brands . Not really worth the price. Does seem like a high quality product though that should last."
    },
    {
        "review": "I like it and carry it almost everywhere to stay hydrated. It doesn’t spill when knocked over, easy to squeeze and squeaks when let go of it. I take it to meetings and have learned to let go slowly🤭"
    },
    {
        "review": "Wide opening allowing adding ice easly, dosnt leak, vibrent colour."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great bottle because it never leaks.  Used it for many bike rides now and it's fine.  Only complaint is it can be a bit hard to squeeze, but otherwise much better than others like the Gatorade ones."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great water bottle.  Really nice color.  My daughter wanted the Gatorade style squeeze water bottle for sports but the color allows us to differentiate from the rest of the teams green Gatorade bottles easily.  Great for the price"
    },
    {
        "review": "A good bottle for football. My son plays for a PL Academy & has gotten through a lot of water bottles over the past few years. This is a good one IMO but not cheap."
