    {
        "review": "Love it. For a cyclist, having a durable/reliable water bottle is imperative. This one checks all the boxes in that respect. Holds plenty for a moderate to long ride, is easy to fill/empty and is still pretty compact. Fits in my holder perfectly as well. Not to mention you can just use it as an all day drink container too. I even fill it at night and leave it on my nightstand for easy access during resting hours. Even stays cold all night too! That's another thing, it insulates PERFECTLY. I live in Nevada, we get 115+ degree days in the summer. So water staying cold in that kind of heat is also imperative. Which it does in this one, for long durations as well. I imagine it will do the opposite for those in cold weather needing to keep liquids warm, as well. Overall, very satisifed with the price and product. 5/5"
    },
    {
        "review": "This water bottle does a good job of keeping things cold, although I do wish it was bigger, but that’s not an issue with the bottle (I thought 40 oz would last me longer than I thought it does). The only thing I don’t really like is the straw because it’s kind of hard to clean and it’s chunky and hard to pull out, but these are pretty minor issues. It does the trick as an insulated water bottle, it’s nice that the lid has two options for drinking out of, it’s easy to carry around and does fit into a purse, and it keeps water cold pretty well. I’ve left ice in the bottle overnight and while the cubes were smaller, they were still frozen in the morning. Overall I wouldn’t recommend this product as I don’t know if it’s any better than any other option out there, but it is a good value for the price, and I wouldn’t say you shouldn’t buy it either."
