[
    {
        "review": "I bought this water jug as a gift for my boyfriend, and he uses it every single day! It’s a great size, keeps his drinks cold, and even keeps ice frozen for hours at a time. He takes it everywhere he goes and uses it for just about everything, so it’s definitely been a versatile and useful purchase.So far, we’ve had no issues with leaking or any other problems with the product. It looks great, the handle makes it easy to carry, and he loves having it with him wherever he goes..So far, we’re very happy customers and would definitely recommend it!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Perfect size, shape, color, durability, leak-proof, and keeps things cold for such a long time. Even storing it in my hot car all day in +100° outside temps it keeps the fluid cold, even when the outside is burning hot. It's got a handy holder for it that fits on my car seat passenger headrest and hangs behind the seat. It's great for emergency water in the car and it can stay there under heated conditions without giving you the chemicals from plastic. The lid opening is great and easy to use. Amazing price. I like the cool color shades."
    },
    {
        "review": "First thing's first: I think this bottle is great. What I'm saying here is generally not a criticism.The material is listed as Stainless Steel. It takes some digging to find that it's 18/8, which means it's an alloy with 18% chromium and 8% nickel. I didn't realize this, and after using the bottle for a couple of days I had developed a really nasty cough that is still with me (greatly diminished) over a week later.Now to the rest of it. The straw lid is not fully leakproof, but it is very resistant to leak and doesn't leak quickly. The other two lids I had no issue with. All that really means is if you're gonna store the bottle sideways, don't use the straw lid.The insulation is very impressive. It was still cold after 48 hours after the bottle sat in room temperature, and after several hours sitting in an unshaded car on the hottest day of the year so far (118F heat index).Probably the biggest thing to keep in mind before purchasing is the handle. Mine hasn't broken, but many others are saying theirs has, and I can tell it's fragile.It's very nice that it comes with a straw cleaning brush, and the bottle sling is nice though the pocket doesn't really hold a phone unless you're willing to really cram it in (and I have to assume doing that a few times will cause the stitching to break). The strap is okay."
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve gone through a lot of water bottles over the years, and this one honestly surprised me. The 64 oz size is perfect because I’m not constantly refilling it throughout the day. I use it at work, in the gym, and when I’m out running errands, and it keeps my water cold for way longer than I expected.The straw lid is convenient, and I like that it comes with multiple lid options depending on what you’re doing. The carrying sleeve is actually useful too—not one of those accessories that just gets thrown in a drawer. The extra pockets are nice for keys, earbuds, or small items.The bottle is definitely large, so if you’re looking for something compact that fits every cup holder, this isn’t it. But if your goal is staying hydrated without refilling every few hours, it’s worth it.Build quality feels solid, the finish looks good, and it doesn’t feel cheap. So far, no leaks and no complaints. If you’re serious about drinking more water, this is a good buy."
    },
    {
        "review": "⭐⭐⭐⭐☆I really like this water bottle overall. The turquoise color is beautiful, and it keeps my water cold for a long time just like it promises. I also appreciate that it comes with multiple lids, so I can switch them depending on what I'm doing.The only reason I'm giving it 4 stars instead of 5 is because it's a little heavy, especially once it's filled with water. That's probably the tradeoff for good insulation, but it's still something to be aware of if you carry it around a lot.Other than the weight, I have no complaints. It's well made, looks great, and has become my everyday water bottle."
    },
    {
        "review": "Really happy with this water bottle. The half-gallon size is great for keeping me hydrated throughout the day without constantly refilling it. I love having three different leakproof lids, especially the straw lid for drinking on the go. It keeps drinks nicely chilled and feels sturdy without being too awkward to carry. A practical bottle for the gym, work or days out."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am so pleased and impressed with this water bottle! I had originally purchased it to keep in my car kit for emergency breakdowns in the hot Texas summers, but I ended up loving it so much that I now carry it everywhere. The bottle is high quality and comes with a variety of different lids. I’m currently using the lid that has a threaded cap and carry ring. The cap is threaded on the inside, which is genius, because the threads stay cleaner and you never have to “search” for them when screwing on the cap (great for fumbling fingers in the middle of the night). The cap screws on tight. Other lids have options for straws or “wide mouth” storage. The carry case serves different purposes. As a coozy, it further insulates the bottle. Because it’s fabric, it keeps the large bottle from loudly clunking when setting it down and also protects from dings and scratches. The strap is a lifesaver on this half-gallon version, and I love that the pouch has multiple pockets! I’ve used them at work for pens, mints, etc. The bottle size is incredible - basically one fill in the morning lasts me most the day.I love a well-designed product and this delivers on every count. I’m already thinking about purchasing a few more for camping and travel. I’ve owned TONS of water bottles over the years, and this is easily my favorite. Not even close."
    },
    {
        "review": "In love with it so far, perfect for my carry-on drink refill container. Keeps ice for over 24hrs. Perfect for my long delivery shifts, cuts stop times more than in half- gotta only stop once throughout the day. Appearance is sleak and vibrant defined coloring. Easy to use and grip. Easy to clean and leak proof from my use so far."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been using it for months to take my tea to work and I didn't want to write it ahead of time. The positive points are: - It keeps the heat for me today, in fact to give you an idea, I make the tea the night before, after opening it for a while I put it in the fridge and it's still hot the next day. - I've dropped it a couple of times and it's only slightly warped on the outside, it hasn't lost its color or warped inside. - The cover it comes with is more than useful for carrying your drink attached to your backpack or piece of clothing (it does not come with a carabiner or anything similar to attach it to). And if anything as a negative point I can only say two things: - Some parts are complicated to clean, such as the crevices of the mouthpiece. - The part of fabric where the metal piece that comes with the cover where you hook the carabiner does not seem to be reinforced and the cover ends up rotating on itself on some occasions. Despite this, I think it is a great product. Additional information: Be careful that since it is a thermos, it is much larger than you may think."
    },
    {
        "review": "PROS: Top thermal insulation: Keeps water ice-cold for hours and hours (even under the sun) and liquids hot for a long time thanks to the well-insulated stainless steel body. The external matte black finish also offers excellent grip and does not retain fingerprints.3 Caps included in the kit: This is the real strong point! In the package there are three different interchangeable caps for every need: one with a removable straw (very convenient for drinking while doing physical activity), a classic wide-mouth cap with handle and one with a spout for a faster flow. Very useful protective case: The included neoprene bag fits like a glove. It protects the bottle from impacts and is equipped with an adjustable and removable shoulder strap which makes it very easy to carry on the shoulder during walks. Easy cleaning: Along with the spare straws, a long metal brush is supplied, which is essential for sanitizing the inside of the straw without going crazy. CONS: Generous dimensions: Having a notable capacity, when full it has a certain weight and does not fit into the classic standard car or bike bottle holders (but the shoulder strap included totally solves the transport problem). Final considerations: Considering everything that arrives at home (bottle, thermal case with shoulder strap, 3 different caps, straws and pipe cleaner), the quality-price ratio is amazing. If you are looking for an indestructible, spacious and super-equipped water bottle, this is the perfect choice. Highly recommended!"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I do physical labor out in all temps and this is great for staying hydrated. Holds enough water to get me through a shift without having to refill constantly but isn't too huge or unwieldy. The handle which flips up at the top is super convenient compared to other bigger water bottles I've used. Streamlined design makes it very easy to tote around.Like all water bottles with an inset handle, cleaning it is kind of a pain, but I alternate baking soda/vinegar, hot water/soap, and salt/ice, and use a wire straw cleaner for the straw. I had issues with leaking at first, but then I figured out how to get the lid on tightly. If yours is leaking, fiddle with twisting the lid back and forth, check to make sure it's even all the way around, and turn the bottle upside down and shake it around to see if that fixed it. I haven't had any problems since doing this troubleshooting.Only negative is that the text (showing ounces and hours) wears off quickly, but I don't use those so I don't really care, and I've seen that happen consistently on bottles like these. If you really need them marked I would try stickers. I put stickers on mine and they stay on fine."
    },
    {
        "review": "This water bottle has quickly become one of my favorite purchases. The 64-ounce capacity is perfect because I can fill it once and know exactly how much water I’ve had throughout the day without constantly refilling smaller bottles.The handle makes it surprisingly easy to carry, even when it’s completely full. I also love the built-in straw and flip-top lid. It’s convenient to drink from, and the lid locks securely, so I don’t have to worry about leaks when carrying it around or placing it in a bag.The time markers are a great feature and help keep me on track with my hydration goals. Instead of guessing how much water I’ve had, I can easily see where I should be throughout the day.The bottle feels sturdy without being overly heavy, and the wide opening makes it easy to add ice and clean. The color is also attractive and looks even better in person.If you’re looking for a large, easy-to-carry water bottle that helps you stay hydrated and doesn’t leak, I highly recommend this one. It offers excellent value for the price and has made drinking enough water much easier."
    },
    {
        "review": "Bought this in 2023 and have used it daily for work since then. The size is perfect to make sure I stay hydrated during my work shifts. I love the straw cover and the fact that it has a side handle as well as the top handle. It’s held up well in the 3 years I’ve been using it, though I do hand wash it only.Knocked one star off because it is not leak proof. Usually this isn’t a problem since it’s on my desk at work, but there have been times I’ve come out of the gym to find it tipped over in my lunch bag and my car seat or floor mat is soaked.If anything happens to this one, I won’t hesitate to purchase another!"
    },
    {
        "review": "First of all, the lilac color is beautiful! It looks even better in person and makes the bottle feel a little more fun to use every day.I also really like the overall design. The straw stays covered when not in use, which is a nice touch, and it has both a side handle and a carry loop, so it’s easy to grab and carry even though it holds a full 64 oz. There’s also an option to lock the opening, which makes it feel much more secure for travel and helps prevent accidental leaks.The time markers are useful for keeping track of how much I’m drinking throughout the day, and honestly, having a bottle this large and convenient has definitely helped me drink more water.Practical, pretty, and thoughtfully designed. Definitely recommend!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love this jug! It holds half gallon and more. It doesn’t have the 64oz mark though. Dropped it and it’s pretty tough. Thick plastic and the handle has a rubber like material for better hold.I only use water but it’s really easy to clean. Purple/ Lilac is a cute color. I think I may get the stormy grey next. It definitely worth the purchase 👍"
    },
    {
        "review": "The bottle is a nice size and so is the handle. The lid is tight and the lock feature is nice.BUT, do you see the tiny hole on the top of the lid? I guess it’s there to help the water come out of the spout. BUT it is positioned in such a way that when the bottle is tilted back for a drink, water comes out the top and runs all over my face! Ugh! I thought that I was doing something wrong, and if I’ve missed something and someone can tell me how to plug the hole, I’ll be glad to retract this review.Depending upon how full the bottle is, sometimes the little hole squirts water on my nose, sometimes in my eyes, sometimes on my cheeks or forehead.Yes, I should be able to turn the lid so the water doesn’t spit out, but it’s not possible. If I turn it upside down, not only is the hinged lid in my way but the water from the little hole dribbles down my chin. Turning it sideways doesn’t work because the main drinking spigot is mouth-shaped, and turning it on its side makes it uncomfortable and not very useful.So….the best way to drink from the bottle is with the lid off completely which sort of defeats the purpose of buying a portable bottle. Also, without the lid, there are ridges for the screw top which have hard edges and make it uncomfortable for drinking.So I’m not recommending this product at all."
    },
    {
        "review": "This water bottle is genuinely TERRIBLE. I’ve been using it for 4 months now and it’s now borderline unusable. It started leaking after owning it for a couple months and it’s only gotten significantly worse. If it’s not upright it’ll leak everywhere. And since the seal is  terrible water will get trapped in parts of the lid where it leaks the trapped water even when it’s standing upright. On top of the horrible leaking problem, when I first got the bottle it REEKED of plastic. It would even make my water taste so strongly of plastic. A couple smaller problems is that the labels on the side wore off really fast and the handle pops out. I wanted to love this and I really tried to overlook the problems but it’s so bad"
