[
    {
        "review": "Omg!!! I love this shirt. FYI I don’t do oversized anything lol but this shirt is just perfect all the way around. It’s soft, the color is deep, and it’s actually flattering, meaning it looks good and perfect for leggings or sweat pants. Great quality at an awesome price. The shape and texture are perfect for summer cause it’s not thick material. I’m about to buy more right now. The size is spot on. Just remember when it says,..medium, it’s a big medium. I weigh 150lb at 5’4 and I usually get large but with this shirt I got medium and it looks great!!! With durability I’d say cold wash and low heat for sure. Fabric is very nice. And it’s awesomely comfortable lol"
    },
    {
        "review": "For size reference, I’m 5'2\" and about 155 lbs, and I usually wear a size L in tops. I wanted a truly loose, oversized look, so I sized up to an XL. I bought both the black and white versions, and I’m honestly impressed.I’ve tried oversized XL tops from other brands before, but many of them looked shapeless or felt like wearing a potato sack. This one is different. The tailoring gives it a relaxed fit without making it look bulky or boxy. The dropped-shoulder design looks natural, and the overall silhouette feels casual but still flattering.For me, the hem hits just below the hips, which is perfect for pairing with biker shorts, leggings, or skinny jeans. If you want a standard loose fit, I’d suggest choosing your usual size. But if you like that effortless, laid-back streetwear look, sizing up is definitely the way to go. The sleeves are also roomy enough to cover the upper arms comfortably without feeling awkward. The fabric feels soft, stretchy, and has a nice weight to it. It doesn’t feel thin, flimsy, or cheap. The white one surprised me the most because it is not see-through. Even with darker undergarments, it still offers great coverage, which is a huge plus for summer. The black color is a true rich black, and after washing it twice, I haven’t noticed any fading or shrinking.Overall, this top is a great value. It’s comfortable enough for lounging or workouts, but also easy to style with high-waisted pants for a cleaner, more put-together look. I’m already planning to buy the light brown and army green colors next time they go on sale. If you’re looking for a soft, well-made, loose-fitting T-shirt that isn’t see-through and still has a flattering shape, this one is definitely worth buying."
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like this oversized T-shirt! The fabric feels soft, lightweight, and breathable, which makes it really comfortable to wear. I love the relaxed fit—it looks cute with leggings or shorts and is perfect for workouts or just everyday casual wear. It fits nicely without feeling heavy or restrictive. Definitely a great basic to have in your wardrobe!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Really nice shirts loose fitting really enjoy for work and everything light and airy very stretchy. The only issue I'm having is the smell. There is a smell no matter how much I wash it it's in the fabric and it smells really don't go away even with scent pods it really can't mask the smell too well"
    },
    {
        "review": "Comfortable fit for workouts and hikes."
    },
    {
        "review": "These are comfortable beyond belief! I bought them for work, (I work in a warehouse and the dirt is ridiculous) but they’re oversized as I want, thin enough that they don’t overheat me but not too thin that they’re fragile, and they didn’t shrink after the first wash! Definitely worth the buy if you are looking for an oversized shirt. (I’ve bought 5, two different sizes and 4 different colors)"
    },
    {
        "review": "If I could give this, no stars,  I would.. This has been the worst product I have ever purchased. I purchased this to make someone’s shirt for an 80s party.  This shirt was filled with so much dye that it changed the color of my nails when I touched it.  I had to soak this shirt three individual times a couple hours before the party when it appeared to be that the dye was out once you add soap the water turned black.  Then I put it in a cycle of wash by itself the only reason why I couldn’t return it is because the person I was making it for really really wanted the shirt for the party because I did a transfer for the theme on the shirt and that was the only thing that they had for that party but do not buy this shirt. I don’t know if I just got a bad one, but I had just got my nails done and then I had to go and fix them. Do not buy the shirt."
    },
    {
        "review": "The fit is very very lose so I would size down from you’re normal size everything matches online product the only thing I didn’t like was the shirts came with like a heavy factory smell 🤢I had to wash it a couple of times to take the smell out over all though I’m happy with my purchase I will be buying more ."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I really like this black undershirt. The material is soft, comfortable, and lightweight, making it great for wearing under shirts or on its own. The fit is nice without feeling too tight, and the black color looks clean and goes with pretty much anything. It also holds up well after washing and doesn’t lose its shape easily. Overall, it’s a comfortable, simple, and good-quality undershirt that I would definitely recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "During COVID I ordered some Hanes shirts that were the exact style that I already had and when they arrived they were extremely short and poorly sewn. This almost made me stop wearing Hanes completely but after wearing them for 20+ years it's hard to change, so I gave them another try recently.Seems to me that Hanes is back! These shirts are excellent. They fit perfectly and they look and feel l great. However, here are a few things people should know.1) They may actually be thinner than in previous years. For me, that is a good thing. I'm not wearing a t-shirt because I need extra warmth but because I want cotton between my skin and the outter. It's softer, cooler, and catches my sweat. Thick undershirts make no sense IMO, but not feels that way (as you can see in the other reviews).2) Out of the package, they feel kind of crusty. This made me worried at first, but I Googled it and learned that they should soften up after a few washes. Today they are on wash number three and they feel like a normal soft t-shirt (which is why I'm leaving this review now). So it may take a couple of washes for them to feel the way you want."
