[
    {
        "review": "I ordered several Hanes products as a requirement for college band camp, and every item I purchased was great with no issues at all. These ComfortSoft t-shirts were exactly what was needed for long, demanding days. They’re soft, comfortable, and easy to wear, even during extended periods of activity.The fit was true to size and allowed for easy movement, which is important during rehearsals and outdoor practice. The fabric is breathable and comfortable, making it suitable for long hours in different conditions. Even after repeated washing, the shirts held their shape, stayed soft, and didn’t develop any noticeable wear or shrinkage.They also held up well through frequent use, sweat, and laundering, which is essential for something worn daily during band camp. The quality remained consistent, and there were no issues with seams, fabric, or comfort.Overall, these t-shirts are dependable, affordable, and perfect for college band camp requirements. They offer great value, consistent quality, and reliable comfort. I’m very satisfied with the purchase and would definitely recommend them for band camp or everyday wear."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've lost over 75 lbs in the last year, so I've been haivng to buy a bunch of new clothes.  I picked up this 4-pack of Hanes ComfortSoft T-shirts looking for something both affordable and comfortable enough to wear daily but still solid enough to hold up after repeated washes—and these have delivered so far.  I like them so much that I've ordered three other colors of these.The first thing I noticed was the fabric thickness. These are a little thicker than most basic tees, which gives them a more substantial feel without being heavy or stiff. They’re soft right out of the package and stay comfortable throughout the day, whether worn alone or as a base layer.Fit is spot on for me. They’re not boxy and not tight—just a clean, relaxed fit that looks good without feeling restrictive. The colors are another pleasant surprise; they pop nicely and haven’t faded or dulled after washing.Wrinkling has been minimal, especially compared to thinner tees I’ve owned. A quick shake out of the dryer and they’re usually good to go without looking sloppy. After several wears and washes, they’ve held their shape well with no noticeable stretching at the collar or seams.If I had to nitpick, they’re not ultra-lightweight, so if someone prefers very thin, airy tees, these might feel a bit more substantial—but for me, that’s actually a plus.Overall, these have quickly become my go-to everyday T-shirts. Comfortable, durable, and a great value for a multi-pack. I’ll definitely be buying more of these."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good product good fit f good price"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was a little concerned with some of the reviews that these may be a mixture of overstocks and factory rejects with the low price, so I inspected them instantly upon arrival. I don't see any popping or crooked seams but I haven't worn them enough to really see if any do pop.The ones I got are from Honduras and list a 98% cotton 2% poly blend. I ordered XL because I wanted large for some loose summer shirts and saw many people noted they shrink a lot. They're relatively thin which thankfully is exactly what I wanted for this summer as many of my shirts are too thick for when temps approach triple digits. They're halfway between what I would consider an \"undershirt\" and a regular t shirt thickness, which is perfect for summer use to just keep the sun off you.The tags are super scratchy but thankfully rip right off with very little effort. The shirts are a little scratchy upon getting them which I'd expect with no poly in them. After the first warm wash with some fabric softener they got a little better but absolutely shrunk to the large size that I wanted. I almost wish I'd gone with 2x for that extra sag but these are fine.I'm picky about my tees material and I'd still have preferred the Hanes Comfortsoft as they're much softer, but Amazon wants TWICE as much for them as these. If I were buying these to be skin tight there's no way I'd choose these over the comfortsoft but for a slightly oversized shirt they're fine for the price, and thankfully don't have the seams down the sides that I absolutely despise feeling on my ribs.Just make sure to buy a size big and maybe 2 sizes if you like a really loose fit as they WILL shrink quite a bit. Other than sizing it's exactly what you expect. I decent cheap t shirt at a decent price."
    },
    {
        "review": "These are good T-Shirts for the price, getting 5 stars due to value, not stand alone quality. The material is labeled 100% Cotton but feels stiff and not very soft compared to other 100% cotton T-shirts from other brands I've bought. I'm hoping and expecting that washing with fabric softener over time will soften these shirts. (I'm going to have to keep an eye on Hanes, since I've never before been disappointed at all in the quality of their cloth over seemingly countless purchases.)After a few washings, I'm recanting some of my comments. They haven't shrunk quite as much as I thought and probably are legitimate X-Large shirts--still a decent bit larger than my typical large shirt. Second, they're getting more pliable and comfortable and don't seem quite so thin to me after some washings too. No real complaints at all now--must have been in a foul, hypercritical mood when I wrote that first review. Excellent value T-shirts fully deserving 5 stars. Maybe I shouldn't have written that first review with a brutally empty stomach.Also the shirt material isn't thin, but it's not heavy either--about normal for an undershirt, but light for wearing as your only shirt. This is fine for me, as I intend to use them as undershirts, but I personally prefer T-shirts I wear as shirts by themselves to be made of thicker material.Lastly, consider going up a size if you're not nice to your clothing and use a hot dryer like I always do. I went Xtra Large after reading a bunch of reviews. After washing and drying them (max heat), I'm glad I did, since they're now about a correct normal Large for me.I'm giving them 5 stars solely because they're easily worth the just slightly more than $3 per shirt I paid. (I noticed that the six-pack went up a few bucks the day after I bought it, which would have dropped them to 4 stars). (Lame, boring review, but at least it's all true and might help somebody.)"
    },
    {
        "review": "All sizes fit different for me. Sometimes 2XL is too small sometimes it’s just right. 3XL is sometimes too big sometimes it’s just right.I originally bought went with the 3XL which fit perfect with what I thought at the time would be just right after washing them (they will shrink because it’s 100% cotton).Wore the whole pack all week and finally washed them. Only for them to come out to smaller than a 2XL but bigger then A XL.It still had the same feel but it became short in length. I did stretch them as much as i could but they looked a bit funky on me.I’m 6’2 and have a long torso so length is def what i look for in shirts. So the 3XL I ordered (I now call them buttcrack shirts) are only used around the house. I won’t dare take the trash out with this shirt in lmao.I went with a 4XL instead which are obviously gonna be bigger and way more room and length than what I want but after a wash should be perfect.All in all it’s not a bad shirt for the price. I use them for work. Material isn’t thick and heavy it’s a thin cotton and very breathable.I did notice with the first shirts I got that I did wash, the collar became stretched out and revealed more neck and chest than what it did when it was new.Might be coming back to edit this after the wash we’ll see.So if you want your shirts bigger or to fit just right go up a size or so."
    },
