[
    {
        "review": "Well worth the price!!! I'm 5'3\" 200 XL size. This shirt is a combo blend of cotton, polyester, and spandex. IT IS THE MOST COMFORTABLE, STRETCHY, SOFT ON MY SKIN, COOL IN THE SUMMER, WARM IN THE WINTER shirt I've ever purchased. I wear black t-shirts under my uniform, but this shirt here, is worthy of wearing with jeans, a sweatsuit, or any causal outfit. It's true to size, has a rich color and it's well made.  It will not disappoint. Try it! I'll be purchasing more!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a great t-shirt, IMO. Just received and tried on, so I cannot speak to how it will hold up, but for fit, it's a winner for me. At 5'5\" and 190-ish lbs, obviously I'm on the chunky side of things. And as most women of a certain age can attest to, the 2nd and 3rd stomach pooches of later mid-life are not a pleasure to behold, let alone dress in a somewhat flattering manner. Being somewhat pear-shaped doesn't help any of this one little bit. All that to explain why I am (ridiculously) excited about this tshirt.  Bought XL. It's relaxed just a little toward the bottom and fits well in the shoulders too. No shoulder seams hanging down off my shoulders. It's forgiving without looking oversized at all. The neckline is truly round, not wide or scooped at all, yet it isn't annoying - soft and comfortable. Sleeves are the ideal length and fit. The fabric is on the thinner side, but that was what I wanted for layering. But it's not too thin to wear alone, either. I bought the blue and a grey and both looked the same in person as they did online.I am very finicky and somewhat sensitive to the feel of fabrics and seams against my skin - and all I can say is when I put this shirt on my first thought was really just a sigh of comfort. Then I looked in the mirror and thought \"oh my gosh, it fits perfectly!!!\"  So I'm wearing it to work today and if my opinion changes I will update this review.  But right now I think I'm just going to be ordering more colors immediately!! :0)UPDATE - Just received and few more of these t-shirts. Be warned - the \"hot pink\" is not at all blue-toned - its very murky and salmon ish. I had a hunch that might be the case... suspicions confirmed. The navy blue is as it should be - a more purple-toned dark blue. The brighter blue that looks mid-tone online is actually almost the same darkness as the navy blue, just a more denim tone to the blue instead of purplish. Not quite as they appear online, but i will use both. Also, the dye/weave combination causes a more heathered look in all the colors. If you are looking for a very solid, saturated color, this is not it."
