[
    {
        "review": "It used to be that you could easily choose your tee shirts going by just the brand name. There were decades of knowing exactly what you were getting, as long as you stuck with a few top brands, and this brand was one of them. Now, there are numerous brands to consider, some are better than others, and you have many different choices. The benefits of more choices outweigh the negatives, but assuming that you are guided by reviews to stick with high quality, the weight of the fabric can still vary wildly. Depending on what I am trying to accomplish with a tee, the wearability and how I wear them can change. I personally prefer the thicker fabric, that affords perfect comfort, works as an under shirt or just plain with jeans, and even makes for a perfect sleep garment. This style and fabric weight accomplishes all of these with an amazing value. I was extremely satisfied with the neckline, and even though I prefer this style, I also wear v necks. There are now many different fabrics available, especially blends that are very versatile and full synthetic fabrics that can still be good. I will always prefer 100% cotton because of the comfort and thermal properties.With all the benefits of pure cotton, of course you have to be careful with how you launder them. If you are the type that wants to throw everything in together and wash at the highest temperature, you can still go with pure cotton, just size up one size to handle the inevitable small amount of shrinkage. Once the cotton shrinks the first time you wash them, the size will be very stable. Once you wear them, they might expand slightly from your body movement (especially if you use them for a workout) but this just makes them even more versatile and comfortable. You absolutely cannot go wrong with these as a top choice."
    },
