    {
        "review": "Good. They fit well and look nice. Keep in mind that there is a visual texture that looks slightly artificial, but I do not find it to be very discernible.The thickness is good, it feels like a regular cotton shirt — not too thin, and not that weird thick feel that some cheap shirts have. The neckline doesnt feel too tight. For me, it sits comfortably below the point where it would become annoying- 6’2 200lbs Size:LI got these as undershirts for jackets and button shirts. They work -and look- great."
    },
    {
        "review": "The Gildan Adult DryBlend T-Shirts (Style G8000) are a dependable go-to when you want comfortable, affordable shirts that can handle regular wear and washing. These are the kind of basic tees that work for just about everything, from daily casual wear to work, events, or layering.Comfort is solid right out of the package. The DryBlend fabric strikes a good balance between softness and structure. It’s not overly thin, but it’s also not stiff or heavy. The moisture-wicking blend helps keep the shirt from feeling damp or clingy, which is especially useful during warmer days or more active use.Fit is consistent and predictable. These shirts run true to size and don’t have an awkward cut. They sit well in the shoulders, aren’t too tight in the chest, and don’t hang like a box. The collar holds its shape nicely and doesn’t stretch out after a few washes, which is something cheaper shirts often struggle with.Durability is one of the biggest strengths. After multiple washes and regular use, the shirts hold their color well and don’t pill or thin out quickly. The stitching stays intact, and the fabric doesn’t warp or twist, even after being tossed in the dryer. That makes them a great option if you need shirts that can take some abuse.These are also excellent for customization. They work very well for screen printing, heat transfer, or embroidery, which makes them popular for team shirts, work uniforms, or events. The fabric accepts prints cleanly without bleeding or distortion.The multipack option adds a lot of value. You get consistent quality across all shirts, and it’s convenient to have several on hand at once rather than buying singles. Whether you’re stocking up for personal use or buying in bulk for a group, the multipack makes sense.Overall, the Gildan DryBlend G8000 shirts are reliable, comfortable, and built to last. They’re not flashy, but they don’t need to be. If you want solid everyday T-shirts that fit well, wash well, and offer good value, these are an easy five-star choice."
