    },
    {
        "review": "I like Amazon Essentials short sleeve T-shirts, even though they aren't the best fit for my shape. I have multiple sets in both crew necks and in V-neck. The V-neck shirts tend to have a looser fit, at least in the V-neck XL. I'm 5' and 1\" tall, 38C, and currently weigh about 143 pounds. I usually wear a medium in shirts that run loose, and a large in shirts that have less fabric or are slim fitted, but up-size to XL in Amazon Essentials Ts. I have a larger waist and stomach, but my legs are not particularly large, so I generally wear slim pants or leggings with elastic waists. Slimmer fitting T-shirts tend to be too tight, so I upsize, which is better for leggings anyway. Large jcp T-shirts fit well, but in Amazon Essentials I have to go up to XL because these shirts tend to run smaller in the chest, and a little narrower. Yes, I realize that the Amazon Basic XL looks too big for me, but the larges that I have hug my stomach too much.  These T's, which tend to run a little on the long side, have nice fabric and quality construction.  You'll need to determine your best fit.  I'd rate them with 5 stars if they fit me better.  I wash them on a short wash, dry them for about 2 or 3 minutes, and then hang them to complete drying. They come out looking new. The colors of this set are just as indicated. Amazon Essential T-shirts, which seem to be designed for taller and more slender customers, are good shirts for the price."
