    {
        "review": "It's a real shame about the actually good quality T-shirts. The fit is very strange and the size is different than my previous Fruit of the Loom shirts. Like all of my others, I ordered size M and was really looking forward to the T-shirts. Picked up today and immediately unpacked at home, marveled at the quality, which is really very good, no threads hanging out at the seams and they don't have a label on the neck, like many other T-shirts from this brand. The material is not very thick but felt very good and pleasantly soft. I thought it was great and tried one on straight away! The shirt was loose and casual and since I prefer \"loose fit\" I thought at first it still fit cool, maybe a little longer than my other \"Fruit of the Loom\" shirts, just bearable... And now for the but......but something wasn't right or somehow didn't feel right in the shoulder, armpit and chest area. So I went to the mirror and looked at myself and saw that the shirt was cut very strangely in the area I just mentioned. The sleeves are very short or far too short for a \"loose fit\" and the loose fit makes it look terrible, as if you had a shapeless sack over it. I don't want to walk around in public like that and I'm actually not that picky about it... :) I don't know, maybe it would look better if the T-shirts were tighter or if I took a size S or if I trained more. :) I think they're more suitable for athletic/muscular people... but they can't be worn in a \"loose fit\". Since I'm too slim for the T-shirts and don't have the money to just wear them underneath, I have to return them with a really heavy heart... I give 4 stars to the quality and the price/performance ratio (I paid just under €27)! 1 star deducted for the somewhat strange fit."
    }
