[
    {
        "review": "I got this small little green notebook because I wanted to start journaling.Something small enough that I could take with me, easy to be portable and put into a backpack or purse, and also big enough to actually write on each page.It does come with 140 pages, which is a good amount, and it has a hard cover. With a little band on the back to use and mark the page, as well as a little clear folder to put any papers/stuff in at the back. Nice and convenient little pouch for that!The pages themselves are good quality, date at the top and numbered page on the bottom (I don't need the content page numbers at the front of the book, but it is handy to have!)For the pages, they are actually good quality and thick enough to not bleed through. I wrote a few pages so far, there isn't like a indenting on the back side of the page where you don't see writing from the front, and it doesn't bleed through when I used a regular black pen. That means the pages are thick enough!It also says designed with 100% recycled paper, I think this is amazing because it is very economical, resourceful, and helping our environment! Definitely a plus. Also super affordable!! I got the green one for just $6."
    },
    {
        "review": "I originally bought this notebook thinking I might gift it to someone, but I ended up keeping it for myself and honestly love it. The quality is really nice, especially for the price. The color is such a pretty dusty sage green, and it feels simple but still cute.I also really like the little details inside. It has a table of contents, page numbers, spots for dates and titles, and even a page in the front where you can write who the notebook belongs to. It makes it feel a little more organized and put together than just a regular spiral notebook.It’s also the perfect size in my opinion. Bigger than a small notepad, but not huge like a regular school notebook. I actually ended up using it as a sticker book/scrapbook after another product didn’t work out, and it turned out SO cute for that. Definitely buying again. I loved the little strap that keeps the book closed! So many uses!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I needed something portable but sturdy for keeping my 'to do' list at work accessible and orderly. I'm glad I got this one. The lined pages are good for me to stay organized and I love that spiral so it is easier to write front and back but the pages are thick enough so no bleed through. Definitely recommend"
    },
    {
        "review": "I recently picked up the Taja Dotted Spiral Journal Notebook, and overall I’m really pleased with it. This notebook strikes a great balance between quality, functionality, and price — perfect for everyday use!📘 Design & BuildThe hardcover feels sturdy and durable, and I love the minimalist design. The spiral binding makes it easy to flip pages and lay the notebook flat when writing or sketching. It’s compact enough to carry around in a bag or backpack without feeling bulky.✏️ Paper Quality (⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️)The 140 dotted pages use thick, bleed-resistant paper that works really well with a variety of pens — even gel pens and markers don’t bleed through easily. The dot grid layout is great for bullet journaling, planning, or freeform note-taking.🧠 FunctionalityThe notebook’s size and design make it versatile. I’ve used it for personal journaling, sketching quick ideas, and jotting down reminders — all with ease. The elastic closure band keeps everything secure when you’re on the go.👍 Final ThoughtsFor the price, this notebook delivers excellent value. It’s well-made, practical, and looks nicer than many notebooks at similar price points. Whether you’re a student, creative, or just someone who likes to stay organized, I’d definitely recommend it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I have a small collection of notebooks that all started with great intentions... and about three pages of actual writing. This one, though? It might finally break the curse.The hardcover feels sturdy without being bulky, the spiral binding lays flat (a tiny luxury that makes a huge difference), and the paper is smooth enough that my pens don't throw a tantrum. The elastic band and ribbon bookmark make me feel wildly organized, even when the notes inside are mostly \"don't forget why you walked into this room.\"The sage green cover is simple, calming, and looks much more sophisticated than the chaos it contains. It's a great size to toss in a work bag without taking up half the space.If you're looking for a journal that's equal parts practical and \"I've got my life together\" aesthetic, even if that's a complete work of fiction, this one's an easy five stars. The best part is that I got it on sale for less than $6"
    },
    {
        "review": "Loved the color. The pages are just heavy enough it's easy to flip through and thick enough to stand up to heavy handed writing. The securing strap stretches over it even when things (like loose paper) are stuck inside it and is really helpful in, of course, keeping the journal closed when transporting it. All in all, great buy!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these for work and they have turned out to be the perfect little notebooks. They're compact enough to easily throw in a backpack or work bag, but still look polished and professional when you pull them out in a meeting.The elastic band is a surprisingly nice feature because it keeps everything together and prevents pages from getting bent up while commuting around. I also like that there's a date section at the top of each page. It makes organizing meeting notes much easier when you're trying to go back and find something later.I admittedly don't use the first couple pages with the index/table of contents setup and usually skip straight to the regular note pages, but that's more of a personal preference than a complaint.The overall quality feels solid, especially for the price. The faux leather cover maybe feels a tiny bit cheaper up close than I initially expected, but honestly once you're actually using it day to day at work, it still looks sleek and put together. Definitely doesn't feel embarrassing to bring into an office or client meeting.I've tried a lot of random notebooks over the years and this one hits a really nice balance of portability, functionality, and appearance. Would absolutely buy again."
