    {
        "review": "Excellent"
    },
    {
        "review": "Detailed Review: Mead Square Wide Ruled Notebooks 12-Pack When it comes to finding functional and affordable notebooks, the Mead Square Wide Ruled 12-Pack is a reliable choice for students, professionals, and anyone who needs to organize their notes. With a practical design and a comfortable format, these notebooks offer an efficient solution for everyday life. Design and materials Mead Square Wide Ruled notebooks have a compact size, making them ideal for carrying in backpacks, bags or even purses without taking up too much space. The cover, although simple, is durable enough to withstand regular use, although it is not rigid like the hardcover versions. As for the binding, they are stapled to the spine, which keeps the pages secure, but does not allow them to be opened completely flat without the risk of them coming unstuck over time. However, this design helps them to be lighter and easier to handle. Paper quality One of the most important points in any notebook is the paper, and in this case, the Meads fulfill their function well. The weight is adequate to prevent the ink from pens or pencils from easily transferring to the next sheet. However, if very wet markers or gel pens are used, slight bleed-through may occur. Wide Ruled ruling is perfect for those who prefer wide spacing between lines, making it easy to read and write neatly. This format is ideal for elementary students, people who write with large handwriting, or those who need to take quick notes without worrying about text alignment.Use and FunctionalityThese notebooks are a great choice for students of all ages, as they offer enough space to write without being bulky. They are also useful for offices, to-do lists or even keeping a personal diary. However, it is important to consider that they do not have binder perforations, so if you need loose sheets, they will have to be detached manually.Advantages and disadvantages✅ Advantages:• Excellent value for money, especially in large packs.• Compact size and easy to carry.• Good quality paper with wide lines for clear writing.• Lightweight and functional design.❌ Disadvantages:• No perforations for binders.• The cover is flexible and could wear out over time.• The Staple binding limits flat opening.ConclusionThe Mead Square Wide Ruled Notebooks 12 Pack is a smart purchase for those looking for practical, affordable and good quality notebooks. They are ideal for school, university or personal use, offering a balance between durability and comfort. Although they do not have some extras such as perforations or rigid covers, they fulfill their function effectively and are a reliable option for everyday use."
