    },
    {
        "review": "This journal is beautifully crafted and nice weight for a smaller size perfect for slipping in your messenger bag or purse! Well worth the money❣️I may buy more in the future in different colors🥰 I love taking on vacations to write my daily activities and what I liked and I would pass on in the future if I went back. I bought the Black w silver foil the design is so pretty and the spin is also decorated. Book mark is also very nice and same quality as the book❣️also a pretty thank you card❣️"
    },
    {
        "review": "I am beyond impressed with the quality of this TIEFOSSI notebook. The vintage hardcover gives it a timeless, professional look, and the binding is incredibly sturdy. With 316 numbered pages, it’s thick enough to last me a long time without feeling bulky. The college-ruled lines are perfectly spaced, and the paper quality is excellent—no ink bleed-through even with my fountain pens! The built-in bookmarks are a lifesaver for keeping track of my notes."
    },
    {
        "review": "EDIT 3: Since I'm unable to do a separate review on the replacement the company sent, I changed this one to 5 stars and am leaving all the review text intact. Just know that the first remarks (marked with *) about a journal with wrinkles and weather/heat/water-like damage refer to the first journal I received and reviewed at1 star, and the second set of descriptions (marked **) belong to the replacement the company sent me, rated at 5 stars.*I was instantly in love with the cover, the silver wash on the page edges, and the bookmark. Beautiful and exactly as advertised, and the cover has a marbled sheen and texture that’s appealing as well. However, be aware that the pages are not at all like those in their bullet journals. They feel pretty low GSM. They are heavily rippled where they are fixed to the spine and my fountain pens are visible through, and make impressions on, the paper. It Is still functional (I don’t have to use fountain pens) and the visibility isn’t bad enough you can’t write on the other side of the pages, but the quality is enough of a step down and the page ripple is so irritating and unattractive that I wouldn’t give it as a gift. Hence 4 stars not 5.*EDIT: After using this journal for several days, I’ve found the pages are so thin and the ripple in them so stubborn that it’s like it was dropped in water. They are problematic to write on and difficult to keep open or turn. I’m reducing my review to 1 star so people read it and because had I not written on several pages, I would return it.EDIT 2: The seller reached out immediately after this review to offer a refund or replacement. I chose the replacement and am awaiting a journal I hope I’ll enjoy as much as I have others from the company. Thanks to them. I’m leaving the review as is for this product but hope to give a great review of the new one.**I'll just embellish my praise for the quality of the exterior: I loved the delicate, magical design on the deep blue cover, the silver wash on the page edges, and the high quality bookmark that went perfectly with the journal. Beautiful and exactly as advertised, and the cover has a marbled sheen and texture that’s appealing as well.Inside, the pages are lush and thick and lie flat when opened, no wrinkle or crease. They easly absorb any inks I've tried (other than alcohol markers of course, which are not meant for this type of paper). They are smooth but not too glossy for all my journaling supplies, washi tapes, and stickers; if it doesn't stick, it's the sticker maker at fault, because I've tried products from a *lot* of vendors on Tiefossi 160gsm paper and have not yet been disappointed.Just to wrap up, wonderful customer service experience! Thank you for being immediately so great. It's what I expected from a company whose products are so good that I've already placed an order for another journal since we made this arrangement and have others in my queue as gifts.I can't comment on whether the 100gsm paper journal experience was a fluke of poor construction on that one book, something to do with it shipping through areas of extreme heat last week, conditions in a specific warehouse or truck, or what. The company likely doesn't know either, since the journal itself has a 4.5+ rating. But they didn't care, they just made it good. For that I thank them both here and with future business. Best of luck, Precious Princess (I think that's the name of the Tiefossi vendor here). I'll keep my eye out for products you handle. You're a real one."
