    {
        "review": "This is advertised as a journal notebook, which gives it a step up from the spiral notebooks the kiddos use in school.This notebook has a firm plastic sheet cover, not paper.Inside you'll find a page to put your contact information in the hopes that someone will return it to you if they find it. You'll just have to hope they haven't read your deepest and darkest secrets before returning it.Just past the first page, you'll find a few pages for contents. This allows you to put the general theme or topic of your writing, along with a page number.Just past this you'll get to the meat of the notebook, the lined pages. Each page has a place to write the date, indicate that days weather, and mark the day of the week, although, sadly, this incorrectly starts with Monday instead of the actual first day of the week. At the bottom of the page you'll find a place to write the page number. These are not pre-numbered, so you have the flexibility to remove pages you've messed up on and not disrupt the numbering.At the end of the notebook, there is a clear plastic pocket which included some adhesive tabs and the famous Mr. Pen mustache.There is also a pen included however the notebook does not have an included pen holder. It does have an elastic band for keeping the notebook closed.For only $4, this is a pretty decent journal notebook."
