[
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love this journal for many reasons. I love the way it handles. It bends just enough. I love the size of it. I love to write and travel. The size is such that I can easily stick it in my handbag or carry-on luggage. I love the color. I got pink. I like fun things and this is not stodgy.  I love the way that elastic band can be used as a bookmark and I usually attach a pen to it so I always have the two together. The lines are just perfect. The weight of the paper is quality. It also has two ribbon bookmarks."
    },
    {
        "review": "Paperage products are an unbelievably good deal. I have had quite a few of the hardbound journal both dotted and lined, but also recently tried the softcover journal as well as the spiral bound journal. All are exquisite. The paper is thicker than Leuchtturm or Rhodia, and the line spacing is wider than either of those brands or Moleskine. It isn't \"wide ruled\" but there are 3 lines of writing in Paperage to every 4 lines in a Rhodia goalbook. It makes a huge difference in my handwriting as well as the look of the page. In the past, when I have tried bullet journals or anything even remotely related to a \"diary,\" my handwriting has looked so abominable that it actually discouraged me from continuing the practice. Paperage actually has inspired me to keep up with new systems. It is all such a pleasure to use."
