[
    {
        "review": "This spiral notebook is cute and functional, and perfect for travel, work, or conferences. The slightly smaller A5 size strikes a great balance, it’s compact enough to carry easily, but still provides plenty of space to take detailed notes without feeling cramped. The spiral binding is sturdy and the hardcover feels durable enough to protect the pages from bending in a bag. The sunset design on the cover is really well done and adds a nice aesthetic touch. Inside, the college-ruled pages are great for fitting a lot of information, and the paper quality feels thick enough to hold up well over time. It also includes nice extras like a side pocket for loose papers or receipts and an elastic strap to keep everything closed and secure. All in all, it’s exactly what I was looking for, feels comfortable to write in, and at a great price! Definitely recommended!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Over time I’ve looked for a specific type of notebook that is similar to the Leuchtturm A5 notebooks.  But at a lower price point.  The Taja spiral notebook is a nice alternative.  It has six pages of index, then over 125 pages (not numbered but with a bottom blank page so you can do the numbering), and each page has a date line, too.  This is a lined notebook which even works for me who has big handwriting.  It’s an A5 size which fits nicely in a tote bag and even some purses.  Plus there are very cute designs.  Lastly, they’ve added a double-sided clear plastic pocket at the back of the notebook and a color-coordinated elastic band.  Now - they aren’t “bullet journal” notebooks exactly - the Taja notebooks I have are lined and not dot grid, and they don’t have fabric  bookmarks, but in all other respects, they are definite value for money.  Plus, because they aren’t as expensive as the “Bullet Journal” (and yes, I also have the fancy one with the embossed cover), you may be more inclined to actually USE them.  Or maybe this is just me - I tend to look at the fancy stuff as almost too precious to write in.  So for me, I kind of NEED notebooks I don’t view that way so I can just use the darn things.  You may be similar - and if so, you’ll be pleased with these notebooks."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very pretty. Pages are thick enough to not show through. It arrived in great shape and the spiral binding is very neat with no ends showing. I'm going to use it to take notes from a daily podcast and it's perfect! It has a place for the date at the top and a place for a list of topics in the front. I am very pleased with my purchase."
    },
