[
    {
        "review": "DETAILED REVIEW : BUY A SIZE AND A HALF UP, DON’T PEEL OFF ANY LABELS OR TAGS YET UNTIL YOU’RE SURE THEY FIT.[July 31st 2026]I am a solid size 9 wide in women’s shoes, with semi-flat feet. It’s hard to find supportive and affordable sneakers. Never purchased Skechers before but I really needed a comfortable, lightweight, affordable shoe for wide support. Read thoroughly through reviews and determined that I should buy a half size up for breathing room. Purchased a 9.5 wide, (Delivered SO fast by the way, next day immediately, I don’t even have prime. For me they arrived in perfect+new condition.), tried just one on, and the sole+arch+heel support was PERFECT and so cushioned. Loved the look of them, but unfortunately they were just an inch too short for the length of my foot, my big toe was *just* scuffing against the tip of the shoe, even in my thinnest/smallest pair of socks.Truly as advertised, minus the sizing discrepancy - which was user error due to my ignorance of the brand styling and sizing. Honestly if you’re scanning through reviews and at your wits end, just order a single size, or a size and a half up. This is the way of ordering online when you can’t try the product on immediately. The shoe is comfortable and easy to slip on and tie. Laces are a little short but they’re genuinely fine to tie loosely about once, twice if you pull them taut for more length. Easy to replace the laces if you’re particular about that.Such a cute shoe, it was perfect for what I needed - absolutely worth reordering for the correct size, I don’t even mind the return process because I caught a glimpse of a genuinely worthwhile, simple, straightforward shoe that I’ll wear often for walking+working out. Even arrived in an adhesive-lined, resealable, bag for convenient and secure returns if needed be - I got a free return! Just printed the labels and secured them on the bag, and inside. (The default order for me arrived with the resealable adhesive lined bag, and inside of that was the brand’s shoe box, for anyone curious on those details.)Don’t stress! Take the leap of faith on the Skechers D’Lites. Order up a size, and at most a size and a half, so your toes aren’t squished if you need that space. Excited to receive my 10 wides!Edit, Monday August 24th, 2026: 10 Wides came in! Perfect fit with extra breathing room - Got 16,000 steps in already! Will definitely have to use some supportive shoe inserts later on in their lifespan as I can already feel the sole compressing downward, but these shoes are great for my long walks so far."
    },
    {
        "review": "These have been my favorite sneakers for years. I have a wide foot from center of foot to toes and these are so comfortable from the start. I have one pair for yard work and one for wearing in public. The one have use when gardening are about 4 years old and if I were to clean them up and purchase new laces they would still be presentable in public. Despite bending over and over they have not cracked like some sneakers do. Pros- durable, comfortable, nice appearance, true to size, well worth the cost. Cons- if you prefer breathable type sneakers these may not be for you but then again breathable sneakers can get wet if you get stuck in rain. These will not."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased the white for nursing school, and I absolutely love them! They’re well-made, very comfortable, and provide great arch support.  As a healthcare worker, I’m on my feet for long hours as it is and will definitely purchase again.I highly recommend them, especially if you’re on your feet for extended periods. They’re comfortable enough to wear throughout long shifts.Ps.I wish they had more colors to choose from."
    },
    {
        "review": "Initially thought they might perform poorly. Was insanely impressed. These shoes came and I almost immediately thought of my 70 year old dad--they are bulky, blinding white, and very \"utilitarian\", thought grandpa shoes are having a moment and I was also sort of going for that look. I panic-bought these the night before a 10 day Ireland vacation because the options i owned for city and country walking shoes were primarily limited to chacos and some very thin mesh runners. I thought the plastic vinyl on these would perform better than my existing footwear and boy---did they.! They arrived 24 hours before departure so I had zero break in. I wore them to the airport to save space in my luggage and to test them out. Guys--I never took them off. These shoes kept my feet warm and dry in an absolute monsoon hike, handled city streets without causing me any back or leg fatigue, and looked equally stylish with my skirts and dresses as with pants. I had zero blisters or pain. They still look excellent despite being put through the ringer and logging over a hundred miles in 10 days. I cannot recommend these enough and am honestly not sure what I would have worn the entire trip had I not brought them along."
