        "review": "Very good, they lasted me almost a year using them daily"
    },
    {
        "review": "Beyond the fact that I have always been an athlete, I must admit that I have a huge passion for sneakers. I buy them all the time, I can't stop. I have about 30 pairs of my favorite brands, which is quite a few. Naturally, Under Armor is on the list and also among the top positions for preference. They are not among the most \"technical\" shoes but they are certainly among the most beautiful and comfortable that can be found on the market. These UA Charged Assert 10 are beautiful and well designed. The fit is excellent, the shoe fits well and the sole, in my opinion, has the right consistency to support a good run, offering cushioning and rebound but without giving way under the weight of the step. To be clear, the sole is made of foam, not the memory type: it is not one of those that give the feeling of walking on hard-boiled eggs like Skechers or like many Nikes. The ultra-soft, slipper-style ones are fine for a few steps, maybe a plane flight but you can't go running or walk on them for tourism for an entire day, not without having pain in your feet. To run you need a sole like the one on these Under Armor ones: not rigid but reactive and supported and the upper cannot be a sock. That also needs to offer some structure on all sides. This is a shoe designed for racing and has the right technical contents. If it is not the sporting performance that interests you and you are considering this shoe as a jeans sneaker, well, in my opinion you are still in the right place because on an aesthetic level, these shoes have nothing to envy of Adidas, Puma, Nike and co.. As regards the numbers, I can tell you that I generally have a 42 and, I have always purchased the 42.5 on Under Armor with success. Hello!"
    },
