[
    {
        "review": "The shoes are good quality and as expected. They have the hands-free slip in feature. I ordered a wide width and sized down one-half size, which was not enough.  Returned the original pair and sized down an additional 1/2 size. The new ones fit well."
    },
    {
        "review": "Theses shoes are very comfortable and the rear slip in shoehorn seems to work well.  There is no bending and easy to slip into without fail.  The durability and workmanship are equally as good does not tear easily construction is firm and looks good.the soles are durable and spongy which helps when standing for long periods of time.  Inner sole I think should be a little bit more lasting as excessive use tends to tear the inner soles then you have to buy another inner sole for the shoe.  Besides this Great shoes"
    },
    {
        "review": "Although your typical 'foreign-made' shoe (Vietnam this time) the 'Slip-in' feature that I made fun of when 1st appearing on TV, turns out to be the lazy-man's dream. Just when you're wondering how much lazier, and fatter can we become, along comes slip-in shoes that look like a traditional shoe, feel comfortable, and properly 'snug' so you don't have heal-rub or feel like the shoe won't stay on...it will!. Construction is solid and the tread/traction is good.So I assume just like our 1st cars with power windows and locks, after these shoes, there's no going back? I did add 3/4 insoles, and the fit still feels fine...comfortable and snug. I don't think I'll abandon my traditional shoes, but check back this time next year and I may have a different story to tell. Does anyone remember Pixar's movie WALL-E! Well, I feel my new Skechers hands free slip-in sneaker's, and my expanding waistband are aiming me in that direction, and fast. I would buy again."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great shoes but the inside lining already has a hole 🕳️ in the right toe area inside the shoe. Cheaply made not great quality especially coming from Sketchers. The slip in is an awesome time saver but they quit at quality. I was disappointed ☹️"
    },
    {
        "review": "The shoes arrived quickly and in good order. They are a gift for my father’s birthday. My father normally wears a 10.5 Wide in classic Reeboks. He hasn't tried \"hands free\" shoes, so I purchased his regular size. The 10.5 W is too large. I quickly ordered a 10 Wide. These seemed to be a little big to, but he wants to keep the 10 Wide. He is 91 years old and is having trouble bending his knees to tie his shoes & he likes to dress himself. So, we thought we would try these. They are bright white, which he loves & look nice on. He has trouble standing without his walker, but he was able to step into these shoes. He wore them for his walk with his physical therapist today and seems to like them. I will return the 10.5 Wide. When we need to order a new pair, I may order a 9.5 Wide because shoes tend to stretch with regular wear. We will see how these wear and wash up."
