[
    {
        "review": "I’ve been looking for a pair of white sneakers that don’t cost $150 but also don't look \"cheap.\" The Lee Specter Retro Court hits that sweet spot perfectly. They have that classic 80s/90s tennis vibe that goes with literally everything.The Highlights:Retro Aesthetics: These look fantastic with jeans, chinos, or even shorts. The silhouette is slim—not bulky—so they don't look like \"dad shoes.\"Surprising Comfort: Usually, \"fashion\" sneakers have all the cushioning of a sidewalk. These actually have a decent footbed. I wore them for a full day of walking around the city and didn't end up with the usual heel pain.Build Quality: The synthetic leather feels durable and, more importantly, it's easy to clean. A quick wipe with a damp cloth and they look brand new again.The Price Point: For the quality you're getting, these feel like a steal compared to the big-name \"Swoosh\" or \"Three-Stripe\" brands.Sizing & Fit:I found these to be true to size. I wear a 10.5 in almost everything, and the 10.5 here fit perfectly. They are a bit stiff for the first hour or two, but once the material breaks in, they flex nicely with your foot.Pros & Cons:ProsConsTimeless, clean designMinimal arch support for flat feetEasy to wipe cleanCan get a bit warm in high summerGreat value for the moneyFinal Verdict:If you want a clean, minimalist sneaker that looks more expensive than it actually is, the Lee Specter is a no-brainer. It’s the ultimate \"daily driver\" for your wardrobe."
