[
    {
        "review": "I absolutely love these sneakers! The cream and black color combination is exactly what I was hoping for and goes with pretty much my entire wardrobe. They have great traction, and they’re comfortable right out of the box. I have wide feet and normally wear an 8, but I ordered a 7.5 since that’s what I’ve been wearing in bowling shoes. They’re a little snug, so I probably could’ve stuck with my usual size 8, but I think they’ll stretch a bit with time. They’re not super lightweight (they remind me more of the weight of dunks), but they’re very comfortable. I’ve been wearing Converse for years, and they always leave my arches hurting, but I had no arch pain at all in these. Overall, I’m so happy with this purchase and can’t wait to wear them with all my outfits!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Due to some pronation, my podiatrist fitted me for custom orthotics and gave me a list of recommended shoes to use with them. Since, I work in veterinary medicine and spend the majority of the day on my feet, I have needed really good shoes. On average, I walk about 3.5 miles during a shift. Trust me, I’ve tried them all with and without the custom orthotics and I’ve still had foot/ankle/knee pain. These shoes alone are the absolute best because they give great ankle/heel/arch support and the fit around the toes is perfect. They are sturdy, clean up easily, and I love the Reebok retro throwback. Over the last few years, I have repeatedly bought them and I hope they never stop production."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very nice and comfortable! Looks good with any pants or jeans."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great shoes. Stylish and comfortable. They are stiff after 3 plus hours on your feet otherwise would have been 5 stars. Definitely worth the price."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've been eyeing these shoes for quite a while, and finally caved as I was due for a new casual but smart looking tennis shoe. I love the platform and neutral color way of these, and I wear them confidently with jeans, trousers, and dresses alike.I purchased them in time for a week long trip to London where I wore them every single day. In fact, I didn't wear any of the other shoes I'd brought along with me as these were so versatile and comfortable.I wear a 10.5 so I sized up into an 11 as 10.5 is not offered. I think the 11 is a little too big, and if I don't take the time to lace them well, I notice that my heel will slip out a bit and cause some discomfort in my calf. However, I figured that out quickly and adjusted as necessary.In the end, I walked miles and miles around London and it's surrounding towns/villages and was very comfortable."
    },
    {
        "review": "Review: Reebok Club C Double Platform SneakersI’ve been wearing the Reebok Club C Double Platform sneakers for a while now, and they’ve definitely become a go-to in my rotation. If you’re into classic silhouettes with a modern twist, these are a great choice.Style:The platform sole gives the traditional Club C design a fresh, elevated look—literally. It adds just the right amount of height without feeling over-the-top. They pair well with everything from joggers and jeans to dresses and skirts, which makes them super versatile for casual or slightly dressed-up looks.Comfort:Surprisingly comfy for a platform sneaker. The cushioning is solid, and the shoe feels stable and supportive, even after a long day on your feet. I wouldn’t call them ultra-lightweight, but they’re definitely not clunky either.Fit:They run true to size in my experience. The leather upper is snug at first but breaks in nicely after a few wears. If you have wider feet, you might want to consider going half a size up, especially if you wear thick socks.Quality:Reebok did a great job with the materials—good leather, clean stitching, and a durable sole that holds up well. They’re easy to clean too, which is a bonus if you like that fresh-out-the-box look.Final Verdict:If you’re looking for a sneaker that balances retro vibes with a modern edge, the Reebok Club C Double Platform is a solid pick. Stylish, comfortable, and versatile—definitely worth it.⸻"
    },
