[
    {
        "review": "First time purchasing this brand. These shoes are very comfy & they also look good. Very affordable. I've purchased similar shoes from the Amazon website for much more & they were very uncomfortable & only wore them once. I ended up donating them.  I definitely won't  be donating these. I'll tell friends & family to purchase Project Cloud shoes & I will return to purchase more Project Cloud shoes in the future."
    },
    {
        "review": "Love these! So comfortable and cute!! I’m on my feet all day and these feel great after wearing them for 12-15 hours"
    },
    {
        "review": "I had wanted these for some time and have looked at new balance and Steve Madden. They are similar style but much more expensive. I was so excited to finally pull the trigger and buy these! I was thinking I’ll save money , and they’re adorable! Soooo disappointing! They are a super cute shoe, but I’m not sure if I had received a dud or what?!?! I have know idea how other reviews say these are comfortable. What is your definition of comfort? These are like walking on a stiff board! No cushion  and they actually seem to run a full size large. They were huge. I wear a 10 in almost every athletic shoe and ordered a 10 in these and were  swimming in them. Far too big, but not worth ordering the right size. They are so hard and uncomfortable. Sadly returning. I’m definitely not keeping an athletic shoe that’s not comfortable. That’s the whole point. Don’t bother. Save time returning and just pay the money and order Steve Madden or New Balance. These are not worth it."
    },
    {
        "review": "These shoes are super cute & pretty comfortable. There could be a bit more cushioning in the sole, but overall I'm pleased with them. They are very lightweight."
    },
    {
        "review": "I can’t make my mind up whether these shoes are more comfortable or more stylish!!  I choose to wear them with EVERYTHING!!  They match all of my leopard and/or cheetah print!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Love these shoes! So comfortable and just really snug me feet! Ordering another pair!"
    },
    {
        "review": "This shoe is marketed as having memory foam and being breathable. Neither of those statements are true. I work in healthcare and am on my feet all day. I tested these shoes out for a solid 2 weeks thinking they just needed to be broken in. Unfortunately the insoles are hard as a rock, flat, and have zero cushion. They are not breathable and your feet will become hot after an hour of moving around. The shoes also squeak terribly on anything other than wood/cement. They are cute and the lacing is secure but they are not suitable for people who are on their feet a lot. The shoes also scuff very easily especially so around the toes."
    },
    {
        "review": "These shoes are nice looking. When I received them and put them on, I honestly didn’t know what to think. They’re not the “walking on clouds” experience you get from Skechers. I read reviews saying a nurse wears them for long shifts honestly, I can’t imagine that. Nursing or retail work would be rough in these.That said, they do look nice. They’re a good-looking tennis shoe that pairs well with my navy winter hoodies, sweatshirts, flannels, and sweaters. They’ve got small touches that suggest quality, but the overall shape leans a little boxy. It’s not bad, but don’t expect the comfort level of Nike, Reebok, Skechers, or Hoka.I wear them in my daycare because I like to look put together, even on leggings-and-hoodie Mondays. They’re a bit less comfortable than my Nikes or Adidas, but they’re fine for daily wear. They actually hold up better in the yard than my New Balances did (those had cheap mesh). The faux suede at the toe scuffs easily, but it’s also easy to rub out.Overall, these shoes are a mix of quality and cheap. I’m surprised I wear them as often as I do because I’m pretty spoiled by better brands. I’ve had jobs where good footbeds were essential just to survive the day these wouldn’t cut it for that. But for my daycare work, light yard tasks, and quick errands to the store or Menards, they’ve done well enough.If I had to do it over again, I’d probably spend an extra $30–40 and get the Steve Maddens these are a dupe of. Still, I don’t regret buying them."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent tennis shoes, the insole is very thin, but I solved it with other insoles, beautiful, very soft and I can walk for hours and hours and it doesn't hurt my feet, I give it a 10."
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking at a model of a New Balance shoe that looked very similar to these (and I have since learned there is a similar Steve Madden shoe as well). The new balance shoe was pricier and the way the rubber on the shoe came up over the toe was not an ideal look for me. I could not justify the price if I was not completely happy.  I thought if they went on sale, maybe, but that happened and I still could not do it.  It was actually in my search for those shoes on sale that I came across these.  I thought about it.  The reviews were good, covered all the things I needed to know, but the price made my wonder, are they really as good as most reviews said? Well, I finally took a chance and I am happy that I did! Since taking that chance I now own 2 pairs - black and grey.I am an avid walker and runner too.  I do both everyday.  I am about comfort and quality. I would not run in these shoes as I have heavier duty runners for that.  I think these would be okay, but I am not sure how they would hold up to that kind of activity.  But walking in them a minimum of 7 kms a day, they are perfect. This is my experience anyway.  They are comfortable, stylish and the quality seems alright.One thing though is that the tongue does not stay in place, it would shift to the side of my ankle after a few steps, which I was not crazy about.  Most shoes of this style, a runner type, have a slot that the laces fit through to hold the tongue in place. These do not. There is material on the tongue though that, with some magivering, I was able to create slots by removing some stitches and adding others.  I am a sewer.  I have done this to both pairs and it works perfectly.  Also, for the grey shoes, I replaced the grey laces with the same lace style, but in white.  I much prefer them this way."
    },
    {
        "review": "Super cute, I loved them, I'm size 25 and they fit me perfectly, they are true to size.  The color is cute and very fresh. I recommend them, very good quality. Super comfortable.  Thanks Project Cloud"
    },
    {
        "review": "Wear your clouds!  Super comfortable fits great size is perfect!"
    },
    {
        "review": "They arrived stained like grease, but other than that, I really liked the model and they are very comfortable."
    }
