    {
        "review": "Skechers are, without a doubt, my favorite sneakers. I honestly don't wear anything else! They're incredibly comfortable with **so much** cushioning—it truly feels like you're walking on a cloud.I work in healthcare and spend 12-hour shifts on my feet, constantly walking, and my feet don't hurt at the end of the day. That alone keeps me coming back to Skechers.They fit true to size, are lightweight, made with great-quality fabric, and I love the thick, supportive sole. They're comfortable enough for long workdays but also great for walking or running.You really can't go wrong with these shoes. If you're looking for comfort, support, and all-day wearability, I highly recommend them!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really like these Skechers. They’re very comfortable and have a lot of cushioning, which makes a big difference when I’m walking for a while.They feel light on my feet and have good support without feeling stiff. I also like the way they look — they’re sporty but still cute enough to wear with everyday clothes.After wearing them for several hours, my feet still feel pretty good, which is probably my favorite thing about them. They’re a great choice if you want something comfortable for walking and everyday use. I’m very happy with them so far."
    },
    {
        "review": "I did a lot of searching to find a top rated shoe that was true to fit, comfortable,  high cushion, high shock absorption, and most importantly arch support for plantar fasciitis. These shoes check all the boxes except for the arch support. I think I'll keep these because they are cute and really needed a new pair. I took away a star because I will need to continue supplemental arch wraps."
    },
    {
        "review": "These are sooo comfortable and I love them.  I’ve had them for a while now and they still look and feel brand new.  The arch support isn’t everything but insoles with arch support are cheap enough.  They’re not too hot in the summer heat (it is now August and I’ve had them for like a month or longer) and with somewhat thin socks my feet do not sweat really bad.  They’re not super light weight but also not super clunky.  The cushion is amazing.  They’ve held up really well and I drive a city transit bus for a living so I’m constantly using both feet bc my signals and bright lights are on the floor on the left side."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love these shoes - it is my fifth pair.  They are wide and very comfortable.  I stand on concrete tile all day and then walk 3-4 miles when I get home and my feet never hurt.  Before I started wearing these, they hurt all the time.  Also, I like the way they look.  I have ordered them in black and navy also and those look great, too."
    },
    {
        "review": "I underpronate (supination) and find my feet are best in maximum cushioning with arch support and minimal or no stability in sole.  I ordered these shoes to wear for my new job in the hospital where I will be getting in my steps.  Although this pair does not have significant arch support, the cushioning makes up for that and my feet are not at all tired after wearing these.  The soles have excellent base so I am not rolling to the outer edge.  The huge plus is that they are washable!  Perfect for working in a hospital (or a dirty environment).  I'll be buying another pair to switch between so they have at least a day to air out.  Highly recommend."
