        "review": "Thinking about buying them for a trip where you're walking a lot? Don't.I went to Europe, and my feet were so sore each night. My feet did not feel supported, and they left my heels/bottom of foot very sore. The toe box pushed my pinky toe in slightly and didn't give it much space. It is the correct size and true to size. It was the narrow spacing of the toe box area that caused the issues. Thankfully, they did not cause any blisters.They are cute but began fraying on the heel the same day I started wearing them. I don't imagine they will last very long.3 stars because they aren't expensive. This is truly a case of \"you get what you pay for\".I would not recommend them for anything over 8,000 steps. Which is very clearly not intended for a trip where walking is key."
    },
    {
        "review": "Extra super duper cute- LOVE!!  Comfortable as far as skater shoes go.  There’s a difference between athletic shoes and casual sneakers.  If you want to walk around and are expecting some comfy- cloud experience,  buy athletic shoes.  These are for casual wear, not long walks.  So know what you’re buying when you order casual sneakers.  As far as sizing, reviews are all over the place.  My other Rocket Dogs (8.5) fit just right.  These are slightly larger, probably more like a 9 but are sooo cute, I don’t even care!"
    },
