[
    {
        "review": "These are an all around great shoe, can be worn well with shorts, Capri, or jeans. Easily slips on and i prefer the short laces myself. I bought these in white but will also be ordering black and maybe a few other colors. They didn't make my feet sweat even in 105° temps. I wear an 8.5 in Brooks, Ariat, Adidas and Sketchers brands. I ordered 8.5 in this shoe with a perfect fit. They are made well and holding up to daily wear. The material felt a little stiff the first day but after wearing a couple times they softened up well."
    },
    {
        "review": "These sneakers are true to size.  I'm usually a size 7 and 7 was a perfect fit.  They are simple, yet cute and comfortable.  They have short laces that aren't meant to be tied.  They are easy to slide on and off, but the company includes regualr tie shoe laces in the box with each pair if you want to change them.  The eyelets are copper colored and a small logo is embroidered in copper stitching.  The upper is made of canvas.  No arch support, but I prefer that.  They match with many casual outfits,"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love these shoes! They are comfortable and so easy to slip on. They look cute with scrubs, dresses and jeans. They run true to size. On me they are a touch wide in the toe area, but I have narrow feet. They wash and air dry well coming out clean. This is my 3rd pair of sketchers and I’ve never been disappointed with this brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered a 6.5 in the \"Natural\" color. The shoes are as I expected. The color I received was exactly what was pictured. I have really high arches, and I was looking for something that would be casual, comfortable, and wearable for walking around for a few hours while at ports of call on our cruise, and using during excursions.These are a little large, which I like - I actually measure for a 5.5-6 and size up 1/2 for breathability and to account for swelling during exercise/heat. I just wish the tied off laces were a little smaller. It does come with standard laces, so those are an option.The quality seems decent. I should be able to wear them in various situations. The soles have a bit of traction, so I should be able to walk in sandy or wet conditions without slipping.The insole is memory foam, but not much of it. It's a very flat feeling. Once worn a couple of times it does reduce, but I don't know that it's enough.Now for my big issue - there are elastic bands on either side that hold the tongue in place and hold the shoes on the feet. I am allergic to latex, so it's not ideal to have rubber in an area that could touch my skin. AI thought they were 100% canvas upper - so my fault for not confirming with the company. The bands make it so that, even though I ordered up a half size, I can't add additional arch support without making it too tight. Even with that, yes, I can and will wear socks to avoid the rubber because I really do like the shoes and I'm fortunate that my allergy is only contact related. These shoes may not work for my intended purpose, but they will work as normal casual shoes. I may even be able to wear them to work."
    },
    {
        "review": "So cute and comfortable size fits well! Memory foam is wonderful feeling and is good for standing long periods of time! Sole feels firm and unmovable which is a big plus and these have great traction! Good foot support! And definitely worth the money my new favorite pair of shoes I’ll never leave the house without ❤️👌"
    },
    {
        "review": "Adorable, my go to shopping shoe!  I bought size 5 first, but exchanged it for a size 5.5 wide which is perfect.  It seems to run small and narrow-  snug fit.  I am a woman if age and find this flat shoe is surprisingly comfortable, enough arch support for me and padding."
    },
    {
        "review": "I LOVE this shoe. I have been looking for this shoe for years. I got it at sketchers forever ago, and then they NEVER had my size in stock. And when they changed the style of ALL of their shoes to the slip ins I had to accept I would never find this shoe again. I am so glad I was able to find this older style on Amazon. And at a great price! (I got the black and white one for only $25 on Amazon Prime Day!) Needless to say I am very excited to have this comfortable, easy to get on, stylish shoe back on my shoe rack!They are very flat but that's exactly why I love them. I usually where these to go run errands since they are easy on and off and comfortable. I would say they are actually pretty durable and last quite awhile even with daily wear. Unfortunately the \"memory foam\" gets very stinky from lack of breathability. Which is why I usually wear them for more low key days.Update:Didn't realize I would need to share a review for different colors. I took some stars away because the white pair I ordered were... damaged? I don't know if that's what they would be considered. But the laces aren't meant to be used like laces. (See photo laces are tied off at the top) the white pair I got the laces were too long. And no, they don't need to be moved down, I tried. I am going to try to return them and get them replaced and will update my review once I get them back!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I really love these for the summer!  Not a lot of arch support but there is a little bit of a cushion sole. They are not as narrow as Keds which is nice. They are well made and have a roomy toe. I consistently wear a size women's 8 but I had to reorder these a full size down. I ended up with a size 7 as my perfect fit.  They just run big but once you find your size you will love them.  Will be super cute with summer skirts, dresses, shorts and leggings!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Nice and comfortable shoes. Sketchers has become my favorite brand."
    },
    {
        "review": "Oh boy do I love them I now have three pairs, thing of getting another one in a different colour 🤩🤩🤩"
    },
