[
    {
        "review": "Great product,  smells great. A lot cheaper then a Yankee candle but looks exactly the same. Jar and all."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this spiced pumpkin candle to get into the fall mood, and it has quickly become my favorite seasonal scent. The fragrance is strong enough to fill the room within minutes but not overpowering—it’s the perfect balance of pumpkin, cinnamon, and a hint of vanilla. It makes the whole house feel warm and cozy, almost like fresh pumpkin bread just came out of the oven.The burn time has been impressive. I’ve been lighting it in the evenings for about two weeks now, and it’s still going strong with an even melt (no tunneling, which is a big plus). The wax burns cleanly, and the wick is easy to trim, so maintenance is minimal.I also appreciate the design of the jar—it’s simple and seasonal without being overly flashy, so it looks nice on my coffee table and blends well with my other fall décor.If I had to mention one small drawback, it’s that the scent is so good that I find myself burning it every day—I may run out sooner than planned! My tip: grab two if you want it to last the whole season.Overall, this candle is a must-have for anyone who loves fall scents. It’s cozy, long-lasting, and makes your home instantly feel festive."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is by far and away my favorite candle. The smell is both comforting and arousing. When you open the candle for the first time the aroma alone, without burning the candle is enough to fill a room. Commonly that is what I will do. Just open the candle, not light it, and let the fragrance fill the room for a few hours.Eventually it is time to light it. Both wicks need to be burning for it to evenly burn down. I hate candles that leave wax in the jar as they burn. This one does not do that. All of the wax burns off as it is used up. At the bitter end all that is left is a jar with two burnt up wicks and a very small amount of the wax residue.This also burns for a very long time. I’d say, end to end, if you light it and just let it burn it would keep burning for about a week total. Maybe 10 days. I have bought many of these and burning it about an hour or two per night I’d say I get roughly 4 to 5 weeks of use out of it. Maybe a little less than that with weekend burning a bit longer sometimes.It normally comes in a very sturdy package. I like to order it with other goods so as to give it extra protection in shipping. But I have had them deliver it in the original shipping container no problem. That being said I have also gotten one broken like some other reviewers mentioned. What I did was take a small ball peen hammer and carefully broke away the glass outside. Piece by piece. Cut myself doing this but not bad, so follow these instructions with caution. Nevertheless, once I got all of the glass away and carefully removed the bottom glass (which is glued to the candle wicks so use a knife [again carefully] to separate the wick bottoms from the glass) so I could put the candle into a container and light it. It worked. But again that happened once and I have bought MANY of these over the years with no issues.Let me also say that pumpkin spice is my favorite. And the ladies like it too. Good for getting in the mood if you know what I mean. But I have burned other flavors and they all seem to be top quality. Very fragrant and delicious smelling.  Everybody loves the smell of my house when I burn these.I don’t write reviews unless I truly hate or believe in a product. So just know that I think this product is worth the cost, definitely. Hope you enjoy one as much as I do."
    },
    {
        "review": "This candle smells great. It's supposed to be Spiced Pumpkin but just smells like cinnamon. It's better than the Sparkling Cinnamon Yankee candle that I wasted $ on!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was looking for a pumpkin scented candle and happy I found this on Amazon . I usually purchased Yankee candles and then went in to look for more affordable alternatives. This Village Candle definitely did not disappoint as the pumpkin aroma was perfect and could smell it from a distance, it has a nice glow and didn’t leave a mark on the tip of jar which is important. I highly recommend if on budget and want a great quality product. It arrived on time and packed well!Note : if you prefer soy or beeswax i would suggest another alternative.  Hope this helps !"
