[
    {
        "review": "If you’ve ever walked into a Yankee Candle store and smelled that specific, intoxicating scent wafting through the air, it was almost certainly Midsummer's Night. It is arguably one of their most recognizable and polarizing fragrances, but for those who love it, it's an absolute classic that's hard to beat.​Scent Profile:This candle is unapologetically bold. Yankee Candle describes it as \"a intoxicating and masculine blend of musk, patchouli, sage and mahogany cologne.\" That description is spot-on. It strongly evokes the feeling of a high-end men’s cologne—cool, fresh, and slightly woodsy, but with a deep, sensual warmth from the patchouli and musk. It is not fruity, floral, or traditionally sweet. If you prefer clean linen or vanilla cupcake scents, this will likely be too strong for you. But if you love deep, \"dark\" scents that feel sophisticated, this delivers.​Throw and Performance:I tested this in the classic 22 oz large jar. The scent throw is phenomenal—a solid 10/10. Midsummer's Night is known for being a powerhouse. Within 30 to 60 minutes of lighting it, the fragrance easily fills my entire downstairs living area and kitchen. It lingers in the air long after the candle has been extinguished.​Quality and Burn:The burn quality is consistent with the standard Yankee Candle reputation. The wax pool melts evenly across the surface, preventing tunneling, provided you let it burn long enough on the first few uses. The two wicks burn cleanly (remember to trim them before each light to minimize soot). The longevity is excellent; the large jar provides many hours of strong fragrance, justifying the price point.​The Vibe:This is a fantastic year-round scent, though it particularly shines in the autumn and winter evenings due to its warm, musky notes. It creates a cozy, confident, and slightly mysterious atmosphere. It’s perfect for movie nights, dinner parties, or simply relaxing after work. Because it is so cologne-forward, some describe it as a \"boyfriend's sweater\" scent.​Verdict:Midsummer's Night is a classic for a reason. It is a bold, long-lasting, and powerfully scented candle that delivers exactly what it promises. If you are a fan of deep, musky, or cologne-style fragrances and want a candle that will unmistakably scent your entire home, this is a must-buy. Highly recommended.​Pros:​Iconic, sophisticated, \"cologne\" scent​Phenomenal scent throw (fills large spaces easily)​Long-lasting burn time (Large Jar)​Creates a distinct, cozy atmosphere​Cons:​The scent is very strong and may be overpowering for those sensitive to heavy fragrances​Polarizing profile; definitely not for lovers of light, floral, or sweet scents"
    },
