        "review": "I'm a guy who likes candles. I believe in scents triggering mental and emotional states. My experience is that anything lavender-based is usually pretty relaxing and zen.This candle has a great scent. Not overpowering like you're in a room sprayed down with perfume, but definitely enough to notice. Very calming, and I usually light it when start my day with a little meditation. I burn it pretty regularly, almost every day for an hour or so, and you can see where it is after a month or so of use. Good longevity.However, something about the soy/wax blend burns very \"straight down\" and creates these sort of wells where the wicks are (see pic). The temperature of the melted mix doesn't seem to melt the material around it, as I'm guessing the melting point is higher than traditional wax. I have to keep digging out the wicks after one or another goes out due to too much melt, and I have a feeling I'm going to have to melt this wax over a stove and pour it back into something else to use it all."
