[
    {
        "review": "I order these for church. They are excellent quality and do really last for hours. They are bright and unscented so they don't cause allergy issues. I highly recommend them."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this set for a small gathering, and it delivered exactly what I needed. The candles come in clear glass holders, which gave them a clean, elegant look on the table. Since they're unscented, they didn’t interfere with food or overwhelm the room—which is a big plus.They burned evenly and lasted close to the 15-hour mark as advertised. I also appreciated that they’re made with a soy wax blend, which tends to burn cleaner than paraffin. These worked great as decor for both dinner and relaxation.They're simple, well-made, and versatile—perfect for weddings, parties, or even just a quiet night in. Definitely worth the price for a pack of 12."
    },
    {
        "review": "These were a great affordable option to add warm ambience to a recent anniversary party for my parents. They burned for probably around 4-5 hours and were only about halfway gone. Very elegant looking and clean burning."
    },
    {
        "review": "This past Christmas I decided to start a little holiday tradition - both my husband and I have heritage from Norway and Sweden so we opted to get some candles for that hygge life. They looked great on the table as a holiday centerpiece and look great now as a year-round centerpiece!There were chips and glass defects in about 5 of the candle holders, but to be honest, I don't notice and if it bothers me, I can just switch them around. These came well packed, although there was a lot of cracked plastic packaging that I cleaned out of the box and you may have to wipe bits of excess wax off the glass.The candles themselves look very nice. Mine doesn't burn fat, but it's pretty as they go down, it hides the flame sometimes. They don't seem like they will last a long time, but I think the 12 hour burn time sounds right. We lit them every Sunday night for about a half an hour to an hour leading up until Christmas, and then through our dinner party on Christmas. There are still about half the candles left in them!All in all, I am happy with them and I would buy from Hosley again. I would recommend this for people planning a wedding or dinner party, and I would also recommend them for people who just want candles around the house. Good size and shape and there is no smell to them!"
    },
    {
        "review": "These votive candles were great for the price! They came in 4 packs of 12 and are VERY heavy. I used some modge podge to decorate half of them with teal glitter to use at my wedding. It worked really well, except when I repackaged them in the cardboard box, they did stick to the cardboard, so make sure you cover them with wax paper if you do anything like that, otherwise the glitter will get pulled off. The packaging is pretty tight to keep them intact so even adding the glitter made it hard for them to fit back in.I gave them 4 stars because they have kind of a gross smelling bread odor upon opening the package. I didn't notice it when they were lit though but the wedding was also outdoors. I did have to wipe the glass part on some of them as it was kind of waxy before painting them but it was pretty easy to clean them. I was not able to pop them out of the glass like I wanted to though to be able to paint more freely, so I did end up getting some glitter on the wax which was hard to get out.Overall, great quality for the price and you could probably reuse the glass once the candle fully burns out. We had them lit for about 6 hours at our wedding and they still had some wax left so I think they would definitely last the 8 hours as advertised. I probably would only buy them for home if I found some nice essential oil or something to make them smell better."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great candles. Last long."
    },
    {
        "review": "I love these candles and got a box in case ever needed in the future. The glass they come in is not cheap thin glass and looks nice on the table. They last for many many hours and no scent."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great packaging!  The candles burn bright for hours!  You can definitely tell they're hand poured, and I love the wax they use because it doesn't smell and burns clean. They are very bright, and I will be reordering."
