    {
        "review": "I am disappointed in amazon. This was my second purchase of Ho--Maui Jim’s -the same exact pair -hello the glasses, HOWEVER, in the first order… amazon sent me the wrong case, much smaller than the case that Maui Jim actually gives their customers for “higher end- use till they break for 10+years” sunglasses. Many people collect them like watches cause they’re so beautiful. Luckily, I had my old case from my last pair of Maui Jim’s purchase direct a hard shell case, I used it to literal pieces. Now was Using the new case from Amazon, clearly too small smooshing in the glasses, and because the case didn’t fit once again.. for the second time.. they fell out- but I don’t know where so I can’t retrieve them.-These WERE my replacements and the same case arrived.. I really tried to make it work. I called Amazon. They said that’s the case to this day. They standby that word HOWEVER I’M NOT PERFECT, BUT I AM A PERFECTIONIST. I don’t lose things. I’m very diligent. - I called Maui Jim-  they know me…and sent me the CORRECT case WOULD THEIR DEEPEST SYMPATHIES THAT THEY COULDN’T SEND ME A PAIR OF GLASSES CAUSE I BOUGHT THEM FROM AMAZON- and those sunglasses SHOULD COME WITH the correct case FOR THAT PRICE POINT. SOMEONE IN THE WAREHOUSE IS SWAPPING CASES OR MISSING THE fulfillment MARK. I have pleaded my case thrice to Amazon for my replacement glasses, I ALREADY BOUGHT TWO PAIR FROM THEM BOTH LOST BECAUSE OF THE CASE even with the evidence of the case and the backing of Maui Jim -over a few hundred dollars they will lose most of my business unless I need to use them Amazon that isNow , I’ll have to save up all over again, but this time I go directly to the MJ store."
    },
    {
        "review": "So far very goodVery comfortable they protect your eyes"
    },
    {
        "review": "I almost let myself not order because of the reviews that this was a fake item. But as a Maui Jim fan for decades and the owner of many Maui Jim sunglasses, I can now say that I actually received an original Maui Jim sunglasses - exactly as described. When you first look through them you can immediately see the perfect colors that are only created by the different Maui Jim filter layers. Once you've experienced that, you don't want anything else. I've tried almost all the well-known brands of sunglasses, but I haven't discovered a lens like Maui Jim's yet. Most other sunglasses color the field of vision depending on the color of the lens - the view becomes correspondingly colored and the image simply becomes dark. A Maui Jim eliminates the glare of the sun, contrasts increase, but without darkening significantly, at least not noticeably, but all colors become significantly richer. The green of the meadow appears lusher, the blue of the sky is much more intensely blue, the turquoise of the sea appears dramatic.  The special polarization allows you to see deep into the water, as the water surface hardly reflects. In addition, the wearing comfort of a Maui Jim sets standards. The glasses are light. Once put on, it stays put and doesn't slip even during exercise. Even wearing it for a whole day does not create pressure points on the nose, thanks to the special Maui rubber nose olives. The temples and frame are typically made of Maui Jim plastic. The material is extremely durable. There is one thing a Maui Jim will never forgive you for: a microfiber cloth that is not specifically suitable for plastic glasses. The surface of the lenses is immediately blinded with a microfiber cloth. Otherwise, the lenses are very resistant to scratches. My oldest Maui Jim, which I still use every day in the car, is more than 15 years old and has no scratches. Only: Maui Jim - what were you thinking with that stupid cover. In the past, every Maui Jim sunglasses always came with a very elaborate case - a very typical one with a zipper, absolutely indestructible, my oldest Maui case is now more than 20 years old and you can't tell by looking at it, it will definitely last another 20 years. The current case is so stupid, there's no other way to describe it, that you have to be very talented to use it. Apparently I don't have enough intellect to store the glasses in them, not to mention the fact that in a suitcase, unlike the old cases, the glasses in them are not protected against pressure. Luckily I still had a case from years gone by. Now you have to say that this is complaining at a high level. Anyone can easily buy a case for little money."
    },
