[
    {
        "review": "I wanted an inexpensive but snug fitting and comfortable polarized pair of sun glasses to wear in my car and ride my bike and these fit the bill perfectly. They are attractive, offer wrap around protection, are incredibly lightweight yet stay in place while remaining very comfortable. The ear  pieces seem to assure they won’t keep sliding down my nose. I gave them a 5 star rating because of the features, comfort and very low cost but I fear they may scratch easily. I am careful with my eyewear but if issues arise such as scratching or breakage I will update this review."
    },
    {
        "review": "Finally, a pair of sun glasses than wont slide down my nose every 2 minutes. Nice and snug around the ears with non-slip surface. Has UV protection and Polaroid view. I got them for fishing but they've become my every day wear. Buy em, you'll like em!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Pretty good sunglasses though not good enough for me to keep. The legs on the sunglasses were too tight on the back of my ears, as the flexible material was pretty strongly flexing inwards towards my skull. For some people, they may like that so the glasses stay on, but it somewhat hurt my head while wearing these & driving. The size of the lenses themselves were also slightly too small vertically, so I could see out the bottom of the glasses and a little bit on the sides, which particularly could be annoying/dangerous if the sunlight hit the side of my eye while driving.The material is really soft though and the nose pads feel really good :) The lenses were perfect darkness & polarization so the main function works well. I wish they made the legs less bent inwards and the lenses slightly bigger (or have another model that's slightly bigger lenses) and I would buy these."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good product at a reasonable price."
    },
    {
        "review": "Looks and feels great, almost the same price as the cheapies from Doller stores but better quality, these are my 3rd, 4th and 5th pair"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good while they lasted. The lens seemed durable as they did not get any scratches on them. Unfortunately, the frame broke after about 6 months of occasional use."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good value for a good price"
    },
    {
        "review": "I usually don't spend a lot of money on sun glasses as they are typically lost or broken in a few a months.  I live in Florida and had previous eye surgery so I'm always cautious  about sun exposure and frequently wear eye protection. I previously purchased the Forster grant line, (which has similar pricing)  but I believe that these have them beat. They are light, have polarization protection that really works against glare, UV, etc.. They also come with a great case for travel and an eye cloth. They clean up nice, seem to be rugged enough for the price range. Comfortable fit for me. I would be cautious of the size since it may not fit all faces. For me it worked well. While the plastic seems to be well built I would suspect that over time if I leave them in the car they will start deteriorate like many steering wheels and dashboards  that are constantly exposed to sun and heat in Florida. But for the money, its well worth buying a few pairs. Bought the first one and then a second for my wife who also liked them. They look good and protect against wind abrasion. Haven't had them long enough to see how scratch resistant they are compared to others. However, they have a thick lens."
    },
