        "review": "The size of the sunglasses is too small in general.Probably will be a good fit for a teenager or younger or a female."
    },
    {
        "review": "Very well"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought it as a gift for my junior in office. While seeing the glass, he was so overwhelmed. He likes it very much and thanked me a lot."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these awhile ago for biking, as during trail riding it is necessary to have eye protection from small rocks and insects. They are light in weight, fit snug but not too tight, seem well constructed, and are supremely affordable. But the biggest surprise was the polarization of the lenses: It really helps mitigate reflections and glare so I see better in bright sunlight. The wrap-around design also enhances side protection. I had bought retainer straps but never used them, because these glasses don't slide down my sweaty nose nor have ever fallen off like the old pair I had, even on the roughest of terrain. Very pleased with this purchase."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "The Meta Ray-Ban Wayfarer smart glasses have a really cool combination of classic style and modern technology. The matte black Wayfarer design looks clean and works well as an everyday pair of glasses, while the smart features add some extra convenience.The Transitions lenses are especially useful because they can adjust to changing light conditions, making them more practical for going between indoor and outdoor settings. The AI features and hands-free functionality also make these more than just regular sunglasses.Overall, these are a great option if you want a stylish pair of glasses with useful smart features built in."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these Meta glasses mainly for creating videos on the go, and they have been incredibly convenient. I love being able to capture hands-free footage while driving, shopping, traveling, or filming product content without constantly setting up my phone and tripod. The video quality is surprisingly good, especially in bright daylight or well-lit environments.I’m still exploring all of the features, but for content creation alone they have been worth it. The only downsides I’ve noticed are the battery life, which lasts only a few hours before needing a recharge, and the fact that some features show as unavailable even though I’m located in Texas. I’m not sure if that’s a software issue or a regional restriction.That said, the charging case makes recharging simple and convenient. I just place the glasses back in the case and they’re ready to go again. If you’re looking for an easy way to create POV content without carrying extra equipment, these glasses are a great option. Just keep in mind that, like most cameras, the better the lighting, the better the video quality will be."
    },
    {
        "review": "I am really upset about this purchase. I loved the glasses but stopped working within first month. It was outside the 30 day wi dow to return them. I purchased the 3 year warranty but when I submitted a claim they basically told me that does not take effect until the manufacturer warranty expires. They gave me the details who to submit a claim through which was rayban. I sent my glasses back as they asked and now I they do not have glasses for me, no refund, I am out the total purchase,  plus glasses and insurance plan. RayBan will not email me back, it says under my claim that an agent will contact me to figure something out since the rayban meta 2 matte black with Grey transitions are not available which I find hard to believe. I either need my full refund or another pair of glasses or atleast some help with RayBan customer service. This has been a 2 week ordeal and is very upsetting. Horrible customer service. The email link I was sent to contact does not work. Beyond furious with Amazon and Rayban for taking care of this issue."
    },
    {
        "review": "Meta has apple envy & it shows - you canNOT access your media unless you use their bloated Meta Ai app on your phone... and ONLY on your phone.  the Ai will tell you otherwise, but it lies!  no matter how much memory i clear  the app says 'phone storage full' so my media capture was a waste & this fashion faux pas is getting returned.  NOW the app is bugging out, so it's all gone. (see screenshots for sizes)  At least on GoPro you can preview lower res files, and even edit/crop, before you download them.  the only thing smart about these glasses is the profit margin for meta's cloud conscription.  these aren't worth $200 much less 400+.UPDATE - retrieved the media on a family member's phone.  it was only ~5Gb in total, yet the phone had >13gb free.  Just 1 annoying example of hours of time wasted, on a product that was designed like a slot machine to steal more recurring revenue."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought them for some random video recordings here and there but after a day of wearing them I realized I needed to use these all the time. I thought the AI stuff would be gimmicky but it’s helped a lot from identifying how to care for vegetable plants to helping me keep mites and records for work stuff. Taking photos and videos is super easy. I didn’t think it would make a difference from me pulling my phone out to take a photo or just using the glasses but it has made a huge impact. It’s only a few seconds but the convenience is def there. I don’t find them heavy on my face and they fit pretty well. Only thing would be after a few hours of wearing them, behind my left ear hurts a bit from where the glasses are sitting. I just have to adjust slightly. Battery life does not match what’s advertised but I kinda figured that when buying them. I’m sure the advertised battery life will be correct if you didn’t use any of the functions of the glasses. I did purchase a aftermarket accessory for the battery that is a must have in my opinion if you plan on using these daily and for long amounts of time. The stick/clip onto the glasses where you can add a tiny battery to charge the glasses while wearing and I don’t even notice any extra weight. The transitions are great. For me they transition fine. They don’t get super dark but I don’t mind."
    },
    {
        "review": "I use these glasses everyday! When im outside, at work, when shopping... its very convenient to use! Some of the features are just party tricks to show to your friends, otherwise with full functionality will last you roughly 2 hours just for having the meta AI on. The quality is really good with the camera and sound but you definitely need lighting to film on these, otherwise you can't see in the dark lol. My only complaint is that when your working with these, your sweat might mess up the sensors. I've had some trouble trying to fix that problem but other than that they're great for music too! Very discreet!"
    },
    {
        "review": "​The Ray-Ban Meta Gen 2 Wayfarers are a remarkable fusion of iconic fashion and cutting-edge technology. The 12MP ultra-wide camera captures incredibly sharp 3K video and high-quality stills from a first-person perspective, making it effortless to document memories without ever reaching for a phone. The open-ear audio system is equally impressive, delivering rich sound for music and crystal-clear calls while still allowing me to remain aware of my surroundings. Having Meta AI built directly into the frames feels like the future; I can ask questions about what I’m seeing or control my media hands-free with simple voice commands.​One of the most significant upgrades is the extended battery life, which now lasts up to eight hours on a single charge—nearly double that of the previous generation. The included charging case is sleek and portable, providing an additional 48 hours of power so I never have to worry about running out of juice during a long day of travel or recording. The matte black finish is understated and premium, ensuring these look like classic sunglasses rather than a tech gadget. For anyone who wants a seamless way to stay connected and capture life as it happens, these smart glasses are an absolute must-have."
    },
    {
        "review": "Enjoying arguing with the Meta AI, which is often wrong until you point it toward a current source of info.Bought them for the headphones, which, like the Xreal AR Glasses. Have an open air implementation that allows hearing stuff around you but playing music others don't hear. And the sound while having little bass, is quite good.The 3k hand free photo and video camera is a bonus, but only shoots in vertical, a stupid idea. But meant to push Instagram and Tic-Tic use.In 3k you can blow things up to 16x9 and have ok results.It also answers calls and will do as much as you connect it to.You get the phone audio over the glasses for calls, playing YouTube videos or anything your phone plays, whether an app the AI uses or not.I have Amazon Music and Audible attached so I can voice command them while driving, but Serious radio and YouTube music are fine, but you have to start them manually. The skip to next song glasses commands work on these apps too.Overall a very entertaining device."
    },
    {
        "review": "The general quality and aesthetics are undisputed, they are in all respects the classic Rayban Werfarer. I initially found problems connecting them to my iPhone, but everything was resolved immediately. If you try to vocally ask hey meta, play music on Apple Music, the voice replies that it cannot do it, but it is only due to the time that the Apple cloud memorizes the pairing and then no problem. Just like for Amazon Music or Spotify. Updates are constantly arriving to download via a dedicated app. Music, calls and AI work very well even when cycling. The transition lenses become impeccably dark after a minute in the sun. As soon as you return home or in the car they become clear again. As for the battery, they don't last all day if you use the maximum potential of the glasses but all in all it's fine (if you want to use them only as sunglasses, just turn them off with the appropriate button). The case is the classic Rayban one in all respects, only more technological given that there are LEDs, USBC port and reset button. For the moment very satisfied with the purchase!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent, original and nothing wrong with it"
    },
    {
        "review": "Meta AI is still at the level of a bonus and almost useless. I bought this because I liked the design. It's a pity that the low bridge type is not on sale."
    },
    {
        "review": "Pros: They fit well, comfortable enough, camera quality is decent, delivery and packaging were all great.Cons:1. Lens quality is cheap. It dosent darken quickly and dosent get dark enough. Also the transition dosent work while driving a car or riding a motorbike as the lenses react to UV light instead of visible light and car windshield and motorbike helmet visors filter out UV light so it dosent get dark while driving or riding. I expected XTRActive lenses at this price point which would transition based on visible light.2. Meta AI app uses way too much bandwidth. While outside it goes through 1GB of my mobile data in 10 minutes even though I am just listening to music on the glasses and not asking any AI questions. Data is crazy expensive in Dubai so remember to block the meta AI app from using cellular data.3. Camera angle is a bit awkward from the top left so feels a bit different compared to what you see but it’s not a deal breaker."
    },
    {
        "review": "Great glasses very handy for a lad with a Disability that allows him to take family pictures and video without having to get his phone out. But be aware there is now places that are banning you using them. Which I do you think is sad for the genuine people that are using them for the right reasons appearance wise they look great on the face they can slip down your nose from time to time. Battery life lasts well. You get most of the day out the battery."
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "I had need of some high quality sunglasses because my eye doctor informed me of developing cataracts.  He told me polarized sunglasses would help by cutting down the UV light.  Compounding this is the fact my vision is losing clarity so needed high quality lenses.  I was advised that Maui Jim sunglasses were superior to the other two top contenders:  Ray Ban and Oakley's.  The advice proved true.  The lens clarity has noticeable high tech treatment of light.  I can look directly at the sun with them on without any discomfort. The clarity of the visual field is fantastic.  The frame is very light and conforms nicely to my head.  Unlike contending brands, the lens was curved to block like from the sides.  And, unlike many sunglasses, my eyelashes did not brush the lenses.  A word of caution: I tried three Maui Jim sunglasses on the :\"try before you buy\" program. Two came in large and one was medium. (I bought the medium root beer)  However, the Amazon description for the sunglasses did have dimensions but did not use the term \"medium\" or \"large\".  The size was noted only on the boxes.  I actually liked the green mirror lenses slightly better but did not like the large frame size.  (They kept slipping) I could not determine how to order the green lenses in the medium size so passed on those.  So Amazon and Maui Jim lost a sale. I hope someone reads this and fixes the description.  They are really good sunglasses and deserve to be bought.  Declaring the size would help that."
    },
    {
        "review": "Couldn't be happier with this product.  Needed a pair of sun-glasses that were a bit on the upscale, more professional look, the Maui Jim's are exactly that!!  Couldn't keep wearing the Half-Jacket Gold Iridium with suits, just didn't look right!!  I still have and love the Oakley's, but wear them more as a casual-sport look!  Cost of the Breakwall's was perfect, the fit and weight is second to none!  Tried on the Oakley Plantiffs & Crosshairs, RayBan Aviators, Bolle Columbus, Serengeti Nuvola, Gargoyles The Marshall, Tom Ford Marko, etc., trust me, I did my research!  All the metal-based frames were heavy, where the Breakwall's were \"light & tight\" but not enough to give you that \"sun-glass headache\" that some brands give you!  You have to treat these glasses well, as they are a bit delicate, but I guess that's the trade off for being light as a feather on your face!  Optics/Vision quality is excellent!  Being polarized was a plus!  Classy, but can still use them while out sporting around, ... beach, golf course, boating, or the classic convertible Sunday drive!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased these shades for wearing when there isn't as much sun but I wanted the benefit of the polarized lenses.  I have to say, so far I wear these more than any other pair of shades I have. They do a very good job with exactly what I was looking for; reduced glare, increased clarity, even in low light (and at night).  These are great in the rain, at dusk, on a semi-cloudy day... I've worn them at night and they are pretty good there too reducing glare, if you can get past the \"I wear my sunglasses at night\" kinda uncool feel :).  Lastly, they are extremely light so they are comfortable to wear for an extended period of time. The only drawbacks with these sunglasses so far are the lenses get dirty real easy so you'll need to wipe them often and the frames are a bit flimsy so I am a little worried about the durability.Overall, a very good buy if you are looking for some lighter (shading and weight) sunglasses."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have a weird nose shape and other sunglasses would hurt my nose bridge. I did an internet search for lighweight sunglass frames and these came up. I stupidly put them away in my bag without their case and one of the temples broke, but was able to get a replacement temple for $15 on Maui Jim's website. Recommend these if you want something lightweight, but always put them in their case!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Literally just lenses held together with a small bridge and use nose pads to keep them comfortable. Ultra light.They really keep the sun out of your eyes, and they can be used for things that require precision because they keep your vision clear. But, the place where the small frame meets the lens at the temple can be an easy spot to snap them if you’re not careful.So, make use of the included case, or you could end up with two halves of a pair of glasses"
    },
    {
        "review": "I’ve been a Maui Jim buyer for 20 years.  The Breakwall is a very nice pair of sunglasses.  The nose bridge is very tough as I’ve been wearing them on top of my head and hit against car when opening door and they don’t even budge.  Very well built and flexible.  The lens size is just right for my face and they have great coverage without looking too big.  The glare reduction is great just like in any Maui Jim.  The performance of these sun glasses makes them worth the full retail price of $190, but I’ve seen them on sale for as low as $140.  If $190 is too steep and they aren’t on sale see if they have any ‘Used-Like New’. I did that for my first pair before they went on sale  and got a great pair of sunglasses.  Any way you buy them, they are worth the money and performance is great."
    },
