    },
    {
        "review": "We have bought at least 10 of these. Great quality and exactly like Maui Jims. My husband lost a pair of his MJs so we swapped to these and order a new pair every-time he loses or breaks his current pair. So worth it!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Good for the $"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very light weight sunglasses. So nice to wear them and not feel like you have anything on. Not great to put on your head as they fall off easily if they are flipped up on top of your head."
    },
    {
        "review": "I purchased the pink tortoise and ice blue versions of these glasses. The ice blue pair has yet to arrive, but unfortunately, the pink ones are a big disappointment.Based on the photos, I expected these to have a soft, sophisticated look. In reality, the pink is barely pink. There is a slight pink hue in the center, but all around, the color has this strange greenish-gold tone. It is not attractive at all and looks quite different from what I expected based on the photos.At this point, I have very low expectations for the blue pair. :-)The fit is OK, and the overall look is OK; they do seem well made. They just do not feel particularly sturdy."
    },
    {
        "review": "Have only had them a day, but also purchased the Jim Halo version of these to compare. In my opinion, the Juli's feel better (higher quality feel) and fit better. They certainly aren't Maui Jim quality, but they offer a better fit and higher quality feel compared to the Jim Halo versions. The lenses (vision clarity, polarization, etc.) seem about the same as the Jim Halo's. I bought these to use in situations that I don't want to subject my Maui Jim's to."
    },
    {
        "review": "I wear Maui Jim's, Smiths, and Suncloud (also by Smith). I am used to high quality lenses, but I've always thought that \"high quality\" lenses were fairly common and easy to make, and I was just aa brand snob.These look exactly like Maui Jim's. I want a new style so... Ordered them.The fit: great.The wright: great.They feel durable.They feel comfortable.The style is great.The lenses: useless and I would honestly say no chance I'd wear these sunglasses. Literally zero chance. Why?1. Put these on and look at a regular light bulb. Any light bulb at home. You'll see three images of that light bulb, one to the left which is faint, one to the right which is faint, and the bulb itself in the middle. Not joking. It's as if there is a \"glare\". This is because the lenses are not perfect thickness and magnification, and the lens coating are layered poorly (I am guessing here). Put on a pair of Maui Jim's (or other high end brand) and you'll see just one light bulb.I'm not making this up. Try it.This will affect everything you look at, brighter objects more.2. Look at these glasses while wearing high end glasses. You'll see the polarization film -- especially around the bridge and arms. Now, look at the high end glasses through these. You wont see the polarization film (it's there, you just can't see it). High end lenses have much better and even polarization.The lenses on these glasses are simply too cheap, the flaws are really noticeable. I wish they were better, really do. I love this rimless style."
    },
    {
        "review": "The glasses were broken"
    },
    {
        "review": "Great product - same like Maui Jim’s and even looks like a fancy expensive pair of shades. Polarization is perfect, arms material are perfect.4 stars though because there is a a small tilt on the face because one of the arms is a but curved more than the other and I tried to adjust it but not perfectly still"
    },
    {
        "review": "Very light, beautiful and with UV protection"
    },
    {
        "review": "Decent Glasses. Delicate Product."
    }
