        "review": "The 90s/ Y2K era trends are so in right now and I am all for it, since this is my favorite style era. These fashion forward, retro, oval, cat eye sunglasses caught my attention, with this timeless and trendy cool 90s look and cat eye shape. I could not wait to get them and try them on.Upon first impression, I was so impressed by the quality of these sunglasses and how classy and chic they looked on me. They looked even better in person. I loved the beige color too and the shine of them. They honestly do not look cheap, and they are also super comfortable. I am so excited for warmer weather to come, because these will be my sunglasses to show off and wear. They are versatile and can be worn dressed down or dressed up. Definitely will enhance any look and make you look polished and on trend.Overall, these sunglasses are truly beautiful and well made. They felt light but solid and quality made. I appreciate the brand included cloth to clean the sunglasses and a little Keychain screwdriver, just in case the screw loosens. It shows attention to detail from the seller and thoughtfulness. I definitely recommend this brand and these sunglasses. They are worth it and I absolutely love them. All the best.⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️⭐️"
    },
    {
        "review": "I recently got these phikttu Retro Oval Cat Eye Sunglasses , and I'm really happy with them. The small Y2K-inspired frame is trendy and gives a fun, vintage vibe that goes with almost any outfit.They're super lightweight , so I can wear them all day without any discomfort. The lenses offer decent UV protection , which is great for sunny days. I also like that they don't slip down my nose, even when moving around.My only minor note is that they're quite narrow, so they might feel snug if you have a wider face. Other than that, they're stylish, affordable, and perfect for adding a retro touch to your look."
    },
    {
        "review": "These Phikttu Retro Oval Cat Eye sunglasses are a fantastic little find. They absolutely nail the Y2K vintage aesthetic with that perfectly petite, narrow frame – it’s a very specific, trendy look that avoids feeling costumey. The \"retro oval\" shape is key; it’s a softer, more modern take on a classic cat-eye, making them surprisingly versatile.The best part is how they wear. They are genuinely lightweight, which, combined with the narrow frame, makes them incredibly comfortable for all-day use. You barely feel them on your face, and there's no pinching on the temples or nose—a common issue with smaller vintage-style frames.Importantly, they don’t sacrifice function for form. The UV protection is essential, and the build quality feels well-built for the price point. The hinges are tight, and the materials feel sturdy without being heavy. They have a solid, confident click when you open or close them.In short: These are more than just a cute accessory. They’re a comfortable, well-made throwback that successfully bridges the gap between a trendy Y2K statement and a practical, everyday pair of sunnies. A total win if this is the silhouette you're after."
    }
]

