[
    {
        "review": "This tripod is very stable because it is made from aluminum other than the camera mount portions. This has a lock ring at the base which really helps stabilize it. Even a full extension with my iPhone 17 Pro Max on this when I pushed it with my hand so it would wobble. It settled to still again surprisingly quickly. I would still say proceed with caution if it's a windy day, but it's better than other selfie stick compact tripods I've seen by far. This has a phone mount and a cold shoe mount with a quarter-inch standard tripod thread on it. These are interchangeable; you could also use other cold shoe mount products on it. If you watch my video, you'll see that I put my phone up there with a fill light. It had no problem holding this steady. On my scale, I got a weight of 1-pound 5.3 ounces; they say it will hold up to 1 kg, which is approximately 2.2 pounds. The remote connected quickly to my phone. The whole thing took less than a minute; you can swivel the head on the top of the tripod. It also has the ability to tilt; there are many different configurations. You could set this up depending on your gear. You could use this with a lightweight camera, a phone as a monitor or phone, or a teleprompter. (If you really want to see what this is like, check out my video.)They say that the remote will work at 10 m. I went beyond this to 35 feet and had no problem getting it to trigger my phone. You could also use this as a remote flash holder for an SLR. If you want an extendable compact phone tripod and selfie stick all in one, I would say that its current price of $39.99 is an excellent value. I would definitely recommend this product."
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a really nice phone tripod that feels well made and is easy to use. The button works great for taking pictures, and I really like being able to use it as either a selfie stick or a tripod.The adjustable height is useful, although it isn't quite tall enough to go from the ground to a full-height person. I also really like the push-button mechanism that quickly pops the tripod legs out—it makes setting it up very easy.One thing to note is that there are arms that fold out to hold your phone, which I didn't know because the directions are very light, but when your kid comes over and shows you that the arms fold out it will hold your phone a lot better.  Just look for that.This is a very nice, versatile tripod/selfie stick."
    }
]

