[
    {
        "review": "Why did I wait so long to get this?So Ive been thinking about getting a phone compatible tripod for a while but didnt want to end up with another piece of junk equipment that just sat unused in the corner. After seeing this on sale I decided to go for it.First off it's sturdy, when I pulled this out I was actually surprised how hefty it was. Not necessarily heavy but the majority of it is a lightweight metal when I was expecting it to be mostly plastic. Even then its less than 2lbs with my phone on it so those who need portability, youre good.It comes fully assembled other than choosing which adapter you want to use (phone or go pro) so no annoying instructions and zillion little pieces to deal with before you can use it.The feet are adjustable to fit the footprint of whatever area you have from quite small to fit on a small tabletop to spread out for more stability on the floor, and you can lock them at whatever place you need them.The phone adapter easily fit my iPhone 14ProMax.Height is easily and infinitely adjustable from about 16\" tall to 62\" tall and feels very stable even at full height (although at full extension I definitely recommend spreading the feet out as far as you have room for)Initially I wasn't even going to use the remote but its as easy to connect as a pair of ear buds, through bluetooth settings, and worked perfectly even with my 3rd party camera app.If youre even considering one of these just get it now while it's on sale. Like I said in the title, Im kicking myself that I didnt do it much earlier. Its a great item at a great price."
    },
    {
        "review": "One of my doctors wanted to do a tele-health visit and I needed a way to set up my phone for the video conference, This thing worked great - easy to adjust the height and the clamp held my phone securely.A good price for something  that worked so well!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought the SENSYNE 62\" Phone Tripod & Selfie Stick as a gift for a friend of mine who’s a singer and uses it to record himself for his social media. He’s been really happy with it, and after hearing all the positive feedback from him, I figured I’d share my experience here.First, he loves the height adjustment. At 62 inches, it's the perfect height for him to get a good shot without needing to find a ledge or prop his phone up somewhere awkward. He’s been using it both for singing videos and live sessions, and the adjustable height has given him a lot of flexibility in how he frames his shots.The selfie stick feature is another thing he’s mentioned he really likes. He’s able to easily switch from tripod mode to selfie mode, which is great when he wants to record himself up close, especially for those personal moments with his fans. And he really appreciates the remote shutter. He can start recording or snap pictures without needing to run back and forth to the phone, which saves a lot of time and hassle.My friend also told me he’s been impressed with the stability of the tripod. Even when he's singing or moving a bit while recording, the tripod holds the phone steady, and he hasn’t had any shaky footage. He’s been using it regularly for recording Instagram videos and live performances, and it’s definitely helped with getting more professional-looking content.Portability is another reason he’s happy with it. The tripod is lightweight and compact enough for him to easily carry around, whether he’s heading to a recording session or just moving between rooms at home. He says it fits easily into his bag and doesn’t add too much bulk, which is great for someone who’s always on the go.As for the build quality, he mentioned that it’s solid but not too heavy-duty. It’s more than sturdy enough for regular use, though. The phone mount is adjustable and keeps his phone secure, even when he’s recording for extended periods.All in all, my friend’s been super happy with the SENSYNE 62\" Phone Tripod & Selfie Stick. He told me it’s made a big difference in the quality of his recordings, and he finds it super easy to use. Based on his experience, I’d definitely recommend this to anyone who’s looking for an affordable and versatile tripod or selfie stick for social media content creation!"
    },
    {
        "review": "Does the job, wish it were easier to angle the camera though. It seems to only go straight but you can raise and lower the camera to fit desired height."
    },
    {
        "review": "Even though this is a lightweight tripod, it’s well made and sturdy enough to hold my iPhone steady in most of the conditions I’m likely to use it. It appears to be made all of aluminum.  (Another Sensyne tripod I tried—the 60”— was all plastic and very flimsy.) Set up is smooth and easy, and it’s easy to attach your phone. It’s useful for selfies, low and overhead shots, too.Highly recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "Either I was in the picture or my wife, or we needed to rely on a passerby (who often times chopped off our heads) to snap a pix. With this stand & the included remote, we can both be in the shot. While I wouldn't recommend it for regular use, this stand can also support a changeable lens camera in a pinch (although the remote only controls a cellphone). Cellphone videos are also a lot more stable with the stand.Do yourself a favor & buy a CaSZLUTION Travel Case when you buy this stand. With the head folded down it fits the tripod nicely with a little room to spare. At only $16 it's a good deal & even better if you catch it on sale."
