    {
        "review": "Durable and well made.  I bought my stand several years ago and it is just as good today as it was when I first got it highly recommend."
    },
    {
        "review": "Pro’s;- Economical, nice fit, finish and packaging especially for the price.- Protective adhesive pads on the contact points for the phone as well as on the stand base.- Sturdy construction. It appears as if it will stand up to frequent use without scratching or scuffing and should not easily bend or dent if dropped etc.- The large hole in the stand to easily run your charging cable through was well thought out. Not unique to this brand but much appreciated.Con’s;- It seems a little small for my iPhone 6+. When I opened the package and saw the stand I thought perhaps I had not ordered the right model for a 6+ but the description clearly listed the 6+ as compatible. It certainly does fit the 6+ plus but with the low weight of the stand combined with it’s relative size (and weight) compared to my iPhone 6+ I have some concerns about stability or resistance to tipping over if lightly bumped or if the lightening cable it plugged in and gets snagged on something.- A wider base footprint with a little more weight would relieve some of my concerns as the elevated phone makes these two combined very top heavy especially in portrait mode. Although they have diminished significantly in the last few years we had a spat of mild earthquakes in central Oklahoma a few year back could easily topple this with a phone in portrait mode.I would have more faith in the phone and stand not toppling over under normal conditions if;- The base foot print was wider and perhaps a little heavier (if you have a semi permanent location in mind double sided tape might be an option).- the back support reached at least 2/3 of the way up the back of my 6+ but with my case installed it reaches less than 1/2 the way up (2/5 the way up to be exact) See included pic from the back with my phone in stand. *Back support is 66mm tall.- the phone support arms were a little wider apart. *The product description does clearly show that the outer edges of the phone support arms are 54mm/2.14” apart so you can compare with your phone before ordering. With my relatively small protective case my 6+ is 82mm/3.125” wide in portrait mode which leaves just over an inch difference or 1/2” on either side if perfectly centered. This may be partially more of an aesthetic preference but considering how top heavy the phone is on the stand I would definitely prefer less than 2-3 mm overlap on either side of the support arms.I set my old iPhone 4S with it’s case in the stand for comparison which is much lighter and quite a bit smaller. This seemed a near perfect fit with the back of the phone support reaching at least 1/2 way up and virtually no phone overlap on the support arms.Although not stated anywhere in the description the picture with the exploded diagram of internal “hinge” led me to believe the amount of tension required to change the angle was adjustable so you could lock down a preferred angle which you cannot. That was my misunderstanding however and so far the tension seems adequate to prevent accidental movement while also allowing easy adjustment. This is not really a con and possibly actually a pro that they achieved a perfect balance on the tension assuming you don’t want the option to lock the angle down to prevent accidental manipulation.Overall a good product especially at the price but I would gladly pay more for a similar design that covered my stability concerns."
