        "review": "Love the duo pack, one for my office at home and office. Adjustable for any options."
    },
    {
        "review": "when I purchased these, it was at 60% discount for $7.98 for2.  So I admit, I did go into this with low expectations.  I gave it three stars as you should consider this to be a \"cheap item\" and you \"get what you pay for\".  even if it was at full price of 2 for $19.99it \"basically works\" as long as I don't bump it much.  if I have to poke around on the screen much while it's on the stand, it's likely going to fall off.the support arms are just too short.  if you look at the photos, they show the phone without any case on it. my phone has the slimmest otterbox case (can't remember the name).  It does not fit when standing in portrait.  it does fit (barely) when in landscape orientation.  another 0.25\" would probably be the solution.another issue when in portrait orientation is the backing is short.  now ... i DO have the Samsung S23 Ultra, which is a big phone.  the top of the stand hits the midway point of the phone. if the arms could have actually wrapped around the bottom of the phone, this would probably be ok.that being said ... it doesn't fall off the stand if I try to tap on the phone screen.  it WILL topple over though.  it's possible if the stand were heavier that at some point tapping the screen might make it jump off the support arms. I'll never know because it will fall over backwards before that ever happens.  the more the angle of the stand is tilted backwards, the worse this becomes.  And being in portrait is much worse than landscape.it's ability to be COMPACT is a PLUS!so despite the unfortunate short arm issue, I still plan to keep using this because 1) it's better than nothing, 2) it does fold up nicely, and 3) It's not worth me paying 20-30$ for one that's slightly bigger.so ... before you buy, consider what I've said.if you just need something to hold it up in the air and you're not typing on it, it's probably a good buy."
