[
    {
        "review": "I bought this 4lb guitar when I learned I was supposed to have surgery and would not be able to lift more than 5 pounds for a couple of months. I’ve had it for about a month or so, and I’m still getting used to it, but it has become my main road guitar. It plays as acoustic or amplified and I’m loving that it’s carbon fiber so I can leave it in the hot truck and not worry about it. The sound isn’t amazing, but it’s good enough for jams and open mics. It’s super light, super cute and the price was easy on the pocketbook. I still have not figured out all of the effects or the app, but I really haven’t tried. Definitely recommended."
    },
    {
        "review": "Wow, really impressed with this guitar, for the price it's a sleek and handsome instrument, doesn't sound as deep and bassy as a conventional acoustic, the tone is different, more bright, and it's still full of natural volume and I like the stylish soundhole that looks like a flame. My 3 year old has a penchant for putting objects into the soundholes of guitars and I hope this will prevent that behavior! I haven't tried the electronics on this yet. It's relatively lightweight and of a manageable medium size, thin body, easy to play and tune and seems to stay in tune well. I'm really going to enjoy using this.Oh, all the accessories too!!(In my photo I have a strap on it purchased separately, it's not the one that came with it).The beautiful color choices were tempting but I ended up going with clean bright white for maximum visual impact.Also the travel case it comes with is good quality and comfortable to wear on your back so the guitar is easily portable for the roving troubador. This is my first time owning a carbon fiber guitar, so it feels like a new adventure. I think this would be a great guitar for people who live in humid environments because the inside won't get that musty smell like wooden acoustics do."
    },
    {
        "review": "A great guitar, especially for the price. Tuning machines keep in tune. The sound is great. There's one thing need to be aware of is the electric one, the saddle was cut to be mass produced for every guitar however the adjustment was not made to accommodate the extra (2mm) height of the pickup wire under the saddle. Caused the action to be too high. I tried cutting/sanding down the saddle, didn't do it exactly correct and needed another saddle. Contacted Enya, and the shipped another saddle out to me, completely free of charge. Great customer service.Other than that, great guitar, great sound, comes with a nice extra set of string. And certainly durable. Dropped it and scratched it a little and still works great. Light weight, great guitar on the go, and great for a first/beginner guitar. The price and value, can't go wrong."
    },
    {
        "review": "I've had this guitar for awhile now and I'm not sure if I would purchase it again.For the price I think putting the money toward a Tonewood amp may have been a better choice for me.I still enjoy this guitar and it does get played.The good points:It has good build quality, the frets are smooth and level, tuners are decent, strings are good, gig bag is nice.Sound is full for such a small acoustic and it holds tune well.You can connect your phone to the guitar and play backing tracks through the internal amp.Guitar also sounds good connected to an amp.The guitar feels durable and is built for travel, I have no fear of damaging it or having a problem due to environmental changes.The areas needing improvement:The action was extremely high, there is an inspection ticket stating the action at less than half of what it actually measured. The saddle had to be sanded to lower the action to the correct height, after that the guitar plays great.The electronics need the app to be usable, out of the box settings you can hardly here any effects coming from the guitar. I had to increase the volume using the app to set the level, not a big deal but should be set higher from the factory as you can adjust the volume down with the knob.Effects are not that great, app adjustability is limited and you are stuck with only the 4 effects. They should have added the ability to choose different effects and create your own patches. Digital processors are cheap and some more usable effects would have been nice.Overall it's a nice travel guitar (after adjusting the action) it sounds bigger than it is.The internal amp is nice even with the limited effects (after adjusting levels with the app).The App connects well and is easy to use, the ability to play backing tracks through the guitar adds to the fun and is a good tool for practice.Keep in mind the guitar may need some setup to play nice like mine did, if you cannot do this yourself it will be an added cost."
    },
    {
        "review": "I have 3 Enya caron fiber guitars and I love all of them. Most recently I bought the NOVA GO SP1 acoustic which I will say I had reservations with, I was a little hesitant about its durability, size and how it would sound, but all for naught as it doesn’t dissapoint in build quality, appearance or sound characteristics. I had been learning to play, on and off for quite a few years, sometimes ardently commited to it, other times half heartedly, but always loving the instrument and loving to “play”. Regardless of if I was any good at it, after all, the only one I had to please or entertain was myself. I was finally getting to a point where I was feeling confident, like I was finally “getting it” when unfortunately, at about that same time, I developed a health condition which caused me chronic pain and to become fatigued very quickly. The weight and size of my guitars was intolerable, so I begrudginly had to give it up completely. I am so grateful to have recently seen these carbon fiber guitars on Amazon, I was intrigued by the positive reviews and all the comments regarding their weight and convenience. I figured I would give them a try even with my low stamina and back pain issues. I started with the XMari and loved it, then the Go Sonic, loved that too, and now the SP1. Enya hit the trifecta on these, the light weight and convenience have allowed me to pick up the thing I loved so much again and the excellent quality of the looks, construction, functionallity and sound is the icing on the cake. I would reccomend these to anyone, from beginner or hobbyist to seasoned pro. I can’t say enough good about all of the Enya products, the kind of quality and value that is a rarity in todays world."
    },
    {
        "review": "Good starter guitar. Does not need an amp for playing, however when playing with an amp I hear a lot of static."
    },
    {
        "review": "Quality: Good quality materialsDurability: Quite sturdyAppearance: Premium look, minimalist & gothicAction: Low action, and still adjustableNeck: Neck is nice, a bit small for me but manageableSound: Not that impressive when speaker is off. But quite nice when speaker is on and with effects.Overall: Very nice product. Very durable, portable, weather proof, and has premium look. Easy 4.5⭐️ to 5⭐️"
    },
    {
        "review": "This guitar is an amazing addition to my collection of budget guitars that hit way above their price point! With it's all fiber carbon body, it's resistant to temp changes, it's extremely lightweight, and very portable!I love the case it came with, and even the strap is perfectly fine here! I love the built in speaker with the 4 different effects! You can Bluetooth to it, so you can actually play to a back track if you wanted to. There's an app for it I haven't checked out yet, but I'm sure it is full of extra goodies for this 21rst century guitar! You get a pretty full, deep sound out of this little guitar, and I dare say it is amazing when plugged into an amp! I got this on sale for 224.99, and it is worth every penny! My only concern is the inevitable day the batterie inside it dies, and how I go about having that replaced, but that should be a good 5 years away or so, and I'll cross that bridge when I get there. For me, this was a self-bought birthday present I picked up and added to my personal collection that does not disappoint! If you've been on the fence about buying one, my advise is to take the plunge and you wont want to look back! A truly exceptional guitar!"
    }
]

