[
    {
        "review": "Awesome guitar! Easy to play, has a built in tuner is beautifully finished and sounds amazing through a matched Fender Acoustisonic amp. Was priced like it was stolen!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I ordered this model Fender Guitar for my 86 year old husband as his Christmas present.  Giving him this beautiful surprise present at Christmas brought joy to our family.  My husband had admired our son's guitar that is this same model and said how much he would love to have one just like it.  At Christmas when my husband first received the guitar I wrote an \"outstanding rave\" review about the guitar.  Less than 2 months later I am back with very bad news.  My husband complained to our son that he was having difficulty tuning his guitar.  Our son checked it out and discovered the problem!  The 6th string (E), 2nd, 3rd and 4th frets have sunk into the keyboard there by making the guitar untunable.  The guitar sounds horrible!  My husband is very disappointed and his Christmas gift has turned into a joyless, sad and expensive mistake.  Fender Company can you help us?July 16, 2023-  Since I wrote my original evaluation about the guitar I bought my Husband, the Fender Guitar Company has come to my rescue.  They have made everything right.  I found them very responsive to my problem and more than willing to help.  My husband now loves playing his beautiful guitar with the fabulous tone."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought the Fender CD-60-SCE. It came in good condition and on time. The action is great right out of the box. And the built in pickup sounds good so far. The built in tuner is also very accurate. About 16 months ago I bought the Fender CD-60S (which is the same thing but without the pickup) it is holding up very well and still sounds great. The only sign of wear is the finish on the neck has worn off a little from my fret hand but it is barely noticeable and not at all an issue. They also stay in tune well. overall REALLY RECOMMEND THESE GUITARS!!!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I was not disappointed in any way with this guitar. It's my northern guitar for when we're home in Massachusetts.  I leave the Gibson in Florida. The fended is way less expensive, but the quality is there, and the sound is excellent - after a couple of tweaks.When the guitar arrived, I knew it'd need SOME work, so I was ready. I'd ordered a set of BONE pins, nut, and saddle. When I immediately replaced the strings upon the guitar's arrival, I fitted the bone components. If you have an inexpensive guitar, it's likely that these pieces are composite. Replace them with bone! Replace them with bone! Replace them with bone. This (https://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B07CQSZQZL/ref=ppx_yo_dt_b_search_asin_title?ie=UTF8&psc=1) is the one I used. I can guarantee (from other guitars I've owned) the proper nut and saddle increase both volume and sustain.If you don't feel up to the job, take it somewhere and have it done. The neck guitar that I received needed no adjustment, and the new saddle matched the original one perfectly.By the way, the built-in tuner and pickups are worth the extra expense."
    },
    {
        "review": "A significant improvement over my beater, Hohner acoustic. Easy on the hands. Seems to be settling in after practicing on it for about a half hour. Strings definitely were not pre-stretched. Nice sound projection and the body resonates nicely. Sustains a note/chord for long time. It rewards you well sonically when you hit the chords and notes just right.I can't say much regarding the \"setup\" because I am not skilled enough to determine if the neck needs adjustment or anything like that. Looks fine to me when I hold it up closely and look down the neck/frets. The saddle and nut also seem fine, but I will likely replace the saddle and nut as well as the pins with those made of bone for both tone and cool factor. Head stock and tuning knobs all seem fine on close inspection and operation.Sorry to report not much useful info from me on the electronics because I don't have an amp. But one thing of note... Be aware that the built in tuner will not work unless you have it plugged into an amp. I confirmed this with the included Fishman instructions. I thought the tuner would come on anytime I wanted so I could tune it. Nope. Must be plugged in to an amp. Thinking back, it makes sense, because the sound is transduced into an electric signal by the Fishman pickup on its way to the amp.Docked one star in craftsmanship for the sloppy application of stain you see in the pic as well as some minor finish aberrations. The builder(s) just let the stain run down into the sound hole; they didn't actually put it there with intent. It would have only taken 3 seconds to correct this during the staining process. I will fix it with one of those stain pens you can get at any DIY store because my eye automatically goes directly to that spot when I pick it up. Leaving it raw wood would have even looked better. Also noticed some aberrations on the body if I hold it at specific angles. You can detect them as distortions of the glare, but not when looking at it \"normally.\" I cannot feel them when I run my finger over those areas though. Maybe just the clearcoat.All told, this seems like a decent guitar for the price. I am not disappointed, even with the small cosmetic flaws. Hopefully one day I will be able to play good enough to get all the potential out of this guitar.Good luck to everyone learning. Anything worth learning requires effort. At least, that is what I keep telling myself."
    },
    {
        "review": "This was a gift for 15 year old god son who recently started taking guitar lessons he is happy with it"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is my 3rd Fender in my collection.  I originally played a Les Paul Jr in the 60s. I loved that one, the stratocaster is my choice now. The other is a 3/4 Fender Acoustic guitar,  nylon strings.  Great practice one for me.The CD 60 is farthest in the photo, the built in tuner works great. After initial tuning, the guitar stayed tuned first couple days.  Seems to have a good setup, the tonal quality is excellent and with amp really nice. Kinda warm, not twangy."
    },
    {
        "review": "Even though this carries Fender's name, it's a very cheap and poorly constructed guitar. The high e and the b string buzz. The neck doesn't adjust easily. I waited past the return date so now I'm stuck with it. Now I have to decide if I want to sink more money into it to set it up properly. In the electronics are subpar. The low e tone overwhelms the other five strings. No matter how I adjust my settings. So for example, when you play an e major chord, All you hear is the overwhelming e bass note from the low e string. The other five strings don't ring out. Cleanly. I'm not happy with this purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "Excellent guitar to get back into it. Easier than an Ovation Celebrity whose neck is thinner (42 mm compared to 45 for the Fender) with my big fingers it's a joy :o). It arrived today. Well done Northerners for sending it to me so quickly (they really are the best ;o))"
    },
    {
        "review": "This is a beautiful guitar and I'm really happy with it. The finish looks fantastic, it feels well made, and it sounds great whether you're practising at home or plugging it into an amp.One thing I noticed straight away compared to cheaper guitars is how much more comfortable it is to play. The strings don't feel as harsh on my fingers, and the guitar was easy to adjust to my preferred setup. That made learning and practising much more enjoyable.I've also had quite a few compliments on how it looks. Both friends and strangers have commented that it's a great-looking guitar, and apparently it makes me look pretty good holding it too, which is a nice bonus.Overall, it's an excellent instrument with great build quality, comfortable playability, and a fantastic appearance. I'd definitely recommend it."
    },
    {
        "review": "For that price you can have a good quality sounding acoustic guitar. Comes with built in tuner so its really a big plus. Build quality is top notch. Looks good overall and feels good as well. Perfect for beginners"
    },
    {
        "review": "The guitar was actually good quality but I sended it back because it was loud and the body a bit to big for me. But I really recommend this guitar to anyone."
    },
    {
        "review": "The d,b and e strings buzz irritably after few months of usage and you can’t help( maybe try using capo on other frets!)Have watched tons of YouTube videos to try correct this but in vain.Just don’t buy this if you look forward to having a guitar that your kids will play (if you’re 25!) coz it won’t last even half a year.Now, instead of sinking the repair costs I’ll have to look for a new one in the nearby store 🥲"
    }
]

[
    {
        "review": "Been playing for 30 years and always wanted a 12 string. With prices this low figured why not. Ordered this and it showed up quickly. Very nice right out the box. The small G string popped on me and took an .010 string from a pile of them I have and tried that, popped that one too. Tried it again and it came right in tune.  After that it took a few days for the strings to stop drifting out of tune and are now pretty solid. I play it daily and its a great player. This is one of those guitars you can just get lost in noodling. Plugged it up to my amp and it sounded great. No fret buzz and the neck plays easy. The built in tuner is a nice feature too.If you always wanted a 12 string acoustic/electric then this one is worth considering. It really is a beautiful guitar."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought this guitar for my son to replace my twenty year old Takamine 12 string that he had been playing for the last five years.From my son's point of view, the guitar is easy to play for a 12 string.  The onboard tuner is an upgrade from the older guitar because it also shows the battery life.  It's also easy to read.  The sound quality is bright and has a higher register.  It is smaller than the Takamine.  He said the fretboard was high quality.As for looks, it's a beautiful guitar.  It's sleek and elegant.We're both happy with the purchase."
    },
    {
        "review": "This brings plays very nicely. I bought the Vangoa 12 string from Amazon and was very disappointed so I replaced it with this Ibanez. The Vangoa did have a nice matte black finish but the tuners were garbage. This Ibanez has a satin neck and glossy body finish. Does have some sharp fret ends that can be fixed with some minor sanding. Tuners hold time nicely even though 12 strings are notoriously difficult to keep in tune. For estethic reasons I changed the tuners to bronze. The action after was great up to the 12th fret but too high afterwards so I did take out bridge saddle and sand it from the bottom end (approximately 1mm) to lower the overall action.  There is a spare saddle included incase you need it. Worked out well afterwards. Overall would highly recommend if you’re looking play Pink Floyd Wish You Were Here or Bon Jovi songs lol at home but if you something more professional for recording then I would recommend something better."
    },
    {
        "review": "The build quality.. the tone.. the attention to detail... the playability This guitar has everything I was looing for, and then  delivered more than I expected"
    },
    {
        "review": "Guitar player for 20 years. I always wanted a 12-string guitar. Ibanez never fails to impress! Even though this price point might be more \"entry-level\", it feels and sounds incredible. Electronic preamp/mic hardware is solid, and onboard tuner works great. Action is low to and strings very playable. I will be using this for a long time!"
    },
    {
        "review": "I love this guitar.  I needed it for one song in my Cinderella tribute band, and it sounds and plays amazing."
    },
    {
        "review": "Came out of the box very badly out of tune. I'm talking wildly out of tune, 1.5-2 steps up or down in tuning. Not only this, but when I was able to get it in tune, almost every single string had fret buzz across the entire neck... I'm not sure how this was built, but I would not pay $50 for it.Action was good. The neck was flat; it should have been fine. I wasn't trying to fix this straight out of the box; I'm sending it back for a refund.I suggest you look at something else or risk having high action on a 12-string cutaway by adjusting the truss rod. NOPE"
    },
    {
        "review": "Took a chance, but sent it back.  Ordered a Fender for just a little bit more..no comparison."
    },
    {
        "review": "It arrived today, in great condition and I played it for an hour, heavily,(after tuning) and it held its tuning very well. I had left the sunburst model in my wish list too long and that color had run out, but I settled for a black one and it looks and plays great. I have small hands and to save my sciatic hip, I stand up to play, most of the time but it puts pressure on my neck so I need a lighter guitar. It has a nice balance (the neck is surprisingly on the heavy side but it balances the body very well, IMO. So it arrived by DHL and they kept me well informed of delivery. Love the guitar. I got a good one. ;-) I plugged it into the amp -- no problem. The guitar has a nice tone -- not too deep and not too bright when played acoustically. The price was right and the guitar was excellent, IMO"
    },
