        "review": "I appreciated the price for this guitar.  Seems solidly made and electronics are well done - no glitches so far.  I like the composition of woods and the resulting sound is clear, can be loud if you want it that way.  The imbedded tuner is handy as heck, and the action on the fret board is remarkably low making it fairly easy to play, bend notes, and move quickly.  HOWEVER - I do not like the finish on the sounding board.  It looks like it is dusty or dirty all the time as a result.  Because it comes without a pick guard - the finish is getting scratched.  The tuners do not move smoothly and so tuning becomes an issue when needed.  And when playing through and amp - it is easy to over power the amp and get some pretty crappy sound as a result.  This guitar plays beautifully as an acoustic - just use some caution when plugging in as the sound is easily distorted.  Major drawback - comes without a case!  I am glad I bought it - love the cutaway - good guitar."
