        "review": "The guitar arrived packaged well and has no damage whatsoever. The finish is lovely and the fretboard inlay is stunning. It's a bit hit or miss buying import guitars online sight unseen and unplayed, but this was a good specimen for me. The frets are well dressed, though the action is a bit on the high side. I don't mind a higher action, so that's not a problem for me. The strings on it, especially the higher three, are kind of dead sounding but will do for now. I'll replace them as needed.The guitar only arrived with the truss wrench, there was no warranty or inspection cards or promotional material whatsoever. This could be good or bad depending on your point of view, but it was worth mentioning.The guitar only took about a day to play in to reach tuning stability."
