[
    {
        "review": "Great sound for my classical guitar.  Rich, mellow tone."
    },
    {
        "review": "I'm not a 'guitarist', nor ever claimed, but I know what good strings are supposed to sound like. And these are it. Granted, the true string player knows more about brilliance, attack, and strength of strings than anyone. But I believe these are the standards for classical guitars. I didn't realize I got the 'tie-on' type rather than 'ball end', but I made do and used my brain to get through the installation. I think I smelled smoke. I had to redo them because they slipped out of the twisty knot I had put them in. Once they were on and not coming loose, the stretching to come was. Each string, methodically, with your fingers in a certain way.  I learned from another musician long ago by watching. It took a while for them to hold their note without going loose and changing its tune. But once they settled into where they're living, they sound fresh and new, with a brilliant tone and timbre. Now, I just have to play it more and take advantage of the newness. The price is mild and close to the range of everywhere else."
    },
    {
        "review": "I got these for my daughter for her classical guitar, and she says they're good quality"
