        "review": "The strings are great! , but the people who packed it at Amazon dropped the strings on detergent and the cardboard box was soaked on it. Thank God the strings come in a plastic bag and did not suffered damages."
    },
    {
        "review": "I bought these strings as I’m helping restore a family members classical guitar. The strings are labeled making it easy to know which string you need to put on next. The sound once I put them on is very full, with a bit of a deeper sound as opposed to twangy (this may vary based on your guitar, the wood, etc.). The strings are also very easy to play on, they are smooth and can be tuned in various ways ways without breaking. Naturally the nylon E, B, & G stretch a bit more when you put them on, so have patience the first few hours as they will stretch and require more tuning than E, A, & D. All in all, they are strong strings but easy to play, neither too thick or too thin. I would purchase these again. :)"
