    {
        "review": "I love the sound of the ProArte Nylon strings on my classical guitar, and the EJ45 weight gives me the right balance of darkness of tone vs ease of playability that I like. Not too dark, not too bright, and I can sing and play some pop or rock in a pinch when I didn't also bring a steel-string guitar. The EJ45 is light enough that I can bend notes in a blues or rock solo when I want to; on the other hand they might be too light for serious classical-only players. I have found ProArte strings to be as consistent from pack to pack as any brand you can name. I say the ProArte are the best value of tone quality vs price."
